{"arxiv_id": "1909.03555v1", "title": "Performance considerations on execution of large scale workflow applications on cloud functions", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Adopt a trigger-based serverless burst playbook: when a GSE batch job exceeds 2 hours wall-clock or 8 vCPU-hours, run the ported benchmark harness (achieved-parallelism curve, wall-clock mean/SD, cold-start rate, cost per unit work) and burst serverless only if it beats the VM on wall-clock at <=1.5x cost; never quote the paper's 2019 figures as current.", "gate": "ADAPT the benchmark methodology (not the 2019 numbers) if a GSE batch job is identified that exceeds the 2-hour/8-vCPU-hour trigger; additionally benchmark cold-start-aware inference cost (serialized XGBoost/ONNX payload, p50/p99 latency vs provisioned-concurrency cost) for live endpoints.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
