{"arxiv_id": "1911.08138", "title": "A regularized hidden Markov model for analyzing the \"hot shoe\" in football", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build gse.regimes.SparseFormHMM (2-3 latent form states, state-varying intercept, LASSO + relaxed LASSO covariate screening via smooth-|.|, 50-value log-spaced lambda grid with BIC selection) with time-gap-aware transitions for irregular NFL event spacing, emitting posterior form-state probabilities as features for player-prop and game models.", "gate": "On 2022-2024 holdout FG data, the sparse form-HMM beats the plain logistic baseline by >= 0.005 log-loss AND the simulation replication selects zero noise covariates in >=75/100 runs. Fail either -> REJECT for production (keep as screening tool only).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "1911.08791", "title": "Bayesian Hierarchical Models for the Prediction of Volleyball Results", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt the three-module factorization to NFL: Module 1 -- home/away points ~ Poisson/NB on pre-game EPA-based unit ratings; Module 2 -- Bernoulli on close-margin bucket; Module 3 -- Bernoulli on win; one posterior yielding coherent P(win), P(cover), P(over), fit in Stan/PyMC with weekly expanding windows.", "gate": "ADOPT the joint three-module factorization if, on 2025 held-out NFL games, the joint model's Brier on moneyline + spread + totals is better than independent-module equivalents on >=2 markets AND no worse than v5.2.7 on the third.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
