{"arxiv_id": "1912.01603v3", "title": "Dream to Control: Learning Behaviors by Latent Imagination", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build GSE-Dream, a latent NFL game simulator (RSSM-style: GRU + stochastic latent s_t over engineered play features, transitions conditioned on pregame team-strength embeddings, decoders for score events and next-play descriptors) for pricing; the actor-critic/policy-learning half is explicitly out of scope.", "gate": "ADOPT the latent-simulator architecture for GSE pricing if on 2024 held-out games: (i) one-step-ahead log-likelihood improves >=5% over the bootstrap baseline, AND (ii) simulated final-score distributions match empirical within 5% total-variation distance per week, AND (iii) simulated kickoff win probabilities have ECE <= 0.03.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "1912.04465", "title": "SoccerDB: A Large-Scale Database for Comprehensive Video Understanding", "normalized_lane": "sports_cv", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build GSE-VideoUnderstand on NFL broadcast: player/ball detection -> per-class object masks -> MRTS two-stream (RGB + mask) event classifier for fine-grained play events (sack, interception, broken tackle) -> BMN-style temporal proposals with play = snap-to-whistle boundaries -> branched multi-task head for event recognition + highlight scoring (never naive shared-trunk multi-task).", "gate": "On GSE's NFL event clips, the object-mask stream must add >=+5 absolute points mAP over the RGB-only SlowFast baseline (paper: +9.41) and the branched highlight head must not degrade event-recognition mAP by more than 0.5 points.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "1912.04871v4", "title": "Deep symbolic regression: Recovering mathematical expressions from data via risk-seeking policy gradients", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Implement risk-seeking fine-tuning as a PySR post-pass: embed PySR hall-of-fame expressions as starting programs and run an RL loop (REINFORCE with top-epsilon quantile baseline, epsilon~0.2) mutating expressions, rewarding held-out-season predictive r under a hard constraint mask (forbid >1 nested trig, single-input expressions, >15 nodes).", "gate": "ADOPT the risk-seeking post-pass if its best <=15-node expression beats the best PySR-only <=15-node expression by >=0.03 test r on 2024-2025, with the constraint mask preventing degenerate solutions; REJECT if the RL loop collapses to PySR's own hall-of-fame or underperforms.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INVENT", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "1912.05129v2", "title": "Measuring Spatial Allocative Efficiency in Basketball", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add an NFL Target Allocation Efficiency (TAE) metric: per team-week (rolling 4-week), rank receivers by efficiency (EPA/target) and by allocation (target share/TPRR) within route-depth x field-zone cells, compute rank correspondence and an NFL LPL (expected EPA lost vs rank-matched optimal allocation), with player-level TPC apportioned by target deviation -- for weekly props and coaching content.", "gate": "ADAPT to a weekly props/coaching metric if, on 2022-2025 nflverse, the TAE-augmented game model beats the baseline (EPA/play + Herfindahl) by >=0.5 points of out-of-sample RMSE per game AND theta's 95% CI excludes 0 with the expected sign.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "1912.05642v4", "title": "Local scale invariance and robustness of proper scoring rules", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add SCRPS (scaled CRPS) as a second, scale-normalized engine ranking in gse-backtest/scoring/ alongside the average-CRPS leaderboard, logging any rank flip between the two, with an rCRPS capped-pairwise-distances option for blowout robustness.", "gate": "Adapt only if, on GSE's last 3 seasons of spread + total backtests, the engine ranking under mean SCRPS differs from the ranking under mean CRPS for >= 2 games-target pairs -- i.e. the scale-normalization changes at least one engine selection decision.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "1912.06806v1", "title": "SemEval-2013 Task 2: Sentiment Analysis in Twitter", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the annotation protocol as GSE's standard sports-text benchmark: 5 annotators per item, majority-label adjudication, the (F_pos+F_neg)/2 metric for bullish/bearish/neutral player-news classification, phrase-vs-message subtasks; evaluate zero-shot LLMs and the 1106 lexicon-CNN against it.", "gate": "ADOPT the protocol as GSE's standard sports-text benchmark if inter-annotator agreement (Fleiss kappa) reaches >=0.6 on a 200-item pilot; REJECT the protocol if kappa < 0.4 (task too subjective for sports text).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "1912.07441v1", "title": "Multi-stream Data Analytics for Enhanced Performance Prediction in Fantasy Football", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Add a DFS/props multi-stream projection layer: per-position gradient-boosting models predicting P(player hits upside threshold) on feature streams of nflverse/FTN stats, Odds-API implied totals and player-prop lines as features, and entity-level beat-writer news sentiment (skip raw tweets); weekly expanding-window retraining.", "gate": "Adopt the multi-stream pattern if, on 2021-2024 backtest, the full-stream model beats the stats-only baseline by >=10% total points with each added stream (odds, news sentiment) contributing positively in ablation; reject the text-sentiment stream (keep odds+stats) if news sentiment fails to add value.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "1912.08726v4", "title": "Econometrics for decision making: building foundations sketched by Haavelmo and Wald", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Add a regret-based staking audit: define a calibration-error state space {true win prob in [engine prob - epsilon, engine prob + epsilon]} with epsilon from calibration analysis, compute worst-case regret vs oracle Kelly across states on 2023-2025 bets, and add 'maximum regret across calibration-error states' to the pick evaluation dashboard alongside EV/ROI/CLV -- used as an engine-honesty risk overlay capping stakes, never as the sizing objective.", "gate": "Adopt the regret-overlay if: on 2024-2025 walk-forward, the MMR-capped rule achieves >=90% of full-Kelly log growth while cutting worst-case (state-space) regret by >=30%.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "1912.10417v1", "title": "Modelling Basketball Players' Performance and Interactions Between Teammates with a Regime Switching Approach", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build teammate-synergy detection: per-player 2-state Markov switching on per-drive smoothed fantasy-points-above-expectation to classify hot/cold regimes, then ARIMAX/logistic on regime labels with on-field co-presence dummies (WR2 in route tree, backup RB on 3rd down) producing a signed synergy network -- QB<->WR positive edges become DFS stack candidates.", "gate": "ADAPT if Test 1 passes (regimes are real, not k-artifacts) AND Test 2 passes (synergies replicate out-of-sample with >=+1.5 pts/game and p<0.05). REJECT if regimes are degenerate or synergies don't replicate.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2001.04197v4", "title": "Causal discovery of linear non-Gaussian acyclic models in the presence of latent confounders", "normalized_lane": "causal_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add an RCD quarantine layer over the ~35-indicator set (reimplemented RCD: ancestor loop with least-squares residualization, parent filtering, bi-directed marking): any indicator pair joined by a bi-directed edge in >=60% of bootstrap runs is quarantined -- neither may be used as a cause in narrative content and at most one enters the prediction stack.", "gate": "ADOPT the RCD quarantine layer if: (a) model (b) matches or beats (a) on 2024-2025 Brier (parity within 0.002) while removing >=15% of directed edges as confounded; (b) bootstrap Jaccard of bi-directed edge set >= 0.5; (c) >=3 of 5 hand-labeled known-confounded pairs are flagged bi-directed.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2001.04226v2", "title": "Prediction and Evaluation in College Hockey using the Bradley-Terry-Zermelo Model", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Ship uncertainty-quantified team ratings: fit Bradley-Terry with a generalized-logistic/Gaussian prior plus a lambda_H home parameter, build the Hessian, invert for the covariance, and serve posterior-predictive win probabilities (MC over the Gaussian, N=20,000) instead of point estimates, with a Bayes-factor model-evaluation protocol using playoff games as the evaluation set.", "gate": "ADOPT (A) and (B) into the ratings/verification stack if the section-12 test passes: posterior-predictive beats point-estimate BT by >=0.02 nats/game on 2015-2025 NFL postseasons.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2001.09097v1", "title": "Forecasting football matches by predicting match statistics", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build GAP-for-NFL: per-team 4-way ratings (home/away offense/defense) on intermediate measures (EPA/play, pressure rate, first-down rate, explosive-play rate) updated via Eq. 7-8 analogues, feeding predicted stat differentials into logistic models for win, spread cover, and total.", "gate": "Adopt if, on 2019-2024 walk-forward, the GAP-featured model beats the market-only baseline by >=0.005 Brier points AND shows positive CLV (mean line move in our favour >= +0.3 points) AND realised ROI CI excludes zero under Level Stakes.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2001.10039", "title": "1163 Prediction Diversity and Selective Attention in the Wisdom of Crowds", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add the weekly ensemble diagnostic identity gamma=(qbar-Y)^2=epsilon-delta as a data-quality check and standing rule: log epsilon, delta, gamma, and delta/epsilon per market; if delta/epsilon is persistently <0.1 the pool is redundant (drop/retrain the most correlated models); never use diversity as single-game confidence.", "gate": "ADOPT the diagnostic permanently if (a) the identity verifies exactly on real data (sanity), and (b) either the Spearman test above holds with p<0.05 OR the decomposition changes at least one model-retention decision in a documented weekly review.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2001.10623v2", "title": "Fast Rates for Online Prediction with Abstention", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add the expert-disagreement no-bet rule to aggregation: compute the exponentially-weighted (by recent Brier) consensus p* over engine model variants + signal experts; no-bet with probability alpha = 2(1-p*) (publish only when p* >= (1-tau/2)), calibrating tau on 2024 to a target no-bet rate.", "gate": "ADOPT if the alpha-rule's cumulative regret vs the best expert over 2024 is <= 50% of the publish-all rule's AND the no-bet rate is <= 40%; otherwise REJECT.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2002.01193", "title": "A copula-based multivariate hidden Markov model for modelling momentum in football", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build gse.regimes.CopulaHMM: drive/play-level bivariate observations (e.g. EPA per play + success rate) with CMP/negative-binomial marginals and a Gaussian/Clayton copula, K=3 states with covariate-driven transitions (score differential, time remaining, home/away, opponent strength); feed posterior state probabilities into the in-game win-probability and live spread/total models.", "gate": "On 2023-2024 holdout, the copula-HMM's one-step-ahead predictive log-likelihood beats the independence-HMM baseline by >= 0.02 nats/observation on average across team-seasons AND the Viterbi state dummies are jointly significant (p < 0.05) for next-drive points.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2002.03448v1", "title": "Kelly Criterion: From a Simple Random Walk to L\u00e9vy Processes", "normalized_lane": "mixed", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the Kelly staking module gse_kelly.py: edge gate E[r] > 0 else stake 0; full Kelly f* = p_hat/a - (1-p_hat)/b clamped to [0,1]; deploy at fractional kappa = 0.25 (0.5 aggressive); stake = f_deploy x current bankroll recomputed per slate; force kappa down when the log-normal sanity gate |mu_hat| < sigma_hat^2/2 fails.", "gate": "ADAPT bar: closed-form stakes must reproduce (i)-(iii) to 1e-6; backtest must show fractional-Kelly (kappa=0.25) beats flat 1-unit staking on log-wealth with lower max drawdown on >=1 full season of engine picks, else staking stays flat.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2002.04148v1", "title": "The role of intrinsic dimension in high-resolution player tracking data -- Insights in basketball", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build an NFL play-complexity (ID) feature from Big Data Bowl tracking: per-frame posterior-median intrinsic dimension via the two-NN Pareto-mixture (Hidalgo, K=3); use pre-snap motion ID as an EPA/play-action-success predictor, post-snap route-combination ID as a defense-confusion feature, and team-level ID as a weekly scheme-unpredictability rating.", "gate": "Adopt the ID feature into GSE's NGS lane if post-snap peak ID adds >=0.005 out-of-sample R-squared to EPA/play over the down-distance-yardline-shotgun baseline, OR pre-snap motion ID beats the motion-flag dummy by >=0.01 AUC on play-action success -- weeks 13-18 holdout, direction matching the paper.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2002.08245v2", "title": "AutoAlpha: an Efficient Hierarchical Evolutionary Algorithm for Mining Alpha Factors in Quantitative Investment", "normalized_lane": "signal_discovery_alpha_mining", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Implement hierarchical GP over the sports operator grammar: seed with depth-1/2 root genes (single operators on single features, e.g. ts_rank(EPA_margin, 4)), crossover preferentially combines high-IC root genes while mutation extends depth, PCA-QD diversity (zero fitness if PCA-similarity > 0.9 vs any recorded signal), warm-start each season from last season's root-gene pool, and an ensemble ranker over top signals -> weekly game rankings -> Kelly-sized positions on top edges.", "gate": "ADAPT->build if AutoAlpha-style miner yields >= 3x the # of diverse test-surviving signals vs. vanilla GP at equal compute AND the ensemble ranker beats the best single signal by >= 0.002 Brier on 2022-2025 with White's-reality-check p<0.05.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2002.09405v2", "title": "Learning to Simulate Complex Physics with Graph Networks", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build GSE-GNS, a within-play tracking simulator: nodes = 22 players (+ball) with (x, y, vx, vy, team, role) features, edges = k-NN/radius graph rebuilt each 100ms frame, encode-process-decode message passing, decoder predicts per-player acceleration plus a global EVENT head (tackle/catch/incompletion/turnover per frame); train single-step on NGS tracking 2018-2025 with input noise corruption and roll out full plays autoregressively; play-call (intent) conditioning is required before production.", "gate": "ADOPT GNS as GSE's within-play tracking simulator if rollout endpoint error beats the no-interaction baseline by >=20% on 2024 held-out plays AND the event head reaches ECE <=0.05.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2002.12860v1", "title": "Quantile Regularization: Towards Implicit Calibration of Regression Models", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add the CKL quantile regularizer (L = NLL + lambda*CKL-bar(s), lambda start 20, differentiable sort of per-batch PIT values) to each GSE probabilistic regression head producing (mu, sigma), and let it replace the isotonic-post-hoc baseline on backtest slices with n < 1,000 where the baseline degrades calibration.", "gate": "Adapt only if, on a held-out NFL season, adding the CKL regularizer to one GSE regression head reduces the L2 quantile calibration error by >= 15% relative (e.g. 0.20 -> 0.17 or better) with held-out NLL not materially worse.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2003.00083", "title": "Nonparametric Estimation in the Dynamic Bradley-Terry Model", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Fit kernel-smoothed dynamic BT (weekly, Gaussian kernel, LOOCV-tuned h) on game outcomes as the 'dumb' power-rating baseline that every feature-rich engine rating must beat on LOO log-likelihood and rank-displacement, and adopt the LOOCV bandwidth tuner plus the existence-condition guardrail as GSE's smoothing primitive for team-strength curves.", "gate": "ADAPT: the method is theoretically clean and practically validated on NFL data, but it is a minimalist benchmark, not a production rating system -- its value to GSE is as the 'dumb baseline that feature-rich models must beat' plus the transferable LOOCV bandwidth discipline and existence-condition guardrail. Not ADOPT: wins-only, no margin, no home field, no covariates; rank agreement, not forecast skill.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2003.01712v1", "title": "Player Chemistry: Striving for a Perfectly Balanced Soccer Team", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the NFL JOI stack metric: per QB-pass-catcher pair, sum EPA of consecutive-play sequences where both touch the ball plus drive-level co-production, normalized per dropback together -> JOI/dropback; predict unseen pairs with gradient boosting on pair features and use predicted JOI for DFS stacking and props.", "gate": "ADOPT the JOI stack metric iff (a) predicted JOI achieves Spearman rho >= 0.40 vs actual next-season JOI/dropback on unseen pairs, AND (b) top-decile-JOI stacks outscore baseline stacks by >= 5% in the DFS backtest (paired t, p < 0.05).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2003.02455v3", "title": "PAC-Bayes Meta-Learning with Implicit Task-Specific Posteriors (SImPa)", "normalized_lane": "metalearning_fewshot", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build SImPa: a small tabular MLP base net (2x64, game features -> margin) with a 2-layer MLP generator over z~U[0,1]^128 producing base-net weights, trained on the paper's PAC-Bayes bound with 5 GD steps lower-level and the KL-free 1000-task warmup; at test time MC over the task-specific posterior (32 samples) -> mean + std -> calibrated win probabilities for new-regime games.", "gate": "ADOPT iff SImPa beats MAML on Brier by >=0.02 on new-regime games at K in {2,4} AND reduces ECE by >=25% relative to MAML on those games.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2003.02743", "title": "A Generalization of the Classical Kelly Betting Formula to the Case of Temporal Correlation", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add correlation-aware Kelly sizing: test for lag-1 autocorrelation of per-pick realized edge by team/market on backtest data; where significant, fit the paper's memory-1/memory-m state-space model per team/market on a rolling window and scale the Kelly fraction by the K_n/(2p-1) adjustment factor behind the existing fractional cap; fall back to classical Kelly when autocorrelation is not significant at 95%.", "gate": "ADOPT correlation-aware sizing if the autocorrelation is statistically significant in at least one major market AND the sizing beats baseline realized log growth by >= 3% on the held-out window.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2003.03271v2", "title": "A Hybrid Approach for Tracking Individual Players in Broadcast Match Videos", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build a broadcast-clip auto-telestration tracker: a generic person detector plus jersey-number/OCR re-ID every jump=5 frames to establish/refresh identity and ROI, with a fast ByteTrack-style tracker on every frame inside the ROI (adjusting the fast tracker only when the slow detector disagrees for >3 consecutive frames); output per-frame player boxes for telestration overlays on seconds-long transformative clips.", "gate": "Adopt into the clip pipeline if the hybrid achieves AUC >= 0.55 AND beats the tracker-alone baseline by >=0.10 AUC AND sustains >=50 fps at 1080p on the test clips.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2003.03685v2", "title": "Discovering contemporaneous and lagged causal relations in autocorrelated nonlinear time series", "normalized_lane": "causal_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Run PCMCI+ per team-season on the nflverse team-week panel (N~30 indicators, T~18 weeks, taumax=4, ParCorr first with GPDC confirmation on the top-50 stable edges), aggregate edge frequencies across ~380 team-seasons (retain edges with cross-team-season frequency >= 0.4), and serve a quarterly graph artifact feeding the Markov-blanket feature-pruning pipeline.", "gate": "ADOPT the PCMCI+-pruned feature set if: (a) held-out 2024-2025 Brier within 0.002 of the all-lags baseline (or better) while using <=60% of features; (b) median cross-team-season edge Jaccard >= 0.5; (c) contemporaneous orientation precision on domain-known directions (pressure->sacks, turnovers->EPA) >= 0.75.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2003.05854v1", "title": "Spatial Modeling of Heavy Precipitation by Coupling Weather Station Recordings and Ensemble Forecasts with Max-Stable Processes", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Adapt the data-driven max-stable recipe to NFL stadium networks: ensemble forecast fields over stadium locations as spectral functions, fit pairwise extremal coefficients of game-day wind/gust maxima, and simulate joint extreme-weather scenarios across all stadiums in a slate week to feed correlated tail weather into Monte Carlo totals/projection simulations; adopt the bootstrap-band diagnostic (2.5-97.5% bands on implied extremal coefficients) as the acceptance test for any spatial-extremes model.", "gate": "ADAPT: one-parameter models beating a five-parameter classical process on out-of-fit triplewise dependence is a strong, portable result -- spatial tail-dependence modeling is a genuine gap in GSE's weather lane.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2003.06505v1", "title": "AutoGluon-Tabular: Robust and Accurate AutoML for Structured Data", "normalized_lane": "nas_automl", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Wrap autogluon.tabular.TabularPredictor for offseason/monthly search over the win-probability/spread/total tabular models: custom time-aware bagging (rolling-origin folds), GSE's hand-tuned LightGBM/XGBoost configs as extra base models, isotonic layer on stacker outputs; full search once per offseason, lightweight 30-min weekly refit in-season.", "gate": "ADOPT if: the AutoGluon-based stack beats the hand-tuned baseline by >=0.003 log-loss on the 2023-2025 held-out seasons AND the search costs <=100 GPU/CPU-hours total. REJECT if: improvement <0.003 log-loss, or any season shows the wrapper leaking future information (positive control: shuffling season labels must destroy the edge), or inference latency >1s/game.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2003.09384v2", "title": "Investigating the efficiency of the Asian handicap football betting market with ratings and Bayesian networks", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Adopt the profit-maximizing static-theta edge-threshold policy: optimize GSE's bet-selection threshold on model-vs-market edge for total realized profit (not per-week ROI) on chronological backtests, deploying the static theta that maximizes total profit when per-window-optimal theta is unstable; quantify the line-shopping uplift by running the identical bet list against consensus-average vs best-available-across-books odds -- threshold discipline as engine-honesty infrastructure, never a profit target.", "gate": "Adopt the profit-maximizing static-theta threshold policy if, on the 2015-2024 NFL backtest: (i) some static theta yields total profit >= 20% above the current GSE threshold policy's total profit at comparable bet counts, AND (ii) per-season-optimal theta is unstable (optimal theta differs by >= 5 pp across >= 3 of the 10 seasons).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2003.10520v1", "title": "Neural Game Engine: Accurate Learning of Generalizable Forward Models from Pixels", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a Graph Neural Game Engine for NFL: represent the play as a player-interaction graph (23 nodes, edges by proximity/assignment), n=3 rounds of message passing per 100ms step so non-local interactions (blitz pickup cascades, coverage rotations) propagate through iteration, with a decoupled reward head predicting play EPA trained separately from the mechanics; serve as a GPU-parallel learned engine for MCTS over play calls and 4th-down decisions.", "gate": "ADOPT if on held-out 2024 plays: (a) n=3 message passing beats n=1 on +1s position error by >=15% (iteration matters), AND (b) 11v11-trained model evaluated on reduced-roster subsets degrades <10% (size invariance holds), AND (c) 500-step (50 s) rollouts stay within 2.0 yards mean error (long-horizon stability).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2003.10791v1", "title": "Predicting play calls in the National Football League using hidden Markov models", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Ship a per-team 2-3 state HMM for pre-snap pass-vs-run probability (multinomial-logit covariate transitions, hierarchical partial pooling across teams, weekly in-season refits) serving (a) prop projection adjustments (attempt share), (b) in-game win-probability conditioning, and (c) game-script-conditioned prop 'script' models.", "gate": "ADOPT as in-game/prop input if the per-team HMM beats the covariate-only logistic baseline by >=0.5 pp accuracy AND >=0.005 log-loss on 2025 holdout, with the improvement concentrated in late-game/script-driven situations.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2003.10865v2", "title": "Model-based Asynchronous Hyperparameter and Neural Architecture Search", "normalized_lane": "nas_automl", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build an async offseason HPO service: N workers pull (config, fidelity) tasks from a queue (fidelity = training seasons 2 -> 4 -> 8 -> full), joint GP (or CQR surrogate) over (config, seasons), bracket sampling per P(s), fantasize pending evaluations -- async because model families have heterogeneous runtimes (CatBoost fast, FT-Transformer slow).", "gate": "ADOPT if: the async method reaches the synchronous-BOHB final log-loss in <=60% of the wall-clock time with 8 workers, AND beats the 1-epoch baseline's final log-loss by >=0.001.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2004.03019", "title": "Disentangled Sticky Hierarchical Dirichlet Process Hidden Markov Model", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build gse.regimes.DSHDPHMM (port the authors' Gibbs code or reimplement in numpyro): per-drive/per-game team observables (EPA/play, pass rate, explosiveness, pace), Poisson/Gaussian emissions, weak-limit L=50, fit per team-season 2018-2024; feed inferred state indicators + kappa_j persistence into matchup and live models as regime features.", "gate": "DS-HDP-HMM wins held-out NLL vs sticky HDP-HMM in >=60% of team-seasons AND inferred kappa_j shows real heterogeneity (spread > 0.3 in >=50% of fits). Fail -> REJECT (fixed-K HMM from 1654 suffices).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2004.08428v1", "title": "Renormalizing individual performance metrics for cultural heritage management of sports records", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Compute era-adjusted player features: per-opportunity prowess (e.g. passing yards/attempt, EPA/play) renormalized against league-average-by-season to a common baseline before use in prop/fantasy models; run a Dickey-Fuller stationarity gate on every candidate feature's league-average time series (deflate non-stationary ones); validate deflators by the distribution-collapse test (era-separated PDFs of the adjusted metric must collapse).", "gate": "DF p < 0.05 on renormalized NFL feature series plus visual/PDF collapse across eras.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2004.08607", "title": "Accumulator Bet Selection Through Stochastic Diffusion Search", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Reimplement the paper as an internal research notebook only (GSE calibrated NFL probabilities + multi-book odds -> optimal-accumulator selector vs singles portfolio, proper held-out seasons, full calibration analysis); publish the honest result as content only if the numbers support it; never expose an accumulator optimizer in the product and keep any parlay-adjacent UI behind existing responsible-play copy -- singles remain the stance.", "gate": "The framework is ADOPTED as a research tool (not a product) if the replication reproduces the paper's qualitative pattern (accumulators: higher headline return, far worse risk-adjusted return and drawdown) on NFL data -- confirming the negative-control thesis. If accumulators somehow win risk-adjusted on held-out NFL seasons, escalate to Garrett before any product discussion.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2004.09368", "title": "Awareness of crash risk improves Kelly strategies in simulated financial time series", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add regime-aware Kelly scaling: when |edge| (GSE calibrated prob vs market-implied prob) is large AND market volatility is elevated, scale down the Kelly fraction (the ECO 'decrease leverage during bubbles' rule); hard-constrain lambda in [0,1] (no leverage/short) for all product sizing; run the multiplicative-error sweep (sigma_e 10^-3..10^2) on every sizing parameter and require stable positive performance up to 10-100% error before shipping.", "gate": "ADOPT regime-aware sizing if it reduces realized max drawdown by >= 15% vs. baseline with realized log growth >= 0.95x baseline on the held-out window.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2004.12099", "title": "Necessary and Sufficient Conditions for Frequency-Based Kelly Optimal Portfolio", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Use Theorem 3.1 as a unit-test certificate on the constrained Kelly solver (assert E[(1+X_{n,i})/(1+K*^T X_n)] <= 1 + tol for zero-weight picks and = 1 +/- tol for positive-weight picks on the empirical distribution -- any violation fails the build); add the R_{ij}(k) sliding-window dominance test over each slate's mutually-exclusive/correlated picks as a walk-forward redundancy screen; replace bang-bang all-in with capped reallocation under the existing fractional ceiling.", "gate": "ADOPT the certificate test unconditionally if it passes on historical data (it is a correctness property, not a performance bet). ADOPT the dominance screen only if it improves realized ROI/drawdown >= 10% walk-forward.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2004.14048", "title": "On Feedback Control in Kelly Betting: An Approximation Approach", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add a survivalClamp to the staking lib: any stake fraction (exact or approximate) is hard-clamped into (-1/Xmax, 1/|Xmin|) from the bet's worst-case return before serving (the paper's SAT_s safety invariant, with a coin-example unit test asserting V(1) > 0 on the worst path); use the Lemma 4/7/8 closed forms to display expected cumulative gain and std-dev for candidate stakes in the internal staking dashboard; log Proposition 9's gap bound as a monitoring metric with alerts.", "gate": "ADOPT the survival clamp if it modifies 0% of current production stakes (pure safety net, no behavior change) and the coin-example unit test passes. ADOPT the dashboard risk display if predicted vs. realized std-dev agree within 20%. REJECT either component otherwise.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2004.14108v2", "title": "Static and Dynamic Models for Multivariate Distribution Forecasts: Proper Scoring Rule Tests of Factor-Quantile vs. Multivariate GARCH Models", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add a variogram-score evaluator (VS_p for p in {0.5, 1, 2}) in gse-backtest/scoring/ ranking engine variants by mean VS_1 alongside the energy score, and pilot an FQ-style joint forecaster for one correlated prop set (QB pass yards/attempts/completions + team total): engine residuals -> PCA factors -> per-target quantile regression at the tail-concentrated 9-node grid -> PCHIP marginal CDFs -> Gaussian/t copula on PIT residuals.", "gate": "Adapt only if, on one GSE correlated-prop backtest set, the FQ-A-style pilot joint forecaster matches the current joint simulator on mean energy score within 3% while calibrating faster. Separately, if VS_1 ranks two engine variants differently than the energy score does, adopt VS_p as a permanent correlation diagnostic regardless of the pilot outcome.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2005.07742", "title": "SEAM Methodology for Context-Rich Player Matchup Evaluations in Baseball", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the SEAM sparse-matchup shrinkage template as GSE's matchup-adjustment standard: any player-vs-player or player-vs-defense projection with thin direct history shrinks toward synthetic comparables (three-way KDE blend with sample-size-driven weights) rather than a flat prior; unit tests assert w_1 -> 1 as n_direct -> large and w_1 -> 0 as n_direct -> 0.", "gate": "Replicate on one MLB season: SEAM-style convex blend beats batter-only and pitcher-only on 0.90-nominal conditional coverage for matchups with >= 10 holdout balls in play; improvement experiment success = 0.90-nominal conditional coverage >= 0.80 with calibration error not worse than the paper's.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2005.09024v1", "title": "Distributed lag models to identify the cumulative effects of training and recovery in athletes using multivariate ordinal wellness data", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a per-player availability model: inputs = snap counts x intensity proxy (workload), days since last game + travel + short-week flags (recovery), 10-game rolling lags, hierarchical partial pooling across players within position group; target = binary availability / ordinal practice-participation (full/limited/DNP); weight availability signals by posterior relative importance R_j; flag players whose workload-lag profile sits in the high-risk region to adjust or withhold picks on their games.", "gate": "ADOPT if held-out 2025 availability AUC beats the pooled baseline by >=3 pp AND individual lag curves show meaningful heterogeneity (psi_ml significantly >0). REJECT if lag curves collapse to a single global curve with no individual signal.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2005.11698", "title": "Phase transitions in optimal strategies for betting", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace the hard-coded 0.25 Kelly default with a frontier choice: compute the (<W>, sigma_W) Pareto frontier over Kelly fractions on GSE's backtest edge distribution and pick the fraction at a configured fluctuation budget (default: the knee); add the TUR-like bound sigma_W >= <W>/sigma_q as a monitoring invariant (violation => probability/odds inputs inconsistent => alert); document the vertical-slope-at-Kelly finding as the fractional-Kelly rationale.", "gate": "ADOPT the frontier-chosen fraction if its realized (<W>, sigma_W) point lies within 15% of the predicted frontier (validating the framework on GSE data) AND it matches or beats baseline realized growth at lower realized fluctuation.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2005.12661v2", "title": "DAG-Net: Double Attentive Graph Neural Network for Trajectory Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build DAG-Net for NFL trajectory forecasting on NGS tracking (10 Hz, 22 players + ball): VRNN backbone (GRU-64, latent-32), Goal-Net for route-intent prediction (route endpoint for receivers, ball-carrier target yardline, defender assignment target), dual attentive GNNs for goal-relationship and hidden-state refinement; train offense and defense models.", "gate": "ADOPT (proceed to NGS-scale build) if full DAG-Net beats Vanilla VRNN by >=10% relative ADE on the ball-carrier/receiver set AND beats A-VRNN (isolating the goal-conditioning contribution) on a held-out season's plays. Secondary gate: min-over-20 ADE must also improve (no mode-collapse).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2005.12853", "title": "Space-Time VON CRAMM: Evaluating Decision-Making in Tennis with Variational generatiON of Complete Resolution Arcs via Mixture Modeling", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt the three-step recipe to NFL NGS tracking: functional encoding of route trajectories (polynomial/spline coefficients) + QB/receiver/defender positions -> generative trajectory model -> condition on observed positions -> outcome model (GAM/GBM) mapping encodings to EPA/success (EPV_t = E[positive EPA | tracking state X_t]); derive Decision IQ (QB read quality, marginalized over execution), Execution+ (receiver catch-point value), and Coverage VACC (defender value denied).", "gate": "ADOPT the three-step recipe and the marginalization-based attribution metrics if the outcome model beats a features-only baseline on 2025 held-out log-loss AND player metrics are split-half stable (r >= 0.35).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2006.00873v2", "title": "A Generalised Signature Method for Multivariate Time Series Feature Extraction", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add signature features to the spread model: per team-game, build the multivariate path x_t = [EPA/play, success rate, pressure rate, explosive-play rate, pace] over trailing 8 games (z-scored per season, time + basepoint augmented), hierarchical dyadic windows depth 3, signature depth 1-3 (<=300 features), selected via the 2185 SHAPEffects procedure; add lead-lag on betting-market channels (team EPA/play, closing spread, spread movement from open) as a market-vs-form interaction family.", "gate": "Accept iff configuration B improves 2024 held-out log-loss by >= 0.003 over A with total signature features <= 300 (dimension discipline), AND the no-time-augmentation ablation performs worse than full augmentation.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2006.01862", "title": "Consistent Estimators for Learning to Defer to an Expert", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the GSE router: log triples (game features x, graded outcome y, Garrett's lean / market-implied pick m) for 1-2 seasons, train the classifier-rejector with the cost-sensitive generalized cross-entropy surrogate in units (not 0/1), and deploy as a pre-card routing step (model-pick, expert-pick, route decision; post the routed pick), with a third route (abstain entirely) making it model/expert/abstain.", "gate": "ADAPT accepted if the router's system units beat both always-model and confidence-threshold routing on walk-forward seasons AND the per-subpopulation audit shows no biased under-deferral; else REJECT.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2006.04551v4", "title": "Cracking the Black Box: Distilling Deep Sports Analytics", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Distill the production probability model into a mimic model tree: generate engine soft labels on the full training corpus plus counterfactual augmentation (perturb game-state features: score diff +/-7, down/distance swaps, timeout changes), fit a linear model tree (iterative segmented regression split-point heuristic, min 100 records/child, L1/L0 pruning); outputs: feature-importance ranking by summed variance reduction plus at least one content-usable extracted rule; train jointly on engine soft labels AND de-vigged market-implied probabilities for an interpretable engine-vs-market disagreement map.", "gate": "Adopt the mimic-tree sidecar if: (i) fidelity correlation >= 0.95 and RMSE <= 0.03 on the time-ordered 2025 holdout; (ii) the top-10 importance ranking agrees with GSE's known drivers (no implausible top-3 feature); (iii) at least one extracted rule is content-usable by analysts.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2006.04779v2", "title": "Conservative Q-Learning for Offline Reinforcement Learning", "normalized_lane": "rl_sequential_decisions", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Train a conservative Q-learning stake policy offline on GSE's historical slate data: state = (week, bankroll, edges, CLV, market features), action = discrete stake {0, 0.25u, 0.5u, 1u, 2u} as actually placed by the historical rule, reward = settled profit in units; small MLP Q-network with CQL(H) conservative penalty; deploy greedy argmax under a per-week max-exposure cap with abstention (action 0) allowed as the learned 'don't bet' behavior; OOD density check with fallback to fractional-Kelly.", "gate": "ADOPT iff on 2024 holdout the CQL policy beats the fractional-Kelly baseline by >=2pp ROI with max drawdown no worse than baseline (within 0.5u) AND the empirical lower-bound diagnostic holds (predicted value <= realized return on >=90% of weeks); if the lower-bound diagnostic fails, REJECT (the safety property is the whole point).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2006.06707v2", "title": "Learning to Learn Kernels with Variational Random Features", "normalized_lane": "metalearning_fewshot", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Deploy MetaVRF as the few-shot regime model: tasks = team-seasons in sequential order, tabular MLP embedding psi on nflverse team-game stats, D=780 RFF bases, meta-learned KRR base-learner predicting next-game margin with an LSTM accumulating league meta-knowledge across seasons; serve meta-test weekly as a forward pass plus a 4x4 ridge solve (no gradient steps); test the classification variant (cover/no-cover) against the engine's existing classifier.", "gate": "ADOPT iff MetaVRF beats the league-average prior by >=0.01 Brier on new-regime first-4-game predictions (2023-2025 LOSO) AND beats fixed-bandwidth RBF-KRR by >=0.005 Brier. Reject if the LSTM context adds nothing over MetaVRF w/o LSTM.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2006.07513", "title": "Bayesian Group Learning for Shot Selection (Log-Gaussian Cox Process + Mixture of Finite Mixtures)", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt LGCP+MFM Bayesian group learning as GSE's probabilistic player-archetype prior for low-sample shooters (rookies, role changes): partial pooling toward the archetype's shot distribution stabilizes prop projections (3P attempt rate, shot diet); pair with AFBART (MFM archetypes as priors, AFBART as the likelihood); improvement experiment: single-stage joint model or propagate Stage-1 posterior uncertainty by fitting MFM on posterior draws of the intensity surfaces.", "gate": "Simulation Rand 0.9988 vs best baseline 0.9005 (K-means), 42/50 correct-K recovery, real-data concordance 0.948; improvement success = concordance RI >= 0.95 maintained AND archetype assignments improve a downstream 3P-attempt-rate prediction task (held-out RMSE).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2006.08189v1", "title": "Estimation of Skill Distributions", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a weekly League Competitiveness Score content metric: estimate the cross-sectional skill distribution of NFL teams each season from win/loss data (rank-centrality + deconvolution KDE) and report -h(P-hat) as a narrative stat ('2026 is the most wide-open NFL season since...'), plus division-level per-season scores; descriptive only, never wired into the prediction engine.", "gate": "ADOPT for content production if, on the 2015-2025 nflverse window, |Spearman(negative entropy, same-season upset rate)| >= 0.5 AND it exceeds the Elo-stdev baseline correlation by >= 0.15; otherwise REJECT as a content metric.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2006.10782v2", "title": "AI Feynman 2.0: Pareto-optimal symbolic regression exploiting graph modularity", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Install aifeynman and run it on nflverse team-game data (target points/drive, 8-12 features) as a complement to PySR, comparing its Pareto front against PySR's hall-of-fame; port the two cheapest ideas into the GSE pipeline regardless: (a) hypothesis-testing candidate rejection replacing hard error cutoffs in PySR selection, (b) Pareto-frontier pruning after every merge/generation step in any evolutionary search; use the normalizing-flow + SR path to discover a closed-form for the distribution of team points per game ('GSE scoring distribution law').", "gate": "ADOPT the Pareto-pruning + hypothesis-testing rejection port if v2-style selection yields the same top-3 equation families on clean and 5%-noise-corrupted training data (Jaccard >= 0.5 on skeleton sets) while v1-style threshold selection diverges; REJECT if the modularity detector fires on pure-noise features (false-structure test: permuted targets must return only trivial fronts).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2006.11909v2", "title": "Two-Sample Testing on Ranked Preference Data and the Role of Modeling Assumptions", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Deploy the permutation two-sample test (Algorithm 2) as a regime-change monitor: split team-vs-team (or QB-vs-defense) matchup outcomes into pre/post windows around candidate change points (coaching changes, QB injuries, trade deadline, season halves), run the test at alpha=0.05, and only re-fit team-strength priors when the test rejects; also use it for model monitoring (test whether the engine pick outcome distribution shifted after a model-version deploy).", "gate": "ADOPT as the regime-change gate if Test 1's false-rejection rate is within [2%, 10%] (calibrated) AND Test 3 rejects at p<0.05 (power against a real break); otherwise restrict to multi-season aggregates only.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2006.12471", "title": "1164 When Social Influence Promotes the Wisdom of Crowds", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt R as a per-game aggregation-regime switch: for each game and market collect the M model probabilities, fit normal and log-normal distributions by MLE (logit-transform first), compute R; R < 0.5 -> equal-weighted mean aggregation, R >= 0.5 -> concentrated aggregation (softmax weights on recent model skill or top-3 skill-weighted mean); backtest both regimes vs fixed-regime baselines on 2024-2025 seasons.", "gate": "ADOPT the regime switch if 2025-season mean Brier beats the better fixed regime by >=2% on at least 2 of 3 markets (spread/ML/total) AND the R>=0.5 fraction of games is between 10% and 60% (the rule must discriminate).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2006.16597v2", "title": "Regression with Reject Option and Application to kNN", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Variance-gated no-bet for margin/total picks: for each slate game compute sigma-hat(x) = CQR interval width (or a dedicated residual-variance model fit on squared CQR residuals); set lambda-hat_epsilon as the (1-epsilon)-quantile over the slate; no-bet games with sigma-hat > lambda-hat_epsilon; grid-search epsilon in {0.1, ..., 0.5} on 2024.", "gate": "ADOPT if at epsilon=0.3 the published set's RMSE drops >=15% vs publish-all (paired test p<0.05) AND achieved rejection rate is within +/-3 pp of epsilon AND the error-vs-epsilon curve is monotone decreasing; the single decisive number: RMSE reduction >= 15% at achieved rejection rate epsilon+/-0.03.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2007.00267v1", "title": "Reconstructing regime-dependent causal relationships from observational time series", "normalized_lane": "causal_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Run regime-dependent causal discovery on the nflverse team-week panel: pool across teams (shared regimes per season, team-specific graphs, or league-week aggregates), nodes = ~15 core indicators (EPA components, pressure, turnovers, injury counts, pace) with ParCorr CI test, N_K in {2,3} by AICc; the live model uses the current-regime graph's Markov blanket, regime identity estimated from the trailing 6-week window; serving offline quarterly.", "gate": "ADOPT if (a) regime model beats baseline by >=0.003 Brier on 2024-2025 held-out; (b) AICc selects N_K >= 2 in >=60% of seasons; (c) the 'disrupted' regime classifier recovers >=70% of documented QB-injury-spell weeks; (d) per-regime link TPR >= 0.85 on synthetic sports-like data. Reject if (a) fails or AICc persistently selects N_K=1.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2007.05507", "title": "Experimental Modeling of Cyclists Fatigue and Recovery Dynamics Enabling Optimal Pacing in a Time Trial", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build gse_work_capacity.py: per-player anaerobic-reserve state W updated per play (dW = -(P-CP) when exertion P > CP; dW = -(P_adj-CP) when P < CP, with P = NGS-derived exertion, CP = position-group aerobic threshold, P_adj = aP + b fitted per position group); P_max(W) = a1 W^2 + a2 W + CP as a per-game 'explosiveness ceiling' feature; serve W and P_max(W) into the availability/injury-risk model and DFS value model (depleted-W players project below market); calibrate on 2023-2024 NGS + injury data.", "gate": "Accepted: experimentally grounded (13-visit protocol), quantified improvement (7.3% time reduction vs own-strategy baseline), asymmetric recovery law with a causality argument, and direct portability to a player work-capacity state -- the missing piece in the existing fatigue ODE.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2007.14870v2", "title": "Decoding machine learning benchmarks", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build an IRT evaluation layer over the engine's backtest history: items = historical game-weeks (or individual spread/total picks), respondents = model versions (v5.2.7 and predecessors/challengers), responses = pick correct/incorrect; fit 2PL/3PL per season, extract per-pick difficulty and discrimination, compute per-model True-Score and run Glicko-2 round-robins across seasons to rank model versions by difficulty-adjusted ability; weight future backtests toward high-discrimination games; diagnose systematically hard game types (divisional, short-rest, weather).", "gate": "ADOPT the IRT layer if (a) item difficulties show meaningful spread AND (b) at least one model version changes rank vs raw accuracy, demonstrating the difficulty adjustment has signal. Reject if all items are near-uniform difficulty or negative-discrimination items exceed ~10% of games.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2007.15508", "title": "1165 The Ambiguous Role of Social Influence on the Wisdom of Crowds: An Analytic Approach", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt as ensemble-diversity governance: alpha_proxy = mean pairwise correlation of week-to-week prediction changes across component models; beta_proxy = each model's correlation with its independent signal vs the ensemble mean; track cross-model variance of log-odds forecasts delta^2(t) weekly and flag 'diversity rot' if it decays while models ingest the same data; enforcement rule: each component model keeps at least one unshared feature family/data source (model-independence registry), and retraining pipelines must not use the ensemble's own past predictions as features.", "gate": "ADOPT the governance rule if the audit finds either (a) a statistically significant downward trend in delta^2(t) over 2025 (p<0.05), or (b) any pair of component models with |correlation| > 0.9 on holdout predictions. REJECT ongoing monitoring (keep the one-time audit) if delta^2(t) is stable and all pairs are below 0.85.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2008.01485", "title": "1166 Wisdom of Crowds: Much Ado About Nothing", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt two instruments: (1) model-pool bias screen -- per game-week test the pool's unbiasedness (Hosmer-Lemeshow / Spiegelhalter z-test on pooled probability forecasts) and flag weeks where the pool is significantly biased; (2) best-single-model baseline -- weekly compare ensemble Brier vs each individual model's, maintain the running fraction of weeks the ensemble beats most models, and keep a 'champion model' lane alive.", "gate": "ADOPT the champion-model lane if, on 2025 data, the single best trailing-8-week model beats the equal-weight ensemble on full-season Brier, OR the ensemble beats most models in fewer than 75% of weeks (paper-consistent regime) while a skill-weighted ensemble recovers >=2% Brier. REJECT the 'ensemble always wins' default if the bias screen flags >50% of weeks -- in that regime shift weight to the champion.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2008.05105v2", "title": "Local Temperature Scaling for Probability Calibration", "normalized_lane": "mixed", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Context-conditional temperature scaling for engine win probabilities (gse_lts_cal.py): inputs = engine raw logit z + context features c (sport, market type, days-to-kickoff, odds bucket, model-version flag); fit a small regressor T(c) > 0 on a hold-out val season minimizing NLL of sigma(z/T(c)) against outcomes; deployed p_cal = sigma(z/T(c)) -- ranking of picks unchanged, pure calibration gain; evaluate ECE/SCE/ACE overall and sliced by context (sport, week, odds bucket).", "gate": "Context-conditional T must beat global temperature scaling on ECE/SCE/ACE on a hold-out season with statistical significance; if T(c) collapses to ~constant (no context signal), fall back to global TS and record the negative result.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2008.05203", "title": "1167 The Wisdom and Persuadability of Threads", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Two adaptations: (1) full-information market feed rule (immediate, zero-code) -- ingest the complete line evolution (openers + every move, full consensus history from The Odds API) as GSE's market feature, never building features on curated 'top steam picks' lists; (2) model-market persuadability screen -- per component model and game, regress the model's log-odds forecast on contemporaneous market log-odds (slope = market-beta_iw); downweight models with market-beta near 1 in aggregation proportionally to their orthogonal (market-residual) predictive information, i.e., weight by Brier improvement over the market.", "gate": "ADOPT the orthogonal-information weighting if, on 2025 data, it beats the equal-weight ensemble on full-season Brier, and beats it by a larger margin on the hard-game subset (top-tercile closing-line uncertainty).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2008.09858v3", "title": "Hi-CI: Deep Causal Inference with High-Dimensional and Highly Correlated Variables", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Use Hi-CI for heterogeneous treatment effects of continuous football exposures: dose-response of target share / snap share / practice load on player fantasy output, with hundreds of covariates (tracking + matchup + weather + line features); PyTorch encoder -> representation with the three-part loss (treatment CE + reconstruction + mixed L2,1 mean difference), outcome head per dose level; reuse GSE's feature store for covariates.", "gate": "Adopt if Hi-CI beats the best modern baseline (not just the paper's weak baselines) on PEHE by >=20% with comparable or better MAPE-ATE on the semi-synthetic NFL test; reject if it only beats the paper's weak baselines.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2008.10423", "title": "1168 Enhanced or Distorted Wisdom of Crowds?", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Per-game adaptive market blending: compute disagreement d = |logit(mean model prob) - logit(market prob)| and direction; if d is in the top tercile of historical disagreements use heavy market blend w_m ~= 0.5; bottom tercile -> light blend w_m ~= 0.1-0.15 (avoid distortion); middle tercile -> 0.25-0.3; per-model conviction term: shrinkage toward each model's own pre-market estimate proportional to its trailing-8-week skill.", "gate": "ADOPT the disagreement-scheduled blend if, on 2025 data, it beats the fixed blend on full-season Brier AND the direction test confirms the asymmetry (blending helps in correctable games, hurts in distortion-risk games). REJECT fixed uniform market blending if the distortion-risk class shows statistically significant Brier deterioration under blending (paired t-test, p<0.05).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2008.13005", "title": "Wisdom of the Crowds Forecasting the 2018 FIFA Men's World Cup", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add the Budescu-Chen aggregation arm: C_j = mean leave-one-out gain over trailing 2 seasons; aggregate sources with C_j > 0 weighted by C_j; compare against Variance-EM and simple average on 2024-2025; run an assertiveness audit ((3/2)Sum(p-1/3)^2-style assertiveness) for the engine's published probabilities vs their Brier scores, applying global shrinkage-toward-0.5 recalibration if systematically over-assertive; adopt the evaluation-honesty rule (no 'model A beats model B' claim on < ~500 games without a truth-knower simulation).", "gate": "Adopt Budescu-Chen if it beats simple averaging on 2024-2025 Brier by >=0.002 OR wins the truth-knower simulation more often than Variance-EM; adopt the evaluation-honesty rule regardless; reject the assertiveness recalibration if the engine's assertiveness already sits at its Brier-optimal point.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2009.00550", "title": "1714 Using social networks to improve group transition prediction in professional sports", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build gse/offseason/social_affinity.py: ingest timestamped follow-graph snapshots (never a single current snapshot); for each pending NFL free agent compute per-team affinity from follows created before the tampering window; combine with existing transition features (cap space, team need, prior-team link, agent representation) in a gradient-boosted destination classifier outputting a destination distribution over 32 teams as a prior in the player-value and team-total adjustment pipeline; guardrail: any follow edge without a creation timestamp is excluded (the paper's failure mode).", "gate": "ADAPT only the recipe -- timestamped per-team social-affinity features inside a walk-forward destination classifier -- if the reproducible test shows >= 2x-random top-3 accuracy on NFL data with strictly pre-tampering-window features. REJECT the paper's numbers outright if timestamped follow data is unobtainable (without edge timestamps the feature is definitionally leaky).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2009.01206v1", "title": "Identification of skill in an online game: The case of Fantasy Premier League", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a per-slate chalk index: player co-occurrence matrix from projected-ownership-weighted lineup fields, hierarchical cluster, report the ownership share of the top-3 clusters = template concentration ('chalk meter' in the weekly DFS packet); contrarian trigger: top-quartile concentration -> tilt GPP lineups to low-Jaccard constructions vs the template core; transfer-regret audit: for every lineup swap/waiver recommendation compute the fraction of same-salary-or-cheaper alternatives that outscored the pick, tracked weekly as a decision-quality KPI.", "gate": "ADOPT the chalk-meter + contrarian tilt iff, on 2023-2025 backtest, template-fading lineups achieve >=10% higher ROI than template-following lineups on top-quartile-concentration slates (paired by slate, p<0.05), with no significant ROI loss on bottom-quartile slates. Otherwise REJECT.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2009.03228v3", "title": "Information Theoretic Meta Learning with Gaussian Processes", "normalized_lane": "metalearning_fewshot", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Deploy deep-kernel GP-VIB on nflverse 2015-2025 (tasks = team-seasons; meta-test = rookie-QB / new-HC / post-trade regimes 2023-2025): Gaussian-likelihood encoder, beta in {0.01, 0.1, 1.0} grid, target = next-game win-probability logit with support = first K games of the new regime; the KL term acts as the anti-memorization gate, beta tuned on 2023 leave-one-season-out; serve weekly refits per new-regime team with closed-form GP posterior, uncertainty bands feeding pick-confidence and Kelly sizing.", "gate": "ADOPT iff GP-VIB (beta tuned) beats the league-average prior by >=0.01 Brier on new-regime first-4-game predictions (2023-2025 LOSO) AND the beta>0 model beats the beta=0 ablation on NLL by a statistically clear margin (paired t-test p<0.05).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2009.06750", "title": "Stop the Clock: Are Timeout Effects Real?", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Estimate the causal effect of icing-the-kicker timeouts on FG/XP make probability on nflverse pbp (all FG/XP attempts 1999-2024): propensity via GBM on confounders (kick distance, weather, kicker quality, score differential, time remaining, dome/outdoor) + exact match on distance bucket and same game, permutation inference; product: 'Icing the kicker is a myth' causal content series for @GalaxySportsHQ and pruning of spurious timeout-effect features from the late-game WP model.", "gate": "ADAPT the DAG+matching template if the NFL icing replication achieves post-match SMD < 0.1 on all observed confounders AND the 99% permutation CI for the ATT either excludes 0 with |ATT| >= 0.03 (real effect -- publish) or includes 0 with CI half-width < 0.03 (clean null -- prune the feature). REJECT if balance fails or CI half-width > 0.05.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2009.07947v1", "title": "Using Machine Learning and Alternative Data to Predict Movements in Market Risk", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Treat this paper as engine-honesty infrastructure, not an objective: build the line-movement-direction model (target = sign(close - now) for spread/total, market data (line history, ticket/handle splits) + alt data (X volume, news counts, Wikipedia page views), 78-style technical expansion on line series) as a bet-timing honesty instrument, and audit GSE's existing backtest pipelines against the paper's walk-forward/no-look-ahead discipline -- any pipeline standardizing on the full sample before splitting has look-ahead bias by this standard; ablate alt-data features per model class (linear vs non-linear).", "gate": "Market-only features must beat 50% balanced accuracy OOS with walk-forward evaluation; then test whether alt-data features add anything under a non-linear model. If nothing beats chance, the transfer fails for that market.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2009.14454v1", "title": "Accurate and Robust Feature Importance Estimation under Distribution Shifts", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Train PRoFILE jointly (LightGBM/3-layer-MLP predictor + contrastive loss estimator) on 2018-2023 game-level rows (target ATS cover); run a weekly pipeline computing per-feature Delta-epsilon via the loss estimator with mean-imputation masking, aggregating to season-level importance = median over games; shift alarm: trailing-4-week mean s-hat exceeding the training-season mean by >2sigma triggers the recalibration review (model-side complement to the existing shock detector).", "gate": "Adopt PRoFILE iff (a) on Test A its top-25% masking degrades log-loss more than SHAP's top-25% by a relative margin >=10%, AND (b) on Test B its fidelity degrades less than SHAP's under the 2022+ era shift, AND (c) on Test C mean weekly s-hat spikes coincide with documented regime breaks at >=60% hit rate.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2010.00526v1", "title": "LiveQA: A Question Answering Dataset over Sports Live", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build 'LiveQA-NFL': sample 2024 NFL games, extract play-by-play + drive text from nflverse; auto-generate quiz questions in the four types (comparison/calculation/inference/tracking) with evidence-location labels; evaluate GSE's game-summary/LLM pipelines on it; use it as the regression test for any live-event narration product; improvement experiment: add counterfactual questions ('if that 4th-down conversion had failed, who gets the ball?') requiring branching timeline reasoning.", "gate": "ADOPT as the standard GSE timeline-QA benchmark if a 200-question pilot shows the four question types are answerable by humans at >=90% (validating question quality); REJECT if auto-generated questions are noisy (human accuracy <80%).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2010.00781v1", "title": "Evaluating realtime probabilistic forecasts with application to NBA outcome prediction", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "In-play calibration surfaces for GSE's live win-probability feed: build U/L calibration surfaces over normalized game time (rank-based M=10 bins, Wilson-Bonferroni intervals, U^min/L^max summary plots) on 2022-2025 NFL games; live skill comparison via Delta-hat_N(t) Brier skill curves with conservative 95% CIs vs the pregame-strength+score logit baseline and live book consensus, with Theorem 1's functional test (D=10 eigenvalues, Imhof) for the aggregate verdict, pooling >=2 seasons (N>=500); fit the NFL PgRSScD-equivalent logit (pregame GSE win prob + live score diff) as the in-play baseline.", "gate": "Adopt as GSE's standard in-play evaluation if: on 2024-2025 pooled games the pipeline runs end-to-end and the functional test has demonstrated power -- i.e., it significantly separates GSE live from the coin-flip/HomeWP baselines (p<0.01). Reject if the surfaces/CIs are uninformative on NFL data (persistent degeneracy or Wilson intervals too wide to ever exclude the reference plane).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2010.02193v4", "title": "Mastering Atari with Discrete World Models", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "'GSE-DreamV2': replace the existing GSE-Dream RSSM's Gaussian latents with a vector of categoricals (32 categoricals x 32 classes), straight-through gradients, KL balancing alpha=0.8, beta tuned for football data; train on nflverse 2006-2025 play sequences; keep the symlog/twohot reward targets; improvement experiment: regime-labeled categoricals -- weakly supervise a subset of categorical dimensions to known game regimes (garbage time, two-minute drill, goal-line), leaving the rest free.", "gate": "ADOPT categorical latents as the GSE-Dream standard if the categorical variant beats the Gaussian variant on 2024 TVD/ECE OR matches them while demonstrating multimodal predictions on high-leverage plays (dip test p<0.05 on >=20% of 3rd/4th downs). REJECT if categoricals underperform Gaussians on log-likelihood -- then keep Gaussians with the symlog improvements.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2010.08784", "title": "DIFER: Differentiable Automated Feature Engineering", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build 'GSE-DIFER' as a second-stage composer on top of the OpenFE base+survivor feature set: numerical time-safe base features only (EPA/play, success rates, pressure/explosive rates, rolling means); parse-tree search space (unary {log, sqrt, minmax, reciprocal, square}, binary {+,-,x,divide zero-guarded}), max order K=3; population init 512 random compositions scored by LightGBM log-loss on expanding-window validation seasons; encoder-predictor-decoder (LSTM-512 + 5-layer MLP) with gradient-ascent feature evolution to 4,096 evaluations and early-stopped top-d selection.", "gate": "ADOPT the DIFER feature set iff it improves 2024 held-out log-loss by >=0.003 over the OpenFE-augmented baseline, with every surviving feature passing the time-safety audit (recomputable from pre-game data only) and an interpretability check (each feature must have a one-line football meaning). REJECT if gain < 0.003, if >30% of survivors fail interpretability, or if validation-selected features degrade on test.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2010.09107", "title": "Conformal Prediction for Time Series (EnbPI)", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "EnbPI-margin: B=25 bootstrap fits of the GSE margin model on trailing seasons with LOO ensemble predictions per game; residuals windowed over the trailing ~100 games (tune T' in {50, 100, 200}); asymmetric beta-optimized intervals at alpha in {0.1, 0.2}; early-season mode with prior-season residuals seeding the window; retrain trigger when trailing-20-game coverage < 1-alpha-0.05 for 2 consecutive weeks.", "gate": "ADAPT if: full-season empirical coverage within +/-2pp of nominal AND mean width <= split-conformal baseline; the early-season (weeks 1-4) coverage must beat ICP by >=3pp (the paper's signature win). REJECT the bootstrap-ensemble component if B=25 refits exceed the weekly compute budget -- fall back to a single-model sliding-window variant.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2010.10435v1", "title": "Time-varying Forecast Combination for High-Dimensional Data", "normalized_lane": "mixed", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Time-varying model combination for the engine (gse_tvcombine.py): inputs = per-game component forecasts (engine v5.2.7 prob, market-implied prob, Elo prob, situational-model prob); target = outcome/cover indicator; local-linear time-varying weights with reflection at the current-week boundary (combine for this week's games using only past weeks), Epanechnikov kernel, bandwidth by leave-one-out CV; two-stage group-SCAD pruning when the component pool is large; online weight updating within a week as lines move.", "gate": "Time-varying combination must beat equal weights and static OLS on OOS Brier/ASCFE with DM p<0.10 on a >=2-season backtest; if weights collapse to near-constant (no time variation found), fall back to static combination and record the negative.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2010.10739v1", "title": "A Bayesian Hidden Semi-Markov Model with Covariate-Dependent State Duration Parameters for High-Frequency Data from Wearable Devices", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Port the duration-regression HSMM to game-state regimes: define latent pace/aggressiveness regimes (pass-heaviness, tempo) from play-by-play with segment durations as zero-truncated Poisson depending on pre-transition covariates (score differential, time remaining, timeouts, weather, QB); fit on nflverse 2018-2025 with the subsampling protocol; use expected-regime-duration forecasts as features for in-game/live models and quantify what extends or shortens aggressive regimes (e.g., do trailing teams stay in pass-heavy states longer?).", "gate": "Adopt if the covariate-duration HSMM beats the constant-duration HSMM on held-out 2025 log-likelihood by >=1% AND at least two duration covariates have 95% CIs excluding zero (the paper's Table 4 standard). Reject if durations are effectively memoryless -- then a plain HMM suffices.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2010.11187", "title": "G-Elo: Generalization of the Elo algorithm by modeling the discretized Margin of Victory", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Implement G-Elo in the ratings module: 7-category NFL discretization ({d<-10}, {-10<=d<-5}, {-5<=d<0}, {d=0}, {0<d<=5}, {5<d<=10}, {d>10}); estimate (alpha, delta, eta) from the last 5 NFL seasons via the paper's frequency formulas; calibrate K-tilde by grid search on log-loss of implied ternary probabilities; convert skills to win probabilities via the AC model for the moneyline head and map skill difference to expected margin for the spread head; run alongside current Elo in weekly diagnostics (log-loss, RPS, accuracy, ranking-violation rate) with quarterly recalibration.", "gate": "G-Elo must beat GSE's current Elo-Davidson-equivalent on the NFL 2019-2023 walk-forward backtest: log-loss improvement Delta-LS >= 0.005 AND accuracy >= baseline + 1pp. If it fails, keep the frequency-based coefficient formulas as the calibration method for the existing Elo and drop the AC update.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2010.12508v1", "title": "Beating the market with a bad predictive model", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Treat this as engine-honesty infrastructure, not the objective: add a decorrelation penalty to GSE's win-probability model training (L = XENT - gamma*(t_i - m_i)^2, with m_i = consensus de-vigged market probability), tuned over gamma in {0.1, ..., 1.0}; run the feature audit with/without market-odds features (with-odds models need larger gamma); keep the fractional-Kelly/drawdown-constrained staking layer; hard regime check -- never deploy gamma > 0 unless the model is confirmed inferior to the market on XENT (decorrelation hurts superior models).", "gate": "Adopt the decorrelation loss (gamma > 0) if, on the 2020-2024 chronological test: (i) some gamma in {0.2, 0.4, 0.6} yields total ROI >= 2 percentage points above the gamma = 0 model under identical sharpe staking, AND (ii) the gamma = 0 model does not already beat market consensus on XENT, AND (iii) model-market correlation decreases monotonically in gamma. Reject (keep pure-accuracy training) if no gamma beats gamma = 0 by >= 2pp ROI or the model is already XENT-superior.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2010.15779v2", "title": "Discrete-time portfolio optimization under maximum drawdown constraint with partial information and deep learning resolution", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "'Learn the edge under a drawdown cap': per-pick-category (spread/ML/total x league) Bayesian posterior over true win probability (Beta-Binomial updating as picks settle); stake = Kelly fraction from the posterior mean, shrunk by posterior uncertainty; hard cap: if bankroll drawdown exceeds q (e.g., 30% from peak), scale to minimum viable stakes until recovery; new categories start at reduced stakes until the posterior tightens.", "gate": "ADAPT if the Learning staker beats the Non-Learning staker on 2025-holdout ROI with worst drawdown no worse (replicating the paper's dual win) -- else the Bayesian layer adds complexity without edge and GSE keeps fixed edge estimates with the simple drawdown governor from 0818.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2011.01324v2", "title": "Valuing Player Actions in Counter-Strike: Global Offensive", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Event-level action valuation on nflverse play-by-play: train an XGBoost win-probability model on 2016-2024 play states (down, distance, yardline, score diff, time, timeouts, spread-implied team strength), add per-event credit by differencing consecutive-state WP at sub-play resolution where charting data allows; adopt the paper's stability/independence/discrimination battery (split-half correlation, correlation vs EPA baseline, bootstrap CIs per player, Fisher r-to-z) for any new GSE player metric; bootstrap player value estimates (100-500 resamples) and publish per-player SD alongside point estimates.", "gate": "ADAPT the event-level WPA + bootstrap-uncertainty design if, on the 2024 test window: (a) the XGBoost WP model beats logistic regression on log loss by >= 0.01 with a calibrated reliability curve (max bin deviation <= 3pp); and (b) player WPA split-half correlation >= 0.35 and its correlation with EPA/play < 0.90 (independence margin).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2011.02077", "title": "Combining Forecasts with Factor Graphical Models (Lee & Seregina, 2020)", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Deploy the static factor-aware ensemble weighting: strip common error factors from GSE's model panel (shared inputs guarantee they exist), estimate the sparse idiosyncratic precision by EBIC-tuned GLASSO, and form the optimal combination weights with SMW reconstruction; include the plain-GLASSO degeneracy diagnostic to confirm the factor structure is actually present (the payoff is largest at longer horizons).", "gate": "ADAPT if the degeneracy diagnostic confirms the factor structure in GSE's model-panel forecast errors and the resulting optimal weights beat equal weights and static OLS on OOS MSFE (the paper proves weight consistency under its assumptions).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2011.02122v1", "title": "Analysing Long Short Term Memory Models for Cricket Match Outcome Prediction", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Replicate the winning pattern on nflverse play-by-play (2000-2025) as the ball-by-ball analog: per-timestep output heads trained on full game sequences with shared input embedding + recurrent core (LSTM first, then GRU/Transformer), features (score differential, time remaining, down/distance/yardline, timeouts, pre-game spread, pre-play WP), targets live spread P(home cover) and total P(over) at each play, loss = mean BCE over all plays with the final spread/total outcome as label at every timestep; append pre-game spread/total to every play input and ablate it explicitly (the paper's +13% ablation analog).", "gate": "ADOPT (proceed to productionization) if the all-outputs recurrent model beats the per-quarter logistic baseline by >=0.01 Brier AND >=3pp accuracy at the half-time checkpoint across the 2023-2025 test window; REJECT otherwise.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2011.06430v2", "title": "Sentiment Correlation in Financial News Networks and Associated Market Movements", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build the NFL news co-occurrence network: entities = teams/players from sports news (ESPN, beat writers), edges = co-mention cosine similarity, Louvain groups (~divisions/conferences + cross-links like shared agents or coordinators); entity-level sentiment per team/player per day; event study on line moves -- does a negative-sentiment QB event propagate to his team's total and the opponent's spread?", "gate": "ADOPT as a monitoring layer if sentiment events predict line moves beyond the official injury designations (i.e., the network catches what the designation dummies miss); REJECT if all line movement is explained by designations + market steam (then the network is descriptive, not predictive).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2011.11277v6", "title": "A paradox of tournament seeding", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Incentive-audit checklist for priced competitions: encode each competition's seeding/draw rules as a function from results to pots; property-test monotonicity by brute force over result scenarios (can a better result ever produce a worse draw?) before GSE prices any tournament's draw-dependent markets (group winners, qualification, outrights); draw simulators must implement actual pot-allocation rules including coefficient quirks, not idealized seeding; run a 'draw mechanics' content series for @GalaxySportsHQ.", "gate": "ADAPT iff the audit finds real violations: apply the monotonicity property test to at least three competitions GSE prices (UCL, World Cup qualifying, one more); if any shows a realizable paradox scenario, the audit becomes a standing pre-pricing check; if all are clean, keep the checklist as a one-time validation.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2011.11691", "title": "The causal effect of a timeout at stopping an opposing run in the NBA", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "NFL 4th-down replication: units = 4th-down decisions (go-for-it vs punt/FG) or 2-point conversion attempts; outcome = integrated centered win-probability difference over the next drive / rest of half; covariates = yard line, yards to go, score differential, time remaining, timeouts remaining, pre-game spread/total, weather, team identities, coach identity; propensity via GAM or gradient-boosted model + genetic matching; estimand = ATT of aggressive 4th-down decisions with heterogeneity by coach; serving offline research.", "gate": "ADOPT the pipeline if on the NFL 4th-down replication (a) post-match |standardized bias| < 0.2 for all covariates, (b) the ATT estimate has |t| > 2 and the sign is unchanged when FG attempts are excluded from the control pool, and (c) Rosenbaum Gamma for loss of significance >= 1.5. REJECT if balance fails or Gamma < 1.2.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2011.14048v2", "title": "Is Support Set Diversity Necessary for Meta-Learning?", "normalized_lane": "metalearning_fewshot", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Change the meta-training episode sampler to fixed support pools: per team-season, a canonical set of K games (e.g., weeks {2, 5, 9, 13, 16} or archetype-matched games), sampled once and frozen; meta-train with fixed supports (query sets still diverse); evaluate under the full objective (random supports) on held-out regimes; test both over-parameterized backbones and GSE's small tabular backbones; improvement experiment: archetype-optimized designed-fixed pools (K games per team-season maximizing coverage of opponent archetypes: elite offense, elite defense, dome/outdoor, division/non-division).", "gate": "ADOPT the fix-ml sampler iff it beats random-support meta-training by >=1pp accuracy on new-regime win prediction (2023-2025 held-out regimes) with run-variance no worse than ml's. Reject if GSE's small tabular backbones show the Conv64 failure mode (fix-ml worse than ml).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2012.00253", "title": "A New Action Recognition Framework for Video Highlights Summarization in Sporting Events", "normalized_lane": "sports_cv", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "RallySeg-3L module: (a) frame-level playing/non-playing classifier per sport on broadcast frames (replace YOLOv3/OpenPose with GSE's current detector or a cheap fine-tuned classifier); (b) middle-level probability-sum fusion across detected athletes; (c) short-window majority vote with tuned k and Prc (grid-search on GSE's own rally timestamps); (d) Delta-t gap-merge to emit final clip intervals for highlight rendering; start with table tennis/pickleball where rally structure is clean, then port to tennis.", "gate": "RallySeg-3L must beat the naive frame-level baseline by >=5pp on F1 (C metric) on the same 5-match set; absolute P >= 90% and R >= 85% required for a production pilot. If the voting cascade does not clear +5pp over flat frame classification, drop it.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2012.01643", "title": "Forecast with Forecasts: Diversity Matters", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "For each game slate compute the pairwise diversity matrix among the K engine sub-models' forecast vectors over the slate horizon (Div per Eq. 3, adapted to predicted cover probabilities or point differentials per game), C(K,2) features per slate; gradient-boosted trees mapping the slate diversity vector -> per-model softmax weights; no historical series features needed.", "gate": "ADOPT the diversity-weighted combiner if, on the held-out 2025 season, it beats the simple-average baseline by >=2% relative log-loss AND beats the static skill-weighted baseline by >=1% relative, with calibration slope within [0.9, 1.1]. REJECT (keep simple average) if it fails either gate or the meta-learner's feature importances concentrate on <3 pairs (degenerate map).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2012.04380v1", "title": "Combining Machine Learning and Human Experts to Predict Match Outcomes in Football: A Baseline Model", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Beat-writer text feature pipeline for NFL: scrape pre-game beat-writer articles (ESPN team writers, The Athletic, local beats) per matchup; sentence-transformer embeddings with sentence->team allocation via an entity-linking/NER pass; per-team aggregate vectors (sum/attention-weighted); ensemble-only design -- feed text-model outcome probabilities as meta-features into a stacking classifier alongside GSE engine probabilities and de-vigged market probabilities (the paper proves the ensemble-only value); props extension: player-level text (injury reports, rotation news) as features for prop/fantasy projections.", "gate": "Reproduce the paper's Model 4 ~= 63% accuracy and the >=7pp ablation drop when text features are removed; NFL pilot: 1 season of beat-writer previews with the same stacking protocol vs the GSE engine baseline, measuring moneyline accuracy delta and CLV on the subset where the text model disagrees with the market.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2012.04455v1", "title": "Ratio of counts vs ratio of rates in Poisson processes", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Implement the closed-form ratio posterior f(rho) (eq. 76) as a GSE utility: inputs (goals_1, minutes_1, goals_2, minutes_2, prior alpha_0/beta_0), outputs posterior mode/mean/sd/credible interval of the scoring-rate ratio for matchup preview content ('Chiefs score at 1.31x [1.05, 1.62] the rate of...'); use the Gamma sequential-update form for rolling team scoring-rate posteriors (replacing ad-hoc exponential weighting); adopt the alpha_0=1.01 floor trick wherever GSE fits Gamma priors on rates to exclude degenerate zero-rate posteriors.", "gate": "Adopt the closed-form ratio posterior as a GSE utility if: on 2024-2025 data, its 80% credible intervals achieve empirical coverage within [0.75, 0.85] on forward rate ratios while being narrower than the Gaussian-propagation intervals. Reject if coverage is off-nominal or intervals are wider than the naive baseline.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2012.04626v2", "title": "Minimax Regret Optimisation for Robust Planning in Uncertain MDPs", "normalized_lane": "uncertainty_decision_theory", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "UMDP construction: sample K=15 'worlds' (bootstrap variants of the engine's calibration crossed with 3 market regimes: normal, sharp-heavy, chaotic), each a mapping from (bankroll bucket x edge bucket) to expected weekly profit per stake tier; stake-tier policy minimizing max_world [V*_world - V^pi_world] via the paper's regret-Bellman DP with 2-step options; serve as a weekly lookup in the minimax-regret policy table, logging per-world regret contributions for audit.", "gate": "ACCEPT if 2024-2025: realized worst-world regret <= 0.7 x maximin baseline's AND mean profit >= maximin's AND posted volume >= 80% of flat-1u (must not degenerate toward passivity). REJECT if worst-world regret isn't better than maximin's or volume collapses below 60% (then it's maximin in disguise).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2012.11717v3", "title": "Social NCE: Contrastive Learning of Socially-aware Motion Representations", "normalized_lane": "selfsupervised_tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Train GSE's trajectory forecaster with Social-NCE on NFL 10Hz tracking (primary agent = ball-carrier; neighbors = 11 defenders + nearby blockers): positive key = ball-carrier's true future location (+noise); negatives = 8 angular samples around each defender's future location at radius rho ~= 0.5-1.0 yd (tuned), horizons delta-t in {1,...,4} frames, tau = 0.1, lambda tuned from 0.1; exclude tackle frames from negative sampling (contact is the positive event there) or invert the prior on labeled tackle frames.", "gate": "ADOPT if: (a) impossible-trajectory rate reduced >= 25% vs vanilla with FDE no worse than +2%, AND (b) random negatives do not beat Social-NCE (sanity check that the prior, not just contrast, drives the gain). REJECT if (a) fails.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2012.14949", "title": "Estimating the change in soccer's home advantage during the Covid-19 pandemic using bivariate Poisson regression", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build gse.scores.BivariatePoissonHA: per-season NFL fit -- (home points, away points) ~ BP with log lambda_1 = mu_s + T_s + alpha_H + delta_A, log lambda_2 = mu_s + alpha_A + delta_H; team attack/defense random effects; T_s = season home advantage; extensions: (a) within-season time-varying strengths (state-space); (b) lambda_3 estimated not fixed; (c) COVID-2020 season as T'_2020 with posterior P(decline) -- direct replication of the paper's natural experiment on NFL data; use posterior attack/defense strengths as features for spread/total models.", "gate": "ADAPT->keep if: simulation replication shows MAB(T-hat) <= 0.10 and >=50% bias reduction vs linear regression AND 2020-season holdout predictive log-likelihood beats GSE's current score model by >= 0.01 nats/game. Fail -> REJECT.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2101.02104v1", "title": "A Probabilistic Model for Predicting Shot Success in Football", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt the rating-decay + blending pattern to GSE's NFL probability pipeline: half-life-weighted MLE for any team-level efficiency parameter GSE rates (red-zone TD conversion, third-down conversion, explosive-play rate allowed) with H swept 30-300 (in games, not days, for NFL); add climatology blending p-tilde = alpha*p + (1-alpha)*p_c as a standard shrinkage step for high-parameter-count rating models, alpha fit by minimizing mean ignorance on a calibration fold.", "gate": "Adopt the half-life-weighted rating + climatology-blending + reliability-gate pattern into GSE's calibration stack if, on the reproducible test, the blended rating model achieves negative relative Ignorance and Brier vs climatology with reliability-diagram points inside the 95% consistency bars, and does not degrade relative skill when odds-implied probabilities are added as regressors.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2101.02703", "title": "Distribution-Free, Risk-Controlling Prediction Sets", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Posted-slate risk control: T_lambda = {games with model |edge| >= lambda}; loss = fraction of posted picks that lose (bounded [0,1], monotone decreasing in lambda); calibration = trailing posted picks; choose lambda-hat via the Hoeffding-Bentkus UCB at (alpha=0.45, delta=0.1); publish only T_lambda-hat; drawdown variant with slate max-drawdown as the loss; recompute lambda-hat weekly and log realized risk vs alpha for the public record.", "gate": "ADAPT if: >= (1-delta) - 0.05 of windows satisfy realized risk <= alpha AND posted volume >= 50% of unfiltered (the UCB conservatism must not strangle volume). REJECT the Hoeffding UCB in favor of the Waudby-Smith-Ramdas (empirical-Bernstein) UCB if volume collapses -- tighter bounds are the paper's own Section 6 remedy.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}

{"arxiv_id": "2101.05388v1", "title": "Evaluating Soccer Player: from Live Camera to Deep Reinforcement Learning", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Treat this as engine-honesty infrastructure, not an objective: adapt EDG to NFL 'Expected Discounted Points' (EDP) -- build a lightweight drive simulator from nflverse 2015-2025 (state = down, distance, yardline, score diff, time, timeouts, roster-strength features; transition model = empirical next-state distribution per (state, play-call category) or a fitted gradient-boosted transition model; reward = points scored on drive end, discounted); run the paper's PPO + credit-spread audit pattern as a valuation-honesty instrument against EPA/WPA.", "gate": "Adopt the EDP framework if, on the 2023-2024 holdout: (i) EDP is well-calibrated (slope 0.95-1.05) AND (ii) team mean EDP/play predicts rest-of-season point differential with R^2 >= EPA/play R^2 + 0.02, OR (iii) the credit-spread audit shows EDP systematically reallocating >= 20% of drive value from scoring plays to setup plays while maintaining (i). Reject (stay with EPA/WPA) otherwise.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2101.08175v1", "title": "Bayesian GARCH Modeling of Functional Sports Data", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Two portable pieces: (1) fit GARCH(1,1) errors on player-season (or team-season) random intercepts for a prop-relevant metric (weekly receiving yards for WRs, team EPA/play) on nflverse 2015-2025; test whether volatility clustering exists and whether the conditional variance h_is predicts next-season prop-line beat rates -- i.e., use estimated volatility as a 'consistency' feature in prop models; (2) reuse the additive decomposition for the trajectory model.", "gate": "Adopt if the GARCH specification wins on LOO by a clear margin (Delta-elpd > 2xse) for at least one prop-relevant metric AND the volatility feature improves a prop hit-rate model (log-loss) by >=0.3% on 2024-2025 holdout. Reject if volatility is unclustered or the feature adds nothing.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2101.08954", "title": "Hierarchical stacking for Bayesian model averaging (Yao, Pir\u0161, Vehtari, Gelman, 2021)", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Upgrade GSE's ensemble from static to regime-dependent stacking: learn input-varying stacking weights with automatic small-cell shrinkage (critical for the short NFL season), gaining robustness to slate-distribution shift and a smoothed local-fit diagnostic pointing at which model fails where; this is the ensemble architecture paper to implement after plain log-score stacking is in place (prior art: Yao/Vehtari/Gelman stacking of predictive distributions, PSIS-LOO, Le & Clarke asymptotic optimality).", "gate": "ADAPT the hierarchical stacking architecture after plain log-score stacking is deployed: input-varying weights must beat static stacking on held-out log-loss with sane local-fit diagnostics, and small cells must show proper shrinkage (no wild weights on thin slices).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2101.10385v1", "title": "Online and Scalable Model Selection with Multi-Armed Bandits", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "'Engine Model Selector': arms = model versions (e.g., v5.2.7, challenger versions with different feature sets or lookbacks); reward = realized pick KPIs over a rolling window (ROI on posted picks and calibration/Brier, computed only on picks each version actually shipped); rotate challenger versions on low-stakes slates weekly (Thursday-only or a subset of props), not 15-minute; decay epsilon-greedy with weekly steps, epsilon_0 = 0.3, alpha ~= 8 weeks.", "gate": "ADAPT if a replay of decay epsilon-greedy on 2024 NFL posted picks shows (a) cumulative-regret reduction >= 20% vs equal-split A/B in ROI terms by Week 9, AND (b) the selector's traffic share for the ex-post best arm >= 70% by Week 12; REJECT otherwise (the mechanism adds complexity without demonstrated traffic-savings).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2101.12072v1", "title": "TimeGrad: Autoregressive Denoising Diffusion for Multivariate Probabilistic Time Series", "normalized_lane": "synthetic_data", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build the first sequential-synthesis prototype: nflverse weekly team stats 2015-2024 -> panel of 32 teams x 18 weeks x K metrics (EPA/play margin, success rate, pace, pressure rate); context = weeks 1-12, prediction = weeks 13-18; covariates (opponent embedding, home/away, rest days, dome/outdoor, week index, bye flag) via learned embeddings; 2-layer LSTM (h=40) model; use synthetic trajectories to augment late-season training data.", "gate": "ADOPT TimeGrad-trajectory augmentation if: (a) CRPS_sum on 2023-2024 weeks 13-18 beats the copula baseline by >=5% relative, AND (b) real+synthetic spread log-loss beats real-only by >=0.003 on held-out late-season weeks, AND (c) the 90% empirical intervals achieve 85-95% coverage (calibration sanity). REJECT if autoregressive rollout error compounds (CRPS_sum degrades).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2101.12523", "title": "Optimal strategies for reject option classifiers", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build GSE-SELE: freeze the pick model h; for each historical graded pick compute realized loss l (0/1 for ATS hit, or negative units for bankroll loss); define psi(x) from pick features (model edge, line movement, consensus disagreement, market count -- the native 'MCP/margin' analog is GSE's raw model probability); learn the gate score by ridge regression on realized loss (REG) and by the pairwise SELE loss (SELE), selecting C by validation AuRC; bounded-coverage publish rule.", "gate": "ADAPT accepted if the learned score's AuRC beats the probability-threshold baseline by >= 10% relative on walk-forward seasons AND the win holds at the actual operating coverage (posted card size); else REJECT. Hard fail: if the learned score's top-coverage picks don't beat the baseline's at the exact card size GSE publishes, do not ship regardless of AuRC.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2102.05107", "title": "Sub-Seasonal Forecasting with a Large Ensemble of Deep-Learning Weather Prediction Models", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Ensemble policy: when building prediction ensembles (spread/total/prop models), generate members by retraining with different random seeds/checkpoint snapshots (SP-style) in addition to data-level perturbations; validate the spread-RMSE relationship on holdout (spread should track RMSE by lead/coverage class); no new data needed.", "gate": "ADAPT if the SP-retrain ensemble improves holdout CRPS by >=2% over the bootstrap ensemble AND its spread-RMSE ratio is closer to 1.0 (within +/-0.15) than the bootstrap ensemble's. Otherwise keep data-bootstrap ensembles.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2102.06024v3", "title": "Feature Selection for Multivariate Time Series via Network Pruning (NFS)", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Reimplement NFS: per-stream 1D-CNN (kernel covering ~4 games) over each candidate feature stream (trailing-17-game window), BN layer, alpha extraction, L1 gamma=0.001, aggregation CNN -> LightGBM/MLP head predicting spread cover; train on 2015-2022, select top-k (k in {15, 25, 40} by validation), freeze selection, retrain downstream on selection; use large batches (full seasons) and season-wise standardization so alpha reflects signal, not batch noise; improvement: season-adaptive alpha_{i,s} = alpha_i * delta_{i,s} with its own sparsity penalty (a 'feature regime map').", "gate": "Accept iff NFS top-k (best k) improves 2024 held-out log-loss by >= 0.003 over both baseline A (all streams) and baseline C (hand-picked), with k <= 40 (deployment discipline). Reject if NFS selection underperforms the full set, if the selected set is unstable across 5 seeds (Jaccard < 0.5), or if it merely rediscovers the hand-picked set with no lift.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2102.07081", "title": "1169 From Proper Scoring Rules to Max-Min Optimal Forecast Aggregation", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Operator-scoring-rule match (immediate): evaluate component models with log loss -> aggregate with logarithmic (geometric) pooling; evaluate with Brier -> linear pooling; never mix (concavity fails under mismatch); GSE's primary metric is log loss -> default to log pooling for the ensemble. Online weight learning (~1-2 days): implement Algorithm B.3 -- online gradient descent on the simplex of model weights, loss = -(log score of the QA pool) per week, weights warm-started at equal weights.", "gate": "ADOPT log pooling as GSE's default ensemble operator if it beats linear pooling on 2025 full-season log loss, and ADOPT OGD-learned weights if the OGD ensemble beats equal weights on 2025 log loss with realized regret vs best-hindsight-mixture consistent with O(sqrt(T)). REJECT fixed equal weighting if OGD's learned weights concentrate (>0.5 on one model) while beating equal weights.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2103.00020", "title": "Learning Transferable Visual Models From Natural Language Supervision (CLIP)", "normalized_lane": "multimodal_fusion", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Zero-shot sports-concept retrieval and classification without per-concept labeling: index broadcast frames / tracking snapshots with a CLIP-style encoder so analysts query in language ('cover-2 shell pre-snap', 'mesh concept vs man coverage') and retrieve moments -- no labeled dataset per concept; start from open CLIP weights, contrastive fine-tune on (tracking-image, pbp-text) pairs; prompt engineering for football; improvement: compositional hard negatives for football (captions differing by ONE compositional element: 'cover-2' vs 'cover-4' on near-identical shells).", "gate": "ACCEPT: fine-tuned model reaches >=70% top-1 on held-out concepts with prompt ensembling beating single prompts by >=3 points. REJECT: fine-tuned accuracy <55% (then web-pretrained representations don't transfer and the lane needs domain pretraining from scratch). Also REJECT the zero-shot-only variant if open-weights zero-shot <40%.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2103.00083", "title": "1170 Flexible Model Aggregation for Quantile Regression", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Post-sort isotonization (ADOPT-ready, ~30 min): after GSE produces any quantile vector (intervals for props/totals), apply Sort (or PAVA) before publishing -- Prop. 2 guarantees WIS cannot worsen and non-crossing is enforced at every x. Medium quantile aggregation (~1-2 days): for interval outputs from each component model, learn per-model x per-quantile-level weights w_{j,tau} via SGD on pinball loss over OOF predictions from trailing seasons.", "gate": "ADOPT post-sort isotonization immediately if raw GSE quantile outputs show any crossing violations on 2025 data (Prop. 2 guarantees no WIS downside). ADAPT the medium aggregator if it beats the equal-weight quantile average on 2025 WIS by >=3% with per-tau weights that differ meaningfully between tail and center levels. REJECT fine aggregation (p x m x m weights) unless the training sample exceeds ~10x the parameter count.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2103.03206", "title": "Perceiver: General Perception with Iterative Attention", "normalized_lane": "multimodal_fusion", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "One pre-game representation per team-game fusing (a) NGS tracking embeddings (player trajectories -> per-play pooled embeddings), (b) broadcast-video features (sampled frames/clips from recent games), (c) injury-report / depth-chart text embeddings, (d) crowd/weather meta -- feeding the existing win-probability / spread model; improvement experiment: per-play Perceiver with causal temporal latents (recurrent latent state updated play-by-play) producing live in-game win probability.", "gate": "ACCEPT (adopt into engine): multimodal Perceiver-fusion beats the tracking-only baseline by >=0.003 log-loss on the held-out 2025 season AND beats-or-matches it on 2024 backtest, with ECE no worse than baseline +0.005. REJECT: fusion fails to clear the 0.003 log-loss bar on either window, or the win comes only from the text modality (then the right move is a cheaper text-only feature).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2103.04349v1", "title": "Markov Cricket: Using Forward and Inverse Reinforcement Learning to Model, Predict And Optimize Batting Performance in ODI Cricket", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt IRL to NFL situational decision-making: define the MDP (states = down, distance, yardline, score differential, time; actions = {go for it, punt, field-goal attempt} on 4th downs or {run, pass} on early downs); expert trajectories = drives of winning teams (or top-quartile EPA teams); linear reward in state+action features with Ng & Russell margin-maximization (Eq. 4), or modernize to MaxEnt IRL / guided cost learning with a small neural reward net; improvement: neural reward function to test whether action rankings become state-dependent (e.g., 'go for it' value spiking at specific yardlines).", "gate": "ADAPT gate: (a) Test 1 must show the IRL recovers a known reward function on synthetic ground truth (the paper never validates its IRL -- do not skip this); (b) inferred NFL weights must not all sit at optimization bounds (the paper's bound artifact); (c) expert-definition sensitivity must be checked (winners vs top-EPA teams). If (a) fails, the method is unvalidated machinery -> REJECT. The cricket simulator and DLS results are not adopted under any gate.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2103.04647", "title": "Flexible marked spatio-temporal point processes with applications to event sequences from association football", "normalized_lane": "live_ingame", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Live in-play NFL modeling with the decoupled marks/times factorization -- the cleanest full Bayesian implementation of a Hawkes-like event model in sports, filling the corpus's Hawkes/self-exciting gap (it does not duplicate iWinRNFL or the marked point-process NFL work already in corpus): map one full NFL week of nflverse PBP (~14-16 games) to the composite-mark schema and fit the S-beta model in Stan; use the per-event-type team-ability rankings as features.", "gate": "Test A (fit): all R-hat < 1.1 and effective sample sizes > 400 for ability parameters (the paper's Section 6.1 bar). Test B (predictive gain): hold out the following week's games; lpd^c must beat the FOMC baseline by >= 1.0 per 1,000 events. Test C: per-event-type team-ability rankings correlate (Spearman rho >= 0.5) with independent season performance measures (e.g., offensive EPA rankings). If the lpd^c gap vs FOMC is < 0.5 per 1,000 events, the NFL event stream carries no Hawkes-like excitation worth the complexity -> REJECT.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2103.06023v4", "title": "The efficacy of tournament designs", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Futures/qualification pricing harness: port the paper's design taxonomy (knockout/Swiss/round-robin generators + seeding rules) into the simulation module so tournament outright and qualification probabilities are simulated with format-faithful brackets, not generic Monte Carlo; the <=3% seeding result gives a citable prior against overweighting draw/seed news in futures (content desk + regularization target); build Swiss-format expertise for UCL/esports futures (e.g., the paper's Swiss-vs-knockout 0.9044 at skill=5).", "gate": "ADAPT iff format-faithful simulation moves GSE's own futures prices: reprice a recent tournament outright market (e.g., a World Cup or UCL field) with format-faithful vs naive simulation; the format-faithful version must differ materially on at least one team's price and backtest better against the realized outcome distribution; if format detail doesn't move prices, keep the naive simulator.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2103.14430", "title": "Combining Distribution-Based Neural Networks to Predict Weather Forecast Probabilities", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "For game totals (and optionally margins), add a binned-softmax distribution head to an existing tabular/NN model: e.g., 60 bins over total in [20, 80]; train with cross-entropy or CRPS-on-CDF loss on 2015-2024 games; train 2-4 small variants on different feature subsets (market-implied features vs pure stats) and combine with a shallow stacking network (2x36 ReLU + softmax) trained on a later season slice, minimizing CRPS; derive win/spread/total probabilities by integration; improvement: bin-adaptive resolution -- quantile-spaced bins concentrated where betting value lives (near key numbers 41/44/47/51 for totals, 3/7/10 for spreads).", "gate": "ADOPT the distribution-head pattern if it beats the Gaussian baseline on 2024 CRPS with no degradation in calibration (PIT histogram uniformity); REJECT if the binning produces worse CRPS than the simple Gaussian or if the stacking layer overfits the single stack-training season (check 2022-as-stack-train sensitivity).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2103.15147v3", "title": "Symbolic regression outperforms other models for small data sets", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replicate the protocol on sports data: build ~20 team-season/QB-season regression problems from nflverse (targets: wins, points/drive, EPA/play); use leave-seasons-out splits; compare PySR vs Lasso vs RF vs GB on out-of-sample R^2; if replication holds, it becomes the cited justification for SR-first metric invention in GSE docs; improvement experiment: sample-size curve at train sizes n in {32, 100, 250, 500, 1000} plotting each method's win-rate vs n to locate the crossover n* where ensembles beat SR -- an operating rule (SR for team-season metrics vs ensembles for play-level predictions).", "gate": "ADOPT the 'SR-first for small-n' doctrine if PySR wins the plurality of first places (>=40% of experiments) AND beats Lasso's weighted score on this sports replication; REJECT (keep ensembles as default) if PySR finishes outside the top 2 -- the vendor claim does not transfer.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2103.16196v2", "title": "AlphaEvolve: A Learning Framework to Discover Novel Alphas in Quantitative Investment", "normalized_lane": "signal_discovery_alpha_mining", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Represent sports signals as small programs (Setup/Predict/Learn over the team-game panel; operands: scalars like rest days, vectors like trailing EPA series, matrices like team-x-week panels); implement the redundancy pruner (build op-graph, drop dead/overwritten ops, fingerprint pruned program -> cache evaluated fitness); mine in rounds with a 15% correlation cutoff vs benchmarks -- directly accelerating the hierarchical GP or QFR miners (estimated 2-5x fewer wasted evaluations); improvement: behavioral fingerprinting (hash the quantized signal vector on a fixed probe panel) plus an adaptive cutoff derived from deflated Sharpe.", "gate": "ADAPT->build if pruning cuts evaluations-to-target-fitness by >= 2x vs no-prune control at equal final test Brier AND the 15%-cutoff set beats the unconstrained set by >= 0.002 Brier on 2022-2025. REJECT if one-epoch/fast fitness doesn't rank-preserve (top fast-eval candidates flop on full eval) or the correlation rounds produce no incremental lift.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2104.02883v1", "title": "Online Feature Screening for Data Streams with Concept Drift", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Reimplement the two cheapest exact methods first: online T-score and Fisher with fading (running mean/MS per class -- spread-cover / over-under as binary labels), sparse-aware via appearance counts; add the quantile-summary MI for continuous metrics; run over the 2015-2024 game stream in chronological order; wire into the weekly pipeline (every Tuesday emit refreshed screening); improvement: drift-triggered reselection -- keep faded scores as a monitor but only swap the production feature set when a drift statistic (top-40 Jaccard < 0.7 between consecutive months) fires, logging every swap with its trigger.", "gate": "Accept iff the faded online top-40 matches-or-beats baseline A on average 2019-2024 log-loss (Delta >= 0.001) AND the online scores reproduce offline scores within rank-mismatch <1% on a static snapshot (parity check). Reject if fading adds nothing over full-history screening (keep the cheaper offline version) or if weekly rank churn is so high the feature set is unstable.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2104.04918v2", "title": "Modelling uncertainty in financial tail risk: a forecast combination and weighted quantile approach", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "For spread/total markets, combine GSE's model margin-quantile curves per quantile level with level-specific weights (FC-WQ, M=5 level grid, per-level quantile-loss weights on trailing 8 weeks), then convert the combined quantiles into a tail functional via a strictly consistent joint loss -- covering the quantile-adjacent combination doctrine absent from Round-1 ensembles; improvement: replace fixed level weights with a cost-aware extension weighting recent games by CLV capture (beat-the-close indicator).", "gate": "ADAPT accepted if walk-forward mean quantile loss >=2% below the simple-average baseline at >= 4 of 5 grid levels AND the joint tail-functional loss >=2% below FC-SA, with per-level VRate within [0.7alpha, 1.3alpha] (calibration guard); else REJECT. Hard fail: if any level's weights collapse to a single model for >80% of weeks (combination adds nothing), reject.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2104.07537", "title": "Variational Inference for the Smoothing Distribution in Dynamic Probit Models", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build gse.statespace.PFMVBProbit: dynamic probit with Kalman-smoother-exact conditional and factorized truncated-normal updates, hyperparameter learning for W via M-step (empirical Bayes) or a hierarchical prior; use cases: (a) in-play binary event probabilities (next-play success, drive TD) with time-varying coefficients; (b) player availability/injury-status dynamics; (c) momentum-style binary regime indicators; serve posterior means +/- SDs at play cadence; monitor ELBO convergence.", "gate": "ADAPT->keep if PFM-VB posterior means within 0.01 MAE of exact MCMC on NFL drive data AND predictive log-loss beats static probit by >= 0.003 on 2022-2024 holdout. Fail -> REJECT (fall back to the EP backend).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2104.08236v1", "title": "Controlled Abstention Neural Networks for Identifying Skillful Predictions for Regression Problems", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add a sigma output (softplus) to GSE's totals regression head; train with baseline NLL first (spin-up), then the abstention loss L = -q log N(y; mu, sigma) - alpha log q, q = min(1, (kappa/sigma)^2); set kappa = P_90% of sigma on a validation season; PID controller holds abstention at GSE's target non-publish fraction; publish rule: publish the total pick iff sigma <= tau, recalibrate tau each season; couple the sigma head with the SDR variance-regime direction as an extra input.", "gate": "ADAPT if the abstention model reduces test-window covered-set MAE vs baseline by >=0.5 points of total (or >=3% relative) with sigma z-scores within [-0.2, 0.2] mean and [0.8, 1.2] std; reject if the MAE gap is smaller or sigma is miscalibrated -- then use the simpler baseline, which the paper itself calls 'a simple yet powerful method.'", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2104.08281v1", "title": "Controlled Abstention Neural Networks for Identifying Skillful Predictions for Classification Problems", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add an abstention output to GSE's cover/no-cover classification head; train with L_NW = -log(p_correct + p_abstain) - alpha log(1 - p_abstain), alpha PID-controlled to GSE's target publish fraction; publish rule: publish iff argmax != abstain class (equivalently p_abstain below calibrated tau); A/B against baseline + post-hoc likelihood thresholding and the DAC loss variant; LRP/gradient-based attribution on abstained games to check what's driving abstention.", "gate": "ADAPT if the abstention model beats the baseline on test-window covered-set accuracy by >=2pp with p<0.05 AND >= the DAC variant (replicating the paper's NotWrong > DAC ordering); reject if it doesn't beat the baseline -- then post-hoc thresholding stands and the extra machinery is dropped.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2104.08312v1", "title": "Data Shapley Valuation for Efficient Batch Active Learning", "normalized_lane": "active_learning", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Training-data audit: fix the engine feature space (engineered features remove the representation-learning caveat); train a KNN (or gradient-boosted) classifier on engine features for binary cover/over; compute exact KNN-Shapley values (linear-time DP) of each training game/season against a held-out validation slate (e.g., 2024 season); rank; drop or down-weight negative-value games; retrain; feed valuation: for each candidate feed (nflverse, FTN charting subset, odds history), compute the block-Shapley of the feed's data block via the same KNN proxy -- renew feeds with positive value, drop/renegotiate the rest.", "gate": "ADOPT the valuation filter iff (b) beats (a) on 2024 held-out log-loss by >= 0.003 AND beats (c) by >= 0.005 (i.e., the gain is from value, not just data removal), with the removed decile concentrated in identifiable regimes (e.g., specific seasons/data-quality flags) rather than scattered noise. REJECT if Shapley values are unstable across validation-proxy resamples (Spearman < 0.5 between two 500-game proxies) or if no decile removal beats full data.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}

{"arxiv_id": "2104.11452", "title": "SportsCap: Monocular 3D Human Motion Capture and Fine-grained Understanding in Challenging Sports Videos", "normalized_lane": "sports_cv", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Pilot SubMotion-Play-GSE on QB throwing technique: define the sub-motion taxonomy (stance/drop/release/follow-through), build per-sub-motion PCA pose spaces from GSE-labeled practice/broadcast clips, train a ResNet/ViT encoder regressing pose coefficients + SMPL params, then parse semantic attributes (release time, hip rotation, arm slot) with a multi-stream ST-GCN (joints/bones/coefficients) and an attribute-mapping block assembling the technique label/score \u2014 starting on isolated single-player clips (combine drills, throwing sessions) before attempting team plays, and adding a second-person defender-context stream for contested catches.", "gate": "Before any NFL adaptation: reproduce SAMB > black-box by >=3 points Top-1 on the diving-number task (paper: 82.2 vs 78.0) with <=1/3 the training epochs (paper: 10 vs 30+). If the attribute-structured head doesn't beat black-box with faster convergence, the added annotation cost isn't justified.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2104.14012v1", "title": "Simplified Kalman Filter for Online Rating: One-Fits-All Approach", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace/augment GSE's static Elo update with the vSKF recursions (44-49) under the Bradley-Terry model (NFL init: s=1, v_0=0.02, eps=1e-4, beta=1, eta=0.06, frequency-estimated HFA recomputed on 2015-2025) and keep the per-team uncertainty v_{t,m}: use it to widen/shrink confidence on published picks, reset v for a team after a QB change to force fast re-convergence (the paper's day-40 switch protocol), and feed it as a feature into the pick-confidence model \u2014 then extend beyond binary outcomes by plugging a margin-of-victory likelihood (Skellam or discretized-normal on point differential) into the same vSKF machinery so the Elo learns from blowouts vs close wins.", "gate": "Adopt if vSKF beats SG-Elo log-score by >=0.3% in the converged window OR reaches 90%-of-final ratings >=2 games faster on average (the paper's Fig. 5 effect). Reject if neither holds on 2018-2025 data: plain Elo remains the GSE default.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2104.14277v2", "title": "Kelly Bets and Single-Letter Codes: Optimal Information Processing in Natural Systems", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Install a feed-pricing rule: for each candidate data feed/feature family F, estimate its incremental mutual information I(F; Y | current features) on a historical window (k-NN or variational estimators); the bound (32) implies the feed can reduce achievable log-loss-distortion by at most that many nats \u2014 buy iff expected profit lift (nats x avg stake x edge conversion) exceeds feed cost. Pair it with a staking diagnostic: the gap between GSE's realized (D, R) operating point and the bound (32) implied by its estimated outcome model flags non-proportional (over/under-confident) staking before it shows up in P&L.", "gate": "ADAPT the feed-pricing rule if incremental-MI rank correlates with ablation log-loss lift at Spearman rho >= 0.6 on two separate seasons AND at least one feed decision (buy/skip) made by the rule would have been profitable ex post; otherwise REJECT the pricing use and keep only the staking-gap diagnostic.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2105.08310v1", "title": "BBE: Simulating the Microstructural Dynamics of an In-Play Betting Exchange via Agent-Based Modelling", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Build GSE-LOB: an NFL pre-game odds-movement simulator reusing BBE's exchange mechanics (price-time priority, partial fills, back/lay ladders) seeded from real opening lines (Odds API / consensus), with an NFL event model swapped in (GSE's game simulator emitting score/time states) and the paper's agent taxonomy ported (RP(d) sharps running the simulator d times, steam chasers, move-followers, public-bias) \u2014 used strictly as calibration infrastructure for staking research: close the loop by using the simulator as the fitness function in an evolutionary search over staking strategies with adversarial calibration of the bettor-agent mix against real 2024 line-movement data.", "gate": "ADOPT the simulator for staking research if, pre-registered: KS distance on move magnitudes < 0.10 AND simulated steam-move frequency within +-20% of observed, on the 2024 season holdout. REJECT for production staking use if either fails \u2014 an uncalibrated simulator teaches the staking optimizer to exploit artifacts.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2105.08877v2", "title": "Deep Reinforcement Learning for Optimal Stopping with Application in Financial Engineering", "normalized_lane": "rl_sequential_decisions", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Formulate bet-timing as optimal stopping: state = (current edge vs market, hours to kickoff, line-movement velocity, book spread, bankroll), actions = {bet now at current line, wait} with forced terminal action at kickoff, reward = CLV captured (or realized profit) relative to acting immediately; train a C51 stopping agent on 2021-2023 line-movement histories with the paper's three-stage protocol (Valid_HP on 2022, Valid_Model on 2023 H1, strictly-future Test on 2023 H2-2024) \u2014 then train a distributional variant minimizing CVaR of CLV regret (best achievable line minus taken line) instead of maximizing expected payout, testing whether tail-aware timing beats expectation-maximizing timing.", "gate": "ADOPT iff on the strictly-future test window the C51 stopping policy beats the best timing benchmark by >=1.5pp of CLV per bet with realized ROI no worse than the 'bet at open' baseline; otherwise REJECT (timing alpha doesn't survive transaction reality).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2105.11982v2", "title": "Quantifying Uncertainty in Deep Spatiotemporal Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Adopt MIS as GSE's standard interval score and a quantile/MIS-regression head as GSE's interval engine for total-line and prop intervals: per the paper's Table 1 mapping (thousands of games, limited compute), rule out MC dropout (worst MIS in all three tasks) and naive bootstrap (25 retrains), train quantile-regression (pinball, 0.025/0.5/0.975) and MIS-regression (eq. 7) heads on the existing engine, plus a DeepGLEAM-style residual model on (engine projection - closing line) \u2014 then extend with a DCRNN-style graph convolution over an NFL team graph (nodes = teams, edges = games played, recency weights) so the interval head conditions on opponent-adjusted residuals, and combine SG-MCMC's posterior-mean point forecast with the MIS-regression interval head.", "gate": "Adopt MIS as the standard interval score and the quantile/MIS-regression head as GSE's interval engine if: on the 2025 test season, the MIS-regression (or quantile) interval beats the current fixed-band practice by >=10% in MIS with coverage in [0.93, 0.97].", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2105.12785v1", "title": "The Anatomy of Corner 3s in the NBA: What makes them efficient, how are they generated and how can defenses respond?", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Port the trajectory-clustering pipeline to GSE's NGS lane: replicate section 3.2 on NGS 10 Hz tracking \u2014 cluster pass-rush arcs (first 1.5 s post-snap) and route stems (first 2 s of routes) with k-means + gap statistic + radius-of-gyration coherence to discover empirical archetypes (e.g., 'anchored edge contain' vs 'stunt inside'); port the commit-vs-help game model to NFL help decisions (safety commit-to-man vs robber on run-pass conflict; edge contain vs crash) \u2014 and replace fixed-window k-means with dynamic-time-warping clustering (k-medoids on DTW distance) to handle variable NFL play timing, testing whether DTW archetypes predict pressure/sack outcomes better (out-of-sample AUC for pressure within 2.5 s) than Euclidean clusters.", "gate": "Adopt the trajectory-clustering pipeline into GSE's NGS lane if the reproducible test yields >=2 clusters each containing >=20% of pass-rush snaps with radius of gyration below the median of all clusters AND the cluster archetypes are interpretable as distinct rush styles on manual review of >=50 sampled snaps.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2106.00170", "title": "Adaptive Conformal Inference Under Distribution Shift", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt ACI as GSE's online coverage controller for published intervals: audit aci-durable.ts/aci-state.ts against the paper's exact update alpha_{t+1} = alpha_t + gamma(alpha - err_t) with err_t computed on the interval the engine actually PUBLISHED (not a post-hoc interval), run a weekly online loop updating a per-market (spread/total/moneyline) alpha_t after each slate resolves, backtest gamma in {0.001, 0.005, 0.01, 0.02} on 2023-2025 scoring long-run coverage error + mean interval width \u2014 and test a regime-aware two-gamma controller (gamma_small in calm weeks, gamma_large for 3 weeks after a detected changepoint) on post-changepoint local-coverage recovery time.", "gate": "ADAPT if: long-run coverage error <= 1.5x the paper's O(1/(T*gamma)) bound AND mean interval width <= 110% of fixed-alpha baseline. REJECT pure-ACI in favor of the conformal-PID variant (ledger 1643) if weekly local coverage sags >5pp below nominal for 4+ consecutive weeks.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2106.00175", "title": "Duckworth-Lewis-Stern Method Comparison with Machine Learning Approach", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build the live engine experiment live/classical_vs_ml.py: (a) a simple closed-form football WP baseline (logistic on time x score-diff, or the ledger-1704 monotone table); (b) gradient boosting / NN on nflverse play-by-play state features INCLUDING the baseline WP as a feature (the paper's stacking trick); compare accuracy AND log-loss vs the baseline alone at game-progression deciles \u2014 and resolve the 1704-vs-1705 tension with a three-way bake-off: (a) unconstrained ML, (b) monotone-constrained Bayesian (1704 recipe), (c) unconstrained ML with the monotone table's output as a feature; success = (c) matches (a) on accuracy and beats both on ECE in extreme states (WP < 0.1 or > 0.9, last 5 minutes).", "gate": "ADOPT the stacked ML live model if it beats the classical baseline by >= 1 pp accuracy AND >= 0.005 log-loss at every game decile on the holdout. REJECT if the ML wins accuracy but loses log-loss \u2014 that reproduces the paper's limitation and is unusable for staking.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2106.01345v2", "title": "Decision Transformer: Reinforcement Learning via Sequence Modeling", "normalized_lane": "rl_sequential_decisions", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a season-episode trajectory dataset for staking: one 'episode' = one NFL season of weekly slates; per week t: R-hat_t = remaining season profit target in units, s_t = slate features (edges, CLV, bankroll, week number, exposure used), a_t = stake-bucket vector (discrete 0/0.25/0.5/1/2u per bet, padded); train a small GPT (4-6 layers, 18-week or K=8 context) with CE loss on stake tokens conditioned on R-hat_1 = +30u season target; each Tuesday prompt with the remaining target and recent (R-hat, s, a) history to emit the week's stake vector \u2014 then extend to distributional conditioning: quantile targets (e.g., 'achieve >=+20u with P(drawdown>10u) <= 0.1') as additional conditioning tokens with a quantile-weighted loss.", "gate": "ADOPT iff on the 2024 season the DT policy beats fractional-Kelly ROI by >=2pp with max drawdown no worse than baseline AND the prompted-target/achieved-return correlation on holdout is >=0.5; otherwise REJECT in favor of the CQL approach.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2106.01972", "title": "SOCCER: An Information-Sparse Discourse State Tracking Collection in the Sports Commentary Domain", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt the sparse-state-tracking protocol to NFL text streams: build a corpus of timestamped NFL beat-writer/X commentary aligned to official play-by-play events (injuries, turnovers, lineup changes); train a classifier over rolling windows of text to flag state-changing items, evaluated with positive recall at fixed precision under heavy class imbalance; apply the paper's sparsity-ablation protocol to measure how non-event chatter degrades detection; use the 10-bit joint-output trick (or multi-label head) to model correlated events (injury + substitution co-occurring) \u2014 then replace frozen-BERT+GRU with a modern long-context encoder and extend the state ontology to NFL-relevant events (injury, ejection, weather delay, coach challenge).", "gate": "For GSE: positive recall >= 0.5 at precision >= 0.6 on a held-out month of NFL news->event labels passes the gate.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2106.02039v4", "title": "Offline Reinforcement Learning as One Big Sequence Modeling Problem", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build GSE-TT: tokenize each play's continuous features (yardline, EPA, win-probability delta, time) with per-dimension quantile discretization (per the HalfCheetah lesson \u2014 uniform bins fail on heavy tails) plus native categorical tokens, interleaved as (state_t, play_descriptor_t, reward_t) tokens; train a GPT decoder (12+ layers for 150-play games) by teacher forcing on nflverse 2006-2025; price via ancestral sampling (beam search only for 'most likely game script' content); combine with the 1944 drive-token hierarchy for long-range structure \u2014 then replace fixed quantile bins with learned VQ discretization (a tiny VQ-VAE over (yardline, EPA, WP-delta) trained jointly with the transformer) so bin boundaries adapt to football's distributional quirks (EPA spikes at turnovers, yardline pile-up at the goal line).", "gate": "ADOPT per-dimension quantile discretization as GSE's tokenization standard if (A) beats (B) by >=5% log-likelihood on 2024 held-out plays AND the best token-transformer meets the 1942 gates (TVD <=5%/week, ECE <=0.03).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2106.05174v1", "title": "UEFA EURO 2020 Forecast via Nested Zero-Inflated Generalized Poisson Regression", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Adapt the nested conditional simulation for NFL exact-score and prop simulation: fit per-team scoring/concession distributions (Poisson/NB from GSE's inventory), add the dependence term log mu_B|A = beta_0 + beta_1*opp_strength + beta_2*location + beta_3*G_A (the garbage-time/prevent-defense mechanism); Monte Carlo: simulate the favorite's points, then the underdog's conditional on the realized favorite score; replace the paper's step-3 parameter averaging with a single joint fit (log mu_A = alpha_0 + alpha_1*Elo_B + alpha_2*loc + alpha_3*attack_A + alpha_4*defense_B in one likelihood) \u2014 and benchmark the nested sampler against a Gaussian-copula Poisson and Dixon-Coles lambda_3 on exact-score log-loss.", "gate": "ADAPT gate: (a) the nested dependence term beta_3 must be empirically != 0 on NFL data (garbage-time/prevent-defense mechanism); (b) exact-score log-loss must improve over the independent baseline out-of-sample; (c) step-3 parameter averaging replaced by a principled reconciliation. If (a) fails, the mechanism is soccer-specific theater and the paper drops to REJECT.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2106.05799v1", "title": "Hybrid Machine Learning Forecasts for the UEFA EURO 2020", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "NFL adaptation of the hybrid architecture: ability estimators = (a) time-decayed Bradley-Terry/Elo on 8 seasons (half-life ~2 seasons, tuned by RPS), (b) bookmaker-consensus via 100k season simulations inverting Super Bowl futures, (c) EPA-based ridge plus-minus -> team roster strength + missing-starters features; covariates = rest/bye, travel/altitude, wind/weather, market-implied total, injury-report counts (difference-coded); feed into XGBoost \u2014 with a copula-coupled score model (Gaussian-copula negative-binomial on (home points, away points), capturing negative correlation in blowouts and positive in shootouts) replacing the paper's conditional-independence assumption. Treated as engine-honesty infrastructure for sharper moneyline pricing, not as a betting objective.", "gate": "Adopt the hybrid architecture if, on the 2015-2024 leave-one-season-out test, the hybrid model's mean moneyline log-loss beats both the market-consensus baseline and the plain-covariate XGBoost by >= 0.005 (absolute), with the improvement present in >= 7 of the 10 held-out seasons.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2106.06317v1", "title": "Automatic Risk Adaptation in Distributional RL", "normalized_lane": "uncertainty_decision_theory", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Wrap the engine's pick/stake decisions in automatic risk adaptation: train a lightweight RND pair on the engine's game-feature vectors (spread, total, team ratings, injuries, weather flags, rest days) over historical seasons; per-game novelty u(game) = normalized prediction error; apply CVaR distortion with alpha = e^{-u} to the engine's outcome distribution for post/stake decisions (familiar divisional game -> full aggression; unprecedented situation -> pass or quarter-stake) \u2014 then learn psi instead of fixing e^{-u}: fit a monotone map from u to alpha via isotonic regression on u-deciles maximizing realized CVaR of weekly profit, and measure novelty in 'ways the engine is wrong' (RND on the engine's residual stream, not raw features).", "gate": "ACCEPT if walk-forward: policy B's worst-week loss (5th percentile of weekly P&L) is >=25% smaller (less negative) than the best fixed-alpha policy's, AND season profit >= 0.95 x best fixed-alpha season profit, AND the u-decile stratification shows monotonically decreasing stake with increasing u.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2106.06427v1", "title": "Neural Symbolic Regression that Scales", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Stand up NeSymReS as the equation-discovery proposer in two phases: Phase 1 (no training) \u2014 use the released pre-trained model as a fast proposer on nflverse slices with BFGS-fit constants, ranked with the 1826 selector, testing whether the generic-math prior transfers; Phase 2 \u2014 build a sports equation generator (skeletons sampled from operator distributions fit to the 1826 sports corpus, constants in sports ranges, support points drawn from real nflverse feature marginals) and fine-tune the Set Transformer->decoder on ~10-50M sports-plausible equations; embed encoder+decoder inference (seconds on CPU) in the weekly research pipeline \u2014 and run prior surgery: fine-tune three checkpoints (100% generic / 50-50 / 100% sports-plausible) measuring the in-distribution->OOD (2024-2025) degradation curve to find the minimum sports-mixture needed.", "gate": "ADOPT NeSymReS as the proposer if, within a 100s test-time budget, its best <=15-node equation is within 5% test RMSE of PySR's 30-minute best on the 2024-2025 window; ADOPT the fine-tune if it beats the released checkpoint by >=10% test RMSE.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2106.07197v1", "title": "DAGs with No Curl: Learning DAGs via Hodge Decomposition", "normalized_lane": "causal_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Swap the NOTEARS solver for DAG-NoCurl as GSE's production continuous-optimization DAG solver: mirror ledger 1962's spec (team-season static snapshot, ~35 indicators, least-squares loss) but replace the solver with the two-step NoCurl procedure (unconstrained L-BFGS -> Hodge projection -> threshold); add a nonlinear variant (NoCurl + DAG-GNN backbone); then build time-series NoCurl by applying the Hodge projection to a lag-augmented cyclic solution (VAR-style, as in DYNOTEARS) \u2014 testing lag-NoCurl vs DYNOTEARS vs PCMCI+ParCorr on synthetic VAR data with known lagged ground truth on SHD and runtime.", "gate": "ADOPT DAG-NoCurl as the production continuous-optimization solver if: (a) SHD within 10% of NOTEARS on synthetic; (b) >=10x wall-clock speedup on the 35-indicator panel; (c) Sachs-style sanity check (or football equivalent: recovers known edges like EPA->win) passes.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2106.08460", "title": "Localized Conformal Prediction", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Implement sample-splitting localized conformal prediction for margins/totals: localizer = product kernel on (total bucket, spread bucket, weather bucket, rest differential) or k-NN in the engine's feature space; implement the paper's ADJUSTED quantile level exactly (not the naive weighted quantile); per-game intervals from the localized calibration distribution; report effective sample size per game ((sum w)^2 / sum w^2) and flag starved games \u2014 then learn the localizer: replace the hand-picked kernel with weights from the residual-QRF of ledger 1642 (leaf co-occurrence = similarity), fusing ledgers 1642 and 1644 into one adaptive-localization pipeline.", "gate": "ADAPT if: worst-stratum coverage gap (max over strata |coverage - nominal|) shrinks >=30% vs marginal CQR at <=105% mean width. REJECT full LCP in favor of Mondrian stratification if the kernel version's effective sample sizes collapse (median (sum w)^2 / sum w^2 < 50).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2106.11397v1", "title": "Evaluating Team Skill Aggregation in Online Competitive Games", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build player-level skill ratings and learn the aggregation: per-player EPA/play with shrinkage toward position means (QB: CPOE/EPA per dropback; receivers: TPRR/YPRR; defenders: pressure rates) treated as mu per player-week via rolling windows; aggregate to unit ratings via SUM/MAX/MIN plus a learned per-role weighted blend (softmax weights over positional groups fit by maximizing walk-forward log-likelihood of game outcomes \u2014 letting the data decide whether the QB is the MAX player and whether the weak-link OL starter is the MIN); team strength = aggregation of unit ratings into logistic win-probability vs closing lines.", "gate": "Adopt the aggregation variant if it beats the current GSE baseline by >=0.003 log-loss on the 2024-2025 walk-forward window AND by >=0.5 percentage points ATS accuracy; ADAPT the blend weights if only the weighted blend beats baseline.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2106.12059v3", "title": "Stochastic Batch Acquisition: A Simple Baseline for Deep Active Learning", "normalized_lane": "active_learning", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Replace top-K charting acquisition with stochastic batch acquisition: wherever GSE takes top-K games by any acquisition/uncertainty score for charting, sample with power sampling p(game) ~ s(game)^beta (beta=1, Gumbel-top-K, 5 lines); formalize a season-aware charting-intensity calendar (small batches weeks 1-6 when scores decorrelate fastest, larger late season); score cost-adjusted (s_i/c_i); then run an adaptive beta schedule beta_t = f(estimated total correlation) from the ensemble's joint-vs-marginal prediction entropy \u2014 high beta late season when TC->0, low beta in weeks 1-4.", "gate": "ADOPT power acquisition as the default batch rule iff it is never worse than top-K on weekly ATS log-loss across the 2024 season (stochastic mean >= top-K in >= 12 of 18 weeks) AND increases mean within-batch pairwise distance by >= 10%.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2106.14345v2", "title": "More on verification of probability forecasts for football outcomes: score decompositions, reliability, and discrimination analyses", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Install the standard verification suite for GSE's published probabilities (win prob, over prob, ATS cover prob): implement the three Brier decompositions exactly as eqs. (1)/(2)/(4) with Siegert binning (eq. 7) + PAV isotonic binning on every backtest window (2020-2026 nflverse, ~1,900 games): report BRS, REL, RES, DIS, VPB, VPW, RIL, COV, skill vs climatology, side-by-side GSE vs de-vigged Pinnacle/OddsAPI consensus; run a weekly logistic calibration monitor (logit(cover) = alpha + beta logit(GSE prob) per market, Wald alert if alpha != 0 or beta != 1); add a joint (win x over) calibration check via copula-style joint reliability diagrams (NFL edges live in the joint tail: favorite-wins-and-covers) with the CORP/T-PAV estimator from paper 0469 for binning. Framed as engine-honesty infrastructure for calibration reporting, not as a prediction objective.", "gate": "Adopt the suite as the standard diagnostic if: on the 2025 test window, the decomposition reveals an actionable deficiency the current Brier-only reporting misses \u2014 e.g., RES_GSE < RES_market - 0.03 on either event, or the logistic test rejects alpha=0 at p<0.01 for a GSE market.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2107.03090", "title": "RISAN: Robust Instance Specific Deep Abstention Network", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build GSE-RISAN as a second gate head: take the pick model's feature trunk, add a rho(x) head outputting a per-pick abstention width, train jointly with a double-sigmoid-style surrogate adapted to unit loss (replace 0-d-1's fixed d with a per-pick cost d(x) = stake fraction at risk), compare against the global-threshold gate and the ledger-1775 learned score on accepted hit-rate at matched card sizes with 10-20% injected outcome noise \u2014 and learn a market-conditioned width rho(x, line-movement) so the abstention band widens when the market disagrees with the model (abstain when the market knows something the model doesn't).", "gate": "ADAPT accepted if the joint (f, rho) learner beats the global gate by >= 3 points of accepted hit-rate at matched coverage on clean data AND degrades less under 20% injected noise; else REJECT (keep the fixed-predictor learned score from 1775).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2107.06268", "title": "Smoothed Bernstein Online Aggregation for Day-Ahead Electricity Demand Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Install a shock-handling ensemble: an event-adjustment front-end (regress historical margins on schedule-event dummies \u2014 Thanksgiving/Christmas/short-rest/byes \u2014 with team-strength controls; train combiners on event-adjusted outcomes, add the event effect back at forecast time); window-diverse experts (copies of GSE's core models on 8wk / 1-season / 3-season windows); smoothed Bernstein Online Aggregation over experts; and 2-D joint smoothing over the (market x week) weight grid with a tensor-product P-spline penalty (lambda_market: spread/total weights share structure; lambda_time: weights evolve slowly, BOA updates as innovations), tuned by discounted validation loss.", "gate": "ADOPT if smoothed BOA beats plain BOA by >=1% on margin MAE OR the event-adjustment front-end improves holiday/short-rest-week MAE by >=5% without hurting normal weeks. REJECT if the smoother's selected lambda collapses to ~=0 AND the front-end shows no holiday-week gain.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2107.07561v1", "title": "Multivariate Conway-Maxwell-Poisson Distribution: Sarmanov Method and Doubly-Intractable Bayesian Inference", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt MultCOMP as a fast two-step estimator (COM-Poisson margins + delta/omega moment-match, no MCMC) for joint low-count NFL outcomes: per-game paired counts of (home explosive plays, away explosive plays) where negative in-game dependence exists (possessions are a zero-sum clock resource); extend the paper with a covariate-dependent delta(z) = clip(delta_0 + beta^T z) inside the per-pair validity interval, letting dependence vary with game-state proxies (pregame spread, total, pace) \u2014 stronger in slow, low-total games, weaker in shootouts \u2014 fit by profile held-out likelihood on 2024.", "gate": "ADOPT the adapted estimator if, on the 2024 holdout window, MultCOMP beats independent Poisson by >= 0.01 nats/observation in mean joint log-likelihood AND the derived P(home out-gains away) calibration slope in decile bins is within [0.9, 1.1].", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2107.08827v1", "title": "Optimal sports betting strategies in practice: an experimental review", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Install fractional/drawdown-Kelly as GSE's sizing protocol: a sizing module g:(p-hat, o)->f for the daily pick slate (NFL moneyline/spread/total legs as n-outcome assets, 10+ parallel games = the parallel-games formulation) \u2014 fractional-Kelly core with fraction omega tuned on walk-forward (grid omega in [0,1], selection = maximize median bankroll growth s.t. <=5% of trajectories draw down below 90%), the Busseti et al. drawdown-constraint convex program (cvxpy) as the production safety rail, robust-Kelly box as the conservative mode for low-confidence slates \u2014 and an adaptive fraction omega_t = clipped(AKL_rolling)/AKL_target on a trailing 8-week window (floored at 0 = no-bet) so the fraction reflects current uncertainty. Engine-honesty infrastructure for sustainable staking, not a profit objective.", "gate": "Adopt fractional/drawdown-Kelly as the GSE sizing protocol iff on the 2024-2025 NFL backtest the tuned-fraction Kelly (or KellyDrawdown) achieves (a) ruin% <= 1%, (b) median final wealth >= 110% of the flat-betting baseline's median, and (c) beats fixed half-Kelly (omega=0.5) on median wealth.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2108.00821v2", "title": "The reaction to news in live betting", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt the SSM news-reaction design to NFL in-play: fit the paper's ARX(1)+ZAGA state model on NFL in-play spreads/totals using 1-minute odds-change velocity (Odds API / oddsPapi / APIVault snapshots) as the observable, with news covariates = touchdowns/turnovers classified by surprise (pre-play win probability from nflfastR's wp, thresholds at <25%); test a contrarian rule fading the line move after surprising events (take the pre-event fair-price side) \u2014 and decompose the observable into ticket count vs handle share where public split data exists, testing whether the overreaction is retail tickets (cognitive bias) or sharp handle (repositioning).", "gate": "ADOPT the adapted design if BOTH hold on the 2024 holdout: (1) the surprising-news coefficient beta-hat_surprising > 0 with 95% CI excluding zero (behavioral replication); (2) a contrarian rule shows positive mean CLV per event at >= +0.5% average with two-sided p<0.05 on >=100 surprising events.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2108.02082v3", "title": "Bayesian Forecast Combination Using Time-Varying Features", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a regime-dependent ensemble blender for GSE pick probabilities: per-game regime features computed from bet-time data (spread bucket, total, rest, weather flags, market disagreement, ATS volatility, home/road, primetime), softmax weights over GSE's constituent models as a linear function of regime features fit by maximizing log-loss via L-BFGS (MAP with N(0,10^3) priors), Gibbs-sampled/L1 variable selection to rank features \u2014 and a CLV-aware objective (log predictive score minus penalty for disagreement with closing-line-implied probability) testing market-shrunk regime weights vs pure log-score FEBAMA weights on out-of-sample Brier AND simulated CLV.", "gate": "ADAPT accepted if feature-conditioned weights achieve >=2% relative log-loss improvement over BOTH SA and constant OP weights on the 2024 weeks-10-18 walk-forward, with >=3 regime features selected in >50% of Gibbs draws. Hard fail: weights collapse to near-constant (max range < 0.05 across games).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2108.02140v1", "title": "Linear regression under model uncertainty", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Install regime-robust trend estimation: moving-block Robust-LSE for pooled game-level regression (e.g., offense/defense strength drift, weather-rest effects on margins) \u2014 rolling windows of ~100-150 games, OLS per window, beta-hat from the min-MSE window, reporting (mu-hat-bar, mu-hat-underbar) and (sigma-hat-bar, sigma-hat-underbar) as regime-uncertainty bounds; apply the small-window centralization + max block MSE recipe to weekly engine residual streams (spread residuals) as a volatility-regime dashboard feeding bet-sizing \u2014 and test a regime-weighted variant (inverse-MSE-weighted blocks instead of hard min-selection) against both OLS and hard-selection Robust-LSE on the synthetic NFL DGP.", "gate": "Adopt if: Robust-LSE reduces mean |beta-hat - 1| by >= 20% relative to OLS at K=4 with T~=1000 injected games, AND the recovered (sigma-hat-underbar, sigma-hat-bar) bracket the injected (3,10) bounds within +-1.5 points.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2108.02419v1", "title": "Implementing the BBE Agent-Based Model of a Sports-Betting Exchange", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Build an NFL-flavoured BBE: replace the 1-D race with a drive-level NFL game simulator (nflverse-based: down/distance/yardline state, EP/WP transition model) and bettor archetypes relevant to NFL live markets (sharp low d-error, public favourite/longshot bias with stake clustering, steam-chaser BTF on line moves); generate synthetic live odds tapes (spread/total/moneyline ladder per minute of game time) with known ground-truth scripts to train/validate GSE's live-betting models and stress-test the Kelly sizing module under adversarial conditions (flash crashes, steam runs) \u2014 with cross-market interplay the authors defer: simulate live spread, total, AND moneyline books jointly with a shared game-state process so arbitrage constraints hold by construction, and study 'synthetic steam' (inject a known informed agent mid-game and measure follower propagation speed) as a laboratory for real steam detection. Engine-honesty infrastructure for staking research.", "gate": "ADOPT the synthetic-live-market simulator if the synthetic-trained live-total model achieves within 10% relative log-loss of the real-trained model on the 2024 test window AND the simulator reproduces closing-line-move distributions within +-0.5 points MAD.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2108.03210v3", "title": "Regression Diagnostics meets Forecast Evaluation: Conditional Calibration, Reliability Diagrams, and Coefficient of Determination", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt CORP as the standard diagnostics suite for the GSE engine: after each training run (XGBoost / tabular models on nflverse features), compute CORP T-reliability diagrams for mean forecasts (margin/spread-total under squared error) and for quantile forecasts (win-probability tails, alpha=0.1/0.5/0.9 under pinball loss) via the PAV algorithm; report MCB/DSC/UNC + R* per model version in the run log \u2014 replacing ad-hoc R^2 for quantile heads; extend to ensemble comparison (cross-fitted out-of-fold isotonic recalibration of the ensemble mean vs each constituent, PAV-recalibrated values per game); stratify CORP diagrams by market regime (closing-line favorite vs underdog) and week-block to test whether miscalibration concentrates in specific regimes.", "gate": "Adopt (ADAPT) if: on the 2025 out-of-sample window, CORP diagnostics detect miscalibration in the current engine (M-hat-CB >= 0.15 x UNC, i.e., >=15% of score variance is recalibratable bias) OR the engine's current diagnostics cannot separate calibration from discrimination.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2108.05053v1", "title": "Managing ML Pipelines: Feature Stores and the Coming Wave of Embedding Ecosystems", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Add the feature-store monitoring layer: a feature authoring registry \u2014 every NFL feature defined as a versioned SQL/pandas transform with declared refresh cadence (e.g., qb_epa_trailing_8w: weekly, Wednesdays post-NGS update), the registry (not cron scripts) owning the refresh schedule; per-materialization quality metrics (freshness = event_ts of latest record vs now, null counts, MI between new/old versions) logged to a feature_quality table; a training-deployment skew monitor (PSI per model version); and a supervised feature-value audit \u2014 after each week, recompute every feature from raw sources, diff against served values, and correlate feature diffs with prediction errors, turning monitoring from 'did the distribution move?' into 'did a bad feature value cost us a pick?'", "gate": "ADOPT the monitoring doctrine iff: the injected-fault test detects the corruption within one materialization cycle with >=95% precision on named feature sets (no false naming of clean features), AND the PSI skew monitor on the 2024 season produces <=1 false alert per month of simulated operation.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2108.08797", "title": "Physics-informed ML for head impact detection", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Adapt the synthetic-pretraining recipe for rare-event detectors in GSE's data pipeline (injury-event flags from tracking data, anomalous-play detection): build a physics/simulation-based synthetic generator for the rare class (the FE head-neck analog), pretrain the detector on synthetic + real negatives, fine-tune on real data, with time-shift augmentation, class-weighted loss, and pre-registered F2 (recall-weighted) reporting \u2014 then extend to uncertainty-aware triage: MC-dropout at inference routes low-confidence events to manual review, quantifying the residual manual workload (hours/season) rather than claiming full automation. Serving = automated triage replacing manual video/charting review.", "gate": "Gate (numeric): ADAPT the synthetic-pretraining recipe if the replication shows F2 gain >= 0.03 with no increase in false negatives. REJECT if synthetic pretraining degrades real-data calibration (PPV drop > 0.05 on real data).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2108.11149", "title": "A Unified Taxonomy and Multimodal Dataset for Events in Invasion Games", "normalized_lane": "multimodal_fusion", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build an NFL event taxonomy refined from the paper's base (game status: whistle/dead-ball vs live; possession: change-of-possession events; individual ball events: snap, handoff, dropback, throw/release [intentional pass/throwaway vs unintentional fumble/strip], reception [catch/drop/breakup], tackle; attributes: yard line, down, coverage shell), a gold-standard multimodal annotation set (broadcast video + tracking + audio) for ~10 games, and an expert-vs-provider audit of one charting source \u2014 then train a multimodal event spotter (video + tracking + audio jointly, ablating modalities per event type): tracking gives exact ball-carrier kinematics, audio gives whistle/crowd cues for game-status changes (the video baseline's weakness from cuts/replays).", "gate": "ACCEPT: (a) annotator agreement meets the >=0.9/>=0.7 bar (top-level / leaf); AND (b) the provider audit finds >=5% label disagreement on at least one high-leverage event type (pass/rush/TD attribution) \u2014 proving the audit adds value over blind trust. REJECT if annotators can't agree at leaf level (<0.6) or providers agree >=99% with experts.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2109.01305", "title": "Video Pose Distillation for Few-Shot, Fine-Grained Sports Action Recognition", "normalized_lane": "sports_cv", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Stand up the VPD-NFL lane: build an uncut unlabeled corpus of NFL broadcast All-22 + sideline video; run HRNet/RTMPose as teacher with confidence filter at 0.5; train a ResNet-34 student (5ch RGB+RAFT flow) to regress (p_t, Delta p_t) per Eq 1, validating on 20% of frames; extract descriptors per play; downstream: BiGRU/DTW-NNS for fine-grained action retrieval (route-type retrieval, tackle-technique classification) and a few-shot classifier head for novel fine-grained labels \u2014 start single-athlete (QB throwing mechanics) before multi-player; then swap the ResNet-34 student for a lightweight temporal ViT consuming 8-frame clips (regressing the pose sequence jointly) and replace the fixed 0.5 confidence gate with a per-joint learned reliability weighting.", "gate": "VI-VPD descriptors must beat the raw teacher-pose baseline by >=5 percentage points top-1 in the 16-shot setting (the paper's own margin on its hardest datasets) before any production adaptation is approved. If <3pp, drop (teacher pose + augmentation suffices).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2109.04720", "title": "6MapNet: Representing Soccer Players by a Triplet Network", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build 6MapNet-style triplet re-identification on NFL tracking: per player-drive, location heatmaps (field grid) + direction heatmaps (velocity vectors above 4 m/s) from Big Data Bowl tracking; identities = player + K-means route/coverage role-cluster; 3-drive augmentation by pixel-wise addition; triplet CNN (alpha=0.1, hard-negative mining, ATL-sim outlier filtering) \u2014 then learn the role assignment jointly (multi-task role classifier + triplet embedding), add ball-relative features (distance/angle to ball) as a third heatmap channel, and test zero-shot transfer (retrieval precision@10) to unseen players.", "gate": "ADAPT if: on NFL tracking, 6MapNet-style embeddings beat raw-heatmap L2 re-identification by >=10 percentage points top-1 accuracy on held-out player-drive entities, with top-10 >= 80%. Otherwise keep only the ATL-sim outlier-filtering trick and drop the triplet network.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2109.06625v1", "title": "Towards optimized actions in critical situations of soccer games with deep reinforcement learning", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Attack NFL critical situations with off-policy RL: Prong A \u2014 states (down, distance, yardline, score diff, time, timeouts, team strengths), behavior policy = historical coach decisions (nflverse 2009-2024), reward = Delta win probability; train off-policy policy-gradient with importance weights, evaluate with IS + doubly robust OPE on strictly held-out seasons (fixing the paper's in-sample OPE flaw), reporting ESS and max weight, and quantify 'coach mistakes' like the paper's player-mistake analysis; Prong B \u2014 a reusable OPE harness: given GSE's historical picks (actions), outcomes, and odds (behavior policy), evaluate any proposed pick-selection/staking policy via IS before deployment.", "gate": "Accept Prong A if held-out OPE shows >=0.5 wins/season gain over coaching behavior with effective sample size >50% of nominal (weights not degenerate) \u2014 and the learned policy's recommendations are interpretable (e.g., more aggressive on 4th-and-short in opponent territory). Reject if IS weights collapse or the policy just rediscovers 'always go for it' without situational nuance.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2109.07581v1", "title": "The Impact of COVID-19 on Sports Betting Markets", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Stand up a continuous market-efficiency monitor as engine-honesty infrastructure: compute alpha = -1 + mean(W/p) per league x market x rolling 4-week window on GSE's own pick/market history; alert when alpha > 0 with Wilcoxon p < 0.01 (a live 'market mispricing' detector); add hard-coded regime flags in the engine \u2014 neutral-site games, no/limited attendance, extreme weather, short-rest disruptions \u2014 that shrink the home-field-advantage prior and widen outcome uncertainty when active; report GSE's edge estimates per implied-probability band (replicating the paper's bin analysis); and run the alpha-monitor forward measuring detection latency before inefficiencies are arbitraged away. This monitors whether GSE's edges are real, never a profit objective.", "gate": "For GSE: gate is detecting alpha > 0 at 1% in any league x window before staking \u2014 the paper's +0.10-0.17 is the magnitude that justified real money (NBA COVID alpha = +0.17/+0.10 at 1% significance; inefficiency concentrated at implied 0.2-0.3; 16.7% flat-stake ROI).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2109.08051v1", "title": "Frame by Frame Completion Probability of an NFL Pass", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Reproduce the two-stage frame-by-frame completion pipeline in Python on Big Data Bowl tracking (2018-2024): Stage 1 target-ID via the paper's inverse-distance weighting; Stage 2 completion|target with the 32-feature set PLUS the missing pieces the authors flagged \u2014 receiver-talent priors (GSE's own receiver ratings), CB coverage grades, ball-height proxy, weather/wind \u2014 then add the missing z-dimension: estimate ball height from a projectile model fit to x/y + event tags (release point, catch point, airtime -> launch angle/height profile), testing height-aware features (ball height at closest approach vs receiver catch radius) on contested catches specifically (defender within 1 yard at arrival). Uses: live in-play completion probability, play-level EPA/WP features, and a CPOE-style QB metric.", "gate": "ADAPT if reproduction hits the Test 1 gates (target-ID accuracy >=85%, Stage-2 AUC >=0.85 on 2024 holdout) AND the talent-augmented model passes Test 2 (AUC gain >=+0.01 with calibration slope in [0.9, 1.1], and the CPOE-style metric correlates >=0.3 with next-season QB EPA/play).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2109.09287", "title": "Park Factor Estimation Improvement Using Pairwise Comparison Method", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build weather/stadium_factors.py: per-season logistic decomposition P(event | offense i, defense j, stadium k) = sigma(o_i - d_j - s_k) for events (TD, FG attempt/make, explosive play 10+ yds, punt) fit by penalized MLE with sum-to-zero identifiability constraints; output a per-stadium factor table s_k per event per season (Denver's FG-distance factor = the verified altitude coefficient; dome vs outdoor splits; wind-bowl stadiums) with year-to-year shrinkage, fed as features into the totals/spread engine \u2014 and re-estimate with time-varying team strengths (weekly random-walk state-space) to test whether static strengths leak mid-season form changes into the stadium terms (expectation: time-varying strengths shrink stadium factors toward zero but make the survivors \u2014 Denver, domes \u2014 more trustworthy).", "gate": "ADOPT the stadium-factor table if the full model beats both baselines by >= 0.003 log-loss on 2025 holdout AND neutral-event factors are ~= 0 (structural sanity) AND Denver's kicking/punting factor is positive and stable across >= 3 seasons.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2109.09871", "title": "Overinference from Weak Signals and Underinference from Strong Signals", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Build an in-game excess-movement monitor: for NFL live markets (spread/moneyline/total implied probs from a live odds feed), compute rolling movement M and uncertainty reduction R per quarter or 5-minute block; compute excess movement M - R; early game (Q1-Q2) fade moves (expect reversal \u2014 overinference), late game (Q4) follow moves (expect continuation \u2014 underinference), calibrating the crossover point on NFL data (the paper's NBA crossover ~= end of Q3; NFL's discrete scoring may shift it) \u2014 and condition on leverage: split game-minutes into high-leverage (within one possession) vs low-leverage, testing whether the over/underinference pattern scales with leverage-weighted signal strength rather than clock time; weight the live model's in-game market signals by leverage accordingly.", "gate": "ADAPT is confirmed if, on 2024 NFL in-play data, excess movement is significantly positive in Q1-Q2 and significantly negative in Q4 (t-test, p < 0.05), AND the fade-early/follow-late rule beats the baseline on CLV.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2109.10814v1", "title": "Fractional Growth Portfolio Investment", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Install variance-budgeted fractional Kelly: for each slate, (1) convert engine edges to per-pick full-Kelly fractions f_full; (2) estimate the slate portfolio's log-growth variance V(1) under f_full via the pick outcome model (or bootstrap of backtest residuals); (3) solve alpha = sqrt(V_target / V(1)) from the drawdown budget (e.g., max acceptable annualized SD); (4) stake alpha * f_full and report alpha alongside picks so the sizing is auditable, not a magic 'quarter' \u2014 then run the comparison on GSE's walk-forward picks (Neon picks, v5.2.7): fixed alpha = 0.25 vs variance-budgeted alpha_t recomputed per slate, scoring realized log-growth per unit of realized variance (expectation: alpha_t shrinks on correlated same-game slates and achieves a better realized growth/risk ratio).", "gate": "Replicated fractional-Kelly portfolio must satisfy: annualized SD in [0.16, 0.19], max drawdown in [38%, 46%], final wealth within 10% of $576,464 \u2014 i.e., reproduce the paper's risk profile, not just its return; then the variance-budgeted alpha must beat fixed alpha on realized growth/risk.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2109.10817v3", "title": "Causal Inference in Non-linear Time-series using Deep Networks and Knockoff Counterfactuals", "normalized_lane": "causal_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Stand up DeepAR-Knockoffs as the nonlinear causal-discovery arm: train ONE global DeepAR over all team-seasons pooled (team embeddings) on the nflverse team-week panel for next-week values of key indicators (EPA components, pressure rates); candidate causes = all indicators at lags 1-4; Gaussian knockoffs per indicator (deep knockoffs if non-Gaussianity is severe); CSS = ln(MAPE_with_knockoff / MAPE_baseline) per team-season with mean CSS > 0 (t-test, FDR-corrected) \u2014 then make it regime-conditioned: add the regime indicator (from ledger 1964's Gamma(t)) as a covariate and run knockoff counterfactuals within regimes, testing whether regime-conditioned knockoffs kill the Danube-style false links while preserving true nonlinear drivers on synthetic data with injected regime shifts.", "gate": "ADOPT DeepAR-Knockoffs as the nonlinear discovery arm if: (a) on synthetic nonlinear sports-like data it beats PCMCI+ParCorr F-score by >=0.1; (b) real-data link Jaccard across season splits >= 0.5; (c) the knockoff driver set improves or matches the 2024-2025 Brier of the PCMCI+-only driver set within 0.002 while adding >=5 nonlinear-only drivers.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2109.12990v1", "title": "Optimal Team Economic Decisions in Counter-Strike", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a Decision Quality Error (DQE) metric for NFL coaching decisions: restrict counterfactual substitution to game states with overlap (only decisions where both actual and candidate choices have adequate support \u2014 propensity-trimmed, fixing the paper's causal flaw); decision types: 4th-down go/kick, 2-point conversions, timeout usage, challenges; compute WP delta (optimal - actual) per occurrence, aggregate to a team-season DQE (mean, fixing the paper's sum/mean ambiguity); serve as an offseason coaching-decision report \u2014 then model decision sequences with a lightweight game-tree (2-3 plies: decision -> outcome distribution -> next decision point), valuing decisions by full expected-WP rather than myopic round-WP, testing whether tree-valued 4th-down decisions disagree with myopic valuations in >=10% of cases and have better cross-season stability.", "gate": "Adopt the DQE metric into the coaching-decision product iff the trimmed version achieves cross-season stability r >= 0.3 AND adds Delta R^2 >= 0.02 to next-season wins over the EPA/luck baseline on 2022-2024 data.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2109.13743v2", "title": "Dynamic Ranking with the BTL Model: A Nearest Neighbor based Rank Centrality Method", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Ship a GSE dynamic rating service on the spectral BTL method: per-week union graph over a trailing window, Rank Centrality eigenvector for team strengths, delta chosen by the paper's T^{2/3} rule tuned by LOOCV on GSE data; serve weekly strength + rank with the l-infinity bound as a published uncertainty envelope \u2014 then make delta adaptive: let the window shrink after detected regime changes (blowout losses, QB injury) and expand in stable periods (change-point-aware delta(t)), testing whether adaptive-delta beats fixed-delta* on rolling week-ahead log-likelihood. Engine-honesty infrastructure for fast, uncertainty-quantified ratings.", "gate": "ADAPT confirmed if DRC's week-ahead log-likelihood on 2024 NFL is within 0.005/game of GSE's current rating AND DRC rebuild time is >=3x faster. Speed parity alone justifies the port given the theory.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2109.14306", "title": "Three-Stream 3D/1D CNN for Fine-Grained Action Classification and Segmentation in Table Tennis", "normalized_lane": "sports_cv", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build PlayType-Fusion-GSE for fine-grained NFL action classification (RPO vs play-action vs dropback from All-22): the three-stream architecture \u2014 RGB clip cuboids, optical-flow cuboids (foreground-masked to players), 1D temporal convolutions over GSE's 2D skeleton streams, fused with bilinear layers, trained with the paper's warm-restart schedule; report trimmed-clip accuracy AND untrimmed detection/segmentation with and without negative segments \u2014 replacing the PoseNet descriptor with GSE's multi-person skeleton tracks (all 22 players) using a per-player attention-weighted aggregation before the 1D temporal convolutions, testing whether multi-agent pose input unlocks the segmentation gain on NFL film that the paper's single-pose stream couldn't reach for team sports.", "gate": "On GSE's own trimmed play-type clips, the three-stream model must beat the two-stream (RGB+flow) twin by >=3 points test accuracy AND beat pose-alone by >=40 points; detection+segmentation without negatives must improve >=10 points over the two-stream baseline.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2109.15046v2", "title": "An Elo-type rating model for players and teams of variable strength", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build a variance-aware Elo: per-team performance variance sigma_i^2(w) estimated weekly from (a) trailing 8-week variance of team EPA/play, (b) injury load (starters out / snap-weighted WAR lost), (c) QB-change indicator; update rule = standard Elo with expected score E = b(theta_i - theta_j) + 1/2 b''(theta_i - theta_j)(sigma_i^2 + sigma_j^2), b(z) = tanh(nu z) calibrated to NFL scale (start from FiveThirtyEight NFL Elo scale, shrink per the paper's (B')-style diagnostic) so injury-hit/high-variance teams' ratings shrink toward the mean automatically; serve weekly alongside the existing Elo and emit per-team sigma as an engine feature \u2014 then learn sigma_i^2 as a latent parameter in a hierarchical model from squared Elo residuals (Glicko-style, but for outcome variance) and publish the per-team sigma series as a GSE 'consistency rating'.", "gate": "Adopt if variance-corrected Elo beats standard Elo log-loss by >=0.5% overall on 2019-2025 rolling AND by >=1.5% on top-quartile-sigma team-weeks, with no weekly refit instability (max week-to-week rating swing <= 2x the baseline's).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2109.15239v1", "title": "Multi Scale Graph Wavenet for Wind Speed Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Reimplement Multi-Scale Graph Wavenet with NFL stadiums (or nearby mesonet stations) as graph nodes: initialize node embeddings from geographic/terrain features and let the adjacency learn; train on hourly wind speed/gust histories; forecast 6/12/18/24-hour horizons scored against persistence and a per-stadium AR baseline; feed the 24-hour-ahead stadium wind distributions into the totals model's weather features, inspecting the learned adjacency for physically sensible structure (coastal vs inland clusters) \u2014 then add exogenous NWP grid features as node inputs, learn a time-varying adjacency (frontal passage vs calm regimes), and extend the target to gust maxima and wind direction for kick-trajectory modeling.", "gate": "ADAPT: a learnable-adjacency spatiotemporal forecaster with a documented 4-5% SOTA margin is exactly the weather-forecasting asset GSE's totals lane is missing (acceptance = reproducing the margin on the Danish five-city data AND on 10+ US stadium-adjacent stations before engine integration).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2110.00637v4", "title": "ML4C: Seeing Causality Through Latent Vicinity", "normalized_lane": "causal_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add a supervised UT-orienter over the consensus skeleton from ledgers 1962-1966: discretize the ~35 team-season indicators into tertiles, synthesize 5000 football-plausible discrete DAGs (layered: game-context -> efficiency -> scoring -> outcome, 20-35 nodes, sparse) with varied edge densities and noise levels to blunt sample-bias, train the ML4C-Learner on UT labels, run the trained orienter on the consensus skeleton's UTs, apply Meek rules -> oriented CPDAG (edges left undirected stay undirected, the honest identifiability ceiling) \u2014 then build continuous ML4C: vicinity features from continuous CI-test statistics (partial correlation profiles, GPDC residuals) trained on continuous synthetic SEMs, to orient the PCMCI+ skeleton natively without the lossy discretization step.", "gate": "ADOPT the supervised orienter if: (a) held-out synthetic UT-F1 >= 0.8; (b) real-data orientation agreement across season splits >= 0.7; (c) >=80% of hand-labeled known colliders recovered (e.g., offensive EPA -> win <- defensive EPA); (d) adding orientations strictly improves the ledger-1967 quantitative-probing hit rate vs the unoriented skeleton.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2110.00864v1", "title": "Probabilistic Prediction for Binary Treatment Choice", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Frame the publish/bet decision as Manski's binary treatment choice: 'bet' (aggressive) vs 'pass' (surveillance) with utility = expected Kelly growth (or realized CLV); compute the maximum regret of the current as-if rule (bet iff edge > threshold) over a plausible interval [p_m, p_M] for the true probability calibrated from historical engine-vs-market disagreement; derive the MMR-optimal randomized threshold (the paper's q formula adapted) and the regret-optimal blended-probability rule (weighted-estimator logic, Table 1 style) \u2014 then extend past the paper's binary limit into GSE's real problem: portfolio regret \u2014 simultaneous correlated bets (spread + total + moneyline on the same game) formulated as a multi-decision minimax-regret problem with Kelly-growth utility, solved for the small-n case (2-3 simultaneous markets) by grid search over the joint disagreement region. Engine-honesty infrastructure for robust publish decisions, not an edge objective.", "gate": "Adopt the MMR threshold policy iff, on the 2024 holdout season, it achieves realized P&L >= 90% of the current policy's P&L AND its worst-decile (by pre-game disagreement) regret is <= 0.7x the current policy's \u2014 i.e., it buys robustness without giving up the edge.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2110.01527v1", "title": "A Markov process approach to untangling intention versus execution in tennis", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build the NFL intention-vs-execution MRP: state = (down, distance, yard line, score differential, time) x personnel/formation; intentions = play-call categories (or finer: route concepts, run gaps); execution distribution = play-level outcome noise decomposed into components (QB placement error a la ledger 0391, drops, protection breakdowns) estimated from nflverse + charting; build the MRP for the empirical play-calling policy (value = win probability / expected points from each state) plus epsilon-scaled execution variants to answer 'how much of this team's red-zone underperformance is play-calling vs execution?'; n-greedy rollout for decision analysis \u2014 then build the two-sided model the authors defer: offense chooses intentions to maximize value while the defense simultaneously chooses coverages/blitzes (a stochastic game, not MDP-vs-fixed-policy), solved for equilibrium strategies as a function of offensive execution error epsilon \u2014 the output being an execution-error-conditioned game-theoretic play-calling chart. Standing rule: never present simulation-based value decompositions as measurements of real players without the section-12 WP-agreement validation.", "gate": "ACCEPT as ADAPT. Standing gate: the MRP-implied state values must match nflverse empirical WP (the section-12 WP-agreement validation). If the NFL port's MRP cannot reproduce empirical WP, demote to REJECT (tennis-specific curiosity).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2110.03874", "title": "Uncertainty Quantification in the Bradley-Terry-Luce Model", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add the SE/CI machinery as post-processing on GSE's BT/Elo ratings: rolling 3-season window BT-MLE with centering constraint 1^T theta = 0 (LBFGS on l_n(theta), eq. 2.3; n=32 so trivial compute), an explicit HFA term h estimated jointly (fold into features before the BT fit if needed), exponential recency weights (the paper assumes static theta*, so windowing is the stationarity hack); emit per-game win-probability point estimates plus 90% CIs from the paper's asymptotic SEs; add an abstention policy (skip games where the CI covers 0.5) \u2014 then test a time-varying variant: exponentially decayed pseudo-counts inside the likelihood itself (game (i,j) at lag t weighted by lambda^t, lambda in {0.90, 0.95, 0.98}) with decay-weighted rho_i^{(lambda)} for the SEs, hypothesizing the decay-weighted fit tracks in-season strength changes (injuries, QB swaps) faster so its CIs stay calibrated late-season.", "gate": "ADOPT the SE/CI machinery if, on the 2024-2025 test window: (i) empirical coverage of the 90% win-probability CIs falls in [87%, 93%] overall AND within +-4pp of 90% in at least 8 of 10 predicted-probability deciles; and (ii) the abstention policy (skip CI-covers-0.5 games) achieves Brier >= 0.005 better than the always-bet BT baseline on the games it does bet.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2110.05750", "title": "SportsSum2.0: Generating High-Quality Sports News from Live Text Commentary", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Adapt the three-step SportsSum2.0 pipeline to NFL English text streams: (a) pseudo-label beat-writer articles to play-by-play/injury-report sentences using the S = lambda*BERTScore + (1-lambda)*ROUGE recipe inside timestamp windows; (b) train a context-aware selector (RoBERTa/DeBERTa) over rolling windows of X posts/articles to extract signal sentences; (c) rewrite with a modern seq2seq LLM and rerank with fluency-aware MMR (perplexity from the LLM itself) to assemble daily NFL recap briefs, injury digest posts, or @GalaxySportsHQ content drafts; budget = target post length.", "gate": "ACCEPTED (ADAPT): clean public dataset + reproduced SOTA + ablations isolating all three contributions. NFL-port gate: the selector's recall on pseudo-labeled NFL sentences must match the paper's ordering (selector + rewrite + MMR rerank beats each ablated variant).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2110.10914v1", "title": "An Empirical Evaluation of Time-Series Feature Sets", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add an auto-feature block on rolling windows of per-team EPA/play, success rate, dropback/rush EPA series (nflverse 2009-2026): pycatch22 (22 features, ~ms) on 8-game and full-season windows, offline tsfresh (efficient, FFT groups) on the same windows, PCA/correlation prune at |rho|>0.9, then stability selection keeping features selected in >=4 of the last 6 seasons into the LightGBM ATS model \u2014 plus a directed-overlap S(T|B) audit quantifying which auto features are genuinely new information vs rediscoveries of GSE's hand-built library.", "gate": "Adopt the catch22 rolling-window auto-feature block iff it improves walk-forward log-loss by >=0.003 on the held-out 2025 season vs the hand-built baseline, with no leakage (verified by lag audit) and feature-importance stability across >=4 of 6 seasons; reject the tsfresh block unless its FFT features add >=0.005 log-loss on top of catch22+baseline.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2110.13561v1", "title": "Non-Gaussian Gaussian Processes for Few-Shot Regression", "normalized_lane": "metalearning_fewshot", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a few-shot new-regime module: meta-train a deep-kernel GP (NN Linear h_phi over team context: roster continuity, QB embedding, coaching tenure, Vegas-implied strength) + per-observation FFJORD flow (non-Gaussian NGGP) on 2015-2022 team-season tasks; at serving time, condition the flow-conditioned GP posterior on the first K=2-4 games of a new regime (rookie QB starts, new HC first 4 games) and serve posterior predictive mean for next-game EPA margin; use a task-conditioned hypernetwork beta=H(context) instead of shared flow parameters if rookie/veteran noise geometries differ.", "gate": "ADOPT into the new-regime module iff few-shot adapted NGGP beats the league-average prior by >=0.01 Brier on new-regime teams' first 4 games, averaged over 2023-2025 leave-one-season-out meta-tests, AND beats the no-flow DKT ablation on NLL.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2110.14632v1", "title": "Heterogeneous Effects of Software Patches in a Multiplayer Online Battle Arena Game", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build a causal-tree HTE module for rule changes: treated = 2024-2025 (2024 dynamic kickoff rule), control = 2022-2023, unit = team-game special-teams EPA outcomes; causal trees (Tran-Zheleva, or causal forest/GRF for honest CIs) on NFL analogs of the paper's skill proxies (pre-intervention ST EPA, returner speed, touchback rate, coach tenure) to find which team archetypes the rule shift helped/hurt most, keeping only subgroups selected in >=70% of bootstraps for stability.", "gate": "Adopt iff on the 2022-2024 fit: (a) >=2 leaves significant at 5% with |tau-hat| >= 0.5 EPA/game, (b) max-leaf |tau-hat| >= 2x the naive pre/post ATE, (c) top-3 split features stable on the 2025 holdout; reject if tree structure flips between fit and holdout windows.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2111.02358", "title": "VLMo: Unified Vision-Language Pre-Training with Mixture-of-Modality-Experts", "normalized_lane": "multimodal_fusion", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a single GSE multimodal Transformer with modality experts \u2014 T-FFN (tracking), V-FFN (video), L-FFN (text) with shared attention: stage-1 pretrain tracking expert on Big Data Bowl masked trajectories, stage-2 pretrain text expert on nflverse/injury-report text via MLM, stage-3 joint tracking-text contrastive+matching training; dual-encoder mode for historical-play retrieval, fusion-encoder mode feeding the engine \u2014 with a learned per-token expert router (replacing the paper's hard-coded expert assignment) so the model decides fusion depth per play.", "gate": "ACCEPT iff the VLMo-style model beats the single-space joint model by >=3 points Recall@10 on text->play retrieval AND its fusion-mode EPA MAE beats the tracking-only baseline by >=2% on held-out seasons; reject if no retrieval gain (MoME complexity unjustified) or no EPA gain.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2111.02859v3", "title": "Large Scale Diverse Combinatorial Optimization: ESPN Fantasy Football Player Trades", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Add boom ratio (P(weekly score > 85th pct of position)) and bust ratio (P(<15th pct)) as standard player descriptors in the DFS feature set from 3-season rolling nflverse game logs; reformulate the DK optimizer as a cost-constrained knapsack maximizing sum(projection) subject to salary cap AND sum(bust_ratio) <= tau; learn the risk scalar alpha as a function of contest payout structure (top-heavy GPP -> more boom exposure, cash -> lower alpha).", "gate": "ADAPT the boom/bust descriptors + cost-constrained knapsack if bust-constrained lineups match the current optimizer's mean score within 2% AND improve top-1% tail hit rate by >=15% relative on a 6-week holdout (GPP relevance).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2111.02874v1", "title": "Deep Artificial Intelligence for Fantasy Football Language Understanding", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Stand up the fantasy-news NLP pilot: ingest ~500 beat-writer RSS/X lists/podcast transcripts, NER for players/teams/injuries, calibrated classifier heads for the four fixed-definition labels (boom/bust/injury-out/sit) trained with proper scoring rules + isotonic recalibration, then blend calibrated probabilities (not hard labels) as a shrinkage prior into GSE projections; evaluate on full 2025-season RMSE backtest.", "gate": "ADOPT into production iff the combined projections beat GSE's baseline RMSE on the full 2025 backtest with p<0.05 (paired Diebold-Mariano); REJECT if the NLP adjustment is directionally inconsistent (worse RMSE like the paper's 6.92) or label precision doesn't exceed base rates.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2111.08140v1", "title": "Bayesian inference of the climbing grade scale", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace fixed-scale Elo in the ratings lane with a dynamic whole-history BT logistic model on nflverse 2015-2025: weekly team strengths follow a Wiener process (Stan, ported from the paper's skeleton), with the rating-scale slope m co-estimated each season (so 'a 100-point gap means X win probability' is recalibrated, not asserted) plus opponent-uncertainty hierarchical error and per-game weather/rest covariates; the learned slope stability across seasons is itself a reported calibration metric.", "gate": "Adopt iff the Wiener-drift + learned-slope model beats fixed-scale Elo log-loss by >=1.0% on the 2024-2025 rolling window AND the learned slope m-hat is stable across seasons (coefficient of variation <= 10%); reject and keep the simpler dynamic-Elo lane otherwise.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2111.08230v1", "title": "Selective Ensembles for Consistent Predictions", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Publish the majority pick from n=10-15 seed-varied models only when the binomial p-value for the majority share clears alpha (tune alpha to GSE's target publish volume); otherwise withhold as 'model disagreement'; two-key gate with the learned-abstention heads (publish only if both predict) or run as independent A/B lanes; optionally calibrate alpha seasonally or replace the binary gate with a margin-graded stake tier if vote margin is monotone in hit rate.", "gate": "ADAPT iff the binomial-gated ensemble beats plain majority vote on test-window covered-set ROI by >=2pp with abstention <=35%; reject if abstention explodes or the gate adds nothing over plain voting.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2111.09695v1", "title": "Features selection in NBA outcome prediction through Deep Learning", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Run a GSE feature-selection audit per league: horse race of single strength-summary features (dynamic Elo K~=30, HFA~=40, 20% offseason regression; win frequency; net rating) vs rich box-score feature sets under strict walk-forward protocol; encode the winner as the default feature set (NBA prior: start from dynamic Elo, not box-score); also test Elo + Four-Factors differentials as a hybrid.", "gate": "ADAPT (weak) confirmed iff under strict walk-forward, Elo-based features match or beat Four-Factors features on AUC (difference >= -0.005 tolerated given the paper's pooled-CV inflation); if Four Factors win walk-forward, the paper's finding is a CV artifact \u2014 keep the audit harness.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2111.12429v2", "title": "tsflex: Flexible Time Series Processing & Feature Extraction", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt tsflex as the feature-extraction backbone: register catch22 (via pycatch22, 8-game window stride 1) and custom gse-lab metrics (4/8/17-game windows) in one FeatureCollection over game-date-indexed series with bye-week gaps; SeriesPipeline for cleaning (dedupe, gap marking, odds alignment); replace ad-hoc rolling loops in the gse-lab build scripts with the serialized collection \u2014 then exploit multi-window registration in one pass to build a scale-space feature tensor with learned per-scale attention in the meta-learner.", "gate": "Adopt iff the reproducibility test passes all three criteria: exact numerical match (1e-9) with hand-rolled features, >=2x speedup on the full 32-team rebuild, correct gap handling \u2014 AND the pinned version's API supports multi-window registration, serialization, multiprocessing without workarounds.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2111.12535", "title": "Knowledge Enhanced Sports Game Summarization", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt KES to English NFL content: build the knowledge corpus (32 teams + ~1700 active players as structured cards: bio, contract, season stats, injury history), NER + entity linking over game rosters, inject knowledge via z_seg/z_know embedding fusion into the seq2seq generator \u2014 adding the missing faithfulness guard the paper lacked: entailment-check every injected fact against its knowledge card before emission.", "gate": "ACCEPTED (ADAPT): largest human-cleaned dataset of its kind + quantified knowledge gap + ablated knowledge-fusion method. NFL-port gate: recaps with knowledge fusion rated more informative than the knowledge-blind baseline with zero entailed-fact errors on a 50-game sample.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2111.15365", "title": "Expert Aggregation for Financial Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Stand up a weekly BOA (Bernstein Online Aggregation) consensus layer over the K engine sub-models: each Tuesday update simplex weights via the BOA rule with the second-order correction on realized weekly losses, publish the weighted consensus as the week's official forecast; run separate aggregations for favorites vs underdogs; add regime-conditional parallel BOA instances (early season/midseason/playoff push, high-vs-low totals) under a meta-BOA for faster adaptation at regime boundaries.", "gate": "ADOPT iff on 2024-2025 the BOA consensus beats the static equal-weight baseline by >=1.5% relative Brier AND the Kelly-staked max drawdown is <=70% of the best single expert's (the paper's tail-risk signature), with week-to-week weight churn not exceeding 2x the uniform baseline's.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2112.01267v1", "title": "Bradley-Terry Modeling with Multiple Game Outcomes with Applications to College Hockey", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a four-bucket margin BT team-strength module on nflverse 2015-2025: outcomes {win by >=14, win 1-13, loss 1-13, loss >=14} with the ordered strength exponents fit as free parameters (prior support p_OW in (1/2,1), season-varying tau for overtime/close-game rates under post-2022 OT rules) instead of fixed 2/3-1/3, Gaussian hierarchical season-to-season prior on lambda_i, explicit HFA term; used for coherent alt-spread/total fair pricing.", "gate": "Adopt iff the four-bucket model beats standard BT log-loss by >=1.0% and beats the market baseline by >=0.25% on the 2024-2025 rolling window, with bucket coverage within 1.5pp per bucket.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2112.06751", "title": "Role of Human-AI Interaction in Selective Prediction", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Implement the deferral-budget abstention rule in the daily pick workflow: choose score thresholds solving max historical accuracy subject to deferral rate <= r (r = daily-card budget), grid-search the accuracy-deferral curve on backtested engine scores; keep r an explicit auditable parameter; and adopt the SPM experiment's messaging rule for the human-review step \u2014 blind DO-style review (status only, no engine lean) to avoid the anchoring penalty the BM-style arm shows, then replicate the DO/BM experiment on GSE's own analysts.", "gate": "ADAPT: the deferral-budget optimization is a ready abstention policy (explicit, auditable r), and the SPM experiment gives an evidence-backed messaging rule for human review. Not ADOPT: anchoring magnitudes come from lay image-labelers; the internal replication decides standing doctrine.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2112.07002", "title": "Optimizing the Expected Maximum of Two Linear Functions Defined on a Multivariate Gaussian Distribution", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add an E[max] duel optimizer for 2-entry Showdown: closed-form E[max] objective over (mu1, mu2, sigma1, sigma2, rho) from GSE projections/variances/game-script stacking correlations, solved via cutting-plane/MINLP; then extend to n-entry portfolios via greedy sequential optimization with moment-matched Gaussian conditioning of the running max \u2014 benchmarked against the SAA approach on 20-entry Showdown portfolios.", "gate": "Adopt iff on 2024 Showdown backtests the exact 2-entry method's realized best-entry score beats the top-2-EV baseline by >=2.0 points on average across >=20 contests AND simulated E[max] improvement is >=4.0 points; reject if the Gaussian assumption systematically misses high-variance captain plays.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2112.11262v1", "title": "Retrodictive Modelling of Modern Rugby Union: Extension of Bradley-Terry to Multiple Outcomes", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Build a GSE ordinal rating model for NFL: outcome bands (win by 10+, win 1-9, loss bands) + totals bands using the p ~ pi_i^a pi_j^b MaxEnt form with shared team strengths, notional-games prior (weight tuned, start at 4), home advantage term, fit via Poisson log-linear GLM; first application is alternative-spread/total fair pricing (coherent probabilities across all bands); then test learned band scores vs fixed scores.", "gate": "ADAPT confirmed iff the NFL ordinal model's held-out (2025 walk-forward) log-likelihood beats plain binary-BT by >=0.01 per game AND band probabilities are calibrated (reliability slope 0.9-1.1); even matching binary BT justifies the build for coherent alt-line pricing.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2112.13001v3", "title": "Forecasting number of corner kicks taken in association football using compound Poisson distribution", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Port the cross-market extractor: de-vigged moneyline + spread + total odds per game, fit a bivariate normal on (home margin, total) via L-BFGS-B to recover market-implied expected total/spread-implied supremacy as covariates; build Bayesian DCP prop models in Stan (geometric-Poisson or NB for team count props: sacks taken, explosive plays, red-zone trips; rate eq with TG/SUP + last-3 averages + opponent adjustments; shape regression on |SUP|); compare elpd_loo, and also fit the CMP-GLM (two links) the authors mention but never fit \u2014 for underdispersed counts like team punts the DCP family cannot represent.", "gate": "ADOPT the DCP prop framework iff the geometric-Poisson/NB model beats naive Poisson by elpd_loo with se_diff >= 3 on 2024 rushing-attempt counts AND the positive-EV simulation shows Sharpe >= 1.0 over >=100 bets; REJECT as a framework if the Poisson is within se_diff < 1 with a flat/negative betting sim.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2112.13593v5", "title": "Multi-modal Attention Network for Stock Movements Prediction", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a credibility-weighted analyst-text fusion for closing-line direction: per NFL game, encode X posts from inventoried analyst accounts with a sentence transformer, compute per-poster credibility from GSE's verification data (historical pick accuracy, CLV of past calls), fuse text embeddings with numeric line-movement features (open->current deltas, steam flags) via credibility-gated cross-attention, with time-to-kickoff positional encoding.", "gate": "Full-model 61.20% accuracy / MCC 0.1193 vs CapTE 59.87% / 0.0976, credibility ablation +1.14pp (60.06% -> 61.20%): ADOPT only if the credibility-weighting ablation reproduces on walk-forward NFL data; do not adopt if it doesn't.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2112.14451v1", "title": "Dynamic growth-optimum portfolio choice under risk control", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Install a Kelly-with-tail-governor: each slate, start from full-Kelly fractions from engine edges, Monte-Carlo the slate portfolio log-return distribution under the pick outcome model, compute ES_alpha; if ES_alpha exceeds the bankroll risk budget, shrink all fractions by scalar s in (0,1) (the paper's interior solution as a convex mixture of growth-optimal and min-risk wealth); run the governor on GSE's walk-forward picks (Neon picks, v5.2.7) comparing fixed quarter-Kelly vs ES-governed Kelly (alpha=0.95, ES budget = 15% bankroll log-return), and pick the operating alpha by the measured exchange rate (growth given up per unit ES reduced).", "gate": "The replicated mean-ES frontier must be (a) concave, (b) anchored at the growth-optimal endpoint with max expected log-return and max ES, (c) terminating at a finite min-ES point, (d) shifting left (weakly lower ES at fixed expected log-return) as alpha goes 0.9 -> 0.99.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2112.14649v1", "title": "Tired of Misattribution, Modeling Player Fatigue in the NBA", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Add fatigue-feature priors with a short leash to the NBA model: rest-differential, westward-travel-hours, and 3-in-4 indicators with the paper's coefficients (+0.35/-1.740/-1.290) as wide-variance Bayesian priors, re-estimated leakage-free (pre-game ratings, not end-of-season net rating), kept only if they improve rolling-origin log-loss/Brier on >=2 held-out seasons \u2014 otherwise retained as null-result documentation ('schedule explains <0.1%'); any future fatigue claim (including tracking-based load) must beat this null bar.", "gate": "ADAPT iff the re-estimated (leakage-free) fatigue features improve the NBA game model on rolling-origin log-loss or Brier on at least two held-out seasons; if they don't move out-of-sample prediction, keep only the null prior as documentation.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2112.14846", "title": "An Analysis of an Alternative Pythagorean Expected Win Percentage Model: Applications Using Major League Baseball Team Quality Simulations", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Fit both win-expectancy forms on NFL team-seasons (nflverse 2000-2025, 17-game): Tullock PF^alpha/(PF^alpha+PA^alpha) vs difference-form 1/(1+e^{alpha(PA-PF)}), both by fractional logit (not the paper's OLS hack), SOS-adjusted; adopt the winner as the expected-win% feature for luck decomposition and the early-season rating prior \u2014 then extend the winning form to game level: EWP = 1/(1+e^{-(alpha*PD + beta*HFA + gamma*rest_edge)}) fit directly on game outcomes, since ratio forms blow up on shutouts at game level.", "gate": "Adopt the difference-form CSF as the win-expectancy function iff it beats the Tullock form on out-of-sample RMSE by >=0.005 win-proportion points on 2020-2024 team-seasons AND wins the 4-game rolling-window stress test (lower RMSE in >=60% of windows); reject (keep ratio-form/empirical) otherwise.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2201.01168v1", "title": "Application of the Pythagorean Expected Wins Percentage and Cross-Validation Methods in Estimating Team Quality", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Fit all three CSF forms (Tullock, difference, serial) on NFL points-for/points-against (2015-2024, 320 team-seasons) by OLS alpha and compare LOOCV RMSE vs GSE's current Pythagorean exponent; if the serial form wins, replace the exponent form in the ratings prior and test the serial form on per-game spread residuals as a 'luck' (actual minus expected wins) regression-to-mean feature.", "gate": "Adopt the serial CSF iff on 2015-2024 NFL data its LOOCV win-RMSE beats optimized Tullock by >=0.2 wins with p<0.05; keep Tullock otherwise; reconsider only with a hierarchical version pooling alpha across teams.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2201.03387v2", "title": "Adaptive strategies in Kelly's horse races model", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add Kelly burn-in + Laplace-smoothed edges: shrink raw model probabilities toward market-implied probabilities p-hat = (n*p_model + tau*p_market)/(n+tau) (bookmaker prior), gate full-Kelly staking on t > t-star = (M-1)/(2*D_KL(p-hat||r)) and use fractional Kelly before that; tune the tau schedule on backtests (larger tau early season, decaying as sample n grows) and measure the crossover where shrunk-Kelly ties raw-Kelly asymptotically.", "gate": "The fitted logarithmic regret coefficient must satisfy |a - 4.5| <= 0.5 and mean log-capital must track D_KL(p||r)*t - 4.5*log t within Monte Carlo error (+-1 std over 200 runs) for t >= 1000.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2201.04480v2", "title": "Learning to Identify Top Elo Ratings: A Dueling Bandits Approach", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Use the MaxIn dueling-bandit scheduler as GSE's evaluation-budget scheduler (not for real scheduling \u2014 the NFL schedule is fixed): when fitting team-strength ratings under a compute budget (Monte Carlo sims, engine-config comparisons), replace uniform matchup sampling with MaxIn scheduling \u2014 maintain V_t over the 32x32 team-pair space, keep a UCB candidate set of playoff-relevant teams, spend simulation budget on the most informative matchups; then test a contextual non-stationary variant (team-game feature vectors, forgetting factor) on strictly time-forward 2021-2025 prediction.", "gate": "Synthetic test: ADOPT/ADAPT the scheduler iff MaxIn-Elo reaches RR=1 with >=30% fewer rounds than random-sampling Elo, with cumulative regret at T=1000 at most 60% of baseline, in >=4 of 5 seeds; real-data pilot: accept iff MaxIn-scheduled ratings match baseline top-4 identification accuracy vs end-of-season futures-implied rankings in >=3 of 5 seasons.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2201.05249", "title": "An Empirical Study of Least Squares Ratings for USA Ultimate Frisbee", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Reproduce least-squares ratings on NFL 2019-2023 walk-forward: weekly LS ratings on point differentials, spread predictions = rating differential + home adjustment, compared against GSE's Elo spread predictions on MAE and ranking-violation rate; then extend past the paper's future-work pointer to weighted/generalized least squares \u2014 per-game variance as a function of rest, travel, rating uncertainty, week of season \u2014 testing whether WLS spread-MAE beats OLS by >=0.05 points, plus an L1 (least-absolute-deviation) variant robust to garbage-time blowouts.", "gate": "LS spread-MAE must be <= GSE Elo spread-MAE + 0.1 points AND LS ranking-violation rate <= Elo's violation rate on the 2019-2023 walk-forward test; if it fails, keep LS only as a diagnostic baseline.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2201.08671", "title": "Random Noise vs State-of-the-Art Probabilistic Forecasting Methods", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Ban CRPS-Sum (and any sum-inside-score metric) from GSE model selection for joint forecasts (spread+total distributions, correlated slates); use mean per-dimension CRPS + Energy Score \u2014 and institute the dummy-model discrimination test as a CI gate: every new evaluation metric must rank a known-good forecaster above (a) a marginal-matched noise forecaster and (b) a constant forecaster on backtest, or the metric is rejected; extend the protocol to economic metrics (can a degenerate always-bet-the-favorite strategy game the ROI metric?).", "gate": "ADOPT the guardrail iff the reproduction confirms CRPS-Sum can misrank on GSE's own joint forecasts (dummy beats or ties the real model under CRPS-Sum while losing under Energy Score); if it ranks correctly on GSE data, still adopt the ban as prophylaxis with the dummy test as an advisory check.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2202.00211v3", "title": "GNNRank: Learning Global Rankings from Pairwise Comparisons via Directed Graph Neural Networks", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port the transferable GNNRank components: per-week directed team matchup graph (nodes = 32 teams, edges = games through week w, weights = point/EPA differential), DIMPA-style directed GNN embeddings (d=32-64) with rest/QB node side-information, 'dist' readout, then unrolled proximal Fiedler refinement \u2014 trained with a supervised time-forward objective (backprop through the proximal steps to minimize next-week predictive log-loss) instead of the paper's in-sample upset reconstruction, benchmarked against dynamic Elo / state-space posterior.", "gate": "ADOPT iff ALL hold on the 2024-2025 test window: (1) calibrated win-prob log-loss beats the better of dynamic Elo/state-space by >=0.005 nats/game; (2) Brier improves by >=0.002; (3) ATS cover >=52.4% with n>=500 picks; (4) ECE within 0.01 of baseline.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2202.00583v1", "title": "A Statistical Model of Serve Return Impact Patterns in Professional Tennis", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build latent style allocation on NGS tracking spatial summaries (start: WR route endpoints/catch-point locations): K,M in 2..8 grid via ELPD, covariates = down/distance/formation/man-zone, player offsets eta (receiver) and delta (defender) \u2014 descriptive validity via ELPD vs finite-mixture baselines on 2024, predictive value via receiver style-membership improving completion-probability log-loss; then make styles dynamic (HMM layer over styles within a game) and defender-specific to capture in-game tendency shifts.", "gate": "ADOPT tracking archetypes as features iff BOTH: (a) ELPD gain over finite mixture replicates (>=2%) on 2024 NGS data, AND (b) style features improve completion-probability log-loss by >=1% on 2024; reject as engine features if (b) fails (keep as content/visualization only).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2202.00769v1", "title": "Distributional Reinforcement Learning with Regularized Wasserstein Loss", "normalized_lane": "rl_sequential_decisions", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the joint-distribution staking policy (SinkhornDRL): weekly state from logged picks/odds, action = stake grid, critic outputs N=32 samples of the 3-dim return vector (settled profit, -max intra-week drawdown, mean CLV) with Sinkhorn divergence to the vector Bellman target; scalarize at decision time with a tunable risk price (e.g., maximize E[profit] - 2*E[drawdown] + 0.5*E[CLV]) \u2014 then learn the risk price itself as a contextual bandit over the season (meta-action from bankroll state, trained to end-of-season Sharpe).", "gate": "ADOPT iff on 2024 the joint policy Pareto-dominates the best scalar policy on >=2 of {ROI, max drawdown, CLV} with the third no worse than -5% relative; otherwise REJECT (compute not justified for a scalar-equivalent result).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2202.02691v1", "title": "TTS-GAN: Transformer-based Time-Series GAN", "normalized_lane": "synthetic_data", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Adopt conditional TTS-GAN for bulk trajectory augmentation: 32-team x 18-week x K-metric panel (nflverse 2015-2024), regime class-embedding (home favorite/dog, divisional, dome, altitude, short-week) on noise + discriminator patches, 3-block transformer encoder G/D, LSGAN losses \u2014 single conditional model instead of per-class models, TSTR-driven early stopping (checkpoint maximizing synthetic-trained probe classifier's real-data accuracy), throughput >=100 trajectories/second/GPU.", "gate": "ADOPT iff: (a) it matches/beats Time-GAN on >=7/10 of the paper's fidelity comparisons on NFL data, (b) TSTR AUC >= 90% of real-trained AUC on held-out seasons, (c) real+synthetic spread log-loss beats real-only by >=0.003, (d) throughput >=100 trajectories/sec on one GPU.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2202.03034", "title": "Modeling the bounce of a gas-filled ball", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Add weather/ball_physics.py: implement epsilon(T) (restitution coefficient vs temperature) anchored at regulation 12.5-13.5 psi at 70F, convert game-day temperature to pressure drop via the ideal gas law then to delta-epsilon, and map to kickoff/punt touchback-rate and fumble adjustments \u2014 then fit the lambda parameters from broadcast data: below-32F vs matched above-50F games (2020-2024) to produce a proprietary cold-weather ball-effects table (pressure drop -> epsilon drop -> touchback/fumble adjustments).", "gate": "ADOPT the epsilon(T) adjustment iff predicted delta-epsilon explains residual touchback variance with the correct sign at p < 0.05 on the 2024 holdout; either way keep the ideal-gas-law pressure correction (that's just physics).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2202.08500", "title": "Causal inference with recurrent and competing events", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Stand up the recurrent/competing-events estimand taxonomy for injury analysis: total vs controlled-direct effect of high acute:chronic workload weeks on recurrent soft-tissue injury counts per player-season, with season-ending IR as the competing event (nflverse injury + snap-count workload 2018-2024); discrete-time g-formula/IPW vs a naive censor-at-IR analysis to show the estimand gap; positivity check via weight truncation [0.1, 10].", "gate": "ADAPT iff the NFL replication shows the naive censor-at-IR estimate and the IPW total effect differ by >=20% (competing-event distinction matters empirically) with identified positivity (no weight truncation beyond [0.1,10] needed for >95% of player-weeks); REJECT the full machinery if the difference is <10% \u2014 keep only the taxonomy as a reporting standard.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2202.09481v2", "title": "TransDreamer: Reinforcement Learning with Transformer World Models", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Fold a transformer-state-space model (TSSM) into GSE-Dream as a backbone variant: transformer over past latent states + play descriptors (replacing the GRU transition), myopic posterior per play (no recurrent encoder \u2014 parallelizes over full game sequences), DreamerV3 categorical latents, attention conditioned on a persistent matchup embedding \u2014 plus sparse/dilated attention (full within-drive, sparse to prior-drive summary tokens) to hold near-RSSM throughput.", "gate": "ADOPT TSSM iff on the 2024 long-context probe it beats the RSSM by >=10% (log-likelihood of 2nd-half outcomes given 1st-half context) AND stays within 2x of RSSM sampling throughput; REJECT if throughput collapses (>4x slower per 100k-game batch) or the gain is <5%.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2202.10085v2", "title": "Bettors' Reaction to Match Dynamics \u2014 Evidence from In-Game Betting", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Build the in-play market-sentiment monitor: Betfair Exchange NFL in-play volume per minute as target, per-drive EPA differentials as the 'momentum' signal (NFL's discrete analogue of VAEP), pre-game vig-adjusted probabilities + live WP + score diff, AR(1) sentiment state g_t with P-spline time-varying coefficients; serving = one-step-ahead relative-volume forecast and a momentum-divergence flag (market live prob vs GSE prob) \u2014 drive-level momentum vs minute-level tested head-to-head.", "gate": "ADAPT iff on 2024: (a) the momentum-SSM beats the no-momentum SSM on per-game log-likelihood with the second-half beta_t effect replicating the paper's shape, AND (b) the momentum-divergence rule produces positive CLV, or (c) the one-step-ahead relative-volume forecast improves RMSE by >=15%.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2202.11834", "title": "Comparison of Combination Methods to Create Calibrated Ensemble Forecasts for Seasonal Influenza in the U.S.", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add a Beta Linear Pool (BLP) post-processing layer on the engine's linear-pool consensus: per-market (spread/total/moneyline) estimate (alpha, beta) by MLE on log score over past seasons, publish B_{alpha,beta}(F_LP(y)) as the calibrated forecast \u2014 with shrinkage-regularized estimation (penalized MLE toward identity, lambda by leave-one-season-out CV) and separate (alpha,beta) for high-vs-low total regimes, attacking the paper's under-prediction pathology.", "gate": "ADOPT iff on the 2025 holdout it improves mean log score over the weight-optimized LP by >=0.02 AND its PIT Cramer distance is <= LP's (no calibration regression), with no systematic under-prediction (PIT CDF within +-0.05 of diagonal at all deciles).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2203.01420v1", "title": "Minimax Decision Rules for Planning Under Uncertainty", "normalized_lane": "uncertainty_decision_theory", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt median-world (or trimmed-mean/top-k-dropped) regret aggregation for GSE's policy computation instead of max-world regret: generate scenario worlds via a fixed, versioned, seeded bootstrap protocol (no hand-added/removed worlds without a logged amendment), compute policies under median regret with a 75th-percentile compromise variant; monthly leave-one-world-out sensitivity audit \u2014 if dropping one world flips >20% of the policy table, flag as scenario-fragile and fall back; plus an adversarial red-team search for the world that maximally flips the policy, then harden against it.", "gate": "ACCEPT iff: the injection experiment confirms scenario sensitivity is real for GSE's world set (flip rate >20% under max-regret) AND median-regret cuts it by >=50% AND backtested worst-world regret is within 10% of max-regret's; REJECT if median-regret sacrifices >15% of worst-world protection.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2203.03003v1", "title": "Offline Deep Reinforcement Learning for Dynamic Pricing of Consumer Credit", "normalized_lane": "rl_sequential_decisions", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the offline-CQL staking policy on GSE's logged picks/odds: state = per-bet feature vector (edge, de-vigged fair odds, market odds, CLV history, book, day-of-week, slate size, bankroll fraction), action = stake in {0, 0.25u, 0.5u, 1u, 2u}, reward = settled profit; train on 2021-2023, evaluate on realized 2024 settlement (stronger than the paper's model-only eval) plus sensitivity re-scoring under 3 alternative outcome models; trust-region constraint: stake MAPD vs historical fractional-Kelly <= 25%; then extend to sequential CQL with bankroll in state and log-bankroll-growth reward to capture stake-smoothing.", "gate": "ADOPT iff on realized 2024 settlement the CQL staking policy beats fractional-Kelly ROI by >=2pp with stake MAPD <= 25% AND the sensitivity re-scoring keeps the sign of the lift under all 3 outcome models; REJECT if the lift vanishes under alternative evaluators.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2203.03279v3", "title": "Evaluating State of the Art, Forecasting Ensembles- and Meta-learning Strategies for Model Fusion", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build three fusion candidates over GSE's constituent model probabilities per game/market: (a) FFORMA-style LightGBM meta-learner on game meta-features (spread bucket, total, market disagreement, ATS form volatility, rest, weather) with weighted log-loss objective -> softmax model weights (weights learned weeks 1-9, applied weeks 10-18); (b) small-MLP NN stack; (c) plain average \u2014 default to (a) with the paper's regime-switching selection rule, then add a second-stage market-shrinkage blender: ridge meta-regression on (market-implied prob, FFORMA blend) vs outcomes, testing a market-aware two-level fusion.", "gate": "ADAPT accepted iff FFORMA-style blender beats SA by >=2% relative log-loss on the 2024 walk-forward AND beats the NN-stack in >=2 of 3 markets; reject if neither beats SA by >=1.5%.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2203.03990", "title": "Skating-Mixer: Long-Term Sport Audio-Visual Modeling with MLPs", "normalized_lane": "multimodal_fusion", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build Game-Mixer: treat each game as a long sequence with quarters (or drives) as clips \u2014 per-quarter features (tracking aggregates, score differential, pace, injuries/lineup changes) plus a [MEM] token carrying game state (momentum, adjustments, fatigue) forward via the Memory-Mixer recurrence; final [MEM] + averaged quarter tokens predict second-half/final outcome and per-quarter WP evolution \u2014 with an event-triggered write gate so only high-leverage events (turnovers, 4th-down conversions, injuries, scores) rewrite memory, making writes interpretable game-deciding moments for content.", "gate": "ACCEPT iff Game-Mixer beats the memoryless baseline by >=0.02 log-loss at halftime on 2024 games AND the no-memory ablation is worse (proving the recurrence, not just features, adds value); REJECT if no gain over score-diff + EPA.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2203.08489v2", "title": "Bayesian Analysis of Formula One Race Results: Disentangling Driver Skill and Constructor Advantage", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the hierarchical logistic QB/team/coach decomposition: logit P(A beats B) = (theta_QB_A + theta_team_A + ...) - (theta_QB_B + ...), cross-classified random effects for QB, head coach, offensive/defensive units + seasonal form (Stan/numpyro on 2009-2025 nflverse); identification via QB team-changes and backup-QB starts; report variance shares (QB vs roster vs coach) with CIs; add the QB x team interaction the paper assumes away as a 'scheme-fit rating' for free-agency analysis; serve the counterfactual engine P(team X with QB Y beats team Z with QB W).", "gate": "ADOPT iff: (a) QB/team/coach variance shares are stable across two independent fit windows (2009-2015 vs 2016-2022; same rank order, magnitudes within 50%), AND (b) on the 2023-2024 QB-change test set the decomposed model beats team-only Elo log-loss by >=1%.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2203.10706", "title": "Predicting Cricket Outcomes using Bayesian Priors (arXiv:2203.10706) \u2014 replaces [1539]", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the opponent-specific player-distribution DFS Monte Carlo: per-player fantasy-point distributions (hierarchical Bayesian gamma with player x opponent random effects, partial pooling, fit by MCMC \u2014 fixing the paper's 'Bayesian in name only' gap) keyed to matchup tables (WR yards vs coverage-shell-specific CB history), stratified sampling -> lineup construction under salary-cap/positional constraints, 10,000+ replications per slate -> lineup score distributions and field-adjusted win probability for GPP ownership optimization; score distributions with proper scoring rules vs an Elo baseline.", "gate": "ADOPT the opponent-specific player-distribution + Monte Carlo aggregation pattern iff the hierarchical gamma beats pooled baselines on 2025 held-out log-likelihood by >=3%; REJECT the paper's literal estimation procedure (moment + 5% tail rule, no pooling).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2204.04049v1", "title": "Efficient tracking of team sport players with few game-specific annotations", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Stand up the few-annotation tracking pipeline: frozen appearance backbone + iterative tracklet association (paper's ~3.5-annotations/player saturation, +26pp IDF1 over ByteTrack) reproduced on the public rugby sevens data; port the annotation loop to American football broadcast (college/public NFL-analog), building the jersey-number OCR training set the paper flags as missing; add active learning (model-suggested highest-identity-entropy tracklets) and cross-game identity transfer so per-game annotation cost collapses to a season-scale labeling pipeline. Standing gates: legal review before NFL footage; never present semi-automatically labeled tracks as ground truth \u2014 report recall bounds.", "gate": "ACCEPT as ADAPT conditional on the public-data reproduction; demote to REJECT if it needs >10 annotations/player to beat ByteTrack.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2204.08276v8", "title": "Tournament schedules and incentives in a double round-robin tournament with four teams", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add stakeless-probability features to any group-stage/round-robin pricing: ex-ante p_stakeless_weak and p_stakeless_strong per game (paper's Poisson-simulation recipe with GSE's team strengths), interacted with rotation/news signals; fit separate conditional outcome models on historical dead rubbers; test whether markets already price stakelessness via closing-line comparisons; extend to a continuous 'incentive gradient' (prize-money/rank movement at stake).", "gate": "ADAPT iff stakeless status predicts outcomes: in GSE's historical group-stage data, weakly/strongly stakeless games show a statistically significant shift in goal/point distributions or favorite cover rates vs matched non-stakeless games; if dead rubbers are indistinguishable from live games, the feature adds nothing.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2204.10185v1", "title": "Social Media Sentiment Analysis for Cryptocurrency Market Prediction", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the news-sentiment -> projection-error channel: collect 2024-season player/team sentiment from X + beat-writer RSS with a fixed lexicon (CNN channel included), compute per-entity daily metrics incl. the contradictive compound and a cross-channel disagreement metric (sentiment variance \u2014 disagreement, not level, as the mispricing predictor), test lagged correlation with next-week projection error at 1-7 day lags under nested walk-forward CV (refit quarterly), then lock the compound indicator and evaluate on 2025.", "gate": "ADAPT into the projection pipeline iff the locked 2025 evaluation shows |r| >= 0.10 with the correct sign and the indicator adds RMSE improvement in a bivariate blend; REJECT if out-of-sample |r| < 0.05 (signal was selection artifact).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2204.11142v1", "title": "Graph Neural Network based Agent in Google Research Football", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Take only the graph-representation idea (discard the DQN/RL scaffolding): per-play player graphs from NGS tracking frames \u2014 22 player nodes + ball node, node features = (x, y, speed, accel, orientation, team, down/distance context), distance-weighted or learned adjacency edges \u2014 GCN/GAT encoder -> play/drive outcome head (EPA, success prob) trained supervised on nflverse 2020-2025 joined to tracking; then upgrade to spatio-temporal GCN (snap-1s to +2s frames) and test whether learned edges recover football structure (OL-DL, WR-CB matchups) as interpretable pick-model features.", "gate": "ADAPT iff on the 2025 tracking holdout the supervised player-graph GCN beats the hand-feature GBM baseline by >=5% EPA-RMSE AND the attention/GAT edge weights correlate sensibly with football structure (nearest defenders/opponents weighted); REJECT the GNN-tracking direction if it fails.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2204.11777", "title": "Bayesian estimation of in-game home team win probability for college basketball", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build NFL live win probability with a time-decayed pre-game anchor: pre-game anchor = vig-free moneyline-implied win prob; in-game likelihood from (time remaining, score differential, possession, down/distance, timeouts); blend weight w(t) on the anchor decaying ~1 at kickoff to ~0 late (early-game cells regularized toward the anchor to kill MLE-style overreaction to a 14-0 Q1 lead); learn w(t, game state) by minimizing held-out Brier instead of asserting it; report reliability curves by game segment.", "gate": "ADOPT the time-decayed anchor + early-game regularization iff it beats market-implied WP on 2024-2025 held-out Brier AND shows calibration slope within [0.9, 1.1]; REJECT the paper's literal beta-prior cell machinery (basketball-specific) \u2014 implement the shrinkage principle inside GSE's existing WP model.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2204.13087v2", "title": "Faster Online Calibration Without Randomization: Interval Forecasts", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Stand up POTC-Cal as a parallel online recalibration signal on GSE's sequential probability stream: 2-epsilon grid over [0,1] (epsilon=0.025), per-bin deficit/excess tracked as games resolve, weekly interval output collapsed to midpoint for downstream consumers while logging interval width as an uncertainty signal; run one POTC instance per market (spread, moneyline, total) with shared epsilon tuned jointly; test the paper's open two-choice extension (score the endpoint closest to the batch-recalibrated probability).", "gate": "Adopt POTC iff over the 6-season chronological backtest its end-of-season epsilon-CE (0.025) is <=0.5x the running-Platt baseline AND prediction SD stays >=0.8x the raw engine's SD (no sharpness collapse) AND Brier is no worse than raw + 0.002; reject (keep batch recalibration only) otherwise.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2204.14198", "title": "Flamingo: a Visual Language Model for Few-Shot Learning", "normalized_lane": "multimodal_fusion", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build 'ask the film a question': few-shot VQA over broadcast clips \u2014 K=4-8 labeled (clip, analyst note) pairs + query clip -> scheme label, coverage call, or injury-mechanism note; open VLM (frozen vision encoder + frozen small LM + trainable gated xattn-dense bridge, Perceiver Resampler to 64 tokens/clip), trained on an 'M3W-sports' corpus of clips interleaved with analyst notes/play-by-play \u2014 plus tracking-conditioned visual prompting: prepend discretized trajectory token streams so the LM cross-attends to both pixels and trajectories (broadcast pixels lose depth/occlusion; tracking preserves disguised coverages).", "gate": "ACCEPT iff Flamingo-style 4-shot prompting beats the fine-tuned video-classifier baseline by >=5 percentage points accuracy on held-out folds AND close-ended likelihood scores are rank-calibrated (top-1 correct >=60% when margin >0.3); REJECT if it fails to beat the fine-tuned specialist.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2205.04173v3", "title": "Nested Zero Inflated Generalized Poisson Regression for FIFA World Cup 2022", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the nested + in-simulation-update playoff engine: per-game team points ~ Normal/NB with mean from nested regression \u2014 mu_A(offense A vs defense B, averaged both-ways), then mu_B|A conditional on realized points_A (garbage-time/defense-relaxation); covariates = GSE ratings instead of Elo points, home/neutral, rest differential; game weights w(m) = (1/2)^{days/H} x importance (playoffs 2-4x) with team-specific regime-aware decay (half-life shortens after coaching/QB changes, learned by backtest log-likelihood).", "gate": "ADOPT iff across postseasons 2020-2024: mean Brier beats GSE's current static-strength sim by >=5% AND beats/ties the futures-implied baseline on RPS in >=4 of 5 postseasons; REJECT if the in-simulation update adds nothing over the static sim.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2205.07193v2", "title": "How Much Does Home Field Advantage Matter in Soccer Games? A Causal Inference Approach for English Premier League Analysis", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build the division-pair HFA causal estimator: paired differences from division games only (home+away per season -> 6 paired differences per team-season, 2018-2025), model Y_{i,j,s} = alpha_{i,j,s} + beta_{i,s} + eps with beta ~ N(Delta_s, sigma^2_s), on team-game offensive/defensive EPA, success rate, penalties \u2014 attributing HFA to offense vs defense vs officiating; extend to time-varying venue effects with crowd size and travel-miles moderators (the 2020 zero-crowd season is the natural experiment) for crowd-adjusted team-specific HFA.", "gate": "Adopt iff on the 2020-2022 fit: (a) league offensive-EPA Delta-hat > 0 with p < 0.05, (b) unbiased variance sigma-hat^2 >= 0 (sanity), (c) the sign of offensive-EPA Delta-hat persists on the 2023-2024 holdout (p < 0.10); reject if Delta-hat is indistinguishable from the naive mean difference.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2205.09991v2", "title": "Planning with Diffusion for Flexible Behavior Synthesis", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build GSE-Diffuser: 1D-temporal-conv U-Net diffusion over fixed-length padded (200-slot) play-state sequences (down, distance, yardline, score diff, time, play-type one-hots, EPA), trained DDPM on nflverse 2006-2025 with padding masked; unconditional sampling -> full-game score distributions; live pricing via inpainting the played prefix (clamp denoised prefix to observed plays each reverse step); return-guidance toward tail scenarios for exotic-prop pricing \u2014 then test hierarchical diffusion (coarse drive-summary diffusion conditioning a fine play-level model via cross-attention) for variable-length games and faster sampling.", "gate": "ADOPT diffusion as a simulation backbone iff on 2024 held-out: final-score TVD <=5% per week AND WP ECE <=0.03 AND sampling throughput >=1k games/minute/GPU (warm-started, <=20 steps); REJECT if throughput falls below that (a beautiful simulator that can't Monte-Carlo in production is useless).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2205.10746v3", "title": "Athlete rating in multi-competitor games with scored outcomes via monotone transformations", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the transformed DLM team-strength feature: nflverse 2009-2025 score differentials, learn monotone I-spline margin transform (3 knots at 25/50/75th percentiles) + parameters via MAP (L-BFGS) on 2009-2019 (report whether the transform shrinks |margin|>21 tails \u2014 itself evidence about NFL margin informativeness), Kalman filter for weekly theta_t with home-field/rest covariates, team-specific observation variances (sigma^2_u per team) via variational/EM M-step keeping closed-form Kalman updates.", "gate": "ADOPT iff on 2020-2024: log-loss beats the no-transform Kalman DLM by >=1% AND beats Elo by >=0.5%, with the learned transform visibly non-identity (shrinkage of |margin|>21 tails); REJECT if the transform collapses to ~identity (like the paper's rugby case) with no log-loss gain.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2205.13532", "title": "Selective Classification Via Neural Network Training Dynamics", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build GSE-NNTD: during training snapshot slate predictions at each boosting round/epoch/seed (25-50 snapshots); per pick compute late-weighted disagreement of snapshot predictions vs the final pick; add as a second gate feature alongside the learned score \u2014 abstain when disagreement is high even if final edge looks good ('changed its mind late' picks) \u2014 weighted by when flips happen relative to line movement (a late-training flip on a pick whose market line moved against it is doubly suspect).", "gate": "ADAPT accepted iff adding the disagreement feature improves AuRC by >=5% relative over the edge-only gate on walk-forward seasons AND the top-disagreement abstentions are enriched for losses (precision check); else REJECT the feature (keep snapshot logging off to save storage).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2206.01038v1", "title": "A Survey on Video Action Recognition in Sports (arXiv:2206.01038v1) \u2014 REPLACEMENT for 0620", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Use the survey's method taxonomy as the build menu for GSE's experimental video lane: (1) reproduce a SlowFast/TSM baseline on public SoccerNet event classification in PyTorch (validation of the pipeline before NFL footage); (2) fine-tune to NFL play-type/event recognition (formation, play result, personnel); (3) add the pose stream (ST-GCN) for the injury-hazard direction; then train a single multi-task model (event classification + temporal localization + pose estimation) instead of the survey's single-task baselines \u2014 localization and pose are the same underlying signal as recognition on small NFL pilots.", "gate": "ADOPT the video lane's architecture menu iff the SoccerNet reproduction lands within 3 points of published accuracy AND a pilot fine-tune on ~200 labeled NFL plays achieves top-1 >= 0.70 on play-type classification; if the NFL pilot < 0.60, park the lane.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2206.02397", "title": "Projectile motion in a medium with quadratic drag at constant horizontal wind", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Implement the closed-form wind-drag formulas (paper's eq. 10) in weather/wind_adjust.py: per kick, inputs = launch speed/angle (charting archetypes), football drag k = 1/V_term^2 (calibrate V_term ~28-30 m/s), stadium wind vector decomposed along kick direction; compute wind-perturbed vs no-wind range -> expected-distance delta in yards as a feature in the FG-make logistic and punt-distance models; runs in microseconds for live recomputation \u2014 then upgrade to a two-layer wind model (free-stream above bowl + per-stadium in-bowl shielding factor fit from punt residuals), turning each stadium into a proprietary wind-transfer-function asset.", "gate": "ADOPT iff the wind-adjusted model reduces RMSE by >= 1.5 yards vs the punter-mean baseline on the windy-game holdout AND the fitted V_term lands in a physically sane range (20-40 m/s).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2206.07212v2", "title": "Explainable expected goal models for performance analysis in football analytics", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build an 'AP what-if' layer over GSE's existing expected-metric models (no new training): for any player/team and feature (aDOT, target location, defensive front), compute aggregated profiles \u2014 fix the feature on a grid, average predictions over that player's actual targets this season; serve in an internal prop-research notebook and content graphics, with guardrails (profiles only on the original data distribution, shade outside observed support, bootstrap CIs) \u2014 then go beyond the paper with coverage-conditional profiles (aDOT split by man vs zone).", "gate": "ADOPT the AP what-if layer iff Test 1 fidelity holds for >= 16 of 20 players (AP value at observed mean aDOT matches actual yards-per-target within +-0.5) AND Test 2 shows AP beats the global PDP by >= 0.10 Spearman points on half-2 efficiency ranking; REJECT if median player curve correlation across halves < 0.7.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2206.09034v4", "title": "Towards Better Selective Classification", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Train GSE's cover classifier with entropy-regularized loss L = CE + beta*H(p) (start beta=0.01, sweep {0.1,0.01,0.001,0.0001}); publish gate = rank games by max softmax probability, publish top-c_target fraction with the threshold calibrated on the prior season; monitor subgroup coverage so the filter doesn't systematically exclude divisional/bad-weather games; test the paper's central claim causally by freezing a SelectiveNet-style classifier and swapping only the selection mechanism (head vs SR vs entropy).", "gate": "ADAPT iff (a) entropy-regularized + SR beats vanilla + SR on test-window covered-set ROI by >=1pp at matched 30% coverage, or (b) vanilla + SR beats the 3-head learned selection head by >=1pp \u2014 either confirms the paper's ordering on sports data; reject if the learned head beats SR.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2206.09654v1", "title": "Performance Prediction in Major League Baseball by Long Short-Term Memory Networks", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build NFL season-total projection LSTMs: input = 5 prior seasons x ~20 features (age, games, attempts/targets, yards, TDs, EPA/play, team context, injuries), stacked LSTM (<=3 layers, <=128 cells) -> FC -> ReLU, MSE/Adam, expanding-window retraining; evaluate with the paper's full scorecard (MAE/RMSE, accuracy within +-k, per-tier correct counts, over/under asymmetry) \u2014 then build the deliberate two-model ensemble the paper implies but never builds: one conservative (MSE, the lower bound) + one aggressive (asymmetric loss penalizing underestimation) LSTM, using the interval for futures/award pricing.", "gate": "Accept iff the LSTM beats GSE's regression baseline on 2023-2024 holdouts by >=3% MAE on at least two of three yardage categories AND the elite-bias diagnostic reveals a correctable asymmetry; reject if it merely matches regression (the paper's own 2018 result: LR essentially tied the LSTMs).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2206.10323v2", "title": "What Makes Forest-Based Heterogeneous Treatment Effect Estimators Work?", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Adopt the paper's CATE ingredient ranking as GSE's default causal recipe: for any binary treatment (short rest, turf, new play-caller) and outcome (EPA/play, win, injury): propensity forest + marginal-mean forest, then a model-based forest on E[Y|x,t] = m-hat(x) + tau(x)(t - pi-hat(x)) with simultaneous prognostic/predictive splits \u2014 minimum viable version = treatment-centering only (mob(W-hat)), which captured most of the gain under confounding; Poisson-forest likelihood for injury counts, interval-censored likelihood for games-missed with heaping.", "gate": "ADOPT the mob(W-hat) implementation iff the semi-synthetic short-rest test shows MSE(tau-hat) <= 1.2x the causal-forest MSE (parity) and >=2x improvement over uncentered mob; otherwise REJECT the custom implementation and use off-the-shelf grf causal forests. The ingredient ranking (treatment-centering mandatory, outcome-centering optional) is adopted as recipe immediately.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2206.10540", "title": "Rethinking Symbolic Regression Datasets and Benchmarks for Scientific Discovery", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Harden GSE's symbolic-regression pipeline against the paper's vulnerability: adopt NED (normalized tree-edit distance to domain reference forms, e.g. logistic in EPA margin) as a structural evaluation alongside R^2; selection rule = among equations within 1% validation Brier of the best, prefer the lowest-NED (structural Occam's razor); acceptance test = inject 3 log-uniform dummy columns into the weekly team-stat matrix and audit what fraction of selected PySR equations include dummies \u2014 then extend the audit with correlated dummies (noisy copies of real features at 0.3/0.6/0.9 correlation) to map the exact failure boundary for pre-grouping correlated stat clusters.", "gate": "ADAPT iff the dummy audit finds >= 30% of currently selected equations include injected dummies (vulnerability is live) OR the mini user study replicates the paper (NED correlates with analyst plausibility ratings at |PCC| >= 0.3 while R^2 does not, p < 0.05); REJECT iff dummy-inclusion < 10% AND R^2/NED selection agree on > 90% of targets.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2206.11258v1", "title": "Developing a Ranking Problem Library (RPLIB) from a data-oriented perspective", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a rankability module in the Sports repo: for any dominance matrix D-bar (pairwise team win counts; unit-advantage indicators), solve the LOP exactly (n=32, scipy.milp/OR-Tools), compute k (distance to nearest perfectly rankable matrix), |P| (optimal-solution count), tau (max Kendall-tau over the pool), and beta (fractional-entry-weighted positional indecision); apply to weekly NFL power-ranking instances (flag ambiguous top-8 weeks -> shrink edge estimates) and to GSE's model-comparison matrices (is 'model A > model B' even rankable?) \u2014 then make beta stake-weighted by betting handle/edge at each rank position, turning a descriptive diagnostic into a risk-management input for bet sizing.", "gate": "ADOPT beta as a diagnostic iff on 2015-2023, preseason beta explains >=10% additional variance (delta R^2 >= 0.10) in next-season Massey prediction error beyond k and |P| alone, with the same sign confirmed on 2024; REJECT if beta adds nothing over the three existing measures.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2206.11578v1", "title": "Doubly-online changepoint detection for monitoring health status during sports activities", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a between-online changepoint monitor over weekly player series (EPA/play, snap share, NGS top speed/acceleration, target share): segment-specific latent trend + week-specific disturbance (game script, opponent), linear-Gaussian state space + online EM; alert when P(changepoint) > delta -> prop-model flag + feature freeze until the new segment has >=3 weeks (delta tuned for high sensitivity \u2014 missing an injury is worse than a false flag); second use = team-level regime detection on offensive EPA/play to trigger model refits; then make the changepoint prior covariate-dependent lambda(X) (injury history, age, snap load, days rest) and allow game-script covariates to modulate week-specific states.", "gate": "Accept iff it beats CUSUM on F1 against injury/role-change ground truth on 2019-2023 AND the within-+-1-week precision justifies the alert volume (<=2 flags per team-week on average); REJECT if the changepoint rate approaches the paper's 40% (pure noise) or EM fails to converge on 17-game series \u2014 fall back to BOCPD.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2206.13580v2", "title": "Ranking with multiple types of pairwise comparisons", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the multimodal team-strength EM: per-drive team-facet matchup outcomes (rushing EPA>0 winner, dropback EPA>0 winner, turnover winner, special-teams winner, penalty-yardage winner \u2014 each logistic-residualized on pre-drive score differential to kill the game-script confound), MAP-EM with logistic prior per season + rolling 8-week windows; outputs = team strengths s_u (a new power rating) + valence vector q_t (which facets carry most strength information \u2014 itself publishable); blend s_u into the engine as an additional strength prior \u2014 then make valence time-varying and matchup-dependent (hierarchical q_{t,week}) with an offense/defense split (separate lambda^O_u, lambda^D_u).", "gate": "ADOPT as an engine input iff across 2016-2023: (a) log-loss on game winners >=2% better than unimodal Bradley-Terry, OR (b) ATS hit rate beats the EPA-ranking baseline by >=1.5 points with the same sign in >=6 of 8 seasons; REJECT if neither holds or q_t signs flip on >2 of 5 facets year-to-year.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2206.14786", "title": "ENS-10: A Dataset For Post-Processing Ensemble Weather Forecasts", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Adopt the EECRPS-style metric: score all GSE weather-edge models with extreme-weighted CRPS on the NFL stadium dataset (high-wind, heavy-precip, cold games) \u2014 extreme games are where weather edges pay; train the baseline ladder (MLP -> LeNet -> per-pixel transformer) on GEFS/HRRR ensemble reforecasts over 30 stadium neighborhoods as the cheap warm-start before the flow model; don't download 3TB \u2014 implement on GEFS reforecast for stadium neighborhoods only \u2014 then train the baselines with an EECRPS-weighted loss and test whether extreme-optimized models beat CRPS-optimized ones on heavy-precip/high-wind kickoff games without losing average CRPS.", "gate": "ADOPT iff any NN baseline cuts CRPS >= 10% vs raw on wind speed AND the EECRPS ranking matches the CRPS ranking (extreme skill not traded away); REJECT if Gaussian-CRPS post-processing can't beat raw on wind speed \u2014 then go straight to the flow/LGBM recipes and this paper stays a metric citation.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2206.15241v2", "title": "Benchmark Dataset for Precipitation Forecasting by Post-Processing the Numerical Weather Prediction", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build the stadium-weather post-processor for game-day features (kickoff wind speed/direction, precipitation probability, temperature): pull NWS/NWP gridded forecasts (GFS/NAM) for stadium coordinates, supervise with METAR station observations (the AWS analogue), train gradient boosting on the curated feature set (graduate to U-Net/ConvLSTM only if justified), split-by-forecast-origin discipline, CSI/Bias categorical verification; feed calibrated weather distributions into the totals model \u2014 then fix the paper's open heavy-tail failure with a two-head model: occurrence classifier + generalized-Pareto/quantile-regression extreme-value tail head, blended by predicted intensity.", "gate": "ADAPT iff the post-processor improves on raw NWP (CSI +>=0.02 on precipitation occurrence, wind-speed MAE - >=5%) on the held-out window AND the calibrated weather features improve the totals model's log-loss/Brier vs raw-weather inputs; REJECT if post-processing adds no skill over raw NWP at stadium scale.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2207.00585v1", "title": "Predicting Ulnar Collateral Ligament Injury in Rookie Major League Baseball Pitchers", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Port the rookie-injury predictor to NFL: rookie injury-risk (hamstring/ACL) from college workload + combine + rookie preseason features (the football analogue of 'rookie-season stats -> career injury'); protocol fixes = published feature list, year-based splits with stated cutoffs, PR-AUC + calibration alongside ROC-AUC, workload-only baseline; start with the paper's MLP winner + XGBoost \u2014 then replace binary classification with a survival model (time-to-first-injury, Cox/DeepHit-style), since the paper throws away when the injury happened and workload->injury is inherently temporal.", "gate": "Adopt iff the NFL port achieves ROC-AUC >= 0.65 with 95% CIs excluding 0.5 on the 2022-2024 forward test AND beats the workload-only baseline (the paper's 0.674 is the meet-or-beat benchmark).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2207.05114", "title": "Bayesian estimation of in-game home team win probability for NBA games", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Upgrade GSE's live-WP blending with the paper's mechanism: gse.live.WPBlender \u2014 per (seconds elapsed, score differential, down/distance bucket) cells, empirical WP with a dynamic beta prior whose alpha,beta come from GSE's pregame model mapped through a prior-strength schedule (high early, decaying); posterior mean (n+alpha)/(N+alpha+beta); logistic blend of pregame and cell WP with features {t, |l|, l^2, I(l=0), possession}, coefficients fit by minimizing Brier on a validation slice strictly before the test slice (fixing the paper's leakage); serve per-second with cell-sample-size diagnostics.", "gate": "ADAPT (keep the blend) iff on the strictly held-out 2022-2024 test the blended estimator beats GSE's current live-WP Brier by >= 0.002 AND beats the no-blend cell estimator by >= 0.003, with calibration slope in [0.95, 1.05]; miss -> REJECT the blend (keep the beta-prior cell estimator only if it alone beats baseline).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2207.07318", "title": "Globally Combining Forecasts (Eckert, Hyndman & Panagiotelis, 2023)", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add CV-tuned soft-global forecast combination: combine GSE's sub-model forecasts per week with weights tuned by cross-validation that blend global (pooled across games) and local (game-specific) combination weights \u2014 comparing CV-tuned soft-global weights against local-only, hard-global, and equal-weight baselines on out-of-sample MSFE/log score, with 2020 as the disruption negative control (global pooling should degrade) and 2022 as the stable-season positive control.", "gate": "No numeric gate specified in the ledger; compare out-of-sample MSFE/log score for CV-tuned soft-global weights against local, hard-global, and equal-weight baselines, with 2020 as the disruption negative control and 2022 as the stable-season positive control.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2207.08635", "title": "GOAL: Towards Benchmarking Few-Shot Sports Game Summarization", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Use GOAL (first English sports-summarization dataset) as the English transfer validation bed: port the select->rewrite->fluency-MMR-rerank pipeline and the KES knowledge-fusion recipe to GOAL's English soccer data \u2014 they must beat LED's ROUGE-L 24.3 on the GOAL test set before any NFL application; replicate the semi-supervised self-training setup on the 2,160 unlabeled docs (analog of training on unlabeled NFL text streams with a small hand-labeled set); use the key-verb probing idea as a diagnostic for sports-domain familiarity in GSE content models.", "gate": "ACCEPTED (ADAPT): first and only English sports-summarization dataset + four benchmark settings defined + public release; as a benchmark and transfer testbed it is solid ADAPT material. NFL-port gate: adapted pipeline beats LED's 24.3 ROUGE-L on the GOAL test set.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2207.08924v2", "title": "On the Efficacy of the Wisdom of Crowds to Forecast Economic Indicators", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Change GSE's consensus computation: wherever multiple probability estimates are blended (model outputs, cross-book market-implied probabilities, pundit panels), compute both mean and median and default the published edge to the median-based blend; add a 'consensus disagreement' diagnostic |mean - median| as an outlier-sensitivity flag (>3pp of probability -> surface the dissenting source for analyst review); track a 'beat-all' statistic per model (fraction of weeks each constituent beats the median consensus in log-loss) as a model-health monitor \u2014 then test trimmed/winsorized means (5/10/20%) against pure median and mean.", "gate": "ADAPT accepted iff median consensus achieves log-loss no worse than mean consensus (within 0.5%) AND beats all constituent models in >=2% of games (matching the paper's 0.026 for median); reject if median log-loss is >1% worse than mean.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2207.11486v1", "title": "Time Series Prediction under Distribution Shift using Differentiable Forgetting", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Deploy learned forgetting weights in the engine's training: per offseason (and Week 9 checkpoint), fit differentiable forgetting curves alpha(tau;eta) = exp(-eta1*tau) and the mixed form on the game-level rows via the paper's bi-level gradient routine (logistic surrogate), then train the season's engine with each historical game weighted by alpha(age;eta-hat) as sample weights into LightGBM (two-stage); refit eta per era segment around major rule changes \u2014 then go beyond the paper with feature-group-specific forgetting curves: fast decay for personnel-dependent features (QB EPA, pressure rate), medium for scheme features, near-zero for structural features (HFA, altitude), with an L2 pull toward the global curve to preserve effective sample size.", "gate": "Adopt learned forgetting weights iff the GradMixedDecay-weighted model beats BOTH baselines (stationary unweighted and 3-season window) by >= 0.003 log-loss on the held-out 2025 season AND the learned decay curve is non-degenerate (effective sample size >= 300 games); reject if it fails to beat the fixed window baseline. Mid-season refit only if the offseason fit clears the gate.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}

{"arxiv_id": "2207.12147v1", "title": "Sparse Bayesian State-Space and Time-Varying Parameter Models", "normalized_lane": "mixed", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build sparse-TVP team ratings: non-centered TVP regression of margin on team dummies + situational features (nflverse 2015-2025 weekly), triple-gamma or horseshoe prior on sqrt(theta_j) (prototype in shrinkTVP, port to Stan/PyMC), read off P(dynamic) per team \u2014 dynamic teams get time-varying ratings, others static; refit weekly with warm-started MCMC/Laplace \u2014 then add a Markov-switching (break) component to the state equation for coaching/QB-change weeks so P(dynamic) concentrates on true regime changes rather than smooth drift.", "gate": "ADOPT iff rolling 2022-2024 RMSE beats the Elo baseline by >=3% AND the posterior classifies at least 20% of team coefficients as dynamic (the model actually uses its flexibility); reject if classification collapses to all-fixed or MCMC makes weekly refits unreliable.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2207.13191", "title": "GCN-WP: Semi-Supervised Graph Convolutional Networks for Win Prediction in Esports", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the calibrated GCN-WP: NFL team-game graph (nodes = 32 teams x 17 games, edges = previous-game + opponent-game per Algorithm 1), delta features (offensive/defensive EPA, success rate, explosive-play differentials), logistic output head for calibrated win probabilities trained semi-supervised on 2015-2024, evaluated on log-loss/Brier vs the engine's current model and Elo (the paper's missing experiment) \u2014 then implement the authors' stated future work properly: directed edges (past->present only, killing leakage structurally), typed edges (self-temporal vs opponent vs divisional), per-edge-type attention, testing whether the directed-heterogeneous 2-3 layer GCN beats the 1-layer homogeneous version.", "gate": "Adopt as a ratings/ensemble arm iff the calibrated GCN beats the engine's current win-probability model on 2023-2024 Brier by >=0.003 with acceptable calibration (ECE within 0.005 of baseline); reject if it merely matches Elo \u2014 keep the BuildLeagueGraph construction as a feature-engineering recipe only.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2207.13287v1", "title": "Detecting Concept Drift in the Presence of Sparsity \u2014 A Case Study of Automated Change Risk Assessment", "normalized_lane": "continual_online_learning", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Stand up the drift-monitor ensemble in the Tuesday cron: three detectors in parallel on the weekly resolved-game stream \u2014 ECDD on the error stream, PUDD on the PU-index stream, Page-Hinkley on the Brier stream \u2014 majority rule: drift declared if >=2 of 3 fire within a 3-week window (NFL-scaled analog of the paper's 1000-2000-instance window); sparse weekly features imputed first per the paper's recipe (sparsity audit, runs test, Q-Q check, kNN-vs-baseline bake-off); score the monitor itself with TPD/drift-count/ADD in weeks against labeled regime episodes \u2014 then test reliability-weighted voting (weights from trailing-season TPD precision, updated annually).", "gate": "ADOPT the majority-vote ensemble as the production drift policy iff on 2020-2025 nflverse: (i) ensemble TPD in [0.8, 1.2] per labeled regime episode, (ii) <=2 false alarms/season, (iii) ensemble ADD <= best single detector's ADD + 1 week; REJECT the ensemble (keep the best single detector) if (iii) fails. Adopt the imputation recipe independently iff >=10% RMSE improvement over median imputation on masked weeks.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2207.13747v1", "title": "Bayesian estimation of in-game home team win probability for Division-I FBS college football", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build GSE live win-probability v1: (1) NFL team pace estimates from nflverse (opponent-adjusted, Pomeroy-style recursion); (2) XGBoost expected-points model for current+next drive from down/distance/field position/time; (3) Bayesian estimator on (tau, omega) cells from 2015-2024 play-by-play with beta prior from GSE's pregame model; blend pregame prob with linear-in-time-and-score weight fit on 2022-2023 holdout Brier \u2014 then replace the expert-imputed beta prior with an empirical-Bayes prior from GSE pregame probabilities binned by cell, and add down/distance/timeout state to the cell definition.", "gate": "Ship live WP v1 iff 2023-2024 holdout Brier beats nflfastR wp on >=60% of games and calibration slope in [0.9, 1.1]; hold as research prototype otherwise.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2208.00139", "title": "1336 Another look at forecast trimming for combinations: robustness, accuracy and diversity", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Stand up RAD (robustness-accuracy-diversity) trimming for the model pool: per season/week, trailing-4-week validation window, per-model MSE-equivalent + pairwise MSEC on point forecasts, Tukey's-fences screen on per-model absolute-error variance, backward ADT elimination (kappa=1, delta=0.05) to the stop rule, combine survivors with simple average; add the RelDiv dashboard rule (RelDiv = AvgMSEC/AvgMSE; <0.2 -> skip diversity handling; >0.5 -> full RAD; 0.2-0.5 -> accuracy-only) \u2014 validating any trimming on BOTH point and interval scores (MSIS), never point scores alone \u2014 then derive a scoring-rule ADT analog (ADT_log with mean pairwise KL/CRPS divergence) for distributional combination under logarithmic pooling.", "gate": "ADAPT the RelDiv-conditional trimming protocol iff the reproducible test replicates the paper's core ordering (RAD >= A > None on point scores, no interval degradation) on 2024 data; REJECT diversity-only trimming (D) outright \u2014 the paper's MCB results void it; if RelDiv stays <0.2 for GSE's pools, downgrade to accuracy-only screening per the paper's own guideline.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2208.01562v2", "title": "Online Sparse Streaming Feature Selection with Uncertainty (OS2FSU)", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the OS2FSU sparse-feature selector for the weekly pipeline: Phase I \u2014 buffer each week's new/sparse features (Bs=8 weeks), LFA via SGD (rank 8) to impute missing team-game entries; Phase II \u2014 Fisher's-z relevance on imputed features vs cover label, fuzzy band mu in [0.01,0.1] via trapezoidal MF, neighborhood-rough-set dependency gamma for fuzzy-band features; selected sparse features feed the feature gate carrying an 'imputed' flag so downstream can down-weight \u2014 then make the fuzzy band missingness-adaptive: scale the band by per-feature imputation confidence (LFA reconstruction error on held-out observed entries), which doubles as data-quality monitoring for the weekly pipeline.", "gate": "Accept iff OS2FSU (LFA-impute + fuzzy select) beats both drop-masked and mean-fill+standard-selection arms on 2024 log-loss by >= 0.002 AND retains >= 5 of the 10 masked features; reject if it <= mean-fill, selections are unstable across seeds, or theta > 0.6 missingness on any real feature (drop the feature instead).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2208.02814", "title": "Conformal Risk Control", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Stand up conformal risk control on the posted-card workflow: C_lambda = {games with |edge| >= lambda}, loss = fraction of posted picks that lose (bounded, monotone in lambda); on a rolling calibration window of past posted picks choose lambda-hat per the CRC rule at alpha = 0.45 (control expected loss-rate below 45%, i.e. win-rate above 55%) and post only C_{lambda-hat}; same machinery for slate drawdown control (loss = max drawdown of the week's posted slate); use the covariate-shift extension with a regime indicator (QB-change weeks) \u2014 then test conditional (Mondrian) risk control within strata (favorites/dogs, high/low totals) with stratum-specific alpha_b, since GSE's failure modes are stratum-specific (e.g., primetime dogs).", "gate": "ADOPT iff the rolling backtest shows mean realized loss-rate <= alpha - 0.01 (tight, like the paper's 0.0987 vs 0.1) at acceptable volume (>=60% of unfiltered); REJECT the drawdown variant if the (B-alpha)/n correction collapses volume below 30% of baseline.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2208.04360v2", "title": "SDWPF: A Dataset for Spatial Dynamic Wind Power Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Use SDWPF as the benchmark substrate for GSE's wind-forecasting lane: reproduce the Autoformer/Informer baselines on the public 48-hour task (RMSE ~= 47.1, MAE ~= 37.6 verification), verify a graph-wavenet variant beats the transformer baselines before committing it to the stadium-wind network (turbines -> stadium locations, power -> wind speed/gusts, retrained on public mesonet data); adopt the paper's data-caveat checklist (missing values, status flags, abnormal readings) as the QA spec for any real wind-data pipeline \u2014 then shorten the horizon to 6-24 hours (game-day relevant) and re-benchmark with turbine-to-turbine attention learned from data vs fixed geographic adjacency.", "gate": "ADAPT: the benchmark data and task definition are exactly what GSE needs to stand up a credible wind-forecasting lane \u2014 value as substrate, not just method.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2208.08135v1", "title": "Gradient-Based Meta-Learning Using Uncertainty to Weigh Loss for Few-Shot Learning", "normalized_lane": "metalearning_fewshot", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build uncertainty-weighted meta-learning for new-regime team-seasons: task pool = team-seasons 2015-2025 (support = first K games, query = next games), small tabular MLP on game features -> margin, checkpoint initialization pool (score each checkpoint on the K observed games, pick argmin-loss), meta-loss Sum_i(L_i/sigma_i^2 + log sigma_i) with learned per-season sigma_i (expect 2020 COVID and injury-decimated seasons to learn large sigma) \u2014 then go heteroscedastic: replace scalar sigma_i with input-dependent sigma_i(x) from game context (weather, injuries, rivalry), marrying the paper's uncertainty weighting to game-conditional noise.", "gate": "ADOPT iff the homoscedastic variant beats vanilla MAML by >=0.02 Brier on new-regime win prediction at K in {2,4} (2023-2025) AND shows the paper's robustness (loss spread across alpha values <= half of MAML's spread); reject if init-selection picks checkpoints no better than the global init at K=4.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2208.08598", "title": "Using Conformal Win Probability to Predict the Winners of the Cancelled 2020 NCAA Basketball Tournaments", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the CPD win-probability head: fit y_uvw = mu_w + theta_uw - theta_vw + epsilon on rolling trailing windows via OLS with team strengths re-fit weekly; for each upcoming game build pi(y_c, 1/2) over a grid of candidate MOV values using signed residuals; moneyline prob = 1 - pi(0, 1/2), spread-cover prob at line s = pi(-s, 1/2); serve per-game evaluation as table lookup + interpolation on the precomputed residual CDF; reuse the Eq. 3 recursion for fixed-bracket contest pricing \u2014 then go beyond the paper with time-decayed weighted least squares (recency weighting) and locally-weighted conformity scores, tested on weeks 12-18 where late-season form shifts matter most.", "gate": "ADOPT into the engine iff on 2021-2024 walk-forward its log-loss is >=1% better than the logistic baseline AND its low-probability calibration (predicted 0.05-0.35 bucket) has |observed - predicted| <= 0.03 in every bucket; otherwise reject and keep logistic.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2209.00451v1", "title": "Group Activity Recognition in Basketball Tracking Data -- Neural Embeddings in Team Sports (NETS)", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the tracking-concept recognition pipeline: weak-label rule engine first \u2014 programmatic detectors for NFL group concepts (play-action via run-fake geometry + QB dropback depth vs handoff; screen via OL release + RB lateral drift; blitz via defender crossing LOS within X frames of snap; RPO mesh; coverage shell rotation), each validated against a few hundred manually watched plays (target >=80% specificity); per-player LSTM trajectory embedders + role one-hots -> Transformer encoder (d_h=256, 6-8 layers) -> team-wise sum pooling -> classification head; training recipe = self-supervised next-H-frame prediction -> weak-label fine-tune -> small manual-label fine-tune; export play embeddings as engine features \u2014 then upgrade to a play-phase-aware hierarchical model (0.5s micro-window encoder for pre-snap/mesh/stem/break feeding a play-level Transformer with learned phase attention).", "gate": "ADAPT/ADOPT iff on the 2024-season manual test set: (a) the sequential recipe (pretrain->weak->manual) beats the weak-label rules' macro F1 by >=3 points, AND (b) absolute macro F1 >= 0.80; REJECT if the recipe fails to beat the hand-written rules (rules alone are then the cheaper solution), or weak-rule specificity can't reach 80% after two revision rounds.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2209.00588v2", "title": "Transformers are Sample-Efficient World Models", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build GSE-IRIS: tokenize each play as a discrete multi-token tuple (play_type, formation_family, direction, rusher/receiver bucket, yardage bucket, EPA bucket, score_event, turnover flag) \u2014 a play-level 'language' of ~2-5k vocabulary; train a GPT-style transformer (causal LM) on nflverse play sequences 2006-2025 with next-token CE + per-play score/termination heads, conditioned on a pregame matchup embedding as context tokens; sample 100k games per matchup in parallel for score distributions \u2014 then add hierarchical tokens: a drive-level summary token every drive (result, points, plays, starting field position) with an auxiliary drive-outcome head for explicit long-range structure and better 4th-quarter tail calibration.", "gate": "ADOPT the token-autoregressive architecture as GSE's primary game simulator iff on 2024 held-out: one-step-ahead log-likelihood >=5% better than the RSSM variant AND final-score TVD <=5% per week AND WP ECE <=0.03; REJECT if it underperforms the RSSM on two of three metrics (transformers are data-hungry and NFL has only ~500k plays). Either way, the losing backbone is dropped.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2209.01697", "title": "Regime-Dependent Factor Graphical LASSO for Forecast Combination (Lee & Seregina, 2023)", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the regime-dependent factor Graphical LASSO combiner for GSE's correlated model zoo: panel of weekly forecast errors from K~10-30 models over 3+ seasons; strip common errors via PCA, fit Graphical LASSO to the residual precision, compute Bates-Granger weights; run Bai-Perron break tests on the loadings and residual-precision sequence around known regime events (mid-season QB changes, COVID seasons) to drive regime-specific combination weights (discrete-kernel regime-dependent loadings + time-varying GL) instead of constant weights.", "gate": "Gate is the break-alignment/post-break MSFE test: detected Bai-Perron break dates must align with the known regime events, and post-break combined MSFE/log-score must beat both equal weights and sample-precision weights (the paper's RD-FGL beat EW by 30-70% MSFE where structure/breaks exist is the reference magnitude) \u2014 with a stable-period negative control (no spurious breaks; FGL no worse than EW in stable periods).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2209.03013v1", "title": "Quantitative probing: Validating causal models using quantitative domain knowledge", "normalized_lane": "causal_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Stand up the quantitative-probe release gate for causal graphs: a versioned YAML probe suite (~25 quantitative probes over team-week indicators, e.g. ATE(pressure rate +10pp -> defensive EPA/play) negative with |effect| > 0.05 EPA/play; ATE(turnover margin +1 -> win prob) in [0.08, 0.25]; ATE(rest days -> offensive EPA) ~= 0 as a null probe that must NOT be 'discovered'); after each quarterly causal-graph refresh, identify probe estimands from the graph, estimate via the same outcome machinery, compute hit rate \u2014 publish graph-derived features/content only if hit rate >= 0.8 AND all null probes hold \u2014 then move to adaptive probe selection (rank probes by how much their estimates move under simulated graph perturbations) and use probe-failure clusters to localize graph errors (offense vs defense subgraph).", "gate": "ADOPT the probe suite as a release gate iff: (a) probe hit rate correlates with downstream Brier improvement across season blocks (Spearman rho <= -0.5), (b) the flipped-knowledge adversarial test drops hit rate below 0.5 (probes actually discriminate), (c) null probes hold at >=90% (no phantom causal claims); reject if hit rate is uncorrelated with downstream performance (|rho| < 0.3) \u2014 then probes are theater.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2209.06346v2", "title": "Prediction of the outcome of a Twenty-20 Cricket Match: A Machine Learning Approach", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build pairwise matchup ratings for NFL (WR-CB, QB-pass-rush): model matchup outcomes (yards per route run above expected) as s_ij = A + a_i - b_j with recency weights w = (1 + t - t_min)/(1 + t_max - t_min) and neighborhood regularization lambda*Sum(r_i - n_i)^2 (lambda ~= 0.7 start), fit by SGD, expanding weekly recompute; use as features in prop/spread models where individual matchups matter \u2014 then go Bayesian (TrueSkill/Glicko-2 style uncertainty so ratings carry confidence intervals into sizing), condition the intercept on game-script covariates (spread, total, dome/outdoor), and tune exponential-decay half-life by CV instead of the paper's linear recency weight.", "gate": "Accept iff on a strictly time-ordered backtest, models using the matchup ratings beat raw-aggregate features by >=1% MAE on player-prop-relevant targets AND the ratings show face-valid correlation with known elite matchups; reject if they don't beat simple expanding-window player averages or SGD fails to converge stably on thin 17-game data.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2209.07018v1", "title": "FRANS: Automatic Feature Extraction for Time Series Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt FRANS-style CNN embeddings: per-team per-season game sequences (nflverse 2009-2026: EPA/play, success rate, pressure rate, turnover margin) through a multi-channel 1D-CNN (Fawaz-style + feature layer, dim 24) on a surrogate team-season classification task (windows cut strictly before the prediction week \u2014 leakage-safe); per-window features -> mean/medoid -> static team-season embedding fed into the engine's meta-learner combining sub-model outputs \u2014 then build the two-tower extension the authors propose: static tower (FRANS identity \u2014 'who are they this year') + dynamic tower (windowed autoencoder of the last 4 games \u2014 'how are they playing now'), since the identity x momentum interaction is where matchup-specific edges live.", "gate": "Adopt FRANS embeddings iff the meta-learner with FRANS features beats the handcrafted-feature meta-learner by >= 0.004 log-loss on 2024-2025 walk-forward AND the leakage audit passes (zero windows crossing the prediction boundary) AND per-team-season embedding stability holds (within-season cosine distance < 0.5x between-season distance); reject if the win is sub-noise or embeddings collapse.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2209.07274v5", "title": "Introducing Grid WAR: Rethinking WAR for Starting Pitchers", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the convexity design rule as a standing GSE metric principle: any metric mapping performance -> wins/value must be computed per game and summed, never from season averages, when the mapping is convex (win probability in points allowed/scored is convex \u2014 allowing 40 vs 30 differs less than 20 vs 10); build an NFL context-neutral per-game QB WPA grid (team points per drive as Poisson(lambda), f(drives_remaining, point_differential), Empirical Bayes shrinkage for <1-season samples) \u2014 then make the grid opponent-adjusted (NFL has 17 games; opponent heterogeneity dominates) and test whether volatile QBs are systematically mispriced in DFS salaries (median-projection pricing undervalues variance) as a GPP leverage angle.", "gate": "Accept the design rule iff Test 1 replicates on NFL QB data (per-game-aggregated value regressed on average-converted value gives slope significantly < 1); accept the Empirical Bayes talent estimator iff it beats raw per-game means on 2024 rank RMSE; reject the Poisson drive grid iff it disagrees with the empirical WP grid by >2pp in any (drives, differential) cell (fall back to the empirical grid with monotonic smoothing).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2209.07581", "title": "Price Formation in Field Prediction Markets: the Wisdom in the Crowd", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Build the informed-flow detector on line moves (paper's eq. 2): regress each market participant segment's price impact (line move caused) on (current line - line they last bet into); segments with significantly negative beta are informed flow \u2014 their subsequent moves get up-weighted in GSE's market-implied features, others down-weighted as noise; at book level where account data is unavailable: only apply per-book after detecting informed segments; never assume a sharp NFL flow is sharp in NBA (estimate informedness per league x market, re-estimate after regime breaks).", "gate": "For GSE the gate is a statistically positive DeltaAUC from line moves (pre->post) stratified by move size \u2014 the paper's +0.037-0.041 DeltaAUC on PS (informed) flow with 95% CI above zero (vs -0.003 to -0.012 for non-PS) is the reference magnitude for 'informed', and 2-3/4+ PS-trader markets beating 0/1 at p < 0.001 is the cross-sectional bar.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2209.08778v1", "title": "Price Formation in Field Prediction Markets: the Wisdom in the Crowd", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Run the informed-flow detector in rolling windows and close the paper's untested loop: test whether the detected informed-flow share predicts the market-efficiency alpha metric \u2014 i.e., does the market become efficient (alpha -> negative) exactly when informed flow dominates? Implement as a rolling validation layer over record 141's detector: per window, compute informed-flow share (2-3/4+ PS-trader market equivalents) and the subsequent window's alpha (mean(W/p) - 1), and test the predicted negative relationship.", "gate": "Gate is the same market-microstructure validation: rolling informed-flow-share windows must predict the alpha efficiency metric with the predicted sign at statistical significance \u2014 if the informed-flow share does not predict efficiency, the detector is descriptive only, not predictive.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2209.07581"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2209.13154v1", "title": "Observation Centric and Central Distance Recovery on Sports Player Tracking", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Reproduce the SportsMOT tracking pipeline with open components (YOLOX-X + OC-SORT + OSNet) with validation-tuned thresholds (fixing the paper's test-tuning): adapt the football post-processing to NFL broadcast (re-derive time-gap/location-gating bins for 25-30 fps, shot-change detection as hard tracklet-termination, jersey-number OCR fused with the OSNet embedding in the association cost + team-classification head restricting the candidate queue to same-team tracklets), add field registration (homography) so image-plane tracklets map to field coordinates. Standing gates: legal review before any NFL footage; never present image-plane tracklets as field-coordinate tracking until registration is validated.", "gate": "ACCEPT as ADAPT conditional on the SportsMOT reproduction (staged HOTA gains OC-SORT < +central-distance < +post-processing on validation, final HOTA within ~3 points of 73.968) AND the NFL-broadcast acceptance test (IDF1 >= 70 on 10+ clips with shot changes); demote to REJECT if reproduction can't reach HOTA ~70 with honest tuning (competition overfit).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2209.14594", "title": "Bayesian Neural Network Versus Ex-Post Calibration For Prediction Uncertainty", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Horse-race a small VI-BNN head (2 hidden layers, mean-field Gaussian, Pyro/PyMC) on GSE's tabular game features for win probability against the current NN + Platt/isotonic/beta-calibration pipeline on rolling time-ordered backtests (train <=2023, calibrate 2024-H1, test 2024-H2/2025), metric = log-loss + Brier + reliability diagrams \u2014 then test the stacking the paper never tries: beta/isotonic calibration of the VI-BNN's own predictive mean (intrinsic uncertainty + empirical recalibration).", "gate": "ADOPT the BNN head only iff it beats the best ex-post calibrator with statistical significance on time-ordered GSE data (paired Diebold-Mariano-style test at 5% \u2014 the paper's own standard, which the paper itself did not meet); otherwise REJECT and keep the cheaper post-hoc calibration stack ('calibration is usually enough').", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2209.15421v1", "title": "TabDDPM: Modelling Tabular Data with Diffusion Models", "normalized_lane": "synthetic_data", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build the TabDDPM synthetic-season pipeline: nflverse team-game rows 2015-2025 (~3,000 rows; EPA/play and success-rate differentials, explosive-play rate, pressure rates, pace, rest, dome/outdoor, wind/temp bins, closing spread/total + season/week conditioning labels), Gaussian quantile transform + one-hot categoricals, class-conditional diffusion (timesteps 100, 4-6 layers x 256-512); offline batch generator producing 3-5 synthetic seasons per real season, mixed real+synthetic at a tuned ratio for spread/total/prop model training \u2014 then condition on market regime instead of raw season label: synthesize 'what would 2018-2022-style games look like under 2024 conditions' via a learned season embedding capturing rule/coaching/meta shifts.", "gate": "ADOPT iff BOTH: (a) real+synthetic beats real-only by >=0.003 log-loss on the held-out 2024 real season, AND (b) fidelity: per-feature TVD between synthetic and real marginals <=5% on >=90% of features (none exceeding 10%); REJECT if log-loss delta <0.003, any fidelity breach, or synthetic-only ML efficiency <95% of real-only. Evaluate over 3 generator seeds.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2210.04018v1", "title": "STaSy: Score-based Tabular data Synthesis", "normalized_lane": "synthetic_data", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Wrap the tabular diffusion with the STaSy training strategy: TabRep roots-of-unity encodings for team/opponent/venue/weather/rest categoricals + quantile transforms for numerics, continuous score-based SDE (VP/VE/sub-VP per Table 7), self-paced learning (SPL alpha0=0.2, beta0=0.9, S=10,000) then probability-flow-ODE log-probability scoring with DSM fine-tuning on rows with log p(x_i) < tau (median threshold); select on CatBoost ML-efficiency on a held-out season + rare-regime coverage (playoff, extreme weather) \u2014 then initialize SPL record weights with a domain difficulty prior (down-weight known high-variance games) instead of uniform, to test whether the curriculum does real work on NFL structure rather than fitting noise.", "gate": "ADOPT the SPL + fine-tuning wrapper iff: (a) real+synthetic log-loss beats the naive VP-SDE baseline by >=0.003 on held-out 2024, (b) rare-regime coverage improves >=10% relative with no column-fidelity regression (Omega_col within 0.02 of baseline), (c) median 2024 log-probability under STaSy exceeds the naive model (the paper's fine-tuning signature 131.734 vs 129.293); REJECT if SPL collapses to near-uniform weights (curriculum does nothing \u2014 check the weight histogram).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2210.06327v3", "title": "Betting the system: Using lineups to predict football scores", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the paper's 4-part scorecard as GSE's standard model-evaluation template: (1) fitness (MAE/RMSE/log-loss/Brier); (2) season-table reconstruction rank correlation (predicted vs actual win totals / playoff seeding); (3) tier accuracy (playoff teams, division winners); (4) flat-stake betting sim at recorded closing odds (ROI + CLV) \u2014 then extend it: replace flat stakes with Kelly-sized stakes from the model's own calibrated probabilities (a fifth CLV component), and run the granularity bake-off by position group (key-position-only lineup model vs full-lineup vs pure-aggregate), since NFL QB vs WR inactives have asymmetric value.", "gate": "Adopt the scorecard as GSE's standard iff it surfaces at least one model-ranking disagreement between fitness metrics and the betting/tier components on GSE's own backtests (must add information beyond MAE/RMSE); adopt the granularity prior iff lineup-level features fail to beat aggregates by >2% MAE on 2024 totals; reject the granularity claim for NFL if lineup features do help (the soccer result need not hold for football).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2210.08740v1", "title": "Risk-Sensitive Markov Decision Processes with Long-Run CVaR Criterion", "normalized_lane": "uncertainty_decision_theory", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Stand up the seasonal risk-sensitive staking MDP: states = bankroll decile (10) x edge-availability bucket (high/low) = 20 states, actions = stake tiers {0, 0.5u, 1u, 1.5u, 2u} (0 = sit out the week), transitions from 2022-2025 weekly P&L, reward = weekly profit; policy iteration (difference-formula, 5 random restarts keeping best local optimum) on objective = CVaR_0.75(weekly cost) + beta*mean with beta in {0.1, 0.22, 0.4} as three policy tables (conservative/balanced/aggressive); regime gating (normal uses this table; loss frame switches to the randomized policy); monthly re-solve \u2014 then test a distributional evaluation (full long-run cost distribution per state-action) against a spectral risk measure instead of pure CVaR, checking the 'CVaR-blindness-to-success' failure mode.", "gate": "ACCEPT iff 2024-2025 simulation: long-run CVaR_0.75(weekly cost) <= 0.7x best baseline's AND mean weekly profit >= 0.9x best baseline's AND max drawdown <= 0.85x best baseline's; REJECT if the local-optimum spread across restarts exceeds 30% of the objective (landscape too unstable) or any beta setting underperforms flat-1u on all three metrics.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2210.11010", "title": "Efficient variational approximations for state space models", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port Efficient-VB as the production inference engine for GSE's dynamic state-space ratings: dynamic bivariate-Poisson team-strength model (attack/defense random walks, Poisson score likelihood) on nflverse 2000-2024 \u2014 train 2000-2019, test 2020-2024 on predictive log-likelihood vs the static-strength model and GSE's current score model, runtime vs MCMC on one season, and the calibration check (Efficient-VB posterior SDs vs MCMC SDs \u2014 median underestimation ratio reported).", "gate": "Gate (ADAPT->keep): predictive log-likelihood beats static-strength baseline by >= 0.01 nats/game on 2020-2024 AND runtime <= 5% of MCMC per season AND median posterior-SD underestimation <= 20% (ratio >= 0.8); fail any -> REJECT for production (keep as research prototype).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2210.11802", "title": "Balance asymmetry predicts subsequent injury", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Add the re-injury cascade feature to GSE's availability model: replicate the prospective design on NFL data \u2014 cohort of player-weeks with a 'minor non-time-loss' designation (appears on injury report limited/questionable but plays) vs matched healthy controls; logistic/survival model for subsequent time-loss injury (missed games) within the next 8 weeks, adjusting for age, position, prior-season injuries, testing concentration in soft-tissue injuries (the mechanistic analogue of the paper's groin-pain cascade); serve 're-injury risk' annotations on injury-report content and availability-risk adjustments in fantasy projections for players carrying minor designations.", "gate": "ADAPT the cascade feature iff the NFL replication shows adjusted OR >= 2.0 for subsequent time-loss injury within 8 weeks of a minor designation (p<0.05) \u2014 a smaller but real analogue of the paper's 7.48; REJECT if OR < 1.3 (the cascade doesn't exist in NFL data, e.g. because NFL medical staffs already manage it).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2211.02417v3", "title": "Diversity is Key: Fantasy football dream teams under budget constraints", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Lift the dominance-pruning preprocessor into GSE's DFS optimizer: before solving the weekly salary-cap MILP, apply the three-step reduction \u2014 per salary bucket and position keep only Pareto-optimal (salary, projection) players; drop any player strictly dominated by a cheaper-or-equal, higher-projected same-position peer; verify identical optima vs unpruned MILP on 20 slates (target >=10x solver-time reduction) \u2014 then test lineup-diversity constraints (salary/projection spread across bins, the paper's Algorithm 3) as a GPP construction heuristic, evaluating whether diversity-constrained lineups improve realized GPP ROI vs pure expected-points maximization (the paper's 72% regularity suggests optimal ex-post lineups are rarely stars-and-scrubs clumps).", "gate": "Adopt the pruning preprocessor iff it reproduces unpruned optima exactly on all test slates with >=10x speedup; adopt the diversity heuristic only iff diversity-constrained GPP sets show positive realized ROI improvement over unconstrained sets across the three-season window \u2014 otherwise keep it as a descriptive curiosity.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2211.02556", "title": "Pangu-Weather: A 3D High-Resolution System for Fast and Accurate Global Weather Forecast", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Adopt two transferable patterns (not the weather model itself): (1) hierarchical temporal aggregation as a design pattern \u2014 train direct multi-week-ahead projection heads (1/2/4/8-week) and greedily compose them to minimize chained calls, instead of iterating a 1-week model 8 times (the paper quantifies naive 28x chaining's super-linear collapse; Pangu's 7x 24h chaining recovers >30% RMSE); (2) the RQE tail metric (Eq. 4, 90%->99.99% log-spaced percentiles) to audit whether GSE's weather inputs (wind especially) systematically underestimate extremes, with asymmetric tail-aware loss on the weather features in the totals head if the audit shows underestimation.", "gate": "ADAPT: the two transferable ideas (multi-lead-time greedy chaining; RQE tail auditing) are concrete, implementable, and map to real GSE subsystems (projection chaining, weather-adjusted totals). Not ADOPT: GSE will not train a weather model \u2014 the 3DEST architecture and ERA5 pipeline stay in the literature, not the repo.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2211.04459v3", "title": "flexBART: Flexible Bayesian regression trees with categorical predictors", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Install flexBART (R package or ported C++ core) as GSE's Bayesian tabular learner and benchmark it as a drop-in replacement for XGBoost on tabular game/team/player tasks: features = team IDs, QB IDs, coach IDs (high-cardinality categoricals currently one-hot/target-encoded) + continuous EPA aggregates; first applications = 4th-down/prop probability models and referee-crew effects on totals (crew ID is the natural categorical input); training protocol = >=4 chains with R-hat checks, 2000+ iterations, batch serving (weekly precomputed posterior means + intervals) \u2014 then hybridize: use flexBART's posterior co-clustering matrix over team levels as a learned similarity kernel inside the existing XGBoost pipeline (team-similarity features from the Bayesian model, point predictions from the fast model).", "gate": "Adopt flexBART iff: (a) out-of-sample RMSE on 2024 improves >=3% over one-hot XGBoost (paper's benchmark gains were 5-30% on categorical-heavy data), AND (b) 80%/90% posterior intervals achieve empirical coverage within +-3 pp of nominal, with runtime acceptable for weekly batch; reject if gains <3% (check the DGP2 singleton-outlier caveat) or MCMC cost exceeds the batch window; reject the network extension if gs2/gs3 don't beat flexBART_unif on the schedule-graph task.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2211.04534v1", "title": "Going for GOAL: A Resource for Grounded Football Commentaries", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build 'GOAL-NFL': NFL highlight clips paired with broadcast commentary transcripts; implement the four grounding tasks with CLIP-style video-text encoders; use retrieval (the paper's strong task: R@1 63%) for a 'find the clip for this storyline' product feature; skip generation entirely (the paper's own numbers don't clear any usable bar) \u2014 and condition retrieval on game state (score, clock, down/distance) as an extra input, which should disambiguate visually similar moments (e.g., any touchdown) and is directly available in GSE's data.", "gate": "ADAPT the retrieval task into the clip-search product iff a CLIP-style modern baseline beats the paper's R@1 by >=5 points on GOAL-NFL pilot data; REJECT the generation task entirely.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2211.06052v1", "title": "Gambling on Momentum", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Build a GSE 'narrative-fade' feature for in-play models: detect salient narrative events (NFL turnovers/big plays, scoring runs), measure the market's overreaction via odds-move vs model-WP-move divergence in the minutes after, and fade the overreaction \u2014 shade GSE's live probabilities against the narrative-driven steam (the paper's +12.7pp/40% overbetting figure calibrates the expected edge size); plus the ready-made content piece ('bettors believe in momentum, momentum doesn't exist') for in-play betting education \u2014 then run the cross-sport momentum audit: NFL pick-six vs methodical TD drive, NBA 12-0 runs, testing whether narrative-salience (not just score change) predicts overreaction size.", "gate": "ADAPT confirmed iff in GSE's odds data, post-goal odds moves systematically exceed model-implied WP moves in the narrative direction (overreaction) in at least one league with p<0.05; if no overreaction is found, the Bundesliga finding is market-specific \u2014 record that boundary.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2211.09510v4", "title": "Self-supervised Trajectory Representation Learning with Temporal Regularities and Travel Semantics (START)", "normalized_lane": "selfsupervised_tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the START-style self-supervised trajectory encoder for NFL tracking: field-graph GNN (1-yd cells as nodes with region features; transfer probabilities from 7 seasons of tracking corpus capturing 'route-tree semantics'), TAT-Enc with play-clock/game-clock/down-distance embeddings + time-interval-aware attention (handles tracking dropouts); pretrain with span-masking (0.2-0.5s windows) + contrastive (trimming at snap/whistle, temporal shifting, dropout), L^pre = 0.6 L^mask + 0.4 L^con, d=256; downstream heads = play-outcome regression, route-family classification, frozen-embedding play retrieval \u2014 then go multi-agent: TAT-Enc jointly over all 22 agents with role embeddings, using 'same play, different coverage' hard negatives from FTN charting (true semantic negatives for free, avoiding the paper's false-hard-negative problem).", "gate": "ADOPT iff: (a) frozen-embedding route-family classification accuracy >= 15pp above the from-scratch Transformer on held-out weeks, OR (b) same-play-concept top-1 retrieval >= 40% (>=10pp over raw-DTW), OR (c) play-outcome regression MAE >= 5% below the no-embedding baseline; REJECT if none hold.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2211.12507", "title": "OpenFE: Automated Feature Generation with Expert-level Performance", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build 'GSE-OpenFE' as a batch feature-discovery service: game/team-game rows from nflverse 2006-2024, expansion operators restricted to time-safe ones (GroupByThenMean/Std/Min/Max/Count with expanding-window semantics keyed by team_id and season \u2014 computed only from prior games), binary ops on rate features, zero-guards; FeatureBoost (LightGBM base + GBDT residual fitter per candidate, delta = train-loss reduction, successive pruning over season blocks); Stage II attribution; survivors promoted to the feature store with provenance (operator, keys, window); offline weekly regeneration, features frozen per season \u2014 then make FeatureBoost time-aware and residual-targeted: score candidates per rolling-season block requiring delta > 0 in >=3 of 4 validation seasons (stability filter killing era-specific flukes), with permutation importance in validation-season log-loss as the final filter instead of MDI.", "gate": "ADOPT the discovered feature set iff test log-loss improves by >= 0.003 on the 2024 NFL held-out vs the hand-built baseline, with zero leakage violations (every GroupBy feature provably computable from pre-game data; audit via recomputation on a row-sample); REJECT if gain < 0.003, any surviving feature fails the time-safety audit, or validation-selected features degrade test (selection overfit).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2211.15657v4", "title": "Conditional Generative Modeling for Decision Making", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build 'GSE-DecisionDiffuser': state-only diffusion over game-state sequences (down/distance/yardline/score-diff/time per play \u2014 no play-type tokens; play outcomes implied by state transitions), conditioning on (a) normalized final margin, (b) total points, (c) binary flags (key injury, weather bucket); train conditional + unconditional noise models on nflverse 2006-2025 with classifier-free guidance; unbiased sampling (omega=0) for pricing distributions, conditional sampling (omega>0) for exotic-prop pricing (e.g., P(home wins by 13+) via return-conditioned generation, 'snow game' portfolio stress tests); drop the inverse-dynamics head \u2014 then compose MULTIPLE conditions at test time (margin AND total AND weather) for joint stress scenarios ('snow game + divisional underdog + backup QB'), replacing a combinatorial explosion of separate conditional models.", "gate": "ADOPT conditional state-diffusion iff on 2024 held-out: unconditional TVD <=5%/week AND ECE <=0.03 (same bar as the unconditional Diffuser) AND conditioning shifts sampled margins >=5 points in the conditioned direction without collapsing diversity (sampled std >=80% of unconditional std); REJECT if conditioning doesn't steer or unconditional quality trails the unconditional variant.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2211.15734v1", "title": "Predicting Football Match Outcomes with eXplainable Machine Learning and the Kelly Index", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "Add a 'market difficulty' classifier to the pick pipeline: compute a per-game Kelly-style index across US books (book odds / market mean x payout rate), classify games easy/medium/hard, train confidence calibration separately per class, and gate published picks (easy + engine confidence >=70% -> full unit; medium -> half unit or pass; hard -> pass); backtest on 2020-2024 NFL ATS vs closing lines \u2014 then replace the count-of-bookmakers rule with a continuous difficulty score (entropy of the de-vigged consensus + max Kelly index) and fit the confidence threshold by maximizing backtested Sharpe per season via walk-forward optimization, testing threshold stability across seasons.", "gate": "Adopt the difficulty classifier iff the backtest shows gated picks beat ungated on ROI by >=3 percentage points with CLV>0 over 2020-2024; keep as monitoring metric only otherwise.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2212.03463", "title": "Sequential Predictive Conformal Inference for Time Series (SPCI)", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build SPCI as GSE's second-order calibration layer for margin/total forecasts: after the engine produces point forecasts, collect trailing residuals, train a QRF (or gradient-boosted quantile model) on residual lags (last w in {4,8,16}, team-specific and league-pooled variants), publish intervals per the SPCI formula at alpha in {0.1, 0.2} with width-minimizing beta-hat; gate on autocorrelation \u2014 enable SPCI only when trailing-50-game residual lag-1 autocorrelation is significant (|rho-hat| > 0.15), else fall back to EnbPI/ACI \u2014 then augment the residual QRF with game-context features (rest differential, weather bucket, QB-change flag), a hybrid of CQR's X-adaptivity and SPCI's residual-adaptivity targeting GSE's regime-driven error spikes.", "gate": "ADAPT iff empirical coverage is within +-2pp of nominal AND mean width <= 85% of the EnbPI baseline on 2024-2025 (the paper's signature is width reduction \u2014 demand a material one); REJECT (fall back to EnbPI) if residual lag-1 autocorrelation is insignificant in GSE data (|rho-hat| < 0.1).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2212.08116v1", "title": "Converting College Football Point Spread Differentials to Probabilities", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the NFL margin-multiplier matrix: historical exact-margin frequencies from nflverse 2000-2024 (~6,000 games); fit zero-mean normal for NFL multipliers (3: ~2.4, 7: ~1.9 with NFL-specific values), conditional SD ~= 13.5-13.86; margin x projection matrix (-60..60 x -40..40), column-normalized, pushes as half-win; wire into the engine (model projected spread + book spread + odds -> cover probability + edge -> Kelly sizing) \u2014 then make the multipliers state-dependent: separate vectors for divisional vs non-divisional, high vs low totals, late-season games (key-number landing rates vary with game script), and replace fixed SD=15 with heteroscedastic sigma(spread) estimated from conditional-margin data.", "gate": "Adopt iff the NFL matrix's cover probabilities are well-calibrated (Hosmer-Lemeshow p > 0.05 or reliability slope within 0.9-1.1 on 2015-2024) AND the edge>2% backtest shows positive ROI with CI excluding zero or positive mean CLV >= +0.5 points; reject if calibration slope < 0.8 or the backtest ROI CI includes zero with negative CLV.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2212.10904v1", "title": "A Bayesian Mixture Model Approach to Expected Possession Values in Rugby League", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port the Bayesian mixture EPV surface to NFL drives: ~40 expert centres on the field (own 10/25/40, mid, opp 40/25/10, goal line x left hash/middle/right hash + red-zone centres treated separately with linear weights), bilinear-interpolation fixed weights, Dirichlet-multinomial posterior per centre (conjugate \u2014 cheap in numpy; MCMC optional), data-driven alpha from historical NFL scoring rates by region, league -> team offense/defense hierarchy; precomputed 1-yard grid lookup serving, priors updated each offseason \u2014 then replace fixed bilinear weights with learned weights: a small NN (or GP kernel over (x,y)) outputting centre weights trained end-to-end against drive outcomes, with game-state covariates (down, distance, time, score diff) as inputs, converting the pure spatial surface into a joint spatial+state EPV model.", "gate": "ADOPT the surface as a GSE feature iff on the 2023-2024 holdout: (a) drive-points MSE <= nflfastR EP MSE (within 2%), AND (b) at least one per-outcome probability surface (e.g., FG probability in the 30-55 yard range) is better calibrated than the EP-implied outcome probabilities \u2014 >=5% lower Brier on that outcome class; REJECT as a standalone predictor if it underperforms nflfastR EP by >5% MSE; keep only as a visualisation tool if surfaces are qualitatively useful but numerically no better.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2212.11041v1", "title": "What Should Clubs Monitor to Predict Future Value of Football Players", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build NFL future-value models: per-position Lasso + RF predicting log(DK salary or projected fantasy points) N weeks ahead from per-snap/per-route normalized nflverse + FTN charting stats, with a team-strength anchor (log team implied total or unit grade) as the league-average-value analogue; rolling-origin time splits (fixing the paper's non-temporal CV), 5-fold within each origin; applications = dynasty trade value charts, award futures (OROY odds vs model), 'buy-low' flags where model value >> market salary \u2014 then fit age as a spline (not age + age^2) within each position model and test whether the spline beats the quadratic on veteran (age 29+) out-of-sample R2, since the spline should capture the late-career cliff fantasy markets misprice most.", "gate": "ADAPT the recipe iff per-position log-value models beat pooled + naive baselines on the \u00a712 gate (per-position R2 >=3 points above pooled on >=3 of 4 skill positions AND beat the current-salary naive) with time-ordered validation; REJECT any claim that crowd-style valuations are the right target \u2014 use realized fantasy points/salaries, not crowd valuations.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2212.12015v2", "title": "Stochastic analysis of the Elo rating algorithm in round-robin tournaments", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add the K-factor scheduler to GSE's Elo module: K_k = s'*beta_{o,k} with beta from the paper's Eq. 71, v-hat estimated each offseason from the prior season's final rating spread (M=32, k = games played so far) \u2014 large K early (fast convergence), decaying through the season; recompute R for the NFL schedule (replace uniform Eq. 14 with the empirical matchup-frequency matrix), re-derive tau1 for a preseason burn-in (ratings provisional before k ~= 3*tau1 games), and enforce K_k < 2*v-hat*s' as a hard cap \u2014 then run the 2x2 with the luck-capped link (paper 0576): fixed/scheduled K x standard/capped link on the walk-forward protocol, shipping both only if the interaction is super-additive in the heavy-favorite tail, otherwise keeping the cheaper one.", "gate": "ADOPT the scheduled K iff it beats fixed-K on pooled 2015-2025 log-loss by >=0.001 AND wins the first-6-weeks split (early-season adaptivity is the mechanism; a win only late-season is suspect); ADAPT (scheduler for weeks 1-6, fixed K after) if it wins early-season only; REJECT if no improvement \u2014 the NFL's non-round-robin schedule may break the R assumption beyond what the trace approximation tolerates.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2212.12092", "title": "1171 Anomaly Detection using Ensemble Classification and Evidence Theory", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Stand up the per-game ensemble conflict monitor + abstention rule: for each game's component-model probability vectors compute (a) UQ_P = Pi_i(1-p_i(win)) and (b) Dempster-Shafer conflict mass b_k from pairwise evidence combination (evidence m_i = [p_i*w_i, (1-p_i)*w_i, 1-w_i], w_i = trailing-season log-loss skill weight); calibrate dual thresholds tau_DS, tau_Y on trailing seasons so flagged games are those where the unflagged ensemble has historically negative CLV \u2014 abstain (no pick) or cap stake on flagged games; pool-selection audit: pre-cut models dominated on trailing-season skill, class specialization (home-favorite/underdog/divisional), and pairwise log-odds correlation diversity \u2014 then make the thresholds regime-adaptive (calibrated per early/late season and model-market disagreement context) and extend the evidence frame to a power set of regime labels (injury + weather + rest) with Yager conflict on the universal set as the 'compound anomaly' signal.", "gate": "ADAPT the anomaly-abstention rule iff on 2025 data, games flagged by the dual-threshold conflict rule have statistically significantly worse ensemble Brier than unflagged games AND abstaining on them improves full-season log-loss; REJECT the raw anomaly thresholds if the flagged/unflagged Brier gap is insignificant; REJECT the full DSET/Yager machinery in favor of the simpler 1169 disagreement dividend if the dual-threshold rule adds nothing over sum w_i D_G(p*||p_i).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2212.12504v1", "title": "Parametric Post-Processing of Dual-Resolution Precipitation Forecasts", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build the weather-for-totals calibration layer: take raw stadium precipitation/wind ensemble forecasts, fit CSG EMOS (or censored Gaussian/logistic for wind) with CRPS-minimizing rolling windows, using semi-local clustering across NFL stadiums (cluster by climate regime and ensemble spread characteristics) to share parameters where single-stadium history is thin; feed the calibrated predictive distributions into the totals model as uncertainty-aware weather features, tracking CRPSS per stadium as the calibration health metric \u2014 then replace the fixed gamma with a learned per-cluster mixture (gamma + point mass), test online CRPS-gradient updates for non-stationary regimes, and extend to joint precipitation-wind-temperature post-processing for a full stadium weather state.", "gate": "ADAPT: CRPS-fitted censored EMOS with semi-local clustering is a production-grade calibration recipe that fills a documented hole in GSE's calibration stack and directly feeds weather-driven totals; validate on public NOAA/GEFS ensembles (match a local-quantile-mapping CRPSS baseline with shorter training history) then confirm totals-model log-loss improvement on the port.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2301.04104v2", "title": "Mastering Diverse Domains through World Models", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Apply the DreamerV3 robustness toolkit to the GSE-Dream latent simulator: categorical latents (e.g., 32 categories x 32 dims) for z_t to capture multimodality of 4th-down decisions, turnover regimes, garbage-time scripts; symlog-transform all vector observation inputs (EPA, yardage, score diff) with symexp-twohot loss for the score/EPA reward predictor (EPA is heavy-tailed \u2014 exactly the failure mode symlog fixes); KL balancing + free bits (1 nat floor) with beta=(1,1,0.1); continue predictor c_t for drive/game termination (end of half, turnover on downs, game end); 1% uniform mixed into categoricals; fixed-hyperparameter discipline (one config across all teams/seasons first) \u2014 then learn a team-conditional prior p(z_t | h_t, team_offense_emb, team_defense_emb) so the dynamics predictor bakes in matchup strength instead of rediscovering it from score context, testing on 2024 games with pregame spread >=7.", "gate": "ADOPT the DreamerV3 toolkit into the GSE simulator stack iff variant (B) improves one-step-ahead log-likelihood >=10% over the naive variant (A) on 2024 held-out plays AND reaches the 1942 gates (TVD <=5% per week, ECE <=0.03); REJECT if (B) shows no significant gain over (A) after <=2 weeks of tuning \u2014 the stabilizers are only worth their complexity if they move the metrics; the actor-critic half stays out of scope.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2301.11898v2", "title": "DAG Learning on the Permutahedron (DAGuerreotype)", "normalized_lane": "causal_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Learn the topological ordering of GSE's team-strength indicators with DAGuerreotype: nflverse team-season aggregates (cross-sectional, ~35 indicators, standardized), DAGuerreotype from the public repo with GSE's own per-target gradient-boosted regressor as the edge estimator (each indicator predicted from candidate parents under the current ordering \u2014 optimizing the ordering against GSE's real predictive loss, not least squares); Bayesian optimization over sparsity/regularization on 2015-2023, ordering per season-block aggregated by rank-stability; output = consensus topological ordering constraining downstream NOTEARS/PCMCI+ runs (edges must respect the learned order), shrinking their search space \u2014 then learn the ordering jointly with GSE's actual game-outcome loss as the edge subroutine, turning causal ordering discovery into a feature-selection objective end-to-end (hypothesis: outcome-loss orderings rank market features late, efficiency fundamentals early).", "gate": "ADOPT the learned ordering as a constraint layer iff: (a) Kendall's tau >= 0.6 between orderings learned on odd vs even seasons; (b) order-constrained NOTEARS matches unconstrained Brier within 0.002 while using <=70% of edges; (c) >=80% of high-confidence order pairs respect football directionality (pressure before sacks before defensive EPA); REJECT if tau < 0.5 (no stable causal ordering) or if only the Gaussian equal-variance likelihood variant converges (estimator-dependence failure).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2301.13576", "title": "Sport Task: Fine Grained Action Detection and Classification of Table Tennis Strokes from Videos for MediaEval 2022", "normalized_lane": "sports_cv", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Define 'GSE-ActionBench': an internal benchmark with the same two subtasks for NFL events (pass-play type from trimmed clips; drive segmentation from full game video), scored with global+per-class accuracy and COCO-style temporal mAP (0.5-0.95) + frame-wise IoU; adopt the 'forbid pre-training on prior benchmark years' rule to keep yearly comparisons honest; require working-notes-style method documentation per model version \u2014 and add a third subtask the paper lacks: boundary-precision scoring (mean absolute boundary error in frames) for the detection task, since GSE's downstream products (clip extraction, highlight boundaries) care about exact cut points, not just IoU-thresholded mAP.", "gate": "The internal action benchmark is only useful iff it reproduces the paper's metric behavior: a trivial baseline must score near chance on classification (validating task difficulty) and a strong model must show the long-tail gap (per-class accuracy spread >= 30 points between head and tail classes), mirroring the paper's 2021 74.2-vs-20.4 dynamic.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2301.13594v1", "title": "View fusion via a Bayesian interpretation of Black-Litterman for portfolio allocation", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Fuse GSE's correlated pick-generating signals (engine model, market-implied/CLV, analyst adjustments, LLM panels) with covariance intersection / inverse covariance intersection instead of naive precision-weighting: GSE's sources share information (market feeds into engine and vice versa), so precision-weighting would be overconfident \u2014 the paper's PW-underperformance is direct evidence; track the epistemic/aleatoric decomposition (eq. 34) separately (model-uncertainty vs market noise) rather than as one variance number \u2014 then blend CI/ICI with adaptive fusion weights tracking which source is currently best (mAFTER-style per ledger 0786), combining correlation-robustness with time-adaptivity, and use CU sparingly for contradictory signals (e.g., engine vs market on injury-news games).", "gate": "ADOPT the ICI/CU/CI fusion iff it beats precision-weighting and simple averaging by >= 1% log-loss improvement over the best single source on the reproducible test (N correlated pick-probability sources on GSE's historical pick set, Diebold-Mariano test), with consistency (fused variance not understated vs empirical).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2302.03201v2", "title": "Near-Minimax-Optimal Risk-Sensitive Reinforcement Learning with CVaR", "normalized_lane": "uncertainty_decision_theory", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Deploy Bernstein-UCB CVaR bandit for weekly pick-category allocation: arms = pick categories (spread-high-conf, spread-mid, ML-dog, total-over, total-under, prop-tier; A~=6-10), reward r_k = realized profit in units mapped to [0,1]; maintain per-category empirical shortfall with Bernstein bonus (delta=0.05, tau=0.25); weekly: compute optimistic CVaR f-hat_k per category, soft-allocate posting slots to top-f-hat categories (top-3, not winner-take-all, to keep exploration); sliding 8-week window for N_k and mu-hat_k (sports aren't stationary, the paper assumes stationarity); the f-hat_k values serve as the audit trail ('why we leaned totals this week') \u2014 then make it contextual: shortfall estimates conditional on game context (home/away, divisional, weather flag) via per-category quantile regression instead of the unconditional empirical CDF.", "gate": "ACCEPT iff on the 2022-2025 walk-forward: realized CVaR_0.25(weekly profit) >= 1.15x best baseline AND mean weekly profit >= 0.9x the 'post-all' baseline (tail protection may cost <=10% of mean) AND number of posted picks >= 60% of post-all volume (must not degenerate to posting nothing); REJECT otherwise, or if the bonus term dominates selection for >50% of weeks (then it's just exploring, not selecting).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2302.06569v1", "title": "Inferring Player Location in Sports Matches: Multi-Agent Spatial Imputation from Limited Observations", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Rebuild the multi-agent spatial imputation model for NFL: replace soccer roles/event types with down, distance, yard line, play type (run/pass/play-action), personnel grouping, formation, pre-snap motion, score differential, time remaining; prev/next play involvement per player (targets/carries/tackles) as the on-ball-event analogue; train on public Big Data Bowl tracking as ground truth with nflverse play-by-play as the sparse event input; build a causal (filter) variant for in-play use alongside the smoother and measure the accuracy cost; add a probabilistic head (per-agent Gaussian or ensemble) since point estimates are insufficient for calibrated downstream use \u2014 then build the Probabilistic Agent Imputer (per-agent mixture-density output, evaluated on calibration via rank histograms and downstream field-control uncertainty bands) and test cross-league transfer (zero-shot on a held-out league/season) to measure how much of 'team structure' is universal.", "gate": "ACCEPT as ADAPT pending the \u00a712 transfer test: (a) test mean Euclidean error within ~15% of the paper's 6.88 m on comparable soccer data, or (b) on NFL data, per-play all-22 imputation error documented by position group with the causal variant no worse than 1.5x the smoother; standing gate: imputed positions must never be presented as measured tracking in any public content or model input without per-role error bounds attached, and the smoother must not be used for anything resembling live prediction; demote to REJECT if the NFL feature rebuild fails to beat a time-scaled interpolation baseline by >=40%.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2302.08981v2", "title": "Black-Box Batch Active Learning for Regression", "normalized_lane": "active_learning", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build the black-box active-learning acquisition pipeline for GSE's regression heads (spread margin, total, team yardage): maintain a small ensemble K=10 (or reuse existing GBM bagged folds as a free virtual ensemble), compute centered prediction vectors per pool game, build the empirical predictive covariance Gram matrix, and run black-box BADGE (k-means++ on prediction-disagreement embeddings) and black-box Core-Set for weekly charting queues \u2014 needs only predictions, so it works unchanged across the heterogeneous stack; monitor the failure signal (if inter-member disagreement collapses, e.g., late season, fall back to uniform/geometric sampling); divide the acquisition score by charting cost c(game) for the knapsack rule (ledger 2008) \u2014 then test disagreement-weighted virtual ensembles: weight each member's contribution to the predictive covariance by its validation-set skill instead of uniform q_k = 1/K.", "gate": "ADOPT black-box BADGE iff it matches or beats white-box BADGE on 2024 held-out margin RMSE at equal batch size (delta-RMSE <= 0 \u2014 no accuracy cost for dropping gradient access) AND runs >= 3x faster per acquisition round, with the win replicated on a second head (totals); REJECT if black-box underperforms white-box by > 0.05 RMSE points (the Fisher-kernel approximation is carrying real signal), or if pool disagreement collapses so black-box ~= uniform (their CatBoost failure mode).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2302.09276v1", "title": "Transformer-Based Neural Marked Spatio Temporal Point Process Model for Football Match Events Analysis", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the NFL neural drive point process: nflverse play-by-play 2018-2025; discretize each play into marks (time-since-last-play, field zone in 20 zones: 5 downfield bands x 4 lateral thirds, play type in 6-8 classes: run/short pass/deep pass/screen/turnover/penalty/kick); trailing-40-play history (truncate at drive boundaries for the drive-score variant); transformer encoder -> history vector -> dependent heads t->zone->play-type (scaled RMSE on seconds + cross-entropies); derive the 'drive utilization score' (DUS) adapting HAS with NFL weights (explosive play = 10, successful play = 5, failed play = 0; red-zone area weight 10) with exponential recency decay \u2014 a drive-level efficiency metric using no scoring data for content ('most efficient drives that didn't score') and as a WP-model feature \u2014 then replace the hand-chosen HAS weights and decay with learned parameters (fit by maximizing DUS's correlation with held-out team offensive efficiency under CV) and run the learned-excitation-kernel variant from ledger 0420 \u00a714 on the same harness (head-to-head 'momentum' formalisms).", "gate": "ADOPT the NFL point-process model iff it beats the AR(2) baseline by >= 0.10 total loss AND the LSTM baseline by >= 0.03 on the 2024 season holdout; ADOPT the DUS metric for content/features iff its team-level correlation with offensive EPA/play is >= 0.70 on 2024; REJECT the whole approach if the transformer fails to beat the LSTM baseline \u2014 the paper's core claim is the architecture win, and without it there is no reason to carry the complexity.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2302.13386", "title": "NBA2Vec: Dense Feature Representations of NBA Players", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port NBA2Vec as GSE's learned player/lineup representation layer: play-by-play with 10 on-court players per play and a discrete outcome taxonomy (~20 classes); train the embedding + MLP model (embedding dim 8-32, hidden 128, cross-entropy) on all non-holdout games; validate on held-out games (mean KL per matchup; require the plateau-by-30-plays behavior as a sanity check); export frozen player embeddings as features into the fantasy/prop projection stack (concatenated with box-score priors); refresh on a rolling window (last 2 seasons) to capture form/role drift \u2014 then replace mean-pooling with an attention/SET-transformer over the 10 embeddings (captures who-guards-whom) and add a temporal component (rolling embeddings).", "gate": "Gate (ADAPT): the embedding-plus-MLP predicts play-outcome distributions with mean KL ~= 0.3 on held-out playoff games, embeddings recover known roles, and the matchup optimizer produces sensible orderings; adopt as ADAPT (weakened only by missing baselines); improvement success = held-out KL <= 0.25 (>= ~17% relative improvement) with the same 25-game validation protocol.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2302.13979v1", "title": "Wasserstein-Kelly Portfolios", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Rebuild the paper's experiment first (10 random S&P 500 stocks, train 2019, OOS 2020-01-01 to 2023-02-20, delta in {0.1,0.2,0.3,0.4}, 1,000 repetitions; verify the robust portfolios' OOS Sharpe and max drawdown dominate standard Kelly's on average), then run the GSE application on the pick history (Neon picks, model v5.2.7): walk-forward robust-Kelly vs standard fractional-Kelly staking, scoring log-wealth and max drawdown per season, with delta chosen on a rolling validation window \u2014 the expectation from the paper: robust Kelly sacrifices a little growth in stable regimes for materially smaller drawdowns across regime changes (season boundaries, model updates); quantify the exchange rate.", "gate": "ADAPT: Wasserstein-robust Kelly is the tail-aware staking layer for GSE's pick portfolio; adopt the walk-forward protocol as the standing staking test \u2014 robust Kelly ships iff the walk-forward shows materially smaller max drawdown across regime changes at an acceptable growth exchange rate (the paper's graphical claim replicated on GSE's own picks); otherwise keep fractional Kelly.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2303.04963v1", "title": "Predicting Elite NBA Lineups Using Individual Player Order Statistics", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replicate the elite-lineup order-statistic technique on NFL DFS: replace the 28 NBA stats with per-player fantasy-relevant stats; define the target as GPP-winning-lineup membership or top-1% lineup finish; expand each slate's player pool into order-statistic predictors per candidate lineup (sorted by projection, ceiling, ownership, leverage); train a diverse classifier set; apply the unanimous-consent rule to generate a high-precision short list of lineups for final optimizer seeding; calibrate the precision/recall trade-off against contest payout structure (top-heavy GPPs favor the unanimity filter) \u2014 then replace unanimity with a calibrated agreement-threshold (k-of-7 votes) tuned per contest payout curve, and add interaction features (teammate/opponent overlap) to recover some of the sacrificed recall; test on NFL showdown and classic slates.", "gate": "ADAPT: elite-lineup identification without shared-court history is a genuinely transferable DFS/stacks technique, and the unanimous-consent ensemble is a portable high-precision filter for any GPP lineup pipeline; first reproduce the paper's 86.7%-level test precision vs the 62.1% prevalence baseline on one NBA season of public data, then confirm optimizer ROI improvement with vs without unanimity filtering on one NFL DFS slate.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2303.05000v1", "title": "Learning Representation for Anomaly Detection of Vehicle Trajectories", "normalized_lane": "selfsupervised_tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the semantic autoencoder for NFL trajectories: 10Hz tracking, plays with field context (yard lines, down/distance as the 'map graph' analog); train the semantic AAE with the latent partitioned into intention (route-concept class, charted), physicality/aggressiveness (speed/accel-derived), residual; decoder reconstructs trajectories (smooth-L1), discriminators regularize partitions; deploy two heads: (a) reconstruction-error anomaly flag for data QA, (b) semantic factors as features for GSE prop models; supervised contrastive variant: contrast normal plays vs synthetically perturbed plays (PGD-style waypoint jitter) to harden the trajectory forecaster \u2014 then switch to football-native anomaly synthesis (swap a player's trajectory with a different play's same-position trajectory \u2014 context-inconsistent but realistic) and run the adversarial loop: train the ball-carrier forecaster on AAE-flagged hardest legitimate plays to test whether 'legitimate hard examples' improve tail performance.", "gate": "ADOPT iff: (a) anomaly-detection ROC AUC >= 0.85 on synthetic perturbations (vs <= 0.70 for the raw-acceleration baseline), AND (b) the intention partition achieves AMI >= 0.30 with charted route concepts; REJECT if (a) fails.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2303.05774v1", "title": "NFL Career Success as Predicted by NFL Scouting Combine", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Use the combine paper as a NEGATIVE prior in GSE's rookie model: cap combine-feature weights in rookie-season projections \u2014 do not let 40-yard dash / 3-cone standouts move rookie fantasy projections materially; draft-market angle: fade rookies whose draft slot was driven by combine testing over college production for rookie-season props (rookie of the year, season-long yardage props), favor productive college players with mediocre testing; concrete rule: rookie projection blend weight = alpha*college production + beta*draft position + gamma*combine with gamma <= 0.1 and 3-cone excluded or signed near-zero for RB/WR/TE, broad jump allowed small positive weight (only drill with any success signal) \u2014 then run position-specific combine validity (per position group with position-relevant success metrics) to test whether the null is a pooling artifact and whether any drill x position cell has real predictive power worth a nonzero weight.", "gate": "ADAPT iff Test 1 replicates (combine predicts matriculation at 0.78-0.88 accuracy but snaps R2 < 0.25 \u2014 the negative prior stands regardless of Test 2); REJECT only if combine metrics strongly predict success on modern classes (R2 >= 0.35 without production features), which would overturn the paper; the adaptation is a modeling constraint, not a predictor \u2014 judge it on whether GSE's rookie projections avoid the combine trap, not on a new edge.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}

{"arxiv_id": "2303.06021v4", "title": "Machine learning for sports betting: should model selection be based on accuracy or calibration?", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "As engine-honesty infrastructure, run GSE's model bake-off with a two-branch selection: same candidate learners optimized on accuracy vs on 20-bin classwise-ECE with the 80%-nonempty-bins guard; adopt classwise-ECE as the primary model-selection metric for the probability engine, replacing accuracy wherever it gates promotion - and replace full Kelly with fractional Kelly <= 1/8 in any sizing module.", "gate": "ADOPT the selection-metric change if, on the 2024 test window, the ECE-selected model achieves >=3 pp lower classwise-ECE than the accuracy-selected model AND its season ROI beats the accuracy-selected model's ROI under both fixed-stakes and 1/8-Kelly rules; REJECT if the accuracy-selected model wins ROI under either rule by more than 5 pp. Pre-registered before running.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2303.10895v1", "title": "Leapfrog Diffusion Model for Stochastic Trajectory Prediction", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Reimplement LED on modern PyTorch and train on multi-season NFL tracking (nflverse / Big Data Bowl), adding conditioning channels the paper lacks (down/distance, personnel, score differential) via the context encoder - with distribution calibration (NLL / rank-histogram checks) the paper omits, since GSE needs calibrated mode probabilities, not just best-of-K coverage - then extend to joint multi-agent decoding (all 22 players + ball with a shared interaction graph) so correlated samples capture joint outcomes like receiver separation + defender angle together.", "gate": "ACCEPT as an ADAPT build candidate conditional on the reproduction: standing gate - do not present LED trajectory predictions as NGS-equivalent or use them in any public pick rationale until the held-out-season test passes and calibration is documented. If reproduction fails to beat baselines on modern data, verdict falls back to REJECT (superseded by 2503.18589-class methods).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2303.11366v4", "title": "Reflexion: Language Agents with Verbal Reinforcement Learning", "normalized_lane": "llm_agents_ai_scientist", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt the Actor-Evaluator-Self-Reflection triad as the executor harness inside the AI-Scientist discovery loop: Actor = code-writing agent editing the nflverse backtest template; Evaluator = deterministic backtest returning binary/scalar signal plus structured diagnostics (which season folds failed, sample sizes, calibration slope), with a permutation-based evaluator-reliability check (flip the feature's sign / permute the target - if the 'signal' persists, flag it); Self-Reflection = LLM writing 3-5 sentence lessons into a bounded SQLite memory (Omega=3) retrieved by similarity - with reflection consolidation every 5 trials, distilling stored reflections into one durable 'doctrine' entry while raw reflections expire.", "gate": "ADOPT if: reflection arm resolves >=6/10 ideas within 12 trials vs <=3/10 for the retry-only arm, mean trials-to-pass is lower in the reflection arm, and the permutation-based evaluator-reliability check flags >=80% of deliberately injected leaky backtests; REJECT the reflection layer if the retry-only arm matches within 1 idea, or reflection shows the Table-3 pathology, or reflections duplicate each other (cosine > 0.9 across trials).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INVENT", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2408.06292v3"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2303.12401v2", "title": "Real-time forecasting within soccer matches through a Bayesian lens", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port the live Bayesian probit to NFL: replace the 90 independent minute-models with a hierarchical Bayesian structure (minute-level coefficients shrunk toward neighbors), play-indexed probits on nflverse (down/distance/yardline/score/time covariates), and add market odds as a covariate to test whether live events add information beyond the price.", "gate": "ADAPT iff the architecture survives chronological evaluation: under rolling-origin validation, the play-indexed Bayesian probit must beat a static pre-match-probability-plus-score baseline on log-loss; if the live model adds nothing once the split is chronological, the adaptation fails.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2303.14857v1", "title": "Paired comparisons for games of chance", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt only the luck function: replace GSE's BT/Elo win-probability link p=1/(1+10^(-Delta/400)) with the beta-capped link p=(1-beta)/2+beta/(1+10^(-Delta/400)), beta tuned on 2015-2025 nflverse moneylines (grid {0.8,0.85,0.9,0.95,1.0}) - applied at the calibration layer (predicted prob -> market prob), not inside the rating update, keeping the existing Elo/Glicko machinery untouched - then test team-specific beta via hierarchical beta_team with shrinkage to the global mean, kept only if beta_team is stable year-over-year (rank correlation >0.3).", "gate": "ADOPT the beta-capped link if it reduces tail-decile log-loss by >=0.002 vs beta=1 on 2015-2025 pooled AND improves overall log-loss (no overall degradation); ADAPT if it wins only in the tail - apply the cap only for |p-0.5|>0.3 (piecewise link); REJECT if beta<1 does not beat beta=1 on NFL data.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2303.16648v1", "title": "Beating the average: how to generate profit by exploiting the inefficiencies of soccer betting", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a 'coverage calculator' for GSE contest products (survivor pools, pick'em pools, correlated parlay portfolios): given m published picks with heterogeneous per-pick hit rates p_i from GSE's calibrated probabilities, payout tiers, entry cost, and desired safety Q, output the number of portfolio entries and their construction - generalizing the paper's eq 15 to heterogeneous p_i via the Poisson-binomial, adding a variance-aware gate (Sharpe ratio of the coverage strategy over the 1.5-year return distribution instead of expected profit alone), and sizing entries to expected closing-line value of each pick subject to the coverage constraint.", "gate": "Adopt the coverage calculator if, on the 10,000-draw simulation using GSE's calibrated per-pick probabilities, empirical coverage at the computed n matches the target Q within +/-1 pp across Q in {90%, 99%, 99.9%} AND the expected-profit sign matches the formula's prediction on historical pick'em data; reject if heterogeneity in p_i breaks the approximation beyond +/-3 pp.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2303.16741v1", "title": "Who You Play Affects How You Play: Predicting Sports Performance Using Graph Attention Networks With Temporal Convolution", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build an NFL analog: nodes = key players per matchup (skill players, QBs, pass rushers, coverage defenders); weighted edges from FTN charting (coverage matchup minutes, alignment, shadow-coverage indicators) instead of the paper's binary complete graph; node features from nflverse per-player-per-game aggregates; GATv2 + TCN on 8-17 week windows; target = next-week player fantasy/prop-relevant stats - with a market-conditioning head (de-vigged prop line embeddings concatenated to node features so attention routes around mispriced lines) and a multi-task target (yards + receptions + TD jointly).", "gate": "Adopt as GSE's prop-graph lane if GATv2-TCN beats the TCN-only baseline by >=5% MAE reduction on 2024 WR receiving yards AND CORR improves by >=0.03 absolute on the test window, with no MAPE deterioration >10%; reject the graph component if it fails to beat TCN; reject the whole approach if it fails to beat GSE's existing per-player features.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2303.16776v1", "title": "Supervised Learning for Table Tennis Match Prediction", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port the pattern, not the sport: NFL analogs of the engineered features - pass-vs-run EPA differential (offense balance), short-vs-long down EPA differential, home/road splits differentials, early-vs-late-down efficiency gaps, and a BALANCE metric (mean of absolute differentials) as a team 'well-roundedness' feature - plus the RANKDIFF non-linearity (saturation applied to Elo-difference features) and the anti-overfit protocol: for every matchup-level feature, compute it from rolling aggregates EXCLUDING the target game (leave-one-game-out) and verify accuracy parity - a cheap leakage audit for the props/engine pipeline.", "gate": "Adopt the differential-feature + LOO-audit pattern if: (a) BALANCE-style features rank in the top half of RF Gini importance on NFL data, and (b) LOO-aggregated features lose <=5 percentage points of accuracy vs leaky features; reject if differentials add nothing over GSE's existing EPA aggregates, or if the LOO audit reveals GSE's current matchup features are leaking target-game data.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2303.17610", "title": "Ensemble weather forecast post-processing with a flexible probabilistic neural network approach", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build weather/postprocess.py: train an ANET2_NORM-style model (fastest MVP) on GEFS/ECMWF-IFS ensemble reforecasts for 30 NFL stadium coordinates - targets = game-time 2m temperature, 10m wind speed, precipitation rate; inputs = ensemble mean/variance at ~6-hour lead times bracketing kickoff, stadium altitude/lon/lat, day-of-year encoding - upgrading to the full spline-flow output once the NORM baseline validates; serve nightly calibrated predictive distributions per Sunday game, feeding P(wind > 15 mph), E[precip], temp quantiles into the totals/spread model - plus stadium-bowl microclimate: bowl openness index, field orientation, surrounding elevation for per-stadium bias corrections.", "gate": "ADOPT if the post-processed model beats EMOS by >=5% CRPS on wind speed AND >=5% on temperature on the 2024 holdout with rank histograms visibly more uniform than raw ensembles; REJECT if CRPS gain <5% on either variable - then GSE stays with off-the-shelf weather APIs.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2303.17863v2", "title": "A Bayesian hidden Markov model for assessing the hot hand phenomenon in basketball shooting performance", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port BLHMM to NFL drive/play sequences: latent states {cold, hot} for offensive efficiency; observation = per-play success (EPA>0 or first-down conversion) with covariates (down, distance, field position, QB injury flag, weather); logit transition probabilities with game-level covariates (opponent defensive strength, rest) to fix the paper's missing-opponent flaw - outputting posterior streak probabilities feeding live in-game win-probability adjustments and a 'momentum flag' for content (never as a primary pick input) - with a three-state (cold/neutral/hot) extension preventing the degenerate 'hot = automatic' collapse.", "gate": "ADOPT as a live-momentum module if the HMM beats the no-HMM baseline by >=0.005 mean log-loss on held-out games AND the posterior hot-state probability is calibrated (slope of observed vs predicted next-drive TD rate within 0.85-1.15); ADAPT if only the streak-quantification outputs are useful (content feature, no pick use); REJECT if the latent states degenerate as in the paper on NFL data.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2304.01239v1", "title": "Online Distillation with Continual Learning for Cyclic Domain Shifts", "normalized_lane": "continual_online_learning", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Teacher-student weekly update: the teacher is GSE's full-history calibrated model (refit monthly); the student is a lightweight model refit weekly on recent games but trained against the teacher's predicted probabilities (soft targets), not hard outcomes - preserving calibration while tracking the current regime fast; serve the student, falling back to the teacher when the student's regime-OOD score is high - with a cyclic replay buffer guaranteeing minimum representation of each regime stratum (early/mid/December-weather/playoffs) from prior seasons, RWalk-style drift regularization on the top-K features, and a regime-conditional teacher variant (4 frozen regime teachers, distilling against the upcoming regime's teacher each week).", "gate": "ADOPT the teacher-student update if on 2020-2025 walk-forward: (i) the distilled student matches or beats hard-label refit on anytime Brier while improving ECE by >=0.002, (ii) adding the cyclic buffer + RWalk improves December/playoff-regime Brier by >=0.003 with no metric worse by >0.001; REJECT distillation if the student's edge comes only from the teacher's information (teacher-frozen-since-August control); REJECT the RWalk half if it adds nothing over the buffer alone.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": ["2308.03810", "2405.04101"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2304.01538", "title": "A doubly self-exciting Poisson model for describing scoring levels in NBA basketball", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt the doubly self-exciting hierarchy to NFL: game level - weekly player fantasy points (or team points) with INGARCH(1,1) + spread/total/home covariates; drive level - points per drive within a game with the weekly posterior mean as offset; self-excitation parameters (kappa, eta) per player/team quantifying 'hot' volume dynamics; cluster players by (eta, kappa) posteriors for matchup typing (relevant to live betting and DFS late-swap decisions) - with a joint (not two-stage) Bayesian fit propagating game-level uncertainty, zero-inflated Poisson for scoreless drives, and attempt-volume vs efficiency decomposition.", "gate": "ADOPT the doubly self-exciting hierarchy and the Wasserstein-barycenter divide-and-conquer if drive-level DSE beats baseline on 2025 held-out log-likelihood; REJECT game-level self-excitation unless WAIC/LOO supports it (the paper's own evidence says it usually does not); REJECT the plug-in offset as a final implementation - propagate uncertainty jointly in the production version.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2304.03870", "title": "ASPEST: Bridging the Gap Between Active Learning and Selective Prediction", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the weekly ASPEST loop: (a) maintain a checkpoint ensemble of the pick model (shared snapshot infrastructure); (b) each week rank the slate by ensemble margin (uncertainty); (c) spend the 'label budget' - analyst deep-review time, e.g. 5 games/week - on the most uncertain games after they resolve, producing gold-standard graded features/notes; (d) fine-tune the model on the reviewed games + self-train on high-confidence pseudo-labels; (e) re-estimate uncertainty and set the week's gate - with market-aware acquisition: prioritize games where ensemble uncertainty is high AND the market line disagrees with the model (the market is a free second labeler).", "gate": "ADAPT accepted if the ASPEST loop beats the static baseline by >= 3 AUACC points on shifted deployment windows AND the analyst-review hours stay within the 5-game budget; else REJECT (keep periodic retraining, drop the active machinery).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2205.13532"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2304.04437", "title": "Monocular 3D Human Pose Estimation for Sports Broadcasts using Partial Sports Field Registration", "normalized_lane": "sports_cv", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a ray-cast 3D pose pipeline for NFL broadcasts: partial sports-field registration to anchor monocular 3D lifting, anchored with Next Gen Stats player (x,y) positions as hard positional constraints (GSE-exclusive data the paper never had) - replacing the ground-plane interpolation step with NGS ground truth - measuring 3D error reduction vs the pure-vision pipeline, directly testing whether GSE's data moat unlocks the kinematic validity the paper was chasing.", "gate": "Ray-cast method must beat MeTRAbs by >=3 cm on 3D error AND >=8 deg on knee-angle error on the synthetic football-field set (matching the paper's own margins: 10.33->6.41 cm, 20.31->9.91 deg) with reprojection error <=3 px, before any real-broadcast pilot; if geometry-injection does not beat MeTRAbs off-the-shelf by those margins, the extra pipeline complexity is unjustified.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2304.05242", "title": "Generation of Threat: Crediting Football Players for Creating Dangerous Actions in an Unbiased Way", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build GSE's sequence-credit engine for red-zone-entry/explosive-play generation: construct NFL threat processes from ball-touch equivalents (targets, carries) per personnel slot + red-zone-entry/explosive-play timestamps, fit a 12-dim Hawkes process with exponential kernels, and compute the four GoT indices per player with parametric-bootstrap SEs - used as sequence-credit features in fantasy projection models (especially for TEs/FBs/role players whose box scores understate contribution) and weekly 'hidden threat generators' DFS content - with opponent-strength and game-state covariates on the baseline intensities (marked Hawkes) and a position-varying danger-area definition.", "gate": "Gate (ADAPT): simulation shows reliable estimation from 600 min (0.4% FP, 18.6% rel. error); case studies must recover both stars and hidden contributors; improvement success = opponent/team confounding reduced (defenders' GoT drops toward the low tier) while offensive rankings stay stable.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2304.05294v5", "title": "Selecting Robust Features for Machine Learning Applications using Multidata Causal Discovery", "normalized_lane": "causal_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Run multidata causal feature selection on the nflverse team-week panel: tigramite M-PC1 over team-seasons (2015-2023) with target = next-week game outcome margin/cover, stringent alpha_PC swept {0.01, 0.001}, min lag 1 week; keep the driver set and train GSE's outcome model on drivers only, with quarterly driver-set refresh - plus stratified multidata discovery: run M-PC1 separately within scheme clusters (pass-heavy vs run-heavy offenses, dome vs outdoor teams) and union the driver sets with cluster-membership interactions, testing whether stratified pooling recovers scheme-specific drivers that global pooling washes out.", "gate": "ADOPT multidata causal feature selection if: (a) driver-set model Brier on 2023-2025 <= all-features Brier using <=50% of features; (b) validation Brier strictly better than lagged-correlation selection at matched feature count; (c) driver sets from odd-season vs even-season ensembles have Jaccard >= 0.5; reject if (b) fails or Jaccard < 0.4 (fall back to per-team discovery).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2304.06333v2", "title": "Priors for Symbolic Regression", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a SPORTS corpus: collect ~100-200 published sports-analytics formulas (passer rating, QBR components, EPA models, DVOA-style expressions, Elo update rules, Pythagorean expectation variants, target-share formulas), parse to operator trees, train the n-gram LM prior (sibling+ancestor phrases, left/right back-off) - then run the selection pipeline: PySR Pareto front -> for each candidate, Laplace-approximated log-evidence with uniform parameter priors + LM log-prior -> rank by -log P(f_i) - log Z, compared against plain accuracy ranking - with a corpus-ablation experiment: train separate pre-2015 and post-2015 priors and test which selects better-generalizing equations for 2024-2025 data.", "gate": "ADOPT the LM-prior selector if its top-3 picks achieve >=10% lower held-out RMSE than the top-3 picks of plain best-fit selection on the 2024-2025 window AND it never ranks a degenerate (constant-only/single-input) equation in the top 5; REJECT if the sports corpus prior underperforms MDL or shows the Nguyen-8 pathology.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2304.09918v2", "title": "Smart Sports Predictions via Hybrid Simulation: NBA Case Study", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Two workstreams: (a) per-predictor lookback-window ablation - sweep trailing windows N in {4,6,8,10,13,17 games} for each core GSE predictor family (EPA/play differentials, success rate, pressure rate) on 2015-2024 nflverse, picking per-predictor N by held-out log-loss; (b) incentive-adjusted season simulation - add rule-based modifiers for weeks 16-18: teams locked into playoff seeds get a strength discount, eliminated-but-alive-for-draft-pick teams get a smaller discount, with the discount magnitudes FIT as parameters by maximizing held-out likelihood on historical meaningless games (separately for 'seed locked' vs 'eliminated', home/away), then checked against observable proxies (starter snap-shares in those games).", "gate": "ADOPT per-predictor windows if, pre-registered: the swept window improves pooled held-out log-loss by >= 0.003 over the fixed window on 2019-2024, with gains in >= 4 of 6 seasons. ADOPT incentive modifiers if they improve log-loss on the 'locked/eliminated' week 16-18 subset by >= 0.01 without degrading the 'meaningful' subset. REJECT either workstream if its gate fails.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2304.12654v1", "title": "CoDi: Co-evolving Contrastive Diffusion Models for Mixed-type Tabular Synthesis", "normalized_lane": "synthetic_data", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Stand up CoDi as the fallback/alternative synthetic-season generator if TabDDPM's cross-type correlations gate fails: same nflverse game-level table but keeping discrete features native (venue type, surface, weather bin, rest category, game-script regime) - continuous diffusion on EPA/pace/market numerics, discrete diffusion on the categorical block, co-evolving conditioning both directions, contrastive negatives via Method 3 (shuffle discrete blocks across games so the triplet loss learns weather x efficiency pairings matter), quantile transform for long-tailed margin/EPA features - with market-aware negatives: pair a game's efficiency vector with the weather/discrete block of a game from a DIFFERENT spread bucket, teaching the model that discrete-continuous correlations are regime-dependent.", "gate": "ADOPT CoDi over TabDDPM if BOTH: (a) real+CoDi-synthetic beats real+TabDDPM-synthetic by >=0.002 log-loss on held-out 2024, OR ties within 0.001 while (b) cross-type correlation MAE is >=10% lower for CoDi; REJECT (stay with TabDDPM) if neither holds, if training instability appears (triplet loss non-convergence across 2+ seeds), or fidelity marginals breach the 5% TVD rule.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2304.14774v3", "title": "A Feature Selection Method Based on Shapley Values Robust to Concept Shift in Regression", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Run SHAPEffects backward elimination on the gse-lab metric set (~60-80 features) with LightGBM + TreeSHAP, margin-of-victory-vs-spread as the regression target: train on seasons <= S-2, validation = season S-1 (current regime), q_low/q_high in {(0.25,0.75),(0.1,0.9)}, keeping the better-validation config - outputting a pruned feature set per season plus a 'regime-casualty report' of eliminated features with their negative-influence magnitude for the DFS packet - with adaptive quantile thresholds set from the validation error distribution's own tail mass, and a classification extension via the same local logic on log-loss residuals (grouping by signed log-loss residual quantiles).", "gate": "Adopt SHAPEffects pruning iff on the 2024 and 2025 held-out test seasons it reduces MAE vs the full-feature baseline by >= 0.15 points AND beats Boruta/Lasso on at least one of the two seasons, with the elimination list stable (>=50% overlap) across the two runs; reject if it merely matches SOTA selectors, eliminates >40% of features, or the dropped-feature sign check fails.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2305.01120v3", "title": "LST-Bench: Benchmarking Log-Structured Tables in the Cloud", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Apply the findings to GSE's Delta lake: (1) default to Delta Lake CoW (read-heavy: weekly bulk feature builds, constant point-in-time reads); (2) maintenance doctrine - schedule Optimize (compaction) + Vacuum after every weekly feature build; (3) write-path discipline - configure the Spark/DuckDB writer for large target file sizes (avoid small-file pathology); (4) track S_DR on weekly feature-build latency and Sunday serving-read p99, alerting if S_DR > 0.1 over 4 weeks as the lake-health KPI; (5) rely on time travel for point-in-time replay tests - plus workload-aware compaction: Z-ordering/compaction keyed on (season, week) so hot recent partitions are optimally laid out while cold history is compacted rarely.", "gate": "ADOPT the maintenance doctrine iff: (i) the no-maintenance run shows S_DR > 0.1 (confirming the degradation mechanism applies to GSE's workload - if no degradation appears at GSE's scale, the doctrine is REJECTED as over-engineering), AND (ii) post-Optimize latency recovers to within 10% of the fresh-table baseline.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2305.01582v3", "title": "Interpretable Machine Learning for Science with PySR and SymbolicRegression.jl", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Wire the PySR pipeline: nflverse play-by-play 2015-2025 -> game/team-season aggregates (net EPA/play, success rate, explosive-play rate, air yards/attempt, pressure rate allowed, sack rate, turnover margin proxy, 3rd-down conversion); operators +,-,x,div,pow,exp,log,sqrt,min/max plus custom sigmoid and relu-like piecewise operators with monotonicity constraint hooks; GP-denoise inputs, multi-population search with adaptive parsimony, select final equation by held-out-season accuracy AND complexity - plus multi-view SR: run two PySR searches in parallel (QB efficiency features, team defensive features), then feed each search's hall-of-fame expressions as custom operator inputs into a third 'fusion' search, testing whether composable discovered sub-metrics beat a single flat search.", "gate": "ADOPT if the discovered closed-form equation beats the better of passer rating / QBR by >=0.05 Pearson r on held-out 2024-2025 seasons AND has <=15 tree nodes (interpretable enough to publish); REJECT if it fails either, or if the top Pareto solutions are all degenerate.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INVENT", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2305.02968v1", "title": "Masked Trajectory Models for Prediction, Representation, and Control (MTM)", "normalized_lane": "selfsupervised_tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Train MTM on NFL 10Hz tracking 2018-2024 as 'states' (22 agents + ball kinematics, snap-relative), 'actions' = per-player frame-to-frame displacements, 'returns' = play EPA / outcome class as a per-play conditioning token - heteromodal regimes (tracking-only, tracking+charting, tracking+charting+odds plays) with missing-modality loss masking - inference modes: (a) forward-dynamics mask -> ball-carrier trajectory forecasting (rushing-yard props); (b) outcome-conditioned generation -> counterfactual play simulation ('what if the safety bites?'); (c) frozen MTM embeddings as features for prop models - with a two-level hierarchy (player-level encoder -> play-level encoder) instead of flat 22-agent sequences, and a 'coverage concept' modality from FTN charting (man/zone/blitz discrete tokens) for coaching queries like 'generate the most likely route combination vs Cover 3'.", "gate": "ADOPT if: (a) heteromodal MTM masked-frame RMSE >= 15% lower than the full-modality-only model on held-out weeks, OR (b) prop-model log-loss improves >= 0.002 with MTM embeddings vs without, on held-out weeks 13-18; REJECT if neither holds.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": ["2507.00028"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2305.03403", "title": "Large Language Models for Automated Data Science: Introducing CAAFE for Context-Aware Automated Feature Engineering", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build 'GSE-CAAFE' as the semantic layer atop the OneBM relational engine: (1) context document with curated schema descriptions of every nflverse/odds table, explicitly stating cutoff semantics ('no column may use post-kickoff information'); (2) candidate generation - LLM proposes <= 20 features/week as pandas code against the relational tables, proposals restricted to pre-kickoff columns by an allowlist filter; (3) execution sandboxed, kept iff validation log-loss improves with a DeLong-style paired test p < 0.05 AND the kickoff-cutoff replay leakage audit passes; (4) analyst review queue with veto - with a sequential keep criterion (paired permutation test with Holm correction) and pre-execution static AST checks rejecting any column reference not in the pre-kickoff allowlist, plus the drift-quarantine list fed as negative context.", "gate": "ADAPT the layer iff (a) 2024 held-out log-loss improves >= 0.003, AND (b) semantic-blinding ablation shows >= 0.002 of that gain is attributable to semantics (LLM > hashed-name run), AND (c) zero leakage-audit failures across all kept features; REJECT if any kept feature fails cutoff replay, if the blinding ablation matches the semantic run, or if > 30% of proposals are faulty code; budget cap <= $50/month LLM spend.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["1706.00327"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2305.03623v1", "title": "Optimizing Hyperparameters with Conformal Quantile Regression", "normalized_lane": "nas_automl", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Replace the GP surrogate in GSE's Optuna/BO HPO loop with a CQR surrogate: quantile GBM over the config space + conformal calibration on a held-out config set, EI acquisition over the conformalized predictive distribution - with multi-fidelity for free (aggregate each config's last-fidelity observation, fidelity = training seasons, plus async successive halving) - and feed the surrogate market-relative config features: each config's log-loss minus the market-implied baseline (de-vigged), optimizing edge-over-market directly with a heteroskedasticity-aware surrogate.", "gate": "ADOPT if: CQR-BO reaches the GP-BO final regret in <=70% of the wall-clock time on the 2023-2025 test HPO runs, AND surrogate calibration error at n>=256 is <= GP's; REJECT if: no wall-clock win, or CQR's early-regime (n<100) miscalibration causes worse candidate selection than GP in the first 50 evaluations.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2312.08528v3"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2305.03780v3", "title": "Boldness-Recalibration for Binary Event Predictions", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Fit boldness-recalibration (LLO delta, gamma) per market on a rolling window (trailing 2 seasons / ~500 games), maximizing prediction SD subject to posterior calibration probability >= 0.90 - evaluated strictly out-of-sample on the next season/slate (fixing the paper's in-sample flaw), falling back to plain MLE-LLO if the constrained optimization fails - serving recalibration parameters versioned per market and refreshed weekly as a final transform before publication or Kelly sizing, gated on out-of-sample log loss and CLV (not SD), with an 'out-of-sample boldness' extension replacing the BIC posterior with a held-out reliability test at 95%.", "gate": "Adopt B-R as the publication-layer recalibrator iff, across the 5 walk-forward seasons, 90%-threshold B-R achieves out-of-sample log loss <= MLE-LLO log loss (within 0.001) AND mean SD >= 1.15x raw SD AND no season shows ECE degradation > 0.01 vs raw; reject (keep plain MLE-LLO/temperature scaling) if B-R loses on log loss in >=2 of 5 seasons or optimization failures exceed 2% of weekly refits.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2305.05665", "title": "ImageBind: One Embedding Space To Bind Them All", "normalized_lane": "multimodal_fusion", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build one joint embedding space binding (a) tracking play embeddings, (b) broadcast-video clip embeddings, (c) commentary-audio embeddings, (d) play-by-play/injury-report text - encoders: inflated ViT on 2s clips, 128-bin mel-spectrogram Transformer on commentary, NEW tracking encoder (per-play 22 players x T frames x [x,y,s,v,dir] -> 1D-conv + Transformer), frozen CLIP/OpenCLIP text encoder; symmetric InfoNCE over (video, M) pairs - then test the paper's core claim by re-anchoring: train the binding with (tracking, M) pairs instead of video-anchored, testing whether emergent (video<->text) and (audio<->text) alignment IMPROVES, since tracking is the causal ground truth of what happened on the field.", "gate": "ACCEPT: (a) emergent text->tracking retrieval Recall@10 >= 2x the keyword-search baseline on the 500-query set; AND (b) engine EPA model with ImageBind-style tracking embeddings beats handcrafted tracking features by >=2% MAE on a held-out season; REJECT: retrieval < 1.5x baseline or no EPA gain - then the binding adds nothing over a Perceiver-style joint model and the cheaper path wins.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2305.09126v3", "title": "Transfer Learning for Causal Effect Estimation", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Adopt the 'never naively merge domains' rule for cross-era/league causal questions (e.g., effect of the new kickoff rule on expected return EPA): fit propensity + outcome nuisance on 2018-2023 source data, then l1 bias-correction of the difference on 2024-2025 target data, then DR plug-in for the ACE (3-headed TARNet + DR variant) - with a pre-flight diagnostic: fit l1-regularized propensity models in both domains and compare supports, proceeding only if the difference is sparse; otherwise report target-only with wide uncertainty - and an adaptive l1-TCL extension using source-domain fitted support overlap as empirical-Bayes l1 weights.", "gate": "ADOPT l1-TCL for a GSE causal question only if the pre-flight support-overlap diagnostic shows a sparse difference AND the semi-synthetic test shows <=0.7x target-only error; otherwise REJECT transfer and report target-only estimates with honest uncertainty.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2305.14612", "title": "Automated ACL injury-risk scoring from 2D video", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Replicate automated landing/cutting-mechanics scoring for NFL draft prospects from Combine drill video: run RTMPose per frame on vertical-jump/broad-jump landings and 3-cone/shuttle cuts, replicate the 5-feature extraction + threshold scoring, then replace the subjective AHP weights with supervised weights - penalized logistic regression of actual prospect lower-body injuries (first-2-season IR) on the five feature scores across 3+ draft classes - turning a screening score into a calibrated injury-probability model, extended to cutting mechanics (the more football-relevant ACL mechanism) with knee-valgus-at-plant as a sixth feature.", "gate": "Gate (numeric): ADAPT if the replication achieves automated-vs-manual ICC >= 0.75 on the composite score; REJECT if ICC < 0.6 (2D pose noise swamps the clinical signal) or if the AHP-weighted composite fails to separate known groups (p > 0.05 for any pair).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2305.14656v1", "title": "RSRM: Reinforcement Symbolic Regression Machine", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Mine top-100 GSE-SR programs for frequent sub-trees (min support 10%); promote top-3 to named operators (e.g. softplus-like, saturating-ratio); rerun discovery with the extended operator set and test whether new metrics get simpler/shorter - plus bandit-style allocation across islands using each island's score distribution (kill islands whose upper quantile trails) - and close the loop with analyst-named operators: present the top mined motifs to Garrett with proposed names ('the dome factor,' 'garbage-time decay') and let him bless/rename them before they enter the operator set, creating publishable GSE intellectual property.", "gate": "ADOPT operator invention if the extended-operator run reaches equal-or-better OOD NMSE with >=20% shorter median expressions (compression without accuracy loss); REJECT if invented operators are used in <5% of final programs or diversity collapses.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2305.16291v2", "title": "Voyager: An Open-Ended Embodied Agent with Large Language Models", "normalized_lane": "llm_agents_ai_scientist", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt Voyager into a lifelong signal library layered on the AI-Scientist discovery loop: (1) skill library schema - vector DB keyed by embedding of each verified signal's natural-language description, value = executable backtest code + 2025-holdout metrics + journal entry, every entry passing the discovery loop's gate before insertion with a deterministic verifier (script re-runs the code, checks Delta-Brier >= 0.002); (2) automatic curriculum for signals - nightly prompt reviewing library coverage (thin lanes: weather, special teams, referee crews) proposing the next discovery task of appropriate difficulty; (3) iterative prompting with three feedback types (backtest output, tracebacks, deterministic re-run gate), giving up after 4 stuck rounds; (4) top-5 related signals injected into the idea generator's prompt - plus a skill-graph with dependency edges letting the curriculum explicitly propose 'gap' tasks in lanes with no nodes.", "gate": "ADOPT if: the with-library arm discovers >=4 new gate-passing signals in 14 nights (vs <=2 in the no-library arm), the deterministic verifier rejects >=95% of curriculum tasks that fail re-run, and library retrieval (top-5) is cited in >=50% of successful proposals; REJECT the library design if the no-library arm matches within 25%, verifier precision < 90%, or the curriculum proposes duplicate/covered tasks >30% of the time.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INVENT", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2408.06292v3"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2305.16735", "title": "Angular Combining of Forecasts of Probability Distributions", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build combined CDFs over margin (and total) via angular averaging: for each game collect predictive CDFs from engine v5.2.7 (bootstrapped historical margin errors), the de-vigged market distribution (spread/total + historical line-error distribution), and the Elo margin model; optimize theta per market by minimizing trailing-8-week CRPS on an expanding window (re-estimated weekly), with a weighted variant (weights proportional to 1/CRPS per expert) and fallback theta = 67.5 deg (the paper's best fixed angle) - then make theta state-dependent: fit theta as a function of ensemble disagreement via gradient boosting on historical CRPS, turning the scalar knob into an adaptive dispersion controller (high disagreement -> horizontal-like low theta; low disagreement -> vertical-like high theta).", "gate": "ADOPT angular combining if optimized-theta angular averaging beats the linear opinion pool by >=1% mean CRPS over the two-season window AND 95% interval coverage stays within [0.92, 0.97]; REJECT if it fails to beat vertical averaging or if theta optimization is unstable (optimized theta bouncing between <10 deg and >80 deg week-to-week, indicating noise-fitting).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2305.20077v1", "title": "Managed Geo-Distributed Feature Store: Architecture and System Design", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build a GSE Feature Store (Feast + Delta Lake): (1) offline store - Delta tables on object storage keyed (entity_id, event_timestamp, creation_timestamp) for player_id, team_id, game_id, week_season; (2) online store - Redis holding latest (event_ts, creation_ts) per entity with Algorithm-2 merge semantics; (3) initial feature sets - QB efficiency rollups (trailing 4/8/17 weeks), OL/DL pressure rates, team pace & pass-rate-over-expected, market features (spread/CLV movement, line-opened timestamps as event_timestamp), weather; (4) point-in-time joins - every training row joins features as-of ts0 - feature_delay with per-source delay configs (NGS re-runs: 48h; odds: 0); (5) lineage (feature_set_version -> model_version -> prediction_id) for every published pick - plus snapshot-based deterministic replay: content-addressed snapshot manifests (entity_id -> (event_ts, creation_ts, sha)) after each materialization, giving a byte-exact 'what the model knew at kickoff' proof.", "gate": "ADOPT the design iff: (i) point-in-time retrieval reproduces hand-computed features exactly (100% row equality) on the 2023-2025 replay, AND (ii) Redis-online vs Delta-offline parity holds at 100% over a one-week simulated serving window, AND (iii) model retrained on store features shows no test-window log-loss degradation beyond 0.5% absolute; serving p99: Redis point lookups <= 50ms p99 during the simulated Sunday window.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2306.00840v1", "title": "What Model Does MuZero Learn?", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a planning-bounds harness for the NFL play simulator: (1) train the learned play simulator; (2) replicate the paper's audit - sample game states from the historical play-call distribution and measure the simulator's value (predicted EPA) error vs realized EPA as a function of rollout horizon (1-8 s) and play-call novelty (route-concept embedding distance from the historical play-call distribution); (3) enforce the paper's fix - MCTS over play calls uses a strong policy prior = the empirical league play-call distribution (down/distance/formation-conditioned), logging TV divergence between prior and MCTS visit distribution as a health metric; (4) gate any 4th-down/go-for-it or play-call optimizer on this audit - then test the paper's untested hypothesis: compare value-equivalence vs reconstruction-based (Dreamer-style) vs hybrid training on the same simulator using the novelty-decile error audit.", "gate": "ADOPT the prior-constrained planning design if: (a) simulator error grows monotonically with horizon AND with play novelty, AND (b) league-prior-constrained MCTS backtests >= +0.05 EPA/play over the historical policy on 2024 held-out weeks, AND (c) uniform-prior MCTS does not beat it; reject the planning use-case if the simulator's error on novel plays is flat or if prior-constrained search cannot beat history.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": ["2608.08600", "2505.20922", "2609.22641", "2605.28816", "2406.15836", "2003.10520"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2306.01740v4", "title": "Not feeling the buzz: Correction study of mispricing and inefficiency in online sportsbooks", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "As engine-honesty infrastructure, install an odds QA and evaluation protocol: (1) odds-sanity filter in the market-capture pipeline - drop/flag any row where a book's quote exceeds the cross-book best by more than 3 SD of the best-minus-mean spread, and any single-book line that is an extreme outlier vs consensus (z-score on implied probability), before backtest data is written; (2) adopt the random-betting bootstrap (100k trials) as the mandatory significance screen for any published GSE strategy P&L - report p_bs alongside ROI, never post a strategy with p_bs > 0.05; (3) cap per-bet Kelly fractions (<= 0.25x full Kelly) to bound single-row data-error damage; (4) extend the paper with an NFL 'buzz factor': Mincer-Zarnowitz mispricing regression on NFL moneylines using a crowd-attention proxy (beat-writer/news volume + X engagement 48h before kickoff) plus a rank/Elo-distance term.", "gate": "ADOPT the QA protocol (no further test needed - the filters are cheap insurance); for the reproducible test: if dropping flagged odds rows changes the 2025 backtest ROI of any published GSE strategy by more than +/-2 pp, or flips any strategy from p_bs < 0.05 to > 0.05, treat the published P&L as data-error-contaminated and re-issue corrected figures before posting any new picks.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2306.06252", "title": "Feature Programming for Multivariate Time Series Prediction", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Implement the three operators as pure pandas functions on the NFL team panel: difference(s1, s2, smooth_w) (rolling-mean smooth then subtract), window(s, lookback, stat) (mean/min/max/std at 3/4/8-week lookbacks), shift(s, delta-tau) (bye-week and rest-differential lags) - 0th-order = weekly box-score and market features, 1st-order = 4-week momentum of offensive efficiency and spread-vs-closing-line drift, 2nd-order = acceleration (momentum itself accelerating), plus discretionary 0th-order injections (weather, injury-report counts, travel distance) - all operators AST-verified past-only, with a pruning stage the paper lacks (|corr|>0.9 dedup + TreeSHAP-interventional recursion) - and ablate the order hierarchy itself: full order-upgrade rule vs the same operators applied flat (matched feature count), comparing walk-forward XGBoost R^2/log-loss to decide whether the {position, momentum, acceleration} discipline or just the operator bank ships.", "gate": "ADAPT if: >=0.003 held-out NFL log-loss improvement on 2025 games versus the basic-features baseline, with all operators provably causal (AST-verified past-only), feature generation time <5% of downstream training time, and the pruning stage removing >=50% of generated features without hurting validation performance; REJECT if no gate improvement under walk-forward splits, leakage scan fails, or the pruned extended set performs no better than hand-built rolling features.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2306.08946v2", "title": "Bootstrap Aggregation for Time Series Causal Discovery", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Discover causal structure in team/season time series (which lineup-usage, pace, and matchup variables drive EPA; momentum/regime questions; injury->performance pathways): tigramite (PCMCI+ reference implementation) + moving-block bootstrap wrapper, B = 100, edge-wise majority vote, cycle-breaking post-pass (drop lowest-confidence edges in cycles), embarrassingly parallel across bootstrap replicates, on nflverse weekly team-level series (2015-2024) - with weighted voting by per-run model fit (conditional-independence test p-value profile or BIC score) instead of one-graph-one-vote, so low-quality bootstrap draws count less.", "gate": "Adopt if bagged-PCMCI+ beats single-run PCMCI+ on adjacency F1 by >=10% relative on the semi-synthetic test with contemporaneous-orientation precision >= single-run's; reject otherwise (if bagging only helps in the paper's synthetic regimes, skip the compute bill).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.02035v1", "title": "Ranking with Abstention", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a pairwise ranking head over weekly games: score s(game) = predicted edge, trained with the exponential surrogate on game pairs (y = which game was the better bet ex post); distance-based abstention - for game pairs with feature distance <= gamma (tuned), assign equal rank (same publish tier rather than artificial ordering), tuning gamma, c on validation to minimize abstention loss - combined with confidence-based abstention: abstain from ordering a pair if EITHER ||x-x'|| <= gamma (too close to call) OR the learned sigma/uncertainty is high, testing whether the two abstention criteria are complementary or redundant.", "gate": "ADAPT if the gamma-abstaining ranker beats strict edge ordering on test-window top-5 ROI by >=1pp with gamma, c stable across validation folds; reject if the optimal gamma collapses to 0 (no abstention) - then distance-based abstention adds nothing and plain edge ordering stands.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2104.08236v1", "2104.08281v1"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.02139v1", "title": "Extending the Dixon and Coles model: an application to women's football data", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Use the Sarmanov/ANS machinery as a challenger joint-distribution model for NFL exact scores and totals: apply the framework to (home TDs, away TDs) bivariate counts from nflverse 2015-2025 with NB marginals and team attack/defence log-linear means (log(theta) = home + att + def, sum-to-zero constraint on defence), fit by numerical MLE - the fitted joint pmf gives exact-score probabilities -> derive totals and spread distributions that respect dependence (negative correlation in low-scoring games), compared against GSE's current Skellam/independent baseline - with time-weighted Sarmanov (reintroduce exponential time weighting into the MLE so recent matches dominate) and covariate-driven omega (dependence as a function of game context: total line, weather, divisional matchup).", "gate": "Adopt the Sarmanov/ANS challenger only if: (a) the reproduction confirms the paper's mechanism (ANS AIC-best on women's data, correlation range reproduced); AND (b) on the NFL TD-count transfer, Sarmanov beats independent NB on out-of-sample mean per-game log-likelihood over 2023-2025 with p < 0.05 (paired test), AND (c) implied-total calibration shows no degradation vs the current production baseline.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.02188v5", "title": "G-score: Variance-Aware Fantasy Basketball Valuation", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Compute for every NFL fantasy-relevant player: weekly fantasy-point mean mu(q) and week-to-week SD tau(q) from nflverse 3-season rolling game logs, cross-player sigma by position; G-value = (mu(q) - replacement_level) / sqrt(sigma^2 + kappa*tau^2), kappa re-estimated for NFL weekly scoring - use cases: DFS value tiers (G per $1k salary), season-long draft rankings, GPP lineup construction - with contest-dependent kappa: fit kappa separately for cash games (expect kappa>0, variance penalized) vs GPPs (expect kappa<0, variance rewarded), backtesting GPP lineups built with negative-kappa G-values vs standard projections in realized DK tournaments.", "gate": "ADAPT if: the backtest gate passes (G >=12% win rate, beats Z by >=5 pp) on actual historical weekly scores; REJECT the kappa=1.04 constant for NFL - re-estimate kappa per position/scoring format; if estimated kappa ~= 0, the method reduces to Z-score and adds nothing.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.02752v2", "title": "Offline Reinforcement Learning with Imbalanced Datasets", "normalized_lane": "rl_sequential_decisions", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build retrieval-based CQL for thin-regime weeks: quantify imbalance by histogramming weekly slate states (2021-2024) over regime features (slate size, mean total, weather flags, holiday) and fitting a power law to identify thin regimes (<30 samples); build D_aux from all historical weeks 2015-2024 (pre-2021 weeks excluded from main training become the auxiliary pool) + bootstrap-perturbed copies of thin-regime weeks (jitter edges/odds within measurement noise); state encoder (small MLP over slate features -> 32-dim embedding) with precomputed FAISS index over D_aux, retrieving k=8 nearest neighbors per thin-regime training state (MIPS); train RB-CQL (CQL loss on main data + retrieved (s,a,r,s') tuples upweighted for thin regimes) - with a learned retriever: train the state encoder contrastively so retrieved neighbors are those whose hindsight-optimal stake matches, not just whose features match.", "gate": "ADOPT iff on 2024 thin-regime weeks RB-CQL beats plain CQL ROI by >=3pp with overall-season ROI no worse than -1pp vs plain CQL; otherwise REJECT (retrieval complexity not justified).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2006.04779"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.05199v1", "title": "Reject Option Models Comprising Out-of-Distribution Detection", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the double-score no-bet gate: score_A = misclassification detector (calibrated P(engine's pick is wrong | features) from a meta-model on past engine errors); score_B = OOD discriminator (distance of the game's feature vector from the training distribution - Mahalanobis / kNN distance in feature space, or isolation-forest score); no-bet rule: skip if a*score_A + b*score_B > tau, with (a, b, tau) tuned on 2024 - learning the (a,b) weights by direct optimization of selective risk at target coverage (fit the linear combination as a 2-parameter logistic model on past engine outcomes) rather than hand-tuning, and testing the variance estimate as a third score (triple-score).", "gate": "ADOPT if the double-score gate cuts selective risk by >=25% relative to the better of the two single-score gates at the SAME coverage (+/-2 pp), on 2024 time-ordered data; otherwise REJECT. The single decisive number: selective-risk reduction >= 25% vs best single score at matched coverage.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.08768", "title": "Decentralized Prediction Markets and Sports Books", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "As engine-honesty infrastructure, build a marginal-price oracle on GSE's multi-book NFL snapshots: fit a logarithmic-utility AMM curve through each book's bid/ask (moneyline) quotes; the oracle's mid marginal price becomes a synthetic consensus; flag books whose quotes deviate from the oracle by more than the paper's implied fee band (~1%) as candidate mispricings for manual review - plus a liquidity diagnostic: invert the framework to back out the implied LP fee gamma* each book is effectively charging from observed cross-book spreads, tracking gamma* over the week as a market-tightness index (falling gamma* into the weekend = sharpening market) - and a time-varying liquidity parameter fit from GSE's line-move data, turning the paper's LP-design tool into a book-profiling instrument (sharp low-fee venues vs high-fee recreational books) for line-shopping guidance.", "gate": "ADAPT is confirmed if the oracle-mid predicts the direction of subsequent book-specific line moves at >=58% on the 4-week sample (paired test vs 50%, p < 0.05); REJECT the oracle as a mispricing detector if the hit rate is within noise of 50% - then the log-utility curve adds nothing over a simple cross-book median.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.10303", "title": "Analyzing Sports Commentary in Order to Automatically Recognize Events and Extract Insights", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build an availability classifier from beat-reporter language: scrape beat-writer tweets/articles (Schefter, Rapoport, team beat writers) + NFL official injury-report text; label sentences with availability outcomes from subsequent injury reports (Out/Doubtful/Questionable/Active); fine-tune DeBERTa-v3-base on the sentence-classification task, 80/10/10 split by SEASON (not shuffled), target = P(player misses next game | news sentence); serve hourly over the beat-writer firehose - when P(miss) crosses 0.6 for a starter, emit an availability signal into the pick engine 15-60 min before books move - with a domain-specific 'injury-language' encoder via contrastive pretraining on paired sentences ('limited in practice' vs 'full participant'), distilled into a 30M-param model for sub-second live inference.", "gate": "ADOPT the availability classifier if: F1 >= 0.80 on 2024-season beat-writer sentences AND the classifier's P(miss) signal, backtested as a line-move predictor, anticipates official injury-report designation changes >= 30 minutes ahead of the market move in >= 55% of cases (n >= 50 cases); REJECT if F1 < 0.70 or the lead-time test fails.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.10411v1", "title": "Stop Simulating! Efficient Computation of Tournament Winning Probabilities", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Replace Monte Carlo with exact fixed-bracket DP for the 14-team NFL playoff bracket: P(team advances past round r+1) = sum over possible opponents o of P(o reaches round r) * P(team beats o), byes carried forward with probability 1 - pragmatic v1: exact bracket DP applied to the current projected seeding each week, published alongside the existing Monte Carlo as a cross-check; recompute weekly and live (clamping completed games to probability 1); output per-team P(win division), P(make playoffs), P(first-round bye), P(reach divisional/SB), P(win Super Bowl) with zero simulation noise - plus exact enumeration of division-race outcomes (<=4 relevant games per division race: 2^4=16 to 3^4=81 combinations) for exact P(win division), and exact joint probabilities (P(Team A AND Team B both reach the Super Bowl)) for pricing correlated playoff futures.", "gate": "ADOPT if: the exact bracket DP reproduces brute-force enumeration on toy brackets exactly, runs in <1s on the full 14-team bracket, and on the 2023-2025 backtest the 100k-run Monte Carlo shows max team-level Super Bowl probability error >0.25% points in at least 2 of 3 seasons (proving simulation noise is worth eliminating); REJECT (keep Monte Carlo) if GSE's playoff probabilities are consumed only as coarse tiers AND the Monte Carlo serves double duty producing joint distributions the marginal DP cannot supply.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.11777", "title": "Prediction of Handball Matches with Statistically Enhanced Learning via Estimated Team Strengths", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Implement the SEL pattern on NFL the right way: estimate as-of-date latent offensive/defensive strengths via an expanding-window count model on nflverse scores (2006-present), updated weekly, never using future games; feed them as features alongside market features into the existing gradient-boosting stack - using a negative-binomial (NFL-appropriate over-dispersed count) rather than COM-Poisson for points, keeping the paper's decoupling (strength model != outcome model) so each can be diagnosed separately, and replicating the with/without comparison honestly on strictly as-of-date data (2022-2025 test window) - then close the loop the paper left open: jointly model strength dynamics and outcomes with a state-space model (Kalman/particle filter) where latent attack/defense strengths evolve week to week and the outcome likelihood is the observation, comparing its as-of-date Brier against the two-stage SEL+GBM.", "gate": "ADOPT the SEL-pattern strength features if the test shows >=0.004 Brier gain with verified as-of-date provenance (audit: no game in the strength fit postdates the predicted game); REJECT if the gain is <0.002 or if any leakage is found in the provenance audit; do not cite the paper's 81.32% / 79.57% figures anywhere - they are not as-of-date results.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.11780v2", "title": "Beep: Balancing Effectiveness and Efficiency when Finding Multivariate Patterns in Racket Sports", "normalized_lane": "mixed", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt 'hit' -> NFL play, 'rally' -> drive: attributes = {down, distance-bucket, personnel, formation, play-type (run/pass + direction/gap or route concept), result-bucket (EPA bin), quarter, score-differential bucket}, continuous values discretized into quantile bins - run Beep per (team x phase) over 2023-2026 nflverse play-by-play (e.g., opponent's defensive play-calling when leading/trailing), outputting a pattern set per opponent for the weekly scout report ('when in 11 personnel on 2nd-and-long, DAL DC blitzes from slot in 34% of cases - pattern P17, support 41 drives') - with a supervised-MDL variant: score candidate patterns not only by description-length reduction but by outcome association (penalty/bonus term lambda*|E[EPA | pattern present] - E[EPA]|), turning unsupervised tendency mining into a weakly-supervised edge detector for matchup modeling.", "gate": "ADAPT-accept iff on the 2025 held-out drives Beep achieves Delta-L% >= 15% vs singleton baseline AND |P| <= 60 patterns per team-season (analyst-manageable) with runtime <= 30 min per team-season on GSE hardware; otherwise reject the adaptation.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INVENT", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.13116v1", "title": "Pathway: a fast and flexible unified stream data processing framework", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "No immediate build - GSE's signal ingestion is batch (weekly). Adopt the parity principle as GSE policy: any future real-time feature path (live odds ticks, injury-news feeds) must run the same logic as the batch path (unified engine, replay-identical results; lambda architecture rejected by precedent) - backfilling as the feature-definition workflow (backfill-then-resume when a feature bug is found) - and formalize a 'frozen-prefix contract' for the feature layer: pin snapshot hashes of weeks 1-17, allow recomputation only of the head week, assert prefix-hash equality in CI (a 1-day test harness giving Pathway's replay determinism on the existing batch pipeline without adopting any new engine).", "gate": "For any future real-time GSE path: ADOPT a streaming approach iff a candidate passes the parity test (bit-identical batch prefix + resumed stream vs from-scratch batch) AND its 95th-percentile event-to-feature latency on GSE's tick rate is <= 1 second at sustained throughput; REJECT any design requiring separate batch and streaming logic.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.13807v1", "title": "Sports Betting: an application of neural networks and modern portfolio theory to the English Premier League", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "As engine-honesty infrastructure, implement multivariate simultaneous Kelly (Eq. 13) as GSE's portfolio staking layer: inputs = engine outcome probabilities p-bar and best-available odds o-bar across books; objective max p-bar'log(1 + W'l-bar - sum l_i*1), constraints sum l_i <= 1, l-bar >= 0; solve with SQP (scipy) - concave, converges in seconds per slate - with the Kelly fraction calibrated the paper's way (Dirichlet(1) simulations over engine backtest picks on validation seasons, choosing the fraction maximizing median final wealth), and an adaptive fraction: make the Kelly fraction a function of recent calibration error (shrink f when the engine's probability estimates are miscalibrated, expand when calibrated).", "gate": "Adopt fractional multivariate Kelly as GSE's staking layer if, on 2025 holdout, it beats flat staking on final wealth with max drawdown <= flat's AND the wealth p-value < 0.10 (a stricter bar than the paper met); if it fails, keep flat/fractional-single-bet Kelly and retain the paper as the reference implementation for the multivariate formulation.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.15422v2", "title": "Is One Epoch All You Need For Multi-Fidelity Hyperparameter Optimization?", "normalized_lane": "nas_automl", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Add the 1-epoch-equivalent baseline to GSE's HPO harness: for neural models, 1 epoch screen + top-3 full train; for GBDTs, the analog is N=50 trees (or 2-season fidelity) screen + top-3 full train; log epochs/season-fits consumed vs final log-loss - with policy: no multi-fidelity scheduler (FastBO, halving, ASHA) is adopted unless it beats this baseline on both final log-loss AND total compute - plus a two-stage screen: 1-epoch rank for speed PLUS learning-curve slope (improvement from epoch 1->3) as a second feature, selecting top-K by a weighted score, separating slow-starting good configs from truly bad ones.", "gate": "ADOPT the baseline as mandatory if: on GSE's tabular task, the min-fidelity screen's top-3 contains a config within 0.002 log-loss of the full-search best while using <=10% of the fits; REJECT the paper's transfer claim if: min-fidelity rank correlation with full-fidelity rank is <0.5 for GBDT configs (screen is noise), or the top-3 misses the full-search best by >0.005 log-loss.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.16642v2", "title": "A Spectral Approach for the Dynamic Bradley-Terry Model", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a KRC module for NFL weekly power ratings: items = 32 teams; outcomes = game results with game dates; Gaussian kernel, bandwidth selected by walk-forward accuracy (~1 season of effective memory, tuned on 2015-2025 nflverse); stationary distribution pi-hat(t) as a weekly power-rating vector, converted to win probabilities via the BT link pi_j/(pi_i+pi_j); implement Algorithm 2 (rank-one online update with the group inverse) so ratings refresh after each game in O(n^2) without refitting - usable for in-week updates - with covariate-augmented KRC: weight each game's kernel contribution by a matchup-specific factor (rest differential, QB injury flag, dome/outdoor), i.e. K_h(t,t_k)*w(x_k) with w learned.", "gate": "ADOPT KRC as a weekly power-rating component if it beats the repo's existing dynamic rating by >=1.0pp pooled winner accuracy over 2015-2025 AND beats Elo on the same window; ADAPT if it matches but does not beat - keep the online-update machinery (Algorithm 2) as the fast in-week refresh; REJECT if it underperforms static RC or Elo on NFL data.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2307.16895", "title": "Conformal PID Control for Time Series Prediction", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Upgrade ACI to PID: keep the alpha_t integrator from Adaptive Conformal Inference; add P-term eta_P*(err_t - alpha) on the score quantile and a scorecaster q-hat_{t+1} = regression of next-week residual-quantile on [weather bucket, QB-change flag, rest differential, December flag, trailing error]; saturating integrator r_t = c*tanh(sum errors / c) to bound runaway; tune (eta_P, eta_I, c) on 2023-2024, validate on 2025 - with learned saturation (scale c learned from data: larger c in stable regimes, smaller c when the scorecaster fires) and market-aware scorecaster features (line movement into the weekend predicts engine error).", "gate": "ADAPT if: shock-stretch coverage improves >=10pp over I-only ACI at <=115% mean width; REJECT the scorecaster component if it adds width without coverage gain - keep the P+I controller (still strictly better than I-only).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2106.00170"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2308.01523v2", "title": "Miss It Like Messi: Extracting Value from Off-Target Shots in Soccer", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Three NFL adaptations in priority order: (1) kicker FG dispersion model - each FG attempt's miss vector (lateral/vertical miss distance from the uprights' center) as a player-specific hierarchical mixture over a coarse spatial grid (the paper's saturate-then-prune recipe), with a coordinate-based make-probability surface (logistic in miss vector); metric RB-FG% (true make probability marginalized over the dispersion process, shrunk toward global components); (2) QB throw-placement surface - NGS/tracking ball arrival coordinates vs receiver position, per-QB placement error as a hierarchical mixture, catch-probability-as-function-of-placement as the PostXg analog (a generative upgrade over CPOE's Bernoulli residual); (3) punt placement model over landing coordinates with a field-position-value surface - plus context-conditional components (mixture weights depend on game context: score differential, pressure/down, weather) and learned per-player covariance scaling via hierarchical variational inference.", "gate": "ADAPT into GSE's accuracy metrics only if: (a) the mechanism check reproduces >=2x stability improvement of the generative metrics over outcome-only baselines on public soccer data; AND (b) on NFL kicking data, year-over-year correlation of RB-FG% with next-season actual FG% beats prior-season raw FG% by >=0.10 in absolute correlation over 2020-2024; AND (c) the miss-vector data source is charted reliably.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2308.02414v3", "title": "A State-Space Perspective on Modelling and Inference for Online Skill Rating", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build an NFL team-rating module ('abile-for-NFL'): bivariate attack/defence SSM - per-team skill x^i = (x^{att,i}, x^{def,i}) with Brownian dynamics; emission = bivariate Poisson with lambda_1 = exp(alpha^h + x^{att,h} - x^{def,a}), lambda_2 = exp(alpha^a + x^{att,a} - x^{def,h}), lambda_3 = exp(beta); two parallel inference engines - (i) Extended Kalman (O(1) per game) for live ratings, (ii) discrete fHMM with S=200-500 states for robustness; EM calibration with closed-form sigma_0, tau M-steps - with an NFL-specific emission: correlated Gaussian margin-of-victory emission instead of low-count Poisson, team-specific rate tau^i with separate tau_off-season vs tau_in-season (single Brownian tau cannot capture within-season stability and off-season churn), and OU mean-reverting dynamics tested against Brownian via marginal likelihood comparison.", "gate": "ADOPT if: on the rolling 3-train/1-test nflverse protocol, the bivariate attack/defence SSM achieves mean test average-NLL improvement >= 0.01 over the Elo-Davidson baseline across all three test windows AND no window shows degradation; REJECT if: the SSM fails to beat Elo-Davidson on >=2 of 3 test windows, or the attack/defence decomposition adds no interpretable signal beyond the single-skill SSM.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2308.03810v2", "title": "AdaER: An Adaptive Experience Replay Approach for Continual Lifelong Learning", "normalized_lane": "continual_online_learning", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Interference-scored replay for the weekly GBM refit: each week, after fitting the challenger model on the new week's games only (one cheap LightGBM fit on 16 games), score every game in the trailing history buffer by s(m) = loss(challenger) - loss(champion) per game; build the refit training set as: new week + top-p interfered historical games + class-balanced reservoir of the rest - with E-BRS buffer maintenance: per-stratum balance (spread band x season-half) instead of pure recency, protecting high-s(m) games from eviction - plus forward-looking interference: score buffer games by predicted interference with the upcoming slate (challenger trained, then s(m) measured on a proxy of next week's games like last season's same-week matchups), selecting buffer games most 'at risk' from the upcoming regime.", "gate": "ADOPT the AdaER-style buffer (interference selection + stratum balancing) into the weekly refit if on 2020-2025 walk-forward: (i) P3 beats P2 (plain replay) on >=3 of the 4 metrics, (ii) worst-4-week Brier improves by >=0.002, (iii) no metric degrades by more than 0.001 vs P2; REJECT if P3 ~= P2; reject the stratum-balancing half independently if it degrades calibration (ECE increase >0.005).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2308.05263", "title": "1172 Solving the Forecast Combination Puzzle", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Install two ensemble-comparison disciplines: (1) in every backtest comparing weighting schemes, REPLACE standard DM/SPA p-values with the two-step-aware test (simulate the generalized-chi critical value per eq. 10; B=10,000 draws; if infeasible, report realized loss differences WITHOUT significance claims, citing Theorem 4.1(iii) as the reason); (2) one-step weight learning as a design rule - when building any learned-weight aggregator, optimize the weights on the COMBINATION's loss in the same optimization pass as any other free parameters, tracking the one-step vs two-step loss gap on trailing seasons as a standing diagnostic; plus a weight-distance bar: before any weighting-scheme comparison, compute ||w-hat_a - w-hat_b|| against the O(T^{-1/4}) bar - if below the bar, skip the comparison (kills wasted backtest cycles).", "gate": "ADAPT the one-step-over-two-step design rule into every future ensemble proposal; ADAPT the two-step-aware testing protocol if the simulated-critical-value test achieves near-nominal size on a placebo (null) backtest on GSE data; REJECT any future 'equal weights are optimal for GSE' claim that rests on a standard significance test of a two-step comparison - Theorem 4.1(iii) voids that evidence.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2308.05566v1", "title": "AutoGluon-TimeSeries: AutoML for Probabilistic Time Series Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "nas_automl", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Forecast team-strength / points-scored-allowed trajectories: panel of 32 teams x weekly offensive/defensive EPA, success rate, market-implied ratings; targets = next-week team EPA distributions (quantiles 0.1/0.5/0.9) feeding the margin/total models as features - TimeSeriesPredictor(prediction_length=1..4, known_covariates=['is_home','rest_days','spread']), static features = team, past-only covariates = injuries/EPA lags; best_quality with 4h budget once per offseason, reduced preset (statistical + tabular members only) with 30-min budget in-season; calibration bridge: recalibrate AG-TS quantile forecasts with GSE's CQR/isotonic code on rolling-origin OOF outputs; weekly batch job Tuesday mornings into the engine feature store - plus a market-aware ensemble member: a forecaster with the betting market's implied team strength (de-vigged spread/total) as a known-future covariate.", "gate": "ADOPT if: AG-TS wQL on 2023-2025 is >=5% lower (relative) than the best single-family baseline AND the full fit costs <=100 CPU-hours; REJECT if: wQL improvement <5% relative, or quantile coverage on the test window deviates >3pp from nominal at any reported level after recalibration, or weekly refit exceeds the Tuesday-morning batch window.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2308.10231v5", "title": "Static and Dynamic BART for Rank-Order Data", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Port ARROBART to NFL weekly team strength: latent scores z_{i,t} = true strength of team i in week t; observation = weekly game outcomes via a score/margin likelihood (point differential ~ N(z_i - z_j + HFA, sigma^2_game)) replacing the rank observation model; latent AR(1)-BART transition z_{i,t} = f(z_{i,t-1}, covariates) + noise with covariates = injury-adjusted roster value, rest days, EPA/play rolling means, FTN charting splits; Gibbs inference (element-wise latent sampling + BART backfitting), S=25 trees - with a regime-switching BART transition: f_regime(z_{t-1}, covariates) where regime in {stable, shock} is a latent binary state triggered by QB injury / coaching change indicators, producing the bimodal jump behavior the paper's smooth BART-AR cannot.", "gate": "ADOPT the BART-dynamic strength model if it beats the linear AR baseline by >=0.003 mean log-loss on weeks 12-18, 2015-2025 pooled, AND wins Kendall tau vs end-of-season SRS in >=6 of 10 seasons; ADAPT if it wins on only one metric (keep as an ensemble component); REJECT if it loses on both.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2308.10328v3", "title": "A Comprehensive Empirical Evaluation on Online Continual Learning", "normalized_lane": "continual_online_learning", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the metric suite for any GSE online-update experiment: report (a) final-season Brier, (b) worst-week Brier (min over trailing-4-week windows), (c) anytime Brier (mean Brier over all weeks, so a policy cannot hide a bad month behind a good finish), (d) forgetting of early-season patterns (Brier on weeks 1-4 evaluated with the end-of-season model) - with the baseline rule: any proposed online-update scheme must first beat plain experience replay (refit the GBM on trailing-N-weeks + reservoir sample of older weeks, N in {4,8,17}, properly tuned) - and apply GDumb's lesson once a season: retrain the win-prob model from scratch on a balanced buffer (equal games per season, 2015-present, class-balanced by spread band) and compare against the weekly-refit champion on the 4-metric suite.", "gate": "ADOPT the 4-metric evaluation suite as the standard for all future GSE online-update experiments if the 2020-2025 walk-forward shows the metrics disagree with final-Brier-only ranking on at least one policy pair; ADOPT plain replay (P2) as the standing update-policy baseline if it beats the frozen model on anytime Brier by >=0.002 with worst-week Brier no worse than +0.003; REJECT any update policy that wins final Brier but loses worst-week Brier by >0.005 (unstable champion).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2308.11142v1", "title": "Graph Encoding and Neural Network Approaches for Volleyball Analytics: From Rally Prediction to Set and Hit Classification", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port the encoding, not the architecture: represent each NFL drive as a temporal graph - plays as nodes (down, distance, yardline, play type, EPA as node features), directed edges between consecutive plays, plus previous-drive terminal nodes (punt/TD/FG/turnover) as context - model: the paper's simplest recipe (1 graph-conv + pooling + dense) in PyTorch Geometric vs GSE's existing flat-feature drive model, on nflverse 2015-2025 with strict pre-play features only and season holdouts (train <=2022, validate 2023, test 2024-2025; never split drives from the same game across train/test) - replacing the hand-built context rule with drive-level memory: a GRU over the sequence of drive-graph embeddings within a game, learning how much prior-drive context matters and yielding an interpretable 'game script memory' artifact for content.", "gate": "ADAPT (run the port) only under pre-registered conditions: the graph model must beat the flat-feature GBM baseline by >= 0.01 AUC AND >= 0.005 log-loss on the 2024-2025 holdout, with the gain present in both seasons separately; REJECT the representation if either condition fails; kill the lane entirely if a feature audit finds any post-snap information in the node features.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2308.14339v3", "title": "Entropy-Based Strategies for Multi-Bracket Pools", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build entropy-targeted DFS portfolios: estimate opponent entropy from real historical DK ownership (replacing the known-opponent assumption); derive salary-cap-constrained entropy families for NFL DFS rather than importing bracket families; extend the objective to expected profit with real payout structures (top-heavy vs flat) - full pipeline: calibrated GSE probabilities + estimated opponent entropy + entropy-targeted selection.", "gate": "ADAPT iff portfolio optimization beats top-N selection on GSE's DFS backtest: over a season of DK/NFL DFS slates, entropy-targeted portfolios must show higher realized maximum score (or simulated win rate vs historical fields) than the top-N-by-EV baseline at equal entry counts; if diversification does not beat concentration, keep the current generator.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2308.15443v1", "title": "Does minimizing the CRPS lead to optimal decisions in day-ahead bidding?", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Install decision-weighted ensemble learning: run the Berrisch-Ziel online aggregation but with the quantile loss replaced by a decision-weighted loss (pinball loss weighted by expected betting edge per quantile region), so the low/high-tail quantiles that drive limit-order profitability get the weight the betting strategy needs - policy: the equal-weight baseline must be beaten before any heavier scheme is justified (the 500x compute ratio is the reminder).", "gate": "Decision-weighted ensemble beats CRPS-optimized ensemble on out-of-sample CLV by a margin that survives a DM test on the decision-loss differential.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2308.15559v1", "title": "Glocal Explanations of Expected Goal Models in Soccer", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Apply glocal XAI to GSE's NFL EPA model: compute per-play SHAP values; aggregate by team-season (aSHAP) to decompose each team's EPA/play into per-feature contributions (e.g. 'EPA/play fell because down/distance mix worsened, not play design'); aggregate by player-group (QB, RB room, receiver corps) for unit-level stories; build aggregated ceteris-paribus profiles for key features per team - plus a temporal glocal extension: rolling (per-4-game-window) aSHAP per team across the season, testing whether feature-contribution shifts precede EPA/play regime changes by 2-3 weeks as a leading-indicator input for team-strength updates.", "gate": "Adopt if the aSHAP team-season decompositions are stable (bootstrap over games within a season changes the top-3 contributing features for fewer than 20% of teams) AND correctly attribute the top-2 drivers for >= 4 of the 5 largest 2024->2025 EPA/play swing teams; reject otherwise - in particular reject if aggregation washes out into noise (features flip sign across bootstrap resamples), since unstable explanations are worse than none.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2309.00756", "title": "Learning Risk Preferences in Markov Decision Processes: an Application to the Fourth Down Decision in the National Football League (arXiv:2309.00756) \u2014 replacement for 1567", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build gse_coach_risk.py: pull nflverse play-by-play 2014-2025; construct 4th-down state grid (yardline bin x yards-to-go) with empirical transitions p-hat(s'|sigma,a), augmenting GO with 3rd-down plays; value function via Chan-Fernandes-Puterman infinite-horizon approximation; next-state value distributions and tau-quantile decision maps for tau in {0.2,...,0.8}, SCAM-style monotonic smoothing; per-team-season-region tau-hat via the Hamming-loss inverse problem (Eq. 5.5), 200 game-level bootstraps for CIs; serve tau-hat(team, region, WP bin) as a feature into GSE's 4th-down decision classifier and WP model (predicted GO probability becomes a calibrated input to drive-outcome and live-WP edges); weekly 'coach risk report' for @GalaxySportsHQ content; refit each offseason - plus a hierarchical extension: team-specific transition probabilities via partial pooling (team effects shrunk to league), separating 'coach is conservative' from 'team is bad at converting', and a third region (red zone / FG range boundary) with identifiability regularized by a fused-lasso penalty on adjacent taus.", "gate": "Accepted: full NFL paper, public data + code, quantified estimand (tau-hat) with bootstrapped uncertainty, coach-level heterogeneity, significant performance association (beta_1=0.769***), and a direct GSE application (opponent 4th-down prediction + content).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2309.01472v1", "title": "FinDiff: Diffusion Models for Financial Tabular Data Generation", "normalized_lane": "synthetic_data", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build embedding-diffusion as a candidate synthetic game-table backbone: nflverse game-level table 2015-2025; learned embeddings E in R^{DxC} with D in {8,16} for team, opponent, venue type, surface, weather bin, rest category; quantile transform then standardize numerics; single Gaussian diffusion over concatenated [embeddings + numerics], feed-forward noise net, 500 steps linear schedule, sinusoidal time + outcome-regime label embeddings for conditional sampling of rare regimes; nearest-neighbor decoding per categorical; head-to-head vs TabDDPM on identical fidelity/utility/privacy suite - with factored team embeddings: team_base + per-team-per-season offset (learned roster/coaching regime), so '2024 Chiefs' and '2019 Chiefs' are nearby but distinct, giving regime-aware synthesis for free.", "gate": "ADOPT embedding-diffusion as the production backbone if: (a) Omega_col >= 0.90 and Omega_row >= 0.80 on the NFL table, AND (b) real+synthetic log-loss beats real-only by >=0.003 on held-out 2024, AND (c) peak training memory <=50% of TabDDPM's one-hot model; REJECT (keep TabDDPM) if any gate fails or if nearest-neighbor decoding aliases teams.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2309.01641", "title": "Expectation propagation for the smoothing distribution in dynamic probit", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Implement gse.statespace.EPProbit alongside the PFMVBProbit backend: shared dynamic-probit interface, Kalman-smoother inner loop, EP site updates with damping; same hyperparameter M-step for W - bake-off harness: both backends + exact MCMC on identical NFL drive-level binary tasks, logging accuracy (vs MCMC), runtime, and predictive calibration - plus: (i) EP with learned W (M-step) for calibration gains; (ii) hybrid: PFM-VB initialization then EP refinement (expect EP convergence failures -> ~0); (iii) extend the winning backend to multinomial drive outcomes.", "gate": "ADAPT->keep: EP converges in >=95% of team-season fits AND matches or beats PFM-VB on both posterior-mean MAE (vs MCMC) and holdout log-loss; if EP loses the bake-off, REJECT it and standardize on the winner.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2309.03808v2", "title": "Improved theoretical guarantee for rank aggregation via spectral method", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build spectral ranker: construct H from game score differentials (margin, MOV-capped at ~28 to blunt garbage-time tails), run Algorithm 1 (unnormalized) and Algorithm 2 (degree-normalized) to produce team rankings; use on CFB (n~=134, sparse cross-conference graph - the paper's exact regime) and NFL (n=32); compare vs Massey/Colley/Elo on the same schedule; use the rho-infinity-style displacement diagnostic (per-team order-violation count) as a stability metric for published power ratings; tune the MOV cap and optional per-game weights by rank-correlation with end-of-season SRS on 2015-2025; recompute weekly - plus a weighted-H variant: H_{ij} = w_t*clip(margin, 28) with w_t decaying by weeks-since-game and playoff-implication weight, matching sports reality.", "gate": "ADOPT spectral ranking as a GSE power-rating input if on CFB 2015-2025 it beats the least-squares baseline on Kendall's tau vs end-of-season SRS in >=6 of 10 seasons with mean Delta-tau >= +0.02, AND its week-to-week rank displacement is <= baseline; ADAPT as a diagnostic only (displacement-stability metric) if the ranking itself does not win but the per-item rho_i diagnostic proves useful; REJECT if it loses on both accuracy and stability.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2309.07856", "title": "SMARTFEAT: Efficient Feature Construction through Feature-Level Foundation Model Interactions", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Run the SMARTFEAT loop on the NFL game panel: dataset description builder (column names, dtypes, domain notes, prediction class, downstream model - versioned 'data agenda'); operator selector (flagship LLM, zero-shot): unary (bucketize temperature, normalize yardage), binary (yards per play differentials), high-order (groupby team/season aggregations of EPA), extractor (weather-API wind chill, injury-report counts); function generator (cheaper LLM) emits pandas code, AST-validated, sandbox-executed, with timestamp-leakage checks on external sources; prioritizing interaction and external-data features over unary transforms - plus a confidence-calibration study: collect every operator proposal with its stated confidence, plot FM confidence against realized validation log-loss lift (reliability curve); if calibrated, gate API spend by confidence thresholds; if uncalibrated, replace self-reported confidence with a cheap surrogate scorer.", "gate": "ADAPT if: >=0.003 held-out NFL log-loss improvement on 2025 games versus the raw-features baseline, <=30 generated features, all groupby/external features AST- and timestamp-verified causal, total pipeline runtime under 60 minutes; REJECT if any of: no gate improvement, feature count exceeds the efficiency budget without proportional gain, external-source timestamps fail the pre-prediction check, or CAAFE beats it on the sports panel.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2309.12239v1", "title": "ContTune: Continuous Tuning by Conservative Bayesian Optimization for Distributed Stream Data Processing Systems", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Apply the pattern to GSE's batch compute: (1) weekly feature-build tuning - stage skew (max/med task duration), spill, idle executor time as controller analog; Big-small skeleton: Big phase = binary-lift partitions on skewed stages until skew < 2x; Small phase = GP over <parallelism, stage-throughput> observations reused across weeks, with the feasibility indicator guarding the build SLA (must finish before the weekly serving window); (2) engine hyperparameter search under serving SLA - CBO template with conservative exploration near unknown regions so no sweep violates the p99 <= 50 ms serving gate; Top-K + mean-reversion noise treatment for noisy build metrics; keep <=2 parameter changes per week - plus grid-search alpha (the paper's untuned known-region radius) in {0,1,2,3,5} on build historical logs via replay simulation.", "gate": "ADOPT the tuning controller iff: (a) >= 25% reduction in total build compute cost (executor-hours) OR >= 25% reduction in build wall-clock vs the 4-week baseline; (b) zero build-SLA violations during the 2-week history-reuse period; (c) GP-guided suggestions never exceed 2 parameter changes per week; REJECT if the GP's suggestions are no better than the binary-lift heuristic alone.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2309.12696v1", "title": "Counterfactual Conservative Q Learning for Offline Multi-agent Reinforcement Learning", "normalized_lane": "rl_sequential_decisions", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Model each slate position i as an agent: action a^i in {0, 0.25u, 0.5u, 1u, 2u}; shared reward = weekly portfolio profit; global state = slate context + running exposure; train CFCQL: joint Q-network over (state, stake vector) with the counterfactual penalty (Eq 4) - penalize agent i's stake deviations holding other bets' stakes at historical values, lambda_i proportional to 1/(number of bets) or Kelly weight; decentralized execution: per-bet stake policy pi^i(a^i | slate features, exposure so far) applied sequentially through the slate with the exposure cap as a hard constraint; keep scalar CQL as the single-bet baseline - with learned lambda_i: weight each bet's counterfactual penalty by its historical edge variance (high-variance bets get more conservatism).", "gate": "ADOPT iff on 2024 CFCQL beats independent-CQL ROI by >=1pp with max drawdown no worse AND the lower-bound diagnostic holds on >=90% of weeks; if MACQL is not actually over-conservative in this domain (gap < 1pp), REJECT the multi-agent machinery as unnecessary complexity.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2006.04779"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2309.14390v1", "title": "Early Churn Prediction from Large Scale User-Product Interaction Time Series", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build audience churn prediction from first-party engagement events: per-user daily aggregates over trailing 30 days (site pageviews, newsletter opens/clicks, X engagement with @GalaxySportsHQ, Kit-page visits); GBT baseline (LightGBM) on mu/sigma aggregates; Transformer encoder (~1-2M params) on the 30-day sequences with 4 sigmoid heads for weeks 1-4; time-ordered split (train months 1-9, validate month 10, test months 11-12), weekly batch scoring feeding the retention playbook (win-back content, promo targeting) - plus exogenous event features the paper excluded: NFL schedule intensity (primetime games, bye weeks), GSE content calendar, promo drops as additional input channels to the Transformer.", "gate": "ADAPT if: the Transformer encoder beats the GBT baseline by >= 0.03 AUC on at least 3 of the 4 weeks on the time-ordered test window; reject otherwise (keep the cheaper GBT).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2309.14807", "title": "Evaluating Soccer Match Prediction Models: A Deep Learning Approach and Feature Optimization for Gradient-Boosted Trees", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Install the baselines-board discipline: for every GSE prediction surface (NFL spread, total, moneyline; props later), maintain a living leaderboard of pi-ratings (implement on nflverse scores back to 2006), de-vigged consensus odds, and historical outcome frequencies - no model ships unless it beats all three out-of-sample; adopt the challenge protocol internally: freeze a full-season blind hold-out (272 regular-season + postseason games) scored by a locked script, reporting RMSE (margins) and RPS-style metrics on the ordinal cover result (cover/push/not) - plus the exact paper comparison on NFL data: XGBoost over ~100 engineered features vs the same features plus pi-rating deltas vs a Transformer-over-recent-games architecture, all trained strictly chronologically on the blind season hold-out.", "gate": "ADOPT the baselines-board discipline if the pi-ratings baseline reproduces its soccer-paper behavior on NFL (beats or matches our current engine's simple variants on 2024-2025 hold-out); ADAPT as above regardless. Any new complex model is REJECTED unless it beats pi-ratings AND de-vigged consensus by >=0.003 Brier and >=0.005 log-loss on both hold-out seasons - the margin below which this paper shows noise dominates.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2310.01748v2", "title": "A generative approach to frame-level multi-competitor races", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "As engine-honesty infrastructure, build a GSE 'game simulator' in the paper's image: concrete first build = in-play NFL win-probability surface from nflverse play-by-play + NGS tracking - fit a generative drive-outcome model conditioned on field position, time, score, and personnel; forward-simulate 10k rest-of-game paths per live game state from any game state; publish the WP surface with uncertainty bands as an independent cross-check of the production live WP model; run counterfactual experiments ('what if the blitz had come from the other side') for model diagnostics - plus an odds-aware variant: calibrate the simulator's outputs against Pinnacle closing lines (Platt scaling per game-state bucket), testing whether miscalibration residuals predict line moves.", "gate": "ADAPT confirmed if the nflverse-level rest-of-game simulator's win probabilities achieve Brier score <= the published nflfastR WP model's Brier on the 2024 season (paired by game), AND the simulator's 80% WP intervals cover realized outcomes at 78-82%; if it cannot match the discriminative baseline, the counterfactual machinery still stands for diagnostics use.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2310.04227v2", "title": "Sparse Identification of Nonlinear Dynamics with Side Information (SINDy-SI)", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Discover GSE's 'laws of the game' equations: reimplement SINDy-SI (cvxpy + SCS/Clarabel or MOSEK, monomial library, SOS constraints via Putinar helper) and encode sports side information: boundedness (win-prob dynamics in [0,1]), equilibrium (tied game at t=0 => drift zero), monotonicity (d(win-prob)/d(score_diff) >= 0, d/d(opponent_timeouts) <= 0), time-decay momentum symmetry; discover dynamics on 2022-2024 nflverse game-state trajectories with constraints active, threshold lambda tuned by leave-one-season-out CV; ship the constrained equation as a guaranteed-sane dynamics model that can veto engine outputs violating the encoded side information - plus data-driven side-information mining: fit an unconstrained SINDy ensemble across 2015-2024, promote only the 10/10-season-stable qualitative properties to SOS hard constraints, and re-fit (a self-bootstrapping discover->constrain->re-discover loop).", "gate": "ADOPT if: SINDy-SI beats unconstrained SINDy on J_k by >= 1 order of magnitude on the leave-one-season-out CV AND the learned model satisfies all encoded side information exactly (verified by SOS certificate, not sampling) AND BFR >= 60% on open-loop 2025 holdout; REJECT if: SDP solve time exceeds 30 min per fit at n=6/degree-4, or constraints reduce fit quality below the unconstrained baseline by > 20%, or J_k gap < 1 order of magnitude.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2310.08278v1", "title": "Lag-Llama: Towards Foundation Models for Probabilistic Time Series Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "timeseries_foundation", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Implement the lag-covariate constructor for weekly sports: lags {1,2,3,4,8,16} games for margins/totals/usage, plus sports-native covariates (rest-day differential, travel distance, dome/outdoor, opponent rolling EPA, line movement) replacing date-time features; decoder-only transformer ~2-10M params, Student-t head; pretrain on the sports pile from ledger 2124, fine-tune per season/task; distributions feed the same pricing layer as Chronos paths - plus a sports-native covariate swap study: (a) paper's lags + date-time vs (b) sports lags + rest/travel/weather/opponent covariates vs (c) (b) + market line as a covariate, measuring CRPS deltas; the (b)-(c) residual gap directly quantifies GSE's forecasting alpha over the line.", "gate": "ADOPT the lag-covariate recipe if the sports Lag-Llama variant's CRPS beats seasonal naive by >=8% on 2021-2024 AND its 80% prediction intervals are calibrated within +/-4 pts; ADAPT further (head/covariate upgrades) if it beats naive but misses calibration; REJECT the frozen/zero-shot variant for any live use; hard reject if interval coverage deviates >8 pts.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2402.03885v2"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2310.08697v1", "title": "The Data Lakehouse: Data Warehousing and More", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Adopt the lakehouse pattern for GSE's analytical/offline layer at small scale: cloud object storage + Delta Lake for bronze (raw nflverse pulls, odds snapshots, NGS dumps), silver (cleaned play-by-play), gold (feature tables); table format over file format (every read gets time travel + schema evolution); data-as-code branching in lightweight form - weekly feature-table builds land on a staging branch, the backtest suite runs against the branch, atomic promotion to prod only on pass (directly implementing the acceptance gates in ledgers 2022/2024); DuckDB/Spark for batch builds reading the same Delta tables as training (zero export ETL); SCD type 2 for team/coach/roster dimensions via Delta time travel - plus lakehouse-native feature lineage: embed the feature-DSL fingerprint and source Delta versions as table properties on every gold feature table, making each feature table self-describing.", "gate": "ADOPT the lakehouse layout iff: (i) time-travel reproduction is byte-identical on the 2024 replay, (ii) the branch gate catches the injected corruption (no prod contamination), (iii) exactly one physical copy of each raw dataset exists; REJECT the branching discipline (keep single-table writes) if branch-merge overhead adds >10% to the weekly build time.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2305.20077v1", "2608.22389v1"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2310.09656v1", "title": "TabSyn: Score-based Tabular Diffusion in VAE Latent Space", "normalized_lane": "synthetic_data", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build TabSyn as the recommended primary synthetic-season backbone: nflverse team-game table 2015-2025 (~30 columns, mixed types), quantile-transform skewed numerics; column tokenizer (d=4 embeddings per column, incl. team/opponent IDs - no one-hot), 2-layer Transformer encoder/decoder VAE with adaptive beta schedule; VE-SDE diffusion on flattened latent, 5-layer SiLU denoising MLP, sampling with <=20 NFEs; regime label embeddings for conditional sampling (required for rare-regime oversampling); generate 3-5 synthetic seasons, downstream GBDT spread model trained real+synthetic - plus conditional latent diffusion with learned regime prompts: a learned 'regime prompt' vector (team-tier x outcome-class x weather-band) added to the latent before diffusion for prompt-conditioned rare-regime generation (blowouts, snow games) without retraining the VAE.", "gate": "ADOPT TabSyn as the production synthetic-season backbone if: (a) its column-density error <= 50% of TabDDPM's on the NFL table, AND (b) real+synthetic GBDT log-loss beats real-only by >=0.003 on held-out 2024, AND (c) sampling cost <= 30 NFEs per season batch; REJECT (fall back to TabDDPM/FinDiff) if the VAE reconstruction degrades team-identity fidelity or training cost exceeds 3x TabDDPM's without meeting gate (a).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2310.10386v1", "title": "Rating of players by Laplace approximation and dynamic modeling", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Per-match Elo variance update (Eq. 25) for GSE's NFL team/QB ratings: insert (sigma^2)' = max(B^2, sigma^2(1-AL)) into GSE's Elo updater with the reduction factor A and lower bound B (Algorithm 1 vElo as a drop-in replacement for the mean-only Elo step); tune (A,B) on train NLL - faster adaptation to new QBs/rookie breakouts without the variance-collapse pathology - plus the surface-transfer formula for NFL context splits: a team's rating on grass vs turf, dome vs outdoor, or home vs away as 'surfaces', estimating cross-split sigmas and rhos from NFL data, then propagating a Sunday result on one split to the others proportionally to correlation x SD ratio.", "gate": "ADOPT only if vElo wins with McNemar p < 0.05 at >= +0.3pp accuracy on 2018-2023 NFL games, time-ordered, vs constant-variance Elo; ADAPT (rookie/QB-change-only usage) if gains concentrate on new players; otherwise REJECT. Do not adopt the tennis (A,B) parameterization - re-tune (A,B) on NFL data.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2310.10553v2", "title": "TacticAI: an AI assistant for football tactics", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Two props wins: (1) receiver-conditional TD model for anytime-TD and receiving props: P(TD on play) = sum_t P(TD | targeted=t)*P(targeted=t) - train a target-distribution model (who gets targeted from pre-snap/matchup features) and a conditional TD model (given the target, from coverage/separation features), marginalize; same for first-down props; (2) pre-snap graph for the NGS lane: 22 nodes with NGS positions/velocities at snap, edges = offense/defense + assignment proximity, GATv2 predicting play outcome (run/pass, yards bucket, TD), with D2-style augmentation: mirror across field axis (with play-direction normalization) to double goal-line/red-zone samples - plus situation retrieval: nearest-neighbor search in the graph embedding space for matchup prep ('find me all 3rd-and-long blitz looks vs this protection').", "gate": "ADOPT the graph + conditional-decomposition stack iff it improves holdout log-loss by >= 5% over the tabular baseline on 2025 plays (paired bootstrap, p < 0.05); if only the decomposition wins (without the GNN), adopt that alone; otherwise REJECT.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2310.10688v2", "title": "A decoder-only foundation model for time-series forecasting", "normalized_lane": "timeseries_foundation", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a sports TimesFM: NFL-specific corpus - weekly team-level sequences 2002-2024 (offensive/defensive EPA per play/game, success rate, score margin, pace, QB-starter injury proxies), NCAA FBS margins, market lines, plus the paper's synthetic recipe adapted to sports (ARMA+seasonality+trend generators calibrated to NFL margins, mean ~0, sigma ~13.5); decoder-only transformer (input patch 8, output patch 16, dim 1024, 12 layers, random masking) with a multi-quantile output head (10 quantiles) instead of MSE; pretrain on synthetic + NFL history, fine-tune per-season on expanding windows; weekly batch inference Tuesday (line release) and Sunday morning (final); CRPS-gated rollout - plus a hybrid pretraining curriculum: cheap synthetic sports-like series (NFL-margin ARMA family with regime shifts for coaching changes) first, then real NFL/NCAA sequences, testing whether regime-shift synthetic generators teach faster adaptation to new coaching staffs/QBs.", "gate": "ADOPT the sports-TimesFM into the engine if, on the 2022-2023 holdout, the fine-tuned quantile model achieves >=0.005 lower mean CRPS than the naive seasonal-margin baseline AND beats it in both seasons individually; REJECT (keep researching, do not ship) if it fails either season or the gain is <0.005; reject unconditionally if any leakage audit flag fires.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2310.11459v1", "title": "Ratings of European and South American Football Leagues Based on Glicko-2 with Modifications", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Implement modified Glicko-2 on NFL (nflverse 2002-2025): standard mu/phi/sigma with paper-ported modifications - (a) home advantage h inside the expectation function (tuned; no pandemic split), (b) season-start update: phi += phi_s and mu += mu_l for teams with >=40% roster turnover (free-agency/draft churn proxy for league-change drift), (c) post-season normalization of the league mean to a fixed constant, (d) drop the draw term; compare Glicko-2 log-loss against GSE's existing Elo baseline on the same games; output per-team (mu, phi) each week - phi (rating deviation) as the new uncertainty signal GSE's point ratings lack - plus an ablation the paper never did: toggle each modification independently on the NFL test block, then try team-specific h_i (e.g. altitude Denver) with hierarchical shrinkage across the 32 teams.", "gate": "ADOPT modified Glicko-2 if it beats BOTH baselines by >=0.004 mean log-loss on the 2021-2025 test block, with the gain robust when 2020 (COVID season) is excluded; ADAPT if it beats only one baseline (keep the winning modification subset); REJECT if it beats neither.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2310.12145v1", "title": "Fairer and More Accurate Tabular Models Through NAS", "normalized_lane": "nas_automl", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Multi-objective NAS+HPO: search space = MLP/ResNet/FT-Transformer architectures (rtdl-style) + training HPs, objectives = (a) log-loss on OOF, (b) ECE on OOF; optimizer: ParEGO or NSGA-II over the two objectives; use case = the win-probability tabular model, where calibration directly prices Kelly stakes - from the Pareto front, pick the knee point and compare against the current log-loss-only champion + post-hoc isotonic - plus a THIRD objective: inference latency (or equivalently ensemble size), making it accuracy-calibration-latency 3D Pareto search; test whether a latency-constrained Pareto pick (<=100ms/game inference) sacrifices >0.002 log-loss vs unconstrained.", "gate": "ADOPT if: the Pareto knee config beats the log-loss-champion+isotonic baseline on BOTH log-loss (>=0.001) and ECE (>=10% relative) on the 2023-2025 holdout - i.e. joint search finds something post-hoc calibration cannot; REJECT if: the Pareto front shows no config dominating the single-objective champion on both axes, or search cost exceeds 100 GPU-hours for <0.001 log-loss gain.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2310.14770v2", "title": "Theoretically Grounded Loss Functions and Algorithms for Score-Based Multi-Class Abstention", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Two-stage no-bet head on the frozen engine: stage 1 = current engine (frozen); stage 2 = train a rejector (gradient boosting / small MLP) on historical engine outputs + game features, with labels = 1 if the engine's pick was wrong (or unprofitable), 0 otherwise, using exponential loss Phi(t)=exp(-t) per the paper, and abstention cost c tuned to a target no-bet rate - the rejector sees the engine's predicted edge, CQR width, line-move features, OOD score, subsuming the confidence-threshold, kNN-reject, and double-score gate scores from ledgers 1006, 1010, and 1011 as inputs - plus a multi-class extension: GSE publishes spread, total, and moneyline - train a SHARED rejector with class-specific abstention costs, testing whether the paper's multi-class machinery beats three independent binary rejectors.", "gate": "ADOPT if the two-stage rejector beats the confidence-threshold baseline on abstention loss by >=15% relative (paired test p<0.05) AND beats it on profit; otherwise REJECT. The single decisive number: abstention-loss reduction >= 15% vs confidence-threshold baseline.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["1905.09561", "2006.16597", "2307.05199"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2310.14772v2", "title": "Predictor-Rejector Multi-Class Abstention: Theoretical Analysis and Algorithms", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Predictor-rejector no-bet head (P-R, two-stage): freeze engine h; train rejector r on a DIFFERENT feature set: line-move magnitude/timing, reverse-line-movement flags, CQR interval width, ensemble disagreement (1009's p*), OOD distance (1011's score_B), news-volume anomaly; surrogate = exponential loss on the rejector per the paper's two-stage family; abstention cost c mapped from the sportsbook vig (a wrong pick costs ~1.1 units of a 1-unit bet; abstention costs 0); tune the accept/reject threshold to a target no-bet rate - plus a deferral cascade: instead of binary abstain, route into THREE tiers - publish (engine confident), human review (Garrett, the 'defer to human' special case the paper's framing explicitly supports), and hard no-bet.", "gate": "ADOPT if two-stage P-R beats two-stage score-based on abstention loss by >=5% relative (paired p<0.05) OR beats the confidence baseline by >=15% relative with rejection ratio <= 30%; otherwise REJECT. The single decisive number: abstention-loss reduction >= 5% vs two-stage score-based (or >=15% vs confidence baseline) at rejection ratio <= 0.30.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2001.10623", "2307.05199"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2310.19343v1", "title": "Quantile Super Learning for independent and online settings with application to solar power forecasting", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a Quantile Super Learner for GSE prop distributions: for each prop market, collect K candidate quantile curves (per-alpha predictions from GSE's projection models + market-implied quantiles inverted from lines); select/combine via rolling-window cross-validated quantile loss (walk-forward, refit weekly); use the continuous variant (convex weights on a simplex grid) for stability, weights >= 0, sum = 1, optimized on the trailing 6-8 weeks of resolved props; output combined quantile function per player-prop, deriving fair P(over) by interpolating at the posted line - plus regime-aware QSL: fit separate weight vectors per regime (pre/post key-injury, dome/outdoor, divisional) selected by a context gate, testing whether regime-gated weights beat global weights on tail-quantile (alpha in {0.1, 0.9}) loss.", "gate": "ADAPT accepted: walk-forward mean quantile loss >= 3% lower (relative) than the simple-average baseline AND >= 1% lower than EWA, with no single week worse than 5% above the best baseline (robustness); else REJECT. Hard fail: if continuous-QSL weights collapse to a single candidate every week (adds nothing over discrete selection), reject as non-value-add.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2311.02971v3", "title": "TabRepo: A Large Scale Repository of Tabular Model Evaluations and its AutoML Applications", "normalized_lane": "nas_automl", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build 'GSE-TabRepo': every model config ever evaluated on every season/market task gets logged (config, OOF predictions, log-loss, fit/inference time) into a permanent evaluations table; markets = spread/total/moneyline x game/team-week granularities; offseason portfolio learning: run the greedy complementarity algorithm over the accumulated table to learn a portfolio of ~15-30 configs; each new season, evaluate ONLY the portfolio on the most recent season (zero-shot), then ensemble-select the top members; guard against non-stationarity by learning the portfolio on rolling 5-season windows, re-derived each offseason - plus a conditional portfolio: a small decision rule mapping season meta-features (pace, scoring environment, market efficiency stats) to a subset of configs, testing whether the conditional portfolio beats the static one by >=0.001 log-loss on held-out seasons.", "gate": "ADOPT if: the portfolio-ensemble matches the full-search log-loss within 0.002 on 2023-2025 while using <=25% of the compute, AND the learned portfolio is stable (>=60% member overlap between consecutive offseason derivations); REJECT if: portfolio log-loss is worse than full search by >0.002, or a regime-shift season makes the portfolio pick a catastrophically bad member.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2311.10051v1", "title": "Tabular Few-Shot Generalization Across Heterogeneous Feature Spaces", "normalized_lane": "metalearning_fewshot", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Meta-learn tabular models across NFL eras: nflverse game-level tabular features 2015-2025, tasks at team-season level with deliberately varying feature subsets per era (drop NGS columns pre-2018, drop tracking pre-2021) to exercise heterogeneous transfer; column encoder over game-stat columns, dataset encoder over the K-game support set, GAT target network with generated weights; binary head (win/loss, cover/no-cover) plus a regression head for margin (linear head on pooled node states); meta-train across eras, meta-test on 2023-2025 new regimes; FLATadapt at inference: 5-10 gradient steps on the support set's embeddings only; per-team weekly serving with no refit of the meta-network - plus a Hybrid FLAT-NGGP head: replace the softmax classifier with ledger 1902's flow-conditioned GP head, outputting calibrated non-Gaussian predictive distributions over margin instead of class labels.", "gate": "ADOPT iff FLAT beats per-task XGBoost by >=3pp accuracy on new-regime win prediction at K in {2,4} (2023-2025 LOSO) AND the heterogeneous-schema variant loses <=1pp vs the homogeneous variant; reject if it cannot beat plain XGBoost at K=4.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2110.13561v1"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2311.13707v1", "title": "Bayes-xG: Player and Position Correction on Expected Goals (xG) using Bayesian Hierarchical Approach", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Hierarchical CPOE as the principled Bayesian upgrade to GSE's ad-hoc shrinkage: hierarchical logistic regression with QB-level (or receiver-level) random effects on completion probability given the nflfastR-style feature set - partial pooling handles small-sample QBs; position-group adjustments for EPA models (TE/RB/WR group effects on EPA/play or success rate) with the paper's key caution: apparent 'position effects' may vanish once situational features (coverage, pressure) are included; adopt the prior-sensitivity protocol (fit wide/tight/ill-suited variants, compare MSD) as the template for any GSE Bayesian model - plus: empirical-Bayes / cross-validated player priors instead of reputation alpha, team-level crossed random effects (QB vs scheme vs supporting cast), extension from binary outcomes to ordered EPA buckets (hierarchical ordered logit).", "gate": "ADOPT only if the reproduction gate holds (recover Table 5 positional adjustments within +/-0.005 on StatsBomb EPL open data), the prior battery ranks the chosen priors first, AND hierarchical wins held-out log-loss on small-sample QBs (<200 attempts); ADAPT (research prior) if it only matches; otherwise REJECT.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2312.00076v1", "title": "Towards A Foundation Model For Trajectory Intelligence", "normalized_lane": "selfsupervised_tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the 3-stage trajectory tokenizer on NFL 10Hz tracking: quantize field to fine cells (~0.5-yd); map each (player, frame) to a hierarchical cell hash; cell-hash encoding -> spatiotemporal clustering (~0.3 s window, adjacent-cell merge to denoise jitter) -> WordPiece sub-hash tokenization to a 30-50k vocab trained on 7 seasons of tracking; pretrain BERT-style masked trajectory model (whole-cell pre-masking 20%) on tokenized play sequences; use token embeddings as input features for GSE prop models, or fine-tune task heads (ball-carrier destination prediction; player-style identification) - plus: (1) add the temporal dimension - interleave delta-t tokens and train with time-aware masking (mask bursts, not just hexagons); (2) hierarchical sub-hashes at two field resolutions (coarse zone + fine cell) as separate token streams.", "gate": "ADOPT if: (a) sub-hash tokenizer achieves >= 50% vocabulary reduction vs raw cell hashing at equal masked-token perplexity, AND (b) frozen-embedding ball-carrier destination prediction F1 >= 10pp above the raw-coordinate baseline on held-out weeks; REJECT if neither holds.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2312.00396v1", "title": "GFN-SR: Symbolic Regression with Generative Flow Networks", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Reimplement GFN-SR-lite in PyTorch: LSTM policy over pre-order token sequences, in-situ constraint masks (from ledger 1824), TB loss, adaptive baseline B schedule; reward = 1/(1+NMSE) on nflverse train slice; use as a DIVERSITY generator: sample 200 post-training equations, cluster by symbolic skeleton, keep cluster medoids as the candidate metric set, feed each through the 1826 selector - plus reward shaping with the LM prior: replace vanilla R(s)=1/(1+RMSE) with R(s)*P_LM(s)^lambda where P_LM is the 1826 sports-corpus n-gram prior - sampling proportional to fit x domain-plausibility, testing whether the GFlowNet's multi-modality survives prior-shaping or collapses back to one mode.", "gate": "ADOPT GFN-SR as the candidate generator if its top-5 diverse set contains an equation beating DSR's single best by >=0.02 test r on 2024-2025 AND the set's cross-season stability (2024 vs 2025 rank correlation) exceeds DSR's top-5-beam stability; REJECT if sampling collapses to near-duplicates or no candidate beats the baseline.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["1912.04871", "2304.06333"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2312.01586v1", "title": "On the Maximization of Long-Run Reward CVaR for Markov Decision Processes", "normalized_lane": "uncertainty_decision_theory", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the risk-seeking drawdown-recovery regime: loss frame = bankroll below its trailing peak by >=8% (drawdown >= 8%) - outside the frame, the risk-averse stack (ledgers 2142/2144/2147) governs; small tabular MDP: states = {normal, hot, cold} bankroll-momentum x {high, low} edge-availability (6 states), actions = stake tiers {0.5u, 1u, 2u, 3u}, transitions estimated from historical weekly P&L sequences, reward = weekly profit; solve the paper's two LPs for max CVaR_alpha (alpha=0.7, right tail) + beta*mean with beta tuned so mean is not sacrificed; extract the stationary randomized policy (expect <=1 randomization per Theorem 2, e.g. 'in (drawdown, high-edge): post 1u with p=0.8, 3u with p=0.2'); precompute the 6-state policy table monthly, weekly lookup by current state, log sampled actions for the audit trail - plus depth-conditioned alpha/beta (re-solve the LPs per drawdown-depth bucket) and a distributionally robust MDP variant (uncertainty set on transitions, a la 2143's outer risk).", "gate": "ACCEPT if walk-forward 2024-2025: recovery time from >=8% drawdown <= 0.75 x best baseline's AND final bankroll >= best baseline's AND max drawdown never exceeds 1.2 x the freeze baseline's; REJECT if recovery is not faster than flat-1u or the left-tail cost exceeds the 1.2x bound.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2606.05551", "2404.13371", "2106.06317"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2312.04338v1", "title": "Stochastic modelling of football matches", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build an NFL live-game Cox/Hawkes-style event model as GSE's live probability engine: events = scoring events {home TD, away TD, home FG, away FG} + intensity shocks {key-player injury/ejection, weather change at open-air stadiums, referee flags}; regressors: score differential, possession state (down/distance/field position), time remaining, timeouts, pregame spread-implied strength, turnover/injury shock indicators, pace (plays per minute); log-linear intensities (concave log-likelihood -> convex solver); attack/defence normalization analogous to the paper's constraint; from any live game state, simulate 100k forward paths -> live win probability, live spread/total distributions, live derivative prices; pre-match fit runs weekly, in-game inference is simulation - plus: (1) self-exciting (Hawkes) terms for momentum bursts - a decaying excitation term on recent scoring events; (2) market-implied regressors - live market-implied team strength as a dynamic regressor updated as the market moves in-game.", "gate": "ADAPT into the live engine only if: (a) the mechanism check reproduces the three headline effects within +/-2 pp; AND (b) the NFL transfer test beats the pregame-spread-carry baseline on mean per-game log-likelihood over the 2024-2025 test window by a statistically significant margin (paired t-test, p < 0.05), AND (c) calibration of the simulated final-margin distribution passes a chi-squared goodness-of-fit test at alpha = 0.05.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2312.04711v1", "title": "Luck, skill, and depth of competition in games and social hierarchies", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "As engine-honesty infrastructure, build a GSE luck+depth rating layer: fit alpha, beta per league (and per season) on GSE's game data - alpha becomes the league's irreducible upset rate, beta its depth; use alpha as a miscalibration diagnostic: compare model-implied underdog win rates vs market-implied, flagging mispriced underdogs when alpha-hat gaps between model and market persist; use beta to set the rating scale's steepness per league instead of a global constant; port to a fast MAP/laplace approximation for production (Stan HMC is the prototype, not the serving path) - plus time-varying depth: let beta(t) drift within a season (early-season parity vs late-season stratification), testing whether dynamic beta beats static beta on rolling log-likelihood as a 'league stratification index' for content and modeling.", "gate": "ADAPT confirmed if luck+depth BT beats plain BT on 2025 NFL walk-forward log-likelihood by >=0.003/game with the alpha-hat estimate stable across halves of the season (confounding check: |alpha-hat_H1 - alpha-hat_H2| < 0.05); if alpha/beta confound (unstable alpha-hat), fall back to the depth-only variant.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2312.08528v3", "title": "auto-sktime: Automated Time Series Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "nas_automl", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Adopt the two mechanisms, not the system: (a) lookback-window successive halving as the fidelity schedule for GSE's forecaster/model selection - evaluate candidate configurations on the most recent 2 seasons (low fidelity), promote winners to 5 seasons, then full history; (b) warm-start each season's HPO from the previous season's optimization trace (store evaluated configs + scores in the feature store); wraps the existing win-probability model HPO and the AG-TS panel forecaster (ledger 1983) - plus regime-aware fidelity: choose the low-fidelity window by detecting the most recent stable regime (e.g. post-coaching-change or post-QB-change break) instead of a fixed 2->5->full season ladder, testing whether regime-aware windows beat fixed recency windows as a fidelity proxy.", "gate": "ADOPT the mechanisms if: successive halving selects a config within 2% wQL of the full-evaluation winner while using <=40% of the compute, AND warm-starting reaches the from-scratch best within <=50% of the evaluations on the 2024-2025 windows; REJECT if: the low-fidelity winner disagrees with the full-fidelity winner on >1 of 3 test seasons, or warm-start shows no evaluation savings vs random init.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2308.05566"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2312.09466v1", "title": "Enhancing Trajectory Prediction through Self-Supervised Waypoint Noise Prediction (SSWNP)", "normalized_lane": "selfsupervised_tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Wrap GSE's trajectory predictor with SSWNP: ball-carrier observed 1.0 s (10 frames) -> predict 2.0 s (20 frames); duplicate each batch into clean + noise-augmented views (omega tuned on validation, start 0.05 in field-normalized units); add noise-prediction head Theta_ss on the encoder; L_total = L_sup + lambda*L_ss, lambda from L_ss convergence (paper: 0.01); validate omega in {0.01, 0.05, 0.1}; ~1 engineer-week (training-loop change + one auxiliary head; zero inference overhead) - plus: (1) structured noise - perturb waypoints along the motion direction (speed noise) vs perpendicular (lateral noise) separately, testing which teaches more useful invariances (cuts are lateral; bursts are longitudinal); (2) adversarial-noise scheduling: increase omega over training (curriculum), testing whether late-training high-noise views further improve robustness.", "gate": "ADOPT if: (a) SSWNP-trained predictor reduces FDE >= 10% vs the same-backbone baseline on held-out weeks, AND (b) under test-time jitter, the SSWNP model's FDE degradation is <= half the baseline's degradation; REJECT if neither holds.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2312.10331", "title": "Gambling under unknown probabilities as a proxy for real world decisions under uncertainty", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the 'delta/sigma gate' for GSE stakes: estimate sigma per market type (spread/moneyline/total, and per edge bucket) as the RMSE of engine win-prob vs realized outcomes on a rolling window (the calibration curve's RMSE); for each pick with perceived edge delta_perc = p_engine - p_market, compute the expected-growth factor from (17); stake only if E[growth] > 0 with margin (e.g. delta_perc > 1.5 sigma), and scale the Kelly fraction by Phi(delta_perc/sigma) (probability the perceived edge has the right sign); re-derive (16)-(17) for general decimal odds before coding (replace a=2delta with f*=(bp-q)/b and redo the xi-integration numerically) - plus a distribution-free version: replace the normal-xi assumption with the engine's empirical error distribution (bootstrap residuals from the calibration history) and recompute the optimal stake by direct numerical integration.", "gate": "ADOPT the delta/sigma gate if gated Kelly beats ungated Kelly on terminal log growth with max drawdown no worse, over 2023-2025, with the improvement concentrated in picks where delta_perc/sigma < 1.5 (the gate's target population); REJECT if the gate just throws away good bets (growth drops).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2312.11955v1", "title": "Vertical Symbolic Regression", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Implement VSR-PySR: round r runs PySR restricted to growing feature subsets S_1 subset S_2 subset ..., seeding each round's population with the previous round's hall-of-fame; approximate control via residualizing on controlled features' current best form, and observational control by binning controlled variables (down/distance buckets) and fitting reduced forms per bin - plus regime-vertical SR: run the vertical rounds over game regimes (round 1: neutral-script plays; round 2: +trailing; round 3: +leading), testing whether football relationships are regime-decomposable.", "gate": "ADOPT vertical staging if VSR-PySR matches or beats horizontal test R^2 with <=50% of the expression length or <=50% of the compute time; REJECT if horizontal wins on both accuracy and simplicity - the oracle-free approximation does not transfer.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2312.12700v1", "title": "Performance rating in chess, tennis, and other contexts", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a PRe module: given an NFL team/unit over an n-game window with per-game pre-game win probabilities w_i, compute the binomial-exact score probability at window-average and solve the paper's constrained max for the implied rating, back-translated to Elo-scale PRe - for content leaderboards ('best defensive 5-game stretch') and as a (PRe - Elo) gap feature - replacing the paper's fixed t=0.75 and average-opponent collapse with the exact sequence likelihood MLE on Pi_i Bernoulli(w_i * shift).", "gate": "ADOPT the PRe module if (a) theorem replication on NFL windows holds within +/-1 Elo point for 0<m<n (mathematical port validated), AND (b) the (PRe - Elo) gap feature improves next-game ATS-residual adjusted R^2 by >=0.002 vs Elo-only on 2015-2025 time-ordered CV; ADAPT as content-only (leaderboard product, no modeling use) if (a) holds but (b) fails.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2312.13619v2", "title": "The many routes to the ubiquitous Bradley\u2013Terry model", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "As engine-honesty infrastructure, add a ratings license checklist in GSE's ratings pipeline: before promoting any pairwise rating model, run assumption diagnostics - (a) transitivity/intransitivity test on the win matrix; (b) quasi-symmetry residual check (PageRank/fair-bets comparison); (c) tie-model comparison (Davidson vs Rao-Kupper vs ignore); (d) MaxEnt-vs-MLE worths comparison - plus a failure-diagnostic dashboard tracking the intransitivity index and quasi-symmetry residuals weekly, triggering automatic re-selection among BT variants (plain / Davidson / Poisson-scoring) when thresholds cross.", "gate": "ADAPT confirmed if, on the 2025 NFL season held-out set, the tie-aware or multi-outcome BT variant selected by the diagnostics beats the plain-BT baseline log-likelihood by >=0.005 per game (paired test p<0.05); if no variant beats plain BT, the diagnostics still stand as guardrails (gate passes on diagnostic implementation, not on finding a violation).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2401.00282v1", "title": "Deep Generative Symbolic Regression", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Reimplement DGSR-lite: Set Transformer encoder + Transformer decoder with tree-state embeddings, pre-trained on synthetic sports-plausible equations (from the NSR Phase-2 generator) with d=4-8 variables; at inference, encode nflverse slices and run NGPQT-style refinement (or REINFORCE fine-tuning on NMSE) before Monte-Carlo MAP search - with a refinement curriculum: refine first on GP-denoised targets, then raw data, testing whether staged refinement beats single-stage on recovery of known synthetic sports equations with injected noise.", "gate": "ADOPT inference-time refinement if it improves held-out RMSE by >=8% over no-refinement decoding at equal-or-fewer equation evaluations on the 2024-2025 window; REJECT if refinement gains vanish on noisy real data or merely recover the pre-training prior's favorite shapes.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": ["2106.06427"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2401.01505v5", "title": "Sports-QA: A Large-Scale Video Question Answering Benchmark for Complex and Professional Sports", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Treat NGS tracking sequences as the 'video' for football QA: transformer encoder over tracking frames with AFA-style multi-focal attention (focal lengths {5,25,100} frames ~ {0.5s,2.5s,10s}), question encoder replaced by a play-context encoder (down/distance, personnel, score) - 'what happens next' play-outcome classification - with focal lengths learnable per attention head and mixing weights alpha_f conditioned on play context (short focus for line-of-scrimmage chaos, long focus for developing routes).", "gate": "Adopt if AFA beats standard attention by >=1.5pp accuracy AND >=1.0pp macro-F1 on the 2024 holdout; reject otherwise (the paper's own margin is ~1.2pp - demand at least parity with that on football data).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2401.02601v1", "title": "Constrained Max Drawdown: a Fast and Robust Portfolio Optimization Approach", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a GSE bet portfolio constructor: inputs = engine edge estimates + bet-outcome covariance (bootstrap from historical pick residuals, block-diagonal by game); implement the constrained-MD MILP (pulp/OR-Tools) maximizing worst historical session return with constraints >=5% per selected bet, <=50% per bet, bankroll budget - plus drawdown-adaptive bounds: run the MILP on rolling 30-day windows, tightening the minimum-allocation bound when recent realized drawdown is high.", "gate": "ADOPT into the sizing layer if, on the 2024 walk-forward, max bankroll drawdown is >=20% lower than flat staking at equal or better ROI; REJECT if drawdown is not reduced or ROI drops >1 pp.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2401.02710v2", "title": "Synergistic Formulaic Alpha Generation for Quantitative Trading based on Reinforcement Learning", "normalized_lane": "signal_discovery_alpha_mining", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Mine signals with synergy rewards: change the mining reward from individual-signal RankIC to marginal contribution (Shapley-style value added to the current ensemble's walk-forward Brier); self-bootstrap by seeding each run's pool with GSE's own accepted signals (combination may drop seeds); cap the combination pool at ~20 - plus explicit synergy accounting: add a per-candidate orthogonality bonus = 1 - max|rho| vs pool, decompose final gains into individual quality + orthogonality via ablation, and test cross-horizon synergy by mining pools at multiple horizons.", "gate": "ADAPT->build if synergy-rewarded mining beats individual-rewarded mining on test ensemble Brier by >= 0.002 at pool size <= 20 AND self-seeding matches or beats hand-seeding; REJECT if marginal-contribution rewards produce no ensemble gain over greedy individual selection - then 'synergy' is just a relabeled greedy forward selection.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2401.02919", "title": "Optimal strategy for trail running with nutrition and fatigue factors", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build gse_fatigue_state.py: per-player latent fatigue Q updated per play from NGS power proxy P = m*v*a, dQ/dt = K*P during sessions and dQ/dt = -rho*Q between sessions (recovery; rho fitted); calibrate K, rho per position group against observed outcomes (missed practices, snap declines, soft-tissue flags) - then add the missing recovery term and a stochastic injury-hazard layer: soft-tissue injury as a point process with intensity lambda(t) = lambda_0*exp(gamma*Q(t)), estimating lambda_0, gamma per position group and testing whether lambda(t) anticipates injuries better than ACWR-based hazards.", "gate": "Accepted (narrowly but genuinely): validated predictive accuracy (0.5-13% finish-time errors across 5 independent races), a mechanistic fatigue ODE directly portable to workload-state modeling, and an explicit parameter-fitting methodology. Not a plug-in predictor; a feature-engineering template.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2401.05451v1", "title": "OpenSkill: A faster asymmetric multi-team, multiplayer rating system", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Prototype OpenSkill (Plackett-Luce) as an NFL team-rating backend: pip-install openskill.py, run weekly updates 2000-2025, benchmark against GSE's house Elo on backtest log-loss - then go beyond the paper: implement score-differential-aware Plackett-Luce updates (weight the Bayesian update by margin of victory relative to expectation) plus lightweight player-contribution weighting via snap shares (starters full update, rotational players fractional), testing whether margin-aware updates close the conceded accuracy gap.", "gate": "ADOPT OpenSkill as the production rating engine if it matches house Elo within 0.002 log-loss on the 2020-2024 walk-forward AND runs the full 2000-2025 weekly backtest in under 50% of the Elo pipeline's wall-clock time; REJECT (keep Elo) if the log-loss gap exceeds 0.002, if the sigma-uncertainty feature adds no Kelly-sizing value, or if margin-of-victory handling proves load-bearing and the package cannot accommodate it.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2401.06086v1", "title": "XGBoost Learning of Dynamic Wager Placement for In-Play Betting on an Agent-Based Model of a Sports Betting Exchange", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "As engine-honesty infrastructure, port the learning loop, not the horse-race policy: build a GSE in-play simulator (or use recorded NFL live-odds + win-probability traces) as the synthetic environment; define simple baseline in-play betting policies (always-back-closing-favorite, momentum-chaser, Kelly-on-live-model-edge); record their actions and profits; train XGBoost to imitate the most profitable agents' back/lay decisions from (game-state, live-market-state) features - then add the online-learning extension (policy updates during live games) and swap the binary back/lay objective for stake sizing (Kelly fraction regression).", "gate": "ADOPT the imitation-learning loop for GSE's in-play lane only if the learned policy beats every scripted baseline on 2025 holdout profit with p < 0.05 (Wilcoxon, as in the paper); if it merely matches the best baseline, keep the scripted policies and the recorded live-odds dataset as the asset; reject the 'learner beats teachers' claim as a simulator artifact.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2401.06412v1", "title": "Understanding whole-body inter-personal dynamics between two players using neural Granger causality as the explainable AI (XAI)", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build a matchup-causality module: on NFL Big Data Bowl tracking (22 players x, y, speed, direction, orientation at 10 Hz), fit neural Granger causality (cMLP) per matchup type (man-coverage CB<->WR, pass-rusher<->QB), extracting inter-body NGC indices (e.g., CB reaction-lag 0.2-0.6s) - replacing fixed-lambda tuning-to-a-usage-band with a stability-selection procedure (bootstrap-resample plays within a matchup, refit cMLP, keep links selected in >=70% of bootstraps) for per-link confidence weights in the matchup tables.", "gate": "Adopt into the matchup-causality module if on the 2022 weeks 1-8 man-coverage set: (a) mean CB reaction-lag index lands within 0.2-0.6s AND (b) WR->CB inter-body NGC correlates with play EPA at R^2 >= 0.10 with p < .05, and the sign persists (R^2 >= 0.05) on weeks 9-17 holdout; reject if the lag indices are unstable across hyperparameter settings or R^2 < 0.05 on the primary window.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2401.07018", "title": "Least squares for cardinal paired comparisons data", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the LS rating engine with precision: per week, form N (Laplacian of games played) and S (score-differential sums); mu-hat=N^+S with sum-mu=0 constraint; publish team strengths WITH standard errors (sigma-hat^2=Q(mu-hat)/n, Var(mu-hat)=sigma-hat^2 N^+) - a GSE differentiator - plus pairwise z-tests for matchup content ('model says KC is better than BUF at 95% confidence, accounting for schedule connectivity'), rejecting the omit-home-covariate simplification for NFL, and an optimal-design lane: weekly 'highest-leverage games for rating precision' via A-optimality (reduction in trace(sigma^2 N^+) per unplayed game).", "gate": "ADOPT the N^+ precision engine if the coverage test passes at 93-97% - then ship SEs on all GSE LS ratings and the pairwise z-tests for content; REJECT the exponential rank-confidence claim for weekly tiers unless the subgaussian error bound is validated.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}

{"arxiv_id": "2401.08718v1", "title": "Investigating Fouling Efficiency in Football Using Expected Booking (xB) Model", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build an NFL xFlag (expected-penalty) model: per-play penalty probability conditioned on game state and officiating - down/distance, yardline, score differential, time, team prior penalty rate, referee crew, EPA of the pre-flag play, pass/run, defender pressure rate; XGBoost/LightGBM binary classifier; outputs expected flags per game by team (xFlags), per-crew tendencies, drive-level expected free yards, fed into the drive/game simulation to adjust totals and spread - with referee-crew embeddings (learned per-crew booking-tendency vectors) and a two-stage hurdle model (flag/no-flag -> yardage conditional on flag).", "gate": "ADOPT the xFlag sub-model into GSE's game simulation only if: (a) out-of-sample AUC >= 0.58 on 2023-2024 hold-outs AND (b) adding xFlag to the totals simulation reduces MAE on closing totals by >= 0.3 points over 2023-2024 (n~=540 games); otherwise keep as research note only.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2401.09940v2", "title": "Biases in Expected Goals Models Confound Finishing Ability", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add a residual-hygiene module to the props pipeline: (1) K-fold cross-fitting so no player's residual is computed from a model trained on his own plays (kills self-contamination); (2) multi-calibration of expected-yards models within position x volume bins with empirical-Bayes priors per position; (3) atypical-play exclusion list (tipped passes, Hail Marys, kneel-downs, spikes) from both training and residual evaluation; (4) volume-dependent shrinkage of all published player residual ratings toward positional means - plus a learned-grouping experiment: decision tree on the residual surface to discover the grouping maximizing residual heterogeneity, multi-calibrating within learned groups.", "gate": "ADOPT cross-fitting + multi-calibration as mandatory pipeline hygiene if EITHER: (a) removing top-5 volume RBs changes their measured yards-above-expected by >=5% (contamination effect); or (b) cross-fit/multi-calibrated residuals predict next-season efficiency better than raw residuals by >=0.03 correlation points; if neither holds, document the null and keep cross-fitting anyway as cheap insurance.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2401.15161v2", "title": "Individual and team performance in cricket", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port four mechanisms to NFL: (1) era normalization nf = <league scoring>_all / <league scoring>_season for cross-era player comps; (2) NFL fractional contribution fc = 1/2*(player yards/team yards + player EPA/team EPA) as a single-game 'how much of the team was this guy' score for player ratings and anytime-TD reasoning; (3) effective team size S_eff as an injury-vulnerability index - low S_eff = concentrated production = a star injury moves the number more - fed into spread/total adjustments when a high-share player is Q/OUT, with a Herfindahl-style concentration measure weighted by positional replaceability; (4) hot-streak shuffle-null tests (1,000 timestamp-shuffled nulls) as features in anytime-TD/yardage-prop models.", "gate": "ADOPT the S_eff injury-vulnerability index iff the S_eff x star-OUT interaction term is significant (p < 0.05) with the correct sign (low S_eff -> bigger line move) on 2023-2025 injury events; ADOPT fc ratings iff they predict next-week EPA with lower MAE than a rolling-EPA baseline; otherwise REJECT.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2401.16392v3", "title": "A comprehensive survey of the home advantage in American football", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add a Bayesian paired-comparison home-advantage module to the engine: score-differential outcomes on nflverse game logs, season-specific team strengths, league HA term with linear drift - fit weekly, feeding the posterior-mean HA as the engine's home-field term instead of a static 3 (2023 estimate 1.73 pts, ~0.65-point 20-year decline) - with decline-trend detection via P(beta_1 < 0) over a rolling 10-year window (re-baseline if P(decline) > 0.9), strength-adjusted HA features for college lanes, and extensions for betting use: dynamic state-space team strengths, a spline/changepoint term on HA for replay-adoption discontinuities, and crew-level random effects for officiating home bias.", "gate": "ADAPT iff a Stan refit of Model 2 on nflverse NFL data reproduces a 2023 NFL home advantage within the paper's 95% credible interval (1.07-2.39 points); failure to replicate the decline signal or HA magnitude means GSE's home-edge implementation cannot trust this paper's calibration.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2401.17185v1", "title": "Multi-Camera Asynchronous Ball Localization and Trajectory Prediction with Factor Graphs and Human Poses", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build an NFL punt/kickoff flight lab: factor graph with variables (ball 3D pos/vel, spin vector, orientation quaternion for a football) and factors - projection, drag+Magnus lift, gravity, a learned bounce/turf factor, and a spin-prior factor from a TCN on kicker pose (15 frames before foot contact) - implemented with GTSAM/ISAM2 (incremental = real-time capable); serve offline over historical kick plays for a 'kick quality vs outcome' table, online variant feeding the live win-probability engine on kickoffs (touchback probability before the ball lands) - testing learned-vs-analytic bounce factors on tumbling punts.", "gate": "ADOPT if on held-out NFL punts: (a) landing-spot RMSE <= 2.0 yards, AND (b) pose-based spin priors cut early-flight prediction error >=30% vs the no-spin factor graph, AND (c) incremental inference runs <50 ms per detection (real-time viable); reject if the TCN spin prior shows no correlation (R<0.3) with fitted spin on NFL data.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2401.17743v1", "title": "Algorithmic Robust Forecast Aggregation", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Implement the paper's log-odds-style robust aggregator with the tuned mixture parameter in GSE's ensemble layer - input = member-model win probabilities, output = combined probability - extending beyond two experts to the n-expert generalization (averaging pairwise applications or fitting the natural extension, measuring regret vs the two-expert rule) - plus a data-driven variant: estimate the empirical joint distribution of member-model forecasts conditional on outcomes from the picks history, then solve the restricted minimax game against an adversary perturbing within a TVD ball of the empirical structure.", "gate": "ADOPT into the ensemble if, on the 2025 walk-forward test, Brier score improves by >=0.002 and log-loss improves by >=0.005 vs. the current combiner, with Diebold-Mariano p<0.05 on both; robustness sub-gate: the aggregator must not lose to the baseline in any single month-slice by more than 0.003 Brier (worst-case behavior is the point of this paper).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.01914v1", "title": "Predicting Batting Averages in Specific Matchups Using Generalized Linked Matrix Factorization", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port GLMF (heterogeneous linked matrix factorization) to NFL matchup matrices: X = receiver x defense (or QB x defense) binomial matrix (completions/targets, EPA>0 plays/snaps) with aggregate offense/defense stats (normal) as Y/Z side matrices - the direct NFL analog of the paper's batter/pitcher setup - reimplemented from Li & Gaynanova (2018) heterogeneous IRLS + O'Connell & Lock (2019) LMF alternating scheme, swapping the paper's weak aggregate Y/Z for NGS-grade side data (separation, pressure rates, coverage shells) and extending to additional linked matrices (weather, venue, referee crew).", "gate": "ADOPT only if GLMF beats the current GSE shrinkage/matchup prior by a statistically significant log-likelihood margin with zero convergence failures across folds; ADAPT (offline research prior) if it only matches; otherwise REJECT.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.02592v2", "title": "Unified Training of Universal Time Series Forecasting Transformers (Moirai)", "normalized_lane": "timeseries_foundation", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Fine-tune Moirai-Base on the sports pile with multivariate game-day groups (margin, total, QB EPA, RB/WR usage as variates) + future-known covariates (rest, dome, spread) with expanding-window seasonal fine-tuning - serving joint predictive distributions per game for consistent spread/total/prop pricing (no more independent models disagreeing) - with a key-number discrete head: augment the mixture output with point masses at margins {3, 7, 10} (learned weights), testing CRPS + calibration near key numbers vs the pure mixture head.", "gate": "ADOPT for joint spread/total pricing if fine-tuned Moirai's margin CRPS <= best univariate variant AND total CRPS <= best univariate variant on 2021-2024 (joint >= independent, plus consistency wins); ADAPT further if joint beats on one target but not both; REJECT the zero-shot weights for live use if they trail seasonal naive on either target; hard reject on any covariate-leakage flag.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": ["2402.03885v2"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.03035", "title": "1626 An Optimality Property of the Bayes\u2013Kelly Algorithm", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a Bayes-Kelly miscalibration monitor: define a conformity score on each settled pick (signed log-loss residual of engine probability vs outcome); implement the tractable Bayes-Kelly special case with a simple parametric alternative (Beta-family miscalibration); run the test martingale over the settled-pick stream per market (spreads, totals, props separately); wire thresholds - martingale crossing L1 -> halve stakes; crossing L2 -> abstain until mean-reversion - with an empirical-Bayes prior refit monthly on GSE's own miscalibration history.", "gate": "ADOPT if the Bayes-Kelly monitor detects the injected miscalibration regimes at least 30% faster (fewer bets to L1) than the rolling-calibration-error baseline at equal false-alarm rates; otherwise REJECT.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.03885v2", "title": "MOMENT: A Family of Open Time-series Foundation Models", "normalized_lane": "timeseries_foundation", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the 'Sports Time Series Pile' (NFL/NCAA team margins + totals 2002-2024, player weekly usage/fantasy points, NGS-derived team metrics, odds-line histories - normalized to fixed windows, released internally as the GSE pretraining corpus) and pretrain a MOMENT-style encoder (patched, RevIN, masked) on it with forecasting + classification (injury-out? regime-shift?) heads on one backbone - with a cross-channel attention probe: pretrain a variant with cross-variate attention over grouped series (team margin + total + QB EPA as one multivariate patch set), testing whether the multivariate variant beats channel-independent on same-team multi-target forecasting.", "gate": "ADOPT the sports-MOMENT backbone if it beats the N-BEATS baseline on the two-season holdout with >=2% MSE gain AND the masked-pretraining ablation shows pretraining contributes >=1 pt of that gain (else the gain is just architecture, and a simpler model ships); REJECT for live use if fine-tuned MAE does not beat GSE's current engine margin MAE; hard reject on any pretraining-window leakage into test seasons.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.04898v1", "title": "The Strain of Success: A Predictive Model for Injury Risk Mitigation and Team Success in Soccer", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build an NFL load-management decision tool: (1) injury-risk model - gradient boosting or survival model predicting per-player game-miss probability from trailing workload (snaps, touches, days rest, travel, surface, age, prior injury history); (2) existing GSE EPA-based team ratings as the team-strength model; (3) optimizer for rest-vs-play decisions for veterans in low-leverage weeks (Week 18, short-week Thursdays) via expected-points MDP framing with playoff-seeding value replacing raw points - with a competing-risks survival extension: time-to-injury with cause-specific hazards (soft-tissue vs contact vs concussion), the optimizer acting only on the load-attributable (preventable) risk component.", "gate": "ADOPT the injury-risk model only if it beats the snap-count heuristic by >=0.005 Brier on the 2024 chronological holdout with team-clustered bootstrap CIs excluding zero AND the top risk decile has >=2x the base injury rate; REJECT the rest-optimizer for betting/DFS use if the observational backtest cannot reject the null - keep it as content-only ('load management watch').", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.06062v1", "title": "Peer Expectation in Robust Forecast Aggregation", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a peer-expectation feature for each engine component (component forecast + peer proxy = historical average deviation from consensus, or market consensus as the 'peer forecast'), implementing the paper's weighted hard-sigmoid aggregator over (forecast, peer-expectation) pairs - then replace the static peer proxy with a learned peer-expectation model (predicting each component's deviation from consensus from game context: week, home/away, market move direction), feeding predicted peer expectations into the hard-sigmoid rule to measure the marginal value of the peer channel on real correlated model panels.", "gate": "ADOPT the peer-feature aggregator if on the 2025 walk-forward it improves Brier by >=0.002 over the forecasts-only combiner (DM p<0.05) and does not lose on log-loss; REJECT (keep forecasts-only) otherwise; if the gain exists but is <0.002, log as a negative result and do not ship.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.06815v2", "title": "0009 Fine-Tuned Large Event Models (arXiv:2402.06815v2)", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build team-contextualized next-play event models: (1) general NFL event model trained on nflverse play-by-play 2020-2025 (all teams): inputs = pre-play state (down, distance, yardline, score, time, personnel groupings, motion indicators); targets = play type, yards gained bucket, success; (2) per-team fine-tuning on that team's recent games (last 2 seasons, home+away) with reduced LR and early stopping -> 32 team-contextualized simulators; (3) matchup-conditioned fine-tuning with a proper predictive holdout - fine-tune team A's offense vs team B's defense using both teams' histories, validated strictly on future seasons, benchmarked against Elo AND GSE's existing state-space ratings (opponent adjustment is most of the signal in the NFL); (4) player-what-if queries ('how would player X perform in team Y's context') treated as scenario explorations, never predictions; serving: offline simulator for matchup/scenario analysis at the research desk, not a user-facing pick product.", "gate": "ADOPT the fine-tuning recipe only if: the fine-tuned team-context models beat the Elo simulation baseline by >= 1.0 win MAE on the held-out season AND beat the un-fine-tuned general model by >= 0.5 wins MAE (proving the team-context fine-tuning, not just the general model, carries the gain); REJECT if fine-tuned models do not beat Elo, or if the general-vs-fine-tuned gap is nil.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.06820", "title": "Forecasting Events in Soccer Matches Through Language", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build an NFL play-sequence simulator: encode each play as a token tuple (play_type, yards_gained, down, distance, yardline, quarter/time_remaining, score_diff, timeouts, shotgun/no_huddle flag, weather bin) - a 60-90-token ordinal-encoded vocabulary; single Transformer (NFL has ~700k+ plays) predicting one token at a time with the paper's masked-sampler design (only sample tokens valid for the current play-slot position); red-zone / 2-minute drill as the 'reset point' analog for error control; pregame-neutral contexts on 2015-2022, validate 2023, test 2024 (time-ordered); pregame, run ~100k simulations per game from the opening-kickoff state for win probability, total distribution, and any-play prop quantiles; in-game, re-simulate each commercial break for live edges vs sportsbook totals - plus an 'injury/ejection' token: feed beat-reporter injury tweets through an LLM classifier into the event vocabulary as a pseudo-event type (PERSONNEL_CHANGE), so the simulator's context updates when a star QB exits.", "gate": "ADOPT the simulator design if: next-play-type accuracy >= 62% on held-out 2024 NFL season AND win-probability calibration (Brier) on 2024 games <= GSE's current model v5.2.7 win-probability Brier on the same games; REJECT if either fails.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.08328v1", "title": "Dual Likelihood for Causal Inference under Structure Uncertainty", "normalized_lane": "causal_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add dual-likelihood 95% confidence regions for causal effects under structure uncertainty: for each high-confidence edge in the quarterly causal graph (ledgers 1962-1966 consensus), compute the dual-likelihood 95% confidence region for the total causal effect (e.g. C(pressure rate -> defensive EPA/play)) - prune ordering space with the DAGuerreotype ordering (ledger 1966) before the bottom-up search; compute regions for the top-20 edges by |effect|; store (edge, effect CI) in the graph artifact; content rule: any published causal claim must cite the interval, claims whose CI covers 0 are downgraded to 'associated with' language - plus a variance-robustness layer: drop equal-variance via computing regions under a grid of variance-ratio bounds (sigma^2_max/sigma^2_min <= kappa for kappa in {1,2,5}), reporting how CIs widen as kappa grows, giving a principled ranking of which causal claims survive realistic variance heterogeneity.", "gate": "ADOPT dual-likelihood CIs for published causal claims if: (a) simulation coverage >= 0.93 at d=20, n=380; (b) real-data runtime < 10 min for 20 edges with pruning; (c) the intervals are informative - median width <= 2x the oracle-structure width; reject if coverage < 0.90 or median width > 3x oracle.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["1803.01422", "2301.11898"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.09444", "title": "Multimodal Action Quality Assessment", "normalized_lane": "multimodal_fusion", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build play-execution quality regression with adaptive modality fusion: predict per-play EPA (or PFF-style grade proxy) from (a) broadcast-video features, (b) tracking-derived 'flow' features (player velocities - the analog of optical flow), (c) stadium audio (crowd noise level, snap cadence); keep the Adaptive Fusion Module with PolicyNet - the learned per-segment fusion weights become an interpretable 'which signal mattered when' readout (e.g. audio weight spikes pre-snap on false starts); train modality branches separately (tracking branch on EPA labels first), then freeze video/tracking and tune the fusion (the paper's two-phase recipe); use: (1) a play-quality feature for the engine, (2) content ('the model says crowd noise decided this drive' graphics), (3) a diagnostic - if the PolicyNet consistently zeroes a modality, drop it (cost saving) - plus event-anchored PolicyNet: anchor fusion decisions to football's natural phases (pre-snap, post-snap-to-throw, catch-point, tackle) with a separate ranked FusionNet bank per phase and a phase classifier gating them.", "gate": "ACCEPT: adaptive fusion beats BOTH the tracking-only model (Spearman +0.03) AND naive weighted fusion (+0.02) on the 2024 test; REJECT: fails to beat naive fusion or loses to tracking-only. Pre-registered before running.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.10979v2", "title": "SportsMetrics: Blending Text and Numerical Data to Understand Information Fusion in LLMs", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build 'GSE Stat-Claim Harness v1' (content-QC, not engine): 50 recent NFL games' nflverse play-by-play + official box scores (public, reproducible); tasks: (1) pbp -> JSON stat fill (team points, passing/rushing yards, turnovers, sacks); (2) masked-recap fill-in on GSE's own published DFS write-ups; (3) affiliation-swap adversarial (swap two players' teams in the roster table); (4) unit-change adversarial (report all yardage in meters); metric: exact-match rate on filled stats + mean absolute deviation, per model; use: gate LLM-generated stat claims before they reach X posts/scripts - any claim the harness shows the model gets wrong at >5% gets routed to deterministic template rendering from nflverse instead of free generation - plus a tool-using variant: the LLM must emit executable pandas queries against the provided pbp dataframe and paste back query results before filling stats (execution-grounded rather than memory-grounded).", "gate": "ADOPT the harness into the content pipeline IF condition (B) beats (A) by >=10 percentage points of exact-match stat accuracy on the 50-game fixture AND the adversarial unit-change task shows <15% degradation; REJECT the scaffold (keep only the eval harness as a monitor) if it fails either.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.11191", "title": "1715 Knowledge graph assisted automatic sports news writing", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build gse/content/recap_pipeline.py in three stages: (1) event ingestion - parse NFL/NBA play-by-play into (period, time, team, event, score) tuples; (2) KEE-style segmentation - replace the fixed 8-point threshold with a sport-specific win-probability-swing detector (segment on |DeltaWP| >= 10 pp or scoring-run extrema); (3) KG enrichment - link entities to GSE's player/team/injury graph and inject verified attributes (season stats, injury status, line movement) into the generation prompt as structured context, every injected fact cited to its source row; generation = template + LLM hybrid, the LLM may only use KG-provided facts for numbers/names, with an entity-linking confidence gate (any linked entity below 0.9 confidence is dropped) - plus: (1) make the KG temporal - snapshot player/team/injury attributes at kickoff, forbid post-game knowledge in enrichment, then run the paper's own ROUGE + human protocol twice (static vs kickoff-snapshot KG) to quantify how much of its reported gain is post-game leakage; (2) a learned segmenter: train a small classifier on analyst-labeled 'news-worthy passage' boundaries using WP swing, scoring-run length, and injury-event indicators.", "gate": "ADAPT the architecture (event segmentation -> entity linking -> KG-enriched generation), not the paper's artifacts; ADAPT only if the reproducible test shows the factual-error reduction with the WP-swing segmenter on NFL data; REJECT the KG-enrichment step (keep KEE-style segmentation only) if entity-linking precision on NFL text falls below 95%.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.12400", "title": "Estimating the age-conditioned average treatment effects curves: An application for assessing load-management strategies in the NBA", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build gse-acte-rest: unit = player-game; treatment definitions: W=1 short rest (<=3 days since last game, TNF short week) vs W=0 normal rest, plus W=1 travel >2000 miles vs 0; outcomes: EPA/play, success rate, fantasy points per game, snap-weighted; team-level: offensive/defensive EPA; covariates: player, team, opponent, home/away/neutral, season+week fixed effects, opponent Elo, weather; model: X-learner with honest RF base + S-learner spline baseline, propensity model on age+covariates; simulation sanity gate first (replicate the paper's 3-scenario DGP with NFL-like treatment prevalence); serving: precompute tau-hat(a) curves per position group; at prediction time, adjust player projections by age-specific rest/travel treatment effect when conditions differ from league average; feed tau-hat into the injury-risk/workload overlay - plus upgrade to continuous dose-response: replace W in {0,1} with days-of-rest as continuous dose via a generalized propensity score / DR-learner, estimating age-conditioned dose-response curves tau(a,d) (a graded rest adjustment, e.g. +x% projection bump per rest day, age-specific).", "gate": "ADOPT the ACTE rest-adjustment into GSE projections only if: (a) on the synthetic DGP, X-learner+RF recovers the true nonlinear tau(a) with MSE at least 30% below the naive difference-in-means estimator; (b) on real NFL data, the 90% bootstrap CI for at least one position group's ACTE excludes zero over a contiguous age band >=3 years AND the direction matches domain sense; (c) cross-learner sign agreement: S/T/X agree on sign in >=70% of age bins with n>=200 games; otherwise reject - fall back to simple age x rest interaction terms.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.15391v1", "title": "Genie: Generative Interactive Environments", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "'GSE-LAM': apply the LAM recipe to structured NGS tracking sequences (not pixels, to keep compute sane): encoder takes tracking frames x_{1:t} and x_{t+1} -> discrete latent action a-tilde_t (codebook |A| = 32-64, larger than 8 for football's richer action space); decoder reconstructs the next tracking frame from history + a-tilde_t; the learned codebook becomes an UNSUPERVISED PLAY-CONCEPT vocabulary - discovered route concepts, run schemes, blitz packages - usable as the action/token vocabulary for the 1944/1948 sequence models instead of hand-engineered play-type labels; encoder/decoder over (x, y, vx, vy) arrays per player - plus hierarchical LAM: a coarse codebook (|A|=8, run/pass/special-teams-ish) plus a fine codebook (|A|=64) conditioned on the coarse code, mirroring football's natural hierarchy (play family -> specific concept).", "gate": "ADOPT the LAM-discovered codebook as GSE's play-descriptor vocabulary if interpretability purity >=80% on run/pass/play-action AND the downstream 1948 test is within 5% of hand-labeled descriptors (parity = free vocabulary, no manual labeling); REJECT if codes collapse (utilization <50%) or purity <60%; REJECT pixel-level Genie replication (compute) - the structured-tracking LAM is the portable core.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2209.00588", "2010.02193"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.15588v1", "title": "Sizing the bets in a focused portfolio", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port the constrained multivariate Kelly to Python (scipy Newton / SLSQP with constraint enumeration for N <= 10; SLSQP directly on the log-growth objective for larger N); inputs: engine win probabilities per pick, odds -> payoff multiples, joint outcome model (start with independence + game-level blocks, graduate to bootstrap covariance); constraints: long-only, no leverage, max 25% per pick, P=1% / K=30% permanent-loss constraint for the public bankroll - plus estimate the joint outcome distribution with a Gaussian copula fit on historical pick residuals (per-pick marginals from the engine's calibration curve) instead of assuming independence, and re-solve (accounting for correlated losses - bad weeks hit many picks - shrinks aggregate exposure and cuts tail drawdown vs the independence solution).", "gate": "ADOPT if walk-forward max drawdown <= 0.25-Kelly's drawdown at ROI within 1 pp of the best baseline; REJECT if the joint-probability estimation step dominates (performance collapses under bootstrap covariance vs independence - then the method is not usable without a better dependence model).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.15862", "title": "SportQA: A Benchmark for Sports Understanding in Large Language Models", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build a GSE LLM content gate: clone SportQA (public GitHub), extract the American-football L2/L3 subsets + all scenario-style L3 questions (all 6 sports, for generalization signal); build a GSE eval harness: run candidate models (the ones GSE actually uses for content: GPT-series, Gemini, Llama, Nemotron via NVIDIA NIM) at temperature 0, 5-shot SP + 5-shot CoT with the repo's dev exemplars, scoring accuracy by level; write ~200 GSE-specific questions in the L3 multiple-select style targeting what the benchmark lacks (NFL rules edge cases, fantasy scoring implications, pick-rationale QA), reviewed by a domain expert; use the harness as the gate for any LLM swap in the x-poster/kit content pipeline - a model must clear >= the incumbent's SportQA-football accuracy before it drafts public copy - plus a decision-weighted score: sample GSE's real content decisions (which reply drafts got posted, which were held at <9.2) and test whether a model's SportQA L3 score predicts its draft-acceptance rate (point-biserial r > 0.3 on >=300 drafts).", "gate": "ADAPT if: (a) the SportQA repo is downloadable and the football subsets extract cleanly (>=1,000 L2 + >=200 L3 football questions parse), AND (b) at least one GSE-used model scores within 5 pp of the paper's GPT-4 L3 football numbers, confirming the harness discriminates on 2026 models; reject (the adaptation, not the paper) if the dataset link is dead or football content is <500 questions - then fall back to the companion paper 2406.14877's instrument instead.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.16300", "title": "1026 Conformalized Selective Regression", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Apply CSR to GSE's prop/DFS point projections: fit two quantile regressors (LightGBM quantile at alpha/2 and 1-alpha/2, alpha=0.10 for 90% intervals) on the existing prop projection feature set; conformalize on a recent calibration window (last 4-6 NFL weeks, ~10-20% of training rows); abstain (don't publish / don't bet) when W_alpha(X) >= lambda, with lambda set to hit a target coverage (e.g. 90%); quantile fits batch-fit weekly, interval width computed per slate at publish time, reject decisions logged with widths for the coverage-error curve - plus weight the economics: replace the paper's unweighted distance with an expected-profit objective - profit = (edge x stake x hit-rate) - (abstention opportunity cost) - choosing lambda to maximize backtested P&L at fixed bankroll; make alpha adaptive per slate (fit on the calibration window to maximize the profit objective); try Mondrian conformalization by position group (QB/RB/WR/TE props) since prop error distributions are strongly position-heterogeneous.", "gate": "ADOPT CSR if, on the held-out weeks 15-18 test window, CSR's 90%-coverage MAE is >= 5% lower than the conditional-variance reject baseline at the same coverage, AND empirical coverage of the conformal intervals on the calibration window is within +/-3 points of the nominal 90%; reject if the width rule does not beat ensemble-spread rejection or if coverage calibration drifts >5 points (exchangeability failure).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2402.17453v5", "title": "DS-Agent: Automated Data Science by Empowering Large Language Models with Case-Based Reasoning", "normalized_lane": "llm_agents_ai_scientist", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a GSE case bank as the memory substrate for the discovery loop, on top of the 2082 harness: case schema (SQLite): (case_id, hypothesis_text, feature_code, backtest_spec, feedback_log (the 2084 Reflexion reflections), dev_score (2025-holdout DeltaBrier), stage3_score (locked-season), retained_flag, embedding); seed with the 5 hand-verified baseline signals + every future discovery-loop attempt (including failures); development stage (nightly): idea generator retrieves top-k cases by embedding similarity to the new hypothesis; ReviseRank step: an LLM re-ranks cases conditioned on the last night's feedback; planner writes the experiment plan reusing the top case; executor runs; retain if it passes the Stage-2 gate; deployment stage (weekly, cheap): retrieve the current best production-pipeline case and regenerate the weekly model-fit code with minor adaptation on a small/cheap model - plus counter-case retrieval: for each retrieved success case, also retrieve the most similar FAILED case and inject its feedback into the planner prompt, testing whether negative cases prevent repeating known failure modes faster than positive cases guide success.", "gate": "ADOPT if: CBR arm passes >=6/10 hypotheses within budget vs <=3/10 cold-start; ReviseRank demonstrably demotes at least one misleading case per night on average; deployment-stage regeneration succeeds one-pass >=80% of weeks over 8 weeks with the small model; REJECT if cold-start matches within 1 hypothesis, or retained cases show score decay on re-run (bank poisoning), or ReviseRank rankings are uncorrelated with next-iteration outcomes.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INVENT", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2408.06292v3", "2303.11366v4"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2403.00578v1", "title": "SINDy vs Hard Nonlinearities and Hidden Dynamics: a Benchmarking Study", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Discover game-state dynamics equations: build game-state trajectories from nflverse pbp: state = [score_diff, time_remaining, yardline, down, distance, EPA_rolling, timeouts] per game (~60-160 steps); observed output = win probability or points scored; PySINDy with control: inputs = game-context controls (home, rest, spread); library = 2nd-order polynomials + abs terms (|score_diff| for garbage-time nonlinearities) + indicator terms for turnovers/red zone; derivative-coordinate trick: add d(score_diff)/d(play) and d(time)/d(play) as constructed states; hidden-state strategy for 'momentum': posit a latent variable h with assumed linear restoring structure, reconstruct h per game from residual dynamics, fit h-dot with a SINDy library (the Bouc-Wen iterative recipe applied to sports); evaluate on open-loop simulation of 2025 games - plus weak-form SINDy for NFL: replace derivative fitting with the integral/weak formulation applied to the game-state trajectories, testing whether weak-form recovers sparser, more stable equations than STLS.", "gate": "ADOPT if: hidden-state SINDy achieves BFR >= 70% on the held-out 2025 Weeks 1-8 window AND beats both baselines by >= 10 BFR points AND the recovered equation contains <= 8 nonzero terms; REJECT if: BFR < 50%, or metric-optimal model is structurally nonsensical on human review, or baselines win.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2403.03862v1", "title": "An analysis of the NCAA college football playoff team selections using an Elo ratings model", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a tuned-Elo baseline on nflverse 2000-2025: all 32 teams init 1500, K-factor tuned (grid 10-60) against log-loss of implied win probability on out-of-sample games, expected-outcome formula with the 400 divisor; add NFL-relevant extensions the paper lacks: home-field offset (~55 Elo points, tuned), margin-of-victory multiplier (scaled by log margin / expected-margin), preseason prior regression toward 1500 (~60-70% carryover tuned); features: game result only, from nflverse schedules - plus a per-season Bayesian Elo with team-specific K drawn from a hierarchical prior (strong teams learn faster; early-season games get lower effective K via time-decay), fit by maximizing out-of-sample log-loss.", "gate": "ADOPT the tuned-Elo spec if grid-tuned K + HFA + regression-to-mean beats the paper's fixed recipe (init 1500, K=25, no HFA) by >=0.005 mean log-loss on 2020-2025, with a Brier-score improvement in the same direction; REJECT if the tuned variant fails to beat the fixed recipe.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2403.04873v2", "title": "The SIDO Performance Model for League of Legends", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Own/ally/enemy attribution for NFL skill positions on nflverse play-by-play: own model - e.g. WR yards/route = beta_0 + b_scheme + b_player + epsilon (scheme/team random effect analogous to champion); ally model - residualize teammates' production (other WRs' yards, RB efficiency) and model the sum of residuals on the player; enemy model - e.g. pass-rusher's effect on opposing QB EPA (metric = -b_p); start with QBs (effect on teammates' EPA) and edge rushers (effect on opponent dropback EPA); adopt the Franks et al. meta-metrics as GSE's metric-QC gate: every new advanced metric must report discrimination (signal vs sampling noise), independence (new information vs existing metrics, Gaussian copula), stability (concordance across season halves); honesty rule: low-discrimination components get bucketed into categories, not published as continuous rankings - plus per-teammate-pair effects: fit QB->specific-WR chemistry as a random interaction rather than one pooled ally effect, testing whether QB-WR pair effects predict next-season performance of reunited pairs (a 'stack' signal for DFS/betting grounded in the SIDO framework).", "gate": "Adopt the attribution framework if the own-effect model beats raw EPA/dropback on out-of-sample prediction RMSE (train 2020-2023, predict 2024-2025 player efficiency) AND achieves discrimination >=0.5 with stability concordance >=0.6; reject ally/enemy continuous scores if their discrimination <0.3: bucket them into the 5 categories instead of publishing numbers.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2403.07815v2", "title": "Chronos: Learning the Language of Time Series", "normalized_lane": "timeseries_foundation", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Chronos for NFL team margins: (1) baseline experiment - zero-shot Chronos-T5-Small/Base on weekly NFL team-margin series (2002-2024), score WQL/MASE vs the engine's current margins; (2) sports adaptation - fine-tune Chronos-T5-Small on GSE's sports corpus (team margins, totals, player usage) using the paper's recipe (AdamW, low LR, early stopping on seasonal holdout); use sampled paths as the probabilistic engine input for spread/total pricing; (3) covariate extension: adopt ChronosX (ledger 2127) adapters on top of the fine-tuned Chronos to inject weather, rest, injuries - do not reinvent covariate handling; (4) serving: batch-infer quantile paths per game, feed WQL-calibrated distributions to the moneyline/CLV pricing layer - plus a tokenization resolution study: re-quantize with finer vocab (8192 bins) or learned quantization on sports series, measuring whether sub-point precision (matters for key numbers 3/7) improves WQL, combined with a mean-scale replacement (robust scale = median absolute deviation).", "gate": "ADOPT into the engine's probabilistic path if fine-tuned Chronos beats the engine's current margin MAE by >=0.3 points AND its WQL is <=0.95x the SeasonalNaive baseline on 2021-2024; ADAPT (keep researching) if it only matches; REJECT the covariate-free variant for live pricing if WQL does not beat naive; hard reject if any sample-path distribution fails a calibration check (empirical coverage of 80% intervals deviates >5 pts from nominal).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2503.12107v1"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2403.10826v2", "title": "MambaMOT: State-Space Model as Motion Predictor for Multi-Object Tracking", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Tracking-upgrade lane shared with ledger 0063 (MambaTrack): defer to 0063's bidirectional predictor for the motion model itself (it beats MambaMOT on SportsMOT, 72.6 vs 71.3 HOTA); the marginal contribution worth taking from MambaMOT is the cheap O(N) tracklet-merging head via trajectory embeddings - directly useful for stitching fragmented player tracklets across broadcast camera cuts and occlusion-heavy pile-ups; build plan: implement the Mamba motion predictor per the mamba-ssm reference (input [x,y,w,h] box history -> linear lift -> 2 Mamba blocks -> MLP heads for box prediction and trajectory embedding); train on GSE-labeled broadcast tracking (SportsMOT as a warm start); plug into a ByteTrack-style association loop replacing the Kalman predict step; add the post-hoc hierarchical-clustering merge (cosine on embeddings, 50-frame/50-pixel veto gates tuned to football); benchmark IDF1/HOTA against the current Kalman baseline - plus fuse the trajectory embedding with an appearance (jersey-number) embedding, tune merge thresholds to football with a shot-boundary-aware merge gate, and extend predictor input to full NGS-style state (velocity, orientation).", "gate": "ADOPT the merging head only if tracklet fragmentation drops >= 20% at equal-or-better IDF1 vs Kalman; ADOPT the motion predictor only if it beats 0063 head-to-head on HOTA; latency must clear >= 25 FPS; if none hold, REJECT and defer to 0063.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2408.09178v1"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2403.11016v3", "title": "Comprehensive OOS Evaluation of Predictive Algorithms with Statistical Decision Theory", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "As engine-honesty infrastructure, adopt minimax-regret (MMR) engine selection: define the state space S = (training-era, prediction-era) pairs (e.g. train 2019-2022 -> predict 2023) plus stressed states (post-rule-change seasons, QB-injury clusters, weather-extreme slates); define the SDF: c(.) = [data -> GSE probabilities -> bet/no-bet + stake rule]; loss = negative bankroll log-growth (or negative CLV) per slate; compute regret per state: for each candidate engine variant (v5.2.7 vs challengers), Monte-Carlo over bootstrap resamples of the training era -> expected loss, regret = expected loss - best-variant loss in that state; report maximum regret across S alongside the usual average backtest; prefer the engine with small maximum regret ('uniformly near-optimal') over the one with the best average but a catastrophic regime - plus make the state space adversarial: an automated 'regime generator' searching over plausible perturbations (injury rates, line-shading shifts, weather distributions) for the state maximizing each engine's regret - max regret by optimization rather than a hand-picked grid.", "gate": "Adopt MMR as a standing engine-selection criterion if the max-regret ranking disagrees with the average-backtest ranking on at least one real engine decision in 2024-2025 (it changes a choice we would otherwise make) - that demonstrates the doctrine adds information; if max-regret and average-backtest always agree, keep reporting MMR as a diagnostic but do not let it override averages.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2403.12385", "title": "Benchmarking Badminton Action Recognition with a New Fine-Grained Dataset", "normalized_lane": "sports_cv", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the architecture-selection ladder for GSE's video action-recognition lane: reproduce the paper's ranking (ST-GCN/PoseC3D top at 10-50 shots; SlowFast/Swin top at full data) and re-run the ladder with player-disjoint folds (group clips by athlete into 5 folds) to measure how much absolute accuracies drop and whether the skeleton-first ranking survives - this quantifies identity-leakage inflation and produces GSE a leak-corrected benchmark; add a VPD-style distilled-pose backbone to the ladder.", "gate": "The architecture-selection harness is adopted only if the reproduced ranking matches the paper's within +/-3pp - if the ranking does not reproduce, treat the paper as dataset-only and re-derive GSE's own ranking from scratch.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2403.12977v3", "title": "SportsNGEN: Sustained Generation of Realistic Multi-player Sports Gameplay", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build an NFL multi-player gameplay generator on NFL Next Gen Stats tracking (22 players + ball at 10 Hz, aligned to play-level outcomes: EPA, win probability added): replace tennis-specific heads (rally stopping) with play-boundary logic (whistle/end-of-play); identity embeddings per NFL player with a fallback 'generic' embedding for rookies/trades (addressing the paper's OOD weakness); grid resolution scaled to the NFL field (finer in x given yard-line value); same decoder skeleton (4-layer transformer, categorical grid offsets, nucleus sampling); add conditioning on play-call context (down, distance, formation, personnel) as context tokens for counterfactual use ('what if we blitzed / ran play-action'); per-season training with walk-forward validation across seasons; realism judged by distributional statistics of generated plays (yards gained distribution, time-to-throw) vs real tracking; offline batch counterfactual studies (100 rollouts per game-state of interest on GPU workers) - plus condition generation on defensive scheme and personnel groupings as structured context tokens (Cover-2 vs Cover-3 shell, nickel vs base), and replace the flat grid with hierarchical coarse-to-fine binning (coarse zone -> fine offset) to reduce output-head parameter count and sharpen fine field-position fidelity.", "gate": "Adopt the simulation lane only if BOTH hold on the Weeks 13-17 test window: (a) the decoder's generated yardage distributions achieve 1-Wasserstein distance <= 0.75x that of the Markov baseline in at least 4 of 6 play-type bins; and (b) the forced-blitz counterfactual shifts sack rate in the historically correct direction with magnitude within 50% of the observed historical blitz/non-blitz gap; reject (do not invest beyond the prototype) if either fails.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2403.13821", "title": "Offensive Lineup Analysis in Basketball with Clustering Players Based on Shooting Style and Offensive Role", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Lineup role-composition features for GSE's NBA projections: recompute shooting styles (Wasserstein + Ward) and roles (fuzzy C-means) on recent seasons; for each projected lineup, emit role indicators + the top role-pair interactions as engineered features (+/-0.2-0.5 OFFRTG-scale adjustments); NGBoost (or GSE's existing probabilistic head) predicting player-level fantasy points with lineup-role features; keep the Bayesian hierarchical pair-effect estimator as an offline diagnostic; use: adjust usage/assist/points props when lineups change (injury/trade), especially for role pairs with |effect| > 0.25 - plus replace hard cluster assignments with fuzzy membership weights as continuous features, and add a scheme/team random effect to absorb the Jokic/Spurs/Warriors idiosyncrasy.", "gate": "ADAPT: role-composition NGBoost beats the prior-style baseline on all three metrics (RMSE 4.786 < 4.850, MAE 3.869 < 3.942, NLL 3.066 < 3.089), and the hierarchical model yields interpretable, signed pair effects up to +/-0.47; improvement success = RMSE <= 4.5 on the same lineup-prediction protocol (>= ~6% relative improvement over 4.786).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2403.13893v2", "title": "DAVED: Data Acquisition via Experimental Design for Data Markets", "normalized_lane": "active_learning", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Reframe weekly model training as the data market: buyer test queries = this week's slate (unlabeled by definition - games unplayed), seller pool = historical games with charting costs c_j, budget B = weekly compute/charting dollars; features phi(x): current model embeddings (or GBM leaf-encodings / last-layer features); run FW herding (Eq. 6-8) or the single-step variant to select the training subset minimizing V-optimal proxy error on this week's slate; train the week's head on the selected subset - replacing 'train on last N weeks / all history' with 'train on the history most informative for these specific matchups' - compose with ledger 2008: the same budget B governs both training-data acquisition (DAVED) and new charting acquisition (ConBatch-BAL) - split B between them by the marginal proxy-loss reduction each buys - plus a hybrid selector: DAVED's V-optimal term for matchup-relevance plus an explicit recency prior folded into the initial weights w_0 (initialize w_0 proportional to exp(-age/tau) instead of uniform 1/n) before FW herding; tau becomes a tunable 'football memory' parameter, ablated over {4, 8, 17, 34} weeks.", "gate": "ADOPT DAVED-selected training sets iff they beat the recency-window baseline by >= 0.003 weekly ATS log-loss averaged over the 2024 season AND beat it in >= 10 of 18 weeks (consistency), with the win holding under both cost functions (sqrt(c), c^2); REJECT if DAVED ~= recency or if it underperforms random selection in any 4-week stretch.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2507.04929"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2403.14769", "title": "Fractional Tackles: A New Defensive Statistic Derived from Player Tracking Data", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Tracking-derived fractional tackle credit: detect contact windows (1.5-yard rule) on run plays; compute window values from a ball-carrier end-of-play model; attribute credit by peak toward-carrier velocity; aggregate per defender per game/season; outputs: per-player fractional-tackle rate (per play, per snap) -> features for IDP projections and tackle-prop pricing; first-contact share as a separate 'disruption' feature; extend to pass plays: pressure windows (distance-to-QB < threshold) with sack/throwaway value attribution - plus learn the attribution shares (gradient-boosted model predicting window value from defender kinematic features) instead of the fixed velocity rule, and extend windows to pass plays.", "gate": "ADAPT: split-half reliability 0.69 > 0.59 overall and better in all three position groups; 2.5x coverage (19,691 vs. 7,720 instances); public code + data; improvement success = split-half reliability >= 0.72 on run plays and >= 0.60 on pass-rush windows, with the learned shares outperforming the velocity heuristic in window-value cross-validation.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2403.16282v1", "title": "The Evolution of Football Betting: A Machine Learning Approach to Match Outcome Forecasting and Bookmaker Odds Estimation", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "As engine-honesty infrastructure, port the two empirical priors as feature-selection guidance: prioritize xG-family features (xG, xGA, SCA, GCA) at the top of GSE's NFL analog feature list (EPA, success rate, explosive-play rate - the NFL equivalents of chance-creation metrics); treat draw/no-result and tie-ish outcomes as intrinsically low-signal classes - do not over-allocate model capacity to them; for NFL this maps to not overfitting push/OT edge cases; REJECT the paper's classifiers themselves - KEEP the feature priors - plus a draw-difficulty analog: quantify the engine's current accuracy on 'coin-flip' NFL games (spread within +/-2.5) vs the rest; if coin-flip accuracy is near 50%, test whether abstaining or stake-reducing on those games improves bankroll growth under fractional Kelly - turning the paper's descriptive finding into a staking rule.", "gate": "If EPA-family features rank top-3 in the univariate screen, the paper's finding is confirmed as a prior and GSE's existing feature hierarchy stands - ledger closes as guidance-only; if raw yardage dominates EPA, flag a feature-engineering review.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2404.00030v1", "title": "Visualization of Unstructured Sports Data - An Example of Cricket Short Text Commentary", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Tendency-rule miner v1: build confrontation matrices from nflverse play descriptions - rows = offensive player response features (target depth, separation proxy, YAC bucket), columns = defensive features (coverage shell, blitz, press); run correspondence analysis per player-season (>=150 routes); extract top-2 'strength' (high-success) and 'weakness' (low-success) rules as <F, G_j> argmax pairs; similar-player clustering via t-SNE/UMAP on concatenated rule vectors for comp-based DFS/prop projections (find cheap comps with the same tendency profile); validate by replicating the paper's two studies - expert check against established scouting reports, Procrustes train/test (prior season vs current season) stability - plus replace the hand-built feature taxonomy with a learned one: run a domain-tuned LLM over the raw commentary to extract (attribute, response) structured tuples, then apply CA on the learned taxonomy.", "gate": "ADAPT the CA rule-mining template now; ADOPT for matchup modeling only if cross-season Procrustes stability holds (median Delta^2 <= 0.35) and weakness-rule matchups predict target-share shortfalls out-of-sample; otherwise REJECT as a descriptive/visualization tool only.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2404.02270v2", "title": "Postprocessing point predictions for probabilistic forecasting: IDR beats DDNN", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Postprocess GSE's point predictions with IDR: calibrate the engine's point forecasts into probabilistic forecasts using isotonic distributional regression, ensembled with the Gaussian-error benchmark (LEAR-N analog) - combine IDR with mAFTER-style adaptive weighting (ledger 0786) across multiple calibration windows instead of the simple vertical average, since window selection is where IDR's volatility lives (the poor Dec-2019-Apr-2021 stretch) - adaptively weighting windows should capture the upside while dampening the bad spells.", "gate": "CPA test: IDR-ensemble significantly outperforms Gaussian-error benchmark at 5% in both market-type subsets; Shapley contribution of IDR to the ensemble > 40%.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["1505.00475v1"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2404.04213", "title": "Modelling handball outcomes using univariate and bivariate approaches", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "ZI-Skellam2 margin model: univariate NFL margin Z (home-away points) ~ ZI-Skellam2(mu, sigma^2, p) with mu_jk = alpha + beta_j + gamma_k (team home/away abilities from nflverse 2015-2025); push handling: interpret p as excess mass at Z == spread (recenter Z' = Z - spread per game) - this converts the ZI trick from 'draws' to 'pushes', directly pricing push probability into spread bets; bivariate half model: (1H diff, 2H diff) with Skellam2 marginals + Frank copula, team abilities shared vs half-specific; output: halftime-conditional P(win), P(cover), P(over) for the live-betting surface; season sim: 10,000 Monte Carlo replications of remaining schedule for playoff-probability content - plus quarter-by-quarter vine copula: extend to four quarters with a D-vine of Frank copulas, Skellam2 marginals, abilities allowed a linear 'fatigue/adjustment' trend across quarters, testing whether NFL halves/quarters are strategically asymmetric.", "gate": "Adopt if ZI-Skellam2 beats plain Skellam2 by AIC >= 10 on the 2024-2025 holdout AND predicted push rate is within 0.5pp of observed AND halftime-conditional Brier beats a naive 'halftime leader wins' baseline by >=0.01; reject otherwise (fall back to the plain Skellam); the bivariate half model is adopted only if Model B (Frank, shared abilities) beats Model A (independence) by AIC >= 10.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2404.06332v1", "title": "X-VARS: Introducing Explainability in Football Refereeing with Multi-Modal Large Language Models", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "GSE 'show your work' cards: for each published pick, inject the engine's structured outputs (win prob, spread, key edges, top features) as text into a fine-tuned LLM prompt, generating a 3-5 sentence analyst-style rationale; data: GSE's historical posted picks + analyst-written rationales (X post history, weekly packets) as the explanation corpus; training: QLoRA fine-tune of an open LLM (same 1%-of-layers recipe as the paper) on (structured prediction -> rationale) pairs, plus a multi-task classification head so the model also predicts the pick, enabling the same agreement diagnostic; serving: batch generation at pick-publication time, human review before posting (fits the existing approve-desk gate) - plus a structured consistency loss: penalize the model when its generated text contradicts the injected numbers (extract numbers from generated text with regex/NER and compare to inputs).", "gate": "Adopt if blind mean rating >= human mean - 0.3 AND prediction-text agreement >= 90% (fixing the paper's faithfulness gap is the point); reject otherwise - a fluent but unfaithful narrator is worse than no narrator for a picks business.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2404.06587", "title": "Bunting and the ghost runner: a causal inference approach", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Compact IPW template for data-vs-conventional-wisdom strategy findings, applied to NFL special teams: causal effect of fair-catching (vs returning) kickoffs on drive expected points - nflverse pbp kickoffs 2018-2024, treatment = fair catch / touchback (no return), outcome = EP of ensuing drive; confounders: returner quality, kicking-team coverage quality (DVOA-style), weather, score/time, kicker hang-time/distance; propensity: logistic/GBM; IPW with [0.1, 0.9] trimming; doubly robust (outcome regression + IPW); product: 'NFL teams are leaving points on the field by returning kickoffs' causal content + a fair-catch recommendation feature in GSE's kickoff model - plus: use Next Gen Stats returner top-speed / coverage-team closing-speed metrics as confounders the paper's box-score stats cannot capture, and run a Rosenbaum-style sensitivity analysis (absent from the paper) to report the Gamma at which the OR=1.86 finding breaks.", "gate": "ADAPT the IPW template if the kickoff replication achieves |SMD| < 0.1 on all confounders, propensity AUC >= 0.65, and the doubly robust EP difference has 95% CI excluding 0 with |effect| >= 0.15 EP/drive; REJECT if the CI includes 0 or the placebo punt analysis shows a 'significant' effect (residual confounding).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2404.08254v1", "title": "Fair Tab Diffusion: Multivariate Guidance + Balanced Sampling for Rare-Regime Synthesis", "normalized_lane": "synthetic_data", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Regime-oversampling module on top of the chosen synthetic backbone (TabSyn or TabRep from ledgers 2066/2067): train the backbone generator with regime attributes included as columns (weather severity, rest days bin, prime-time, division game, dome/altitude); add multivariate classifier-free guidance head: condition on (outcome class c, regime attrs S) with the security gate (tune lambda, delta, w_s on a validation slice); balanced sampling: empirical outcome distribution x uniform regime distribution, balancing dial i in {0, 5, 10} - i=0 replicates history, i=10 uniform over regimes; generate tail-regime synthetic seasons at i=10 (e.g. 2x historical rate of severe-weather and short-rest games), mix with empirical synthetic seasons at low weight - plus a learned balancing schedule: make the balancing level a function of downstream need - i(s) per regime cell, set proportional to the current model's tail-slice calibration error on that cell (worse-calibrated cells get more synthetic mass), turning the static dial into an active-learning loop for synthetic data.", "gate": "ADOPT the balancing module if: (a) tail-slice log-loss improves by >=0.01 at i=10 vs i=0, AND (b) overall 2024 log-loss does not degrade by more than 0.001 vs i=0, AND (c) the security gate keeps outcome-marginal drift <=2% TVD between i=0 and i=10 samples; REJECT if any gate fails or if tuning (lambda, delta, w_s) proves unstable across 3 seeds.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2310.09656", "2504.04798"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2404.10495v2", "title": "Assumption-Lean Quantile Regression via Efficient Influence Functions", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Distributional prop analysis with honest CIs: the effect of matchup/weather/rest variables on a player's yardage distribution (median vs 90th percentile), for GSE's 'most calibrated' positioning; implementation: DoubleML-style cross-fitting + TMLE fluctuation; nuisance models = gradient boosting for E(A|L) and quantile forests for Q_tau; kernel density for f(Y|.) at the quantile; start at tau in {.25, .5, .75} before attempting extremes; data: nflverse player-game features 2015-2024 - plus stabilized density estimation: replace the paper's density-at-quantile estimator with a conformalized quantile-density approach (density estimated on held-out folds with conformal cutoffs that fall back to a wider-bandwidth estimate when density < epsilon), targeting the paper's admitted near-zero-density failure mode and extending the usable tau range toward the tails.", "gate": "Adopt if TMLE-CF achieves 90-98% coverage with |bias| <= 25% of the plug-in's bias at tau=.5 and tau=.75 on the semi-synthetic test; reject if coverage collapses at tau=.9 (then restrict the lane to central quantiles and say so explicitly).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2404.11350v3", "title": "Calibrating Bayesian Learning via Regularization, Confidence Minimization, and Selective Inference", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Selective calibration stack: (1) add an MMCE-style calibration regularizer to GSE's classification head loss (lambda swept on validation) - cheap, no architecture change; (2) build the selective-calibration selector: inputs = (model confidence r-bar, outlier scores vs historical game embeddings via kNN distance + isolation forest); train to minimize selective MMCE on a validation season with coverage target xi (e.g. 0.5); publish iff selector score >= tau; (3) OOD analog: treat cross-era games (e.g. pre-2020 rule changes) as the uncertainty set for confidence minimization - penalize overconfidence on era-shifted games - plus replace the paper's four hand-built outlier scores with a single learned 'game typicality' score: distance in GSE's own embedding space to the k nearest historical games, testing whether the selector's rejection decisions correlate with known hard-game indicators (backup QB, extreme weather, large line moves).", "gate": "ADAPT if selective calibration reduces test-window selected-set ECE by >=20% relative to the MMCE-only variant with accuracy not worse by more than 1pp; reject if the ECE gain requires >60% rejection or accuracy drops - then keep only the MMCE regularizer.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2404.13371v1", "title": "On Risk-Sensitive Decision Making Under Uncertainty", "normalized_lane": "uncertainty_decision_theory", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Per-game rho-penalized Kelly rule: for each engine pick with estimated win prob p-hat and decimal odds o, compute the rho-penalized Kelly fraction by solving the paper's optimality equation numerically (1-D root find on f(p-hat,K,rho)=0 with payoff X in {o-1,-1}) - a fractional-Kelly-like stake with rho calibrated, not an arbitrary 0.25/0.5 fraction; rho calibration: grid-search rho in [0,2] on rolling backtest to maximize Calmar ratio (not raw growth) - answering the paper's open 'how to choose rho' with data; slate extension: use the multi-alternative simplex form (each week's picks = alternatives, K = stake fractions summing to <=1, cash = deterministic alternative with r=0), payoffs correlated via historical pick-residual correlation; serving: precompute stake per pick nightly after odds sync, cap single-game stake at 3% bankroll regardless of formula output - plus make rho adaptive to bankroll state: rho_t = rho_0 x (1 + kappa*(DD_t/DD_max)), where DD_t is current drawdown - the variance penalty tightens automatically as the bankroll dips (a drawdown governor the static paper lacks).", "gate": "ACCEPT if on locked 2024-2025 window: Calmar_rho-Kelly >= 1.10 x Calmar_best-baseline AND max-drawdown <= 0.90 x that of full-Kelly baseline AND CAGR >= CAGR of fixed-fraction baseline; REJECT otherwise, or if optimal rho on the tuning window is 0 (then it is just Kelly) or unstable across tuning folds.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2404.15018", "title": "Conformal Predictive Systems Under Covariate Shift", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Weighted conformal under covariate shift: (1) build a regime discriminator - logistic regression distinguishing 'current-regime games' (last 4 weeks) from the calibration window (trailing 2 seasons) on covariates (QB identity flags, injury counts, weather, home/away, line movement); (2) use its predicted odds as w-hat(x) in a weighted conformal interval layer for totals/spreads (via crepes-weighted or a port); (3) compare coverage/width vs unweighted rolling conformal on 2023-2025 backtests, with regime-shift weeks (starting-QB changes) flagged - plus doubly-robust CPS: combine WSCPS weighting with a conditional (Mondrian) calibration split by regime - testing whether weighting + stratification beats either alone during shift episodes.", "gate": "ADOPT if WSCPS restores episode-conditional coverage to within 3pp of nominal without >10% width inflation vs unweighted; REJECT if the discriminator's w-hat estimates are unstable (effective sample size of calibration < 30% of nominal - weight collapse) or if P(Y|X) drift dominates (WSCPS still miscalibrated during episodes).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2404.18400v3", "title": "LLM-SR: Scientific Equation Discovery via Programming with Large Language Models", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build 'GSE-SR': prompt template with (a) problem spec in analyst prose (features, target, no-known-metrics constraint listing passer rating/QBR/EPA as forbidden), (b) evaluation function code (NMSE on nflverse train + OOD future seasons), (c) one seed skeleton; LLM proposes Python skeleton programs with placeholder params; fit with scipy BFGS; score -MSE; islands-model experience buffer (m=4 islands, Boltzmann cluster sampling favoring high score + short programs); backbones: any instruction-tuned LLM (cost-controlled: batch proposals, cache); data: nflverse team-season 2009-2023 (ID), 2024-2025 (OOD); targets: points/drive, next-season wins - plus 'adversarial prior refresh': after each island converges, prompt the LLM with the current best program and explicitly instruct it to propose a structurally DIFFERENT family (e.g. 'no ratios; use only additive terms' or 'must include an interaction between pressure rate and air yards') - using the LLM's language ability as a diversity operator that GP mutation cannot provide.", "gate": "ADOPT if GSE-SR's best program achieves >=20% lower OOD NMSE than the best PySR expression at comparable complexity (<=15 nodes) on the 2024-2025 window AND the program is not a recitation of a known metric (verified by symbolic inspection); REJECT if OOD NMSE is within 10% of PySR or the LLM merely rediscovers passer-rating variants.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2404.19383", "title": "Cross-Block Fine-Grained Semantic Cascade for Skeleton-Based Sports Action Recognition", "normalized_lane": "sports_cv", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add the cross-block fine-grained semantic cascade (CFSC) to GSE's skeleton-based action recognition: learn a per-level lambda_v (attention over cascade depths) instead of scalar lambda, comparing against fixed-lambda on GSE data; test CFSC on 3D skeletons (the paper used 2D OpenPose) to see if depth information reduces the bone-stream advantage.", "gate": "CFSC must deliver >=+1.5pp top-1 on the strong-backbone setting (the paper's own minimum on HD-GCN was +1.4 on FD-7 bone) with <=10% inference-cost increase, else drop - the value proposition is 'cheap +2pp', and anything less is not worth the module complexity.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.00158", "title": "BayesBlend: Bayesian Model Averaging and Stacking in Python", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt (or vendor-inspire) BayesBlend's Draws + stacking-model pattern as GSE's ensemble plumbing - the reference implementation candidate for the stacking lane: standardize the heterogeneous model zoo via the Draws abstraction (log-likelihood matrix + posterior predictions, first dim = posterior samples); concrete workflow: collect per-model LOO log-predictive densities -> BayesStacking (Bayesian weights with informed priors, e.g. prior preference for the production incumbent) or MleStacking for speed -> .predict produces the blended posterior-predictive Draws consumed downstream by calibration (CQR/conformal) and Kelly sizing; HierarchicalBayesStacking gives turnkey regime-dependent weights (spread bucket, dome/outdoor, week) as a Stan-backed fit rather than custom code; train blending on early weeks, apply to future weeks (leave-future-out over the season structure) - plus test backend-agnosticity: wrap non-Bayesian inputs (gradient-boosted point models with predictive distributions) in Draws and verify blended ELPD, and check hierarchical-over-time weight behavior (weight migrates between models mid-season).", "gate": "Prototype on one backtest season: convert 3-5 existing models' outputs into Draws, fit MleStacking vs BayesStacking vs HierarchicalBayesStacking (covariate: week), and compare blended ELPD on leave-future-out weeks; validate .predict on unseen future weeks; ADOPT if blended ELPD beats the best single candidate on leave-future-out weeks AND weights agree with the manual pipeline of ledgers 1672-1673; REJECT if blending loses to the best candidate (the paper's own pseudo-BMA insurance result shows blending is not always the best).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["1704.02030", "2101.08954"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.01598v1", "title": "Predictive Decision Synthesis for Portfolios: Betting on Better Models", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Decision-tilted model combination for the weekly betting portfolio: define the GSE decision as the weekly portfolio of spread/moneyline/total bets sized by fractional Kelly from engine probabilities vs market prices; candidate set = engine model components/versions x stake-size/risk-target settings; replace the paper's decision score with realized Kelly log-growth (or ROI) on a selection window; apply relaxed entropic tilting to the BMA-style component weights to get decision-tilted combination weights; recompute tilted weights monthly from the picks history + historical odds (OddsPapi lane) - plus go beyond the paper: tilt on a risk-aware decision score the paper does not use - expected Kelly growth penalized by a drawdown term (growth - lambda*max-drawdown) - comparing relaxed-entropic-tilt, hard subset selection (their greedy 0.95 bar), and fully Bayesian decision-theoretic weighting.", "gate": "ADOPT the BPDS-tilted weights if 2025 holdout Kelly log-growth exceeds the accuracy-weighted baseline by >=10% relative (or ROI by >=1.0 point at matched stake) with a bootstrap p<0.05; REJECT otherwise; hard veto: if the tilted portfolio's worst-month drawdown exceeds the baseline's by >25%, reject regardless of full-season growth (decision-awareness must not smuggle tail risk).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.02412v1", "title": "Deep Learning and Transfer Learning Architectures for English Premier League Player Performance Forecasting", "normalized_lane": "markets", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "BASELINE", "improvement": "As engine-honesty infrastructure, keep the paper's 'points-only + matchup difficulty' feature-minimal 1D-CNN as a reference baseline: 1D-CNN forecaster for NFL week-ahead fantasy points (PPR), per position group (QB/RB/WR/TE): input = past w weeks of fantasy points (+ matchup difficulty from spread/total), single 1D conv layer -> flatten -> concat matchup difficulty -> one dense layer -> scalar output; MSE + ElasticNet loss, Adam, early stopping, player-wise splits; head-to-head vs GSE's current NFL projection baseline and vs LightGBM on the same features, evaluated on both MSE and Spearman rank correlation (the paper's key insight: ranking quality matters more than MSE for fantasy/prop selection) - plus direct Spearman optimization: train directly for ranking via convex-hull projection differentiable sorting instead of MSE, testing whether a rank-optimized model beats the MSE-optimized CNN on top-decile hit rate (fraction of predicted top-10 players finishing in the actual top-10).", "gate": "Adopt the 1D-CNN as a candidate NFL player projector if it beats the current engine's fantasy-points MSE by >=5% on holdout AND Spearman rho >= 0.55 in at least two position groups; if it merely ties LightGBM or fails to beat the current engine, reject and keep the paper as the feature-minimal baseline reference.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.03708v3", "title": "Delta Tensor: Efficient Vector and Tensor Storage in Delta Lake", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Apply to the self-learning/self-growing engine mandate: (1) discovered-signal storage format - as the engine learns dense matchup embeddings or player-skill matrices, store them in Delta with FTSF-style chunking (id, chunk, dims metadata) rather than numpy/PyTorch blobs (buys the ~90% slice-read win for batch-time feature extraction - the 'fetch only this game's embeddings' pattern); (2) sparse interaction features (rare event tensors - trick plays, injuries per matchup): COO or CSF layout when nonzeros < 10%; (3) model checkpoint registry: store model weights as versioned Delta tables - time travel gives parameter history for free (pairs with ledger 2026's rollback story) - plus an access-log-driven auto-chunker: log which (week, team) slices the feature pipeline actually fetches over one season, then optimize chunk shape to minimize expected bytes-fetched (greedy search) - turning FTSF from a fixed layout into a learned layout.", "gate": "ADOPT the layout iff: (a) FTSF slice-read latency <= 25% of blob read-slice latency on GSE's season tensor; (b) write overhead <= 2x blob write; (c) exact numeric round-trip parity (decode(blob) == original to float32 precision); REJECT if slice reads do not beat blobs on GSE's smaller tensors.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2310.08697v1"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.04101v2", "title": "Continual Learning in the Presence of Repetition", "normalized_lane": "continual_online_learning", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Frozen-expert ensemble over one forgetting monolith - NFL's stream is repetition-rich (divisional rematches, recurring coaching trees, repeated QB-vs-DC matchups): keep the live weekly-refit model (ledger 1888's interference-scored replay) as the 'current experience' expert, but maintain a bank of frozen specialist models: one per division (8), each trained only on that division's games through the prior season and frozen, plus one frozen 'rivalry/rematch' model trained on second-meetings; at inference, gate by OOD logic: each expert reports a confidence/OOD score for the matchup (distance of the game's features from its training distribution); final probability = reliability-weighted average, live model weighted by recency; cheap first step: before building 8 division experts, test (a) one weekly-refit monolith vs (b) monolith + frozen prior-season model (2-model ensemble, OOD-gated) on 2020-2025 walk-forward; add a 'rematch split' to the 1887 metric suite - report Brier separately on second-meetings vs first-meetings - plus learn the repetition structure: cluster historical games by matchup-embedding similarity (team-pair, coaching-tree, scheme tags) and train one frozen expert per cluster (e.g. 'Shanahan-tree vs Cover-3 teams'), cluster assignment refreshed each offseason.", "gate": "ADOPT the frozen-expert ensemble if on 2020-2025 walk-forward it beats the monolith on >=3 of the 4 metrics from 1887 with rematch-split Brier improving by >=0.003 and no metric degrading by >0.001; ADOPT the 2-model version (B) alone if it captures >=70% of (C)'s rematch gain at a fraction of the serving cost; REJECT the division bank if the shuffled-season control shows the same gains (then it is generic ensembling, not repetition exploitation); sunset rule: any frozen expert older than 2 seasons is retired unless it still wins its division split.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2308.03810"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.07354", "title": "SoccerNet-Echoes: A Soccer Game Audio Commentary Dataset", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt the audio-commentary curation recipe to NFL: run Whisper large-v3 (best hallucination resistance) over full NFL broadcast audio per game; segment at segment-level timestamps; translate any non-English (Spanish broadcasts) to English; apply unique-word-ratio per-game model selection + VAD preprocessing; mine transcripts for (a) injury mentions and lineup changes (cross-validated against official reports), (b) mention-frequency-based player influence signals feeding summary/game-recap word budgets, (c) tactical-discussion extraction for coaching-adjustment signals; feed cleaned transcripts into the 1594-1597 text-event pipelines and the 1602 SoccerRAG-style QA layer - plus add VAD pre-processing + speaker diarization (separating commentators from crowd/stadium), entity linking to a player/team knowledge graph (fixes Whisper entity errors), segment-level (not batch) translation, and a human-verified injury-mention subset as a benchmark.", "gate": "ADAPT (not ADOPT): it is a data asset and curation recipe, not a predictive model; the transcription noise (WER ~0.5) means downstream extraction must be confidence-weighted; accepted on open dataset + code, honest quality metrics, hallucination-aware model selection, direct injury/tactical intelligence applications.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2307.10303", "2406.01273"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.09865", "title": "Assessing Course Difficulty and the Effect of Weather in Amateur Cross Country Running Races", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Module weather/field_conditions.py: Bayesian log-scale mixed model for NFL weather/field-condition effects - log(total points) or log(team offensive yards) per game = lambda + alpha_offense_i + alpha_defense_j + beta_stadium_k + delta_week + gamma*(temp) + rho_0*(rain week of game) + rho_1*(rain prior 7 days) + dome/turf interactions; random effects for teams and stadiums, corner constraints, JAGS/Stan inference; the two-lag rainfall structure becomes game-day precipitation + trailing-7-day precipitation (field degradation), interacted with surface (grass vs turf); rain x temp interaction (frozen/saturated ground) and a wind x stadium-orientation term (bowl geometry); output: posterior distributions of weather/field effects per surface type -> calibrated totals adjustments (e.g. 'heavy trailing-week rain on grass: -1.5 points, 95% CI [-2.8, -0.3]') - with stadium-coordinate gridded reanalysis (replacing central-station weather to remove attenuation bias), and a hypothesis test: with stadium-level weather, wind shows an effect only in open, wind-aligned stadiums (Buffalo, Chicago), not domes or sheltered bowls.", "gate": "ADOPT the field-condition adjustment if (a) out-of-sample RMSE on 2025 totals improves >= 1.5% over the no-weather baseline, (b) trailing-week rain on grass has a 95% CI excluding zero with the correct sign, and (c) turf/dome rain effects are ~= 0; REJECT if weather terms add nothing out-of-sample.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.10247", "title": "Alternative ranking measures to predict international football results", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Bayesian Bradley-Terry-Davidson strength covariate: fit Bayesian BTD in Stan/PyMC on nflverse 2002-2026 team-week W/L/T outcomes (no draws in NFL -> gamma->-infinity limit, or plain BT with home-field order effect via Beaver/Gokhale additive term): psi ~ N(0, sigma^2_psi), hierarchical sigma_psi estimated; posterior median psi_k per team per week using an expanding window (fit weekly, strengths as of that week - avoid the paper's pooled-window lookahead); feature: omega_n = MAD-normalized (psi_home - psi_away) added as a linear covariate to GSE's points/spread regression or as a model-blend input; dynamic extension: per-year AR(1) attack/defense adapted to offense/defense efficiency splits at week resolution - plus make the BTD strength time-varying within season via a state-space random walk psi_{k,t} ~ N(psi_{k,t-1}, sigma^2) (Glickman-style dynamic BT) with a score-differential (margin-of-victory) weighted likelihood (Stern/Harville style) so blowouts move strengths more than 1-point wins.", "gate": "ADOPT the covariate into the engine if, on the 2023-2025 walk-forward test, adding omega_n reduces moneyline Brier score by >=0.002 (paired, by week) AND does not worsen spread-cover Brier; REJECT (drop the feature) if the Brier delta is <0.001 in either direction or negative.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.10453v2", "title": "Expected Points Above Average: A Novel NBA Player Metric Based on Bayesian Hierarchical Modeling", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replicate the EPAA pipeline for NBA props: cluster players by shot-region selection and accuracy profiles (hierarchical Multinomial/Binomial), compute expected points at fixed usage N-tilde, define player EPAA vs league-average posterior; convert to betting: EPAA posterior -> expected points distribution for tonight's game (usage-adjusted); edge = E[points] - prop line; post only if edge > 0 and 95% credible interval excludes the line (ties to the 0714/0716 abstention gates); extend to other prop types: rebound/assist region profiles (analogous regions = court zones) - plus fix the paper's top-100 restriction: fit the hierarchical model on ALL rotation players with partial pooling (small-sample players - the paper's excluded set - are exactly where Bayesian shrinkage adds most value and where prop lines are softest); make the 'average' baseline time-varying (rolling 4-week average team) so EPAA tracks in-season regime change instead of a season-fixed baseline.", "gate": "ADOPT if the replicated EPAA pipeline shows positive backtest ROI on 2024-25 NBA props and EPAA-vs-line edge predicts covers better than the engine's current player model; REJECT if EPAA adds nothing over raw usage-adjusted averages.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2505.23437v2", "2509.21514v4"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.11802", "title": "Counterfactual Explanation-Based Badminton Motion Guidance Generation Using Wearable Sensors", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Build gse_latentcf.py: (1) train a Transformer classifier on NGS tracking to predict play success (e.g., route -> target & catch, or ball-carrier -> broken tackle) from joint/position trajectories; (2) train a trajectory autoencoder on the same data; (3) for failed plays, run Algorithm 1 to generate the minimal counterfactual trajectory that flips the prediction to success; (4) two outputs: (a) @GalaxySportsHQ film-room content - ghost-overlay 'the 20 cm wider stem that makes this a completion'; (b) a counterfactual-gap feature per player (mean latent distance between actual and successful-counterfactual routes) fed into GSE's reception/prop models as a route-running quality signal orthogonal to raw athleticism - plus close the paper's open loop: content-side A/B testing whether film-room posts built on LatentCF counterfactuals outperform standard chart posts on engagement, validating that minimal-edit counterfactuals are the more compelling explanatory format.", "gate": "Reproduce Table II on MultiSenseBadminton (public): LatentCF must beat 1NN-DTW on DTW-closeness and FMD by >=25% relative; then port to NGS: train the success classifier on 2024 routes (gate: 5-fold BalAcc >= 0.70), generate counterfactuals for 200 failed routes, and gate on plausibility - mean LOF/OCSVM of CF trajectories within 1 SD of real successful routes; if CF trajectories are implausible (outside the real manifold), the explainer is unusable for content - stop.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2508.17611"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.12588v1", "title": "An analysis of factors impacting team strengths in the Australian Football League using time-variant Bradley-Terry models", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Time-variant Bradley-Terry with team random intercepts: nflverse play-by-play 2009-2025 (regular season); team-game-level differential features (off/def EPA differential last-4 and season-cumulative, success-rate differential, pressure-rate differential, turnover-margin differential, plus rest/travel days); target: ATS cover or straight-up win; model: logistic/Bradley-Terry with team random intercepts (epsilon_i ~ N(0, sigma^2)) fit via lme4/glmmTMB or PyMC; match-difficulty terms: home-field, rest differential, altitude/travel; ridge regularization over the PI differential coefficients (the paper's univariate screening + backward elimination is fragile); serving: weekly refit on a rolling 3-season window (the paper's 'medium-term drift' finding); output team strengths lambda_ir for downstream EPA opponent-adjustment and a calibrated win probability (add a Platt/calibration layer - the paper lacks one) - plus replace the feature screen with grouped elastic-net over the PI-differential blocks (EPA/SR/pressure/turnover blocks), add opponent-adjusted feature variants (iterated like EM), and model the spread margin with a team-effect linear model instead of win/loss.", "gate": "ADOPT if the BT time-variant model beats baseline (a) Elo on Brier score by >= 0.003 on the 2018-2025 test window AND matches or beats the closing-spread implied probability on log-loss; REJECT if it fails to beat Elo on Brier or trails the market by > 0.005 log-loss.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.13397v1", "title": "Multi Player Tracking in Ice Hockey with Homographic Projections", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Adapt the homography+MPN tracking architecture to football (hockey model is not directly usable): (1) homography module: train or license an NFL-field registration model that maps broadcast frames to a top-down field template using field markings (yard lines, hash marks) as correspondences - deliverable: per-frame 3x3 H and per-player footpoints in field coordinates; (2) detection: fine-tune a detector (Faster R-CNN or YOLO variant) on football broadcast frames, with jersey-number OCR as an extra node feature (NFL advantage over hockey); (3) association: replicate the paper's bipartite-graph MPN: nodes = 512-D appearance + 2-D homography footpoints, edges = relative appearance/positional distances, L = 6 message-passing steps, focal-loss training, xi = 0.9 pruning, connected-component ID assignment; (4) training data: annotate an in-house football broadcast-tracking dataset (~80-100 clips) - no public equivalent of VIP-HTD exists for NFL; (5) serving: offline batch pipeline - ingest game footage -> tracklets -> bird's-eye positional trajectories -> feed into GSE's tracking-data consumers (NGS replacements, CFB games without tracking data) - plus jersey-number OCR as a node feature (near-deterministic identity signal), and camera-motion-compensated homography refinement (temporal smoothing on the H matrix sequence via Kalman filter) so pan/tilt/zoom jitter does not inject noise into footpoint trajectories.", "gate": "ADOPT the football adaptation only if ALL hold: (a) legal review clears processing of broadcast footage for the target sport/league (NFL excluded unless licensed - CFB or other leagues first); (b) a reproduction of the homography+MPN concept on public hockey data achieves IDF1 >= 90 with >=5 percentage-point gain over the appearance-only ablation; (c) an annotated football pilot set (>=10 games of broadcast clips) yields IDsw per game below a SORT-on-broadcast baseline by >=50%; reject otherwise - especially if legal review fails.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.17214v2", "title": "Modelling between- and within-season trajectories in elite athletic performance data", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Decompose team form into between-season level and within-season trajectory: model each NFL team's weekly EPA/play (or GSE's rating) 2015-2025 as y_{team,season,week} = g(season-index) + f_{team,season}(week/18) + opponent/confounder terms, with f split into between-season level and within-season RBP - separating 'the Chiefs are declining as a roster' from 'the Chiefs start slow and peak in December'; player-prop age curves: fit the cubic B-spline population ageing function to position-level performance (QB EPA/dropback, WR yards/route by age) for age-adjustment in props - the reverse-J with position-specific peaks; replace Gaussian error assumptions with the asymmetric-tail skew-t (downside tail heavier - injuries -> sudden collapse is more likely than sudden superstar emergence); start with a non-Bayesian prototype (penalized likelihood) - plus build the forward-looking version: extend the model with a predictive distribution for the remaining within-season trajectory given weeks 1-k (the hierarchical prior naturally supports this - teams with few observations borrow from population/athlete-level curves), backtested at each week k=4..14 against GSE's current form estimator.", "gate": "Adopt the decomposition if the within-season trajectory component reduces second-half prediction MSE by >=5% vs the flat-season-average baseline on the 2015-2025 rolling test; reject if the gain is <2% (NFL's 17-game season may be too short for the within-season component to beat a simple recency-weighted average).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.17680v2", "title": "Sports-Traj: A Unified Trajectory Generation Model for Multi-Agent Movement in Sports", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "UniTraj for trajectory imputation + prediction on NFL Next Gen Stats tracking data - one model for GSE's three failure modes: partial tracking (occluded/missing frames), short-history rollout prediction (25-40 of 50 frames observed), fully-missing agents (dropped receiver ID); applications: (1) route/defender trajectory forecasting for EPA-added / separation features - generate 20 plausible continuations of all 22 players + ball from the first ~0.5 s of a play, deriving distributions of expected separation, YAC, tackle probability; (2) counterfactual play simulation - mask the ball-carrier's future, generate completions under different defensive masks (a generative complement to GSE's EPA models); (3) tracking-data QA - the OOB + Step metrics give an automatic quality gate for incoming NGS feeds; build plan: Phase 0 - reproduce the authors' code on Football-U (minADE20 within 5% of 3.55 yards); Phase 1 - NGS modern-schema data adapter - plus: variable agent counts (Perceiver-style latent bottleneck or padding-with-mask), replace the MLP decoder with a diffusion decoder for sharper cuts and better uncertainty calibration, add contextual conditioning the paper omits (down, distance, score differential, personnel grouping, weather).", "gate": "ADOPT only if UniTraj beats GSE's Kalman-filter rollout baseline by >= 15% on minADE20 with OOB < 1e-03 on time-ordered NGS (train 2023-2024, test 2025 weeks 1-4) over the paper's prediction masks; ADAPT (imputation-only use) if it wins only on imputation masks; otherwise REJECT.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2405.20957v3", "title": "Causal-ICM: Multi-task Gaussian Processes for Combining RCT and Observational Data", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Two-source GP combining GSE's trusted pick outcomes with large biased historical model outputs: source A = GSE's own verified pick outcomes (small, trusted, post-hoc verified - the picks DB); source B = large historical model outputs (biased: stale, miscalibrated eras); shared RBF kernel on game-state covariates (spread, total, rest, weather); single global rho first, then region-specific rho via a second ICM factor; gpytorch with inducing points (<=500) for ~10k rows; rho grid {0.1,...,0.9} via rolling-origin time-split CV on source-A outcomes only (never tune rho on source B - that reintroduces the confounding the parameter is meant to absorb); output per-pick: posterior mean edge and the bound-inflated posterior variance -> feed into calibration (Venn-Abers/isotonic) and Kelly sizing rather than point picks - plus region-adaptive rho: rho(x) = sigmoid(g(x)) with g a second GP or linear model on covariates, so borrowing shrinks where source B is known to be unreliable (stale-rating eras, weather-affected totals).", "gate": "ADOPT if: on the 2026 holdout, Causal-ICM beats pooled-GP Brier by >=0.005 on all picks AND by >=0.01 on the out-of-support slice, with rho-hat selected by rolling CV stable across folds (SD of rho-hat <= 0.15); REJECT if rho-hat collapses to ~=0 or ~=1, or if any baseline (pooled GP or engine) beats it on total Brier.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2406.00814v1", "title": "Expected Possession Value of Control and Duel Actions for Soccer Player's Skills Estimation", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build an NFL 'Expected Drive Value' (EDV) framework: data = nflverse play-by-play 2018-2025; possession = drive, control actions = plays, 'shots' = scoring plays (TD/FG) with xP (expected points) replacing xG; fit drive-value models: per-play EDV = 1 - Pi(1 - gamma^Delta-t * xP_future) with gamma per-second-of-game-clock tuned ~0.90-0.99 on the drive length distribution; possession-risk variant subtracting opponent's next-drive decayed xP; player attribution: per-play Delta-EDV credited to the primary actor (passer/receiver split 60/40 per GSE convention; rusher full), turnovers penalized double; duel-skill analog: contested-catch and pass-rush/win rates via modified Glicko-2; custom loss: weight each play's loss by 1/(player appearance count) when fitting projection models for low-volume/deep-roster players - plus replace the ad hoc gamma with a learned per-situation discount: fit gamma as a function of field position and down (early-down midfield plays decay faster since drives routinely die there; red-zone plays decay slower).", "gate": "ADAPT into GSE's player-projection pipeline only if: (a) EDV-based next-season prediction achieves the R^2 gains on 2023 AND 2024 holdout seasons, and (b) the Glicko-2 contested-catch rating shows rank stability (Spearman >= 0.45 year-over-year for players with >=30 contested targets); otherwise park as research.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2406.01273", "title": "SoccerRAG: Multimodal Soccer Information Retrieval via Natural Queries", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port the pipeline to NFL: (a) structured SQLite/Postgres DB of GSE's archive - games, play-by-play, rosters, injuries, odds/CLV history, commentary transcripts (Whisper on Game Pass audio, mirroring the paper's ASR step); (b) extractor schema for NFL properties (team, player, week, season, stat, market); (c) validator with NFL abbreviation tables ('KC', 'Mahomes', 'MNF') + Levenshtein resolution - the paper's ablation proves the validator is the component to build first; (d) few-shot SQL RAG with human-crafted exemplar queries for common GSE questions (splits, line-movement, injury-report lookups); (e) expose as the natural-language query interface behind @GalaxySportsHQ content research and the engine's internal analytics - plus swap GPT-3.5/4 for a modern function-calling open model and re-run the 20-question ablation; add a determinism/robustness metric (5 repeated runs per question); fix list-truncation with paginated SQL + structured output; measure validator recall on deliberately misspelled/abbreviated NFL entity queries; extend to multimodal retrieval (return video clips keyed to event timestamps).", "gate": "ACCEPTED (ADAPT): open-source reproducible pipeline + controlled ablation isolating the validator's contribution + honest failure documentation; ADAPT rather than ADOPT: soccer schema/LLM choices are dated - reimplement with current open models and GSE's NFL schema.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2406.02141", "title": "Leveraging Deterministic Weather Forecasts for In-Situ Probabilistic Temperature Predictions via Deep Learning", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Calibrated probabilistic kickoff-condition forecasts: data = deterministic high-res forecast grids (HRRR/NAM) at 30 NFL stadiums + ASOS/METAR obs; steps: (a) build the 25-style predictor set for wind speed, gusts, temperature, precip at kickoff lead times; (b) train one BQN (d = 16) with stadium + lead-time embeddings on all lead times jointly; (c) output per-stadium calibrated quantile functions for kickoff conditions; (d) pipe into the totals/spread weather adjustment model - plus add ensemble members (GEFS) as extra inputs (the paper shows the 2nd member is the high-value one) and test CRPS gains vs the deterministic-only BQN; extend Bernstein degree by validation and add an EVT tail model for extreme cold/heat games (the Texas-2021 failure mode).", "gate": "ADAPT if the BQN achieves >=10% relative CRPS improvement over the naive probabilistic baseline on a holdout season AND rank histograms are flatter (central-bin deviation from uniformity reduced by >=30%); otherwise fall back to EMOS.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2406.03321v2", "title": "Decision Synthesis in Monetary Policy", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Decision-utility weighting for the GSE ensemble: (1) component predictive densities: each sub-model j produces p_j(y|x) over game outcomes y given a candidate action x (stake profile across spread/total/moneyline, or a slate of picks); (2) decision-dependent weights pi_j(x): weight each sub-model by its historical betting utility - realized CLV or ROI of the picks it would have recommended - with weights varying by bet type/market (a totals model gets more weight on totals decisions); (3) outcome calibration alpha_j(y|x): upweight models in outcome regions where they excel (a model strong in high-total games gets upweighted when the predicted total is high); (4) bounded score functions on (predicted edge, bankroll drawdown, stake smoothness) with entropic tilting to a target expected score per slate; monitor importance-sampling ESS as a feasibility check (if ESS collapses, the target is unrealistic - shrink it); final pick: x maximizing expected utility under the BPDS mixture - plus make pi_j(x) depend on the market state (line movement, public-betting splits) as well as bet type, and replace the hand-set target scores m_f(x) with an adaptive rule driven by the ESS diagnostic (shrink targets when ESS < 50).", "gate": "Adopt decision-utility weighting if walk-forward 2024-2025 shows the BPDS-weighted ensemble beating predictive-fit-weighted (BMA-style) combination by >=1.0% ROI or >=0.5% CLV with no worse max drawdown; reject (keep current combination) if decision-utility weights underperform - the paper's own caveat: if historical decisions were bad, weighting by past decision outcomes fossilizes the mistake; use expected decision utility under a corrected staking rule instead.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2406.04062v1", "title": "Online Learning in Betting Markets: Profit versus Prediction", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Defensive book-shading monitor: given GSE's own released picks flow as a proxy for informed-bettor beliefs, use the paper's profit-decomposition (profit proportional to deviation between bettor beliefs and truth, amplified by tail heaviness) to predict when books will move lines against GSE-style positions - time GSE's releases/picks to precede anticipated shading, or flag markets where the book's margin already prices in the informed flow (no edge left); benchmark: implement the fair-odds FTL price a-star (eq. 27) as a 'market-consensus' baseline - compare GSE's model probabilities against the FTL-implied consensus from a simulated crowd, persistent deviations indicate either GSE edge or model bias; simulation lab: reuse the authors' repo to simulate how a book would price against a population of GSE-like Kelly bettors, stress-testing GSE's staking plan against adversarial pricing dynamics - plus invert the model: have GSE learn the bookmaker's belief g from the observed price path (inverse SA) - estimate g per market from opening->closing line movement, then compare implied g against GSE's model probability as a direct edge-detection signal.", "gate": "ADAPT the shading-monitor if, on one full NFL season, games flagged 'book already shaded against informed flow' show GSE's realized CLV >=2 points worse than unflagged games (the flag correctly identifies dead-edge spots); otherwise REJECT the defensive application and keep only the FTL-consensus benchmark.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2406.07496v1", "title": "TextGrad: Automatic \"Differentiation\" via Text", "normalized_lane": "llm_agents_ai_scientist", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt TextGrad to optimize the signal-discovery pipeline itself: graph: SignalCode = LLM(IdeaPrompt + SignalHypothesis) -> BacktestResult = Executor(SignalCode) -> Loss = -DeltaBrier(BacktestResult) (deterministic - NOT an LLM judge); variables with requires_grad: IdeaPrompt, SignalCode; backward: a backward-engine LLM receives the backtest diagnostics (which folds failed, sample sizes, calibration slope - the structured evaluator output from 2084) as the 'gradient' on BacktestResult, producing criticisms for SignalCode ('the wind interaction fails because...') AND for IdeaPrompt ('hypotheses about weather need a minimum-games guard...'); chain rule = one backward call per edge; TGD.step: update SignalCode and IdeaPrompt with the Eq.-9-style prompt; 5 iterations max per idea (paper's budget); minibatch mode: batch 4 ideas, tg.sum their losses, concatenate gradients - improves the IdeaPrompt across ideas, not just one; effort: 2-3 days (Variable/graph wrapper around the 2082/2084 harness) - plus a gradient-clip analogue: cap each TGD.step to changing at most K lines of SignalCode / K tokens of IdeaPrompt per iteration (like gradient clipping in SGD), testing whether clipped steps reduce the variance of DeltaBrier across the 5 iterations and raise the fraction of ideas that monotonically improve.", "gate": "ADOPT if: arm B clears the 0.002 gate on >=5/8 ideas vs <=3/8 for arm A, AND the transferred IdeaPrompt improves first-attempt DeltaBrier on the 4 held-out hypotheses by >=0.001 on average (the prompt itself is learning - the TextGrad value-add over Reflexion), AND total LLM calls per idea <= 20; REJECT if arm B ~= arm A (joint optimization adds nothing over single reflection), or the IdeaPrompt drifts into prompt-bloat, or any iteration's 'gradient' contradicts the deterministic backtest numbers (backward engine hallucinating - fall back to 2084's simpler reflection).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INVENT", "effort": "small", "depends_on": ["2408.06292v3", "2303.11366v4"]}
{"arxiv_id": "2406.09597", "title": "Tractable Ridge Regression for Paired Comparisons", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "PEB-ridge for early-season paired-comparison ratings: on the NFL 2019-2023 early-season protocol (train weeks 1-6, predict weeks 7-17), with the closed-form lambda-hat; if the lambda-hat closed form underperforms full PEB on NFL data, use full PEB - plus build a dynamic PEB where lambda_t evolves via a random walk (or is re-estimated on a rolling window) so shrinkage adapts to within-season regime changes (injuries, QB changes), tested on the 2022-2023 NFL seasons with known mid-season QB injuries (dynamic-PEB log-loss vs static-PEB on post-injury weeks); extend the concordance-based lambda-hat to the spread domain by correlating paired ATS outcomes instead of paired SU outcomes.", "gate": "On the NFL 2019-2023 early-season protocol (train weeks 1-6, predict weeks 7-17), PEB-ridge log-loss must be <= GSE current early-season rating log-loss - 0.01, and must beat the naive frequency baseline by >= 0.05 in every season; if PEB ties CV-ridge within noise, adopt PEB for the compute savings.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2406.11584", "title": "Modeling cyclicality and intransitivity in paired comparisons data", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Cycle-aware paired-comparison diagnostics for NFL: deploy the cyclic pipeline as a monitoring diagnostic - lack-of-fit flags at p < 0.01 on walk-forward seasons; extend FTBS to incomplete graphs (NFL: 17 games/team, not round-robin) - the tick-table machinery needs the incidence-matrix generalization the authors defer - and test detection power on simulated NFL-like schedules with planted cycles; longer cycles (r >= 4) as first-class dictionary entries for interpretability ('A beats B beats C beats D beats A' narratives for content).", "gate": "Deploy the cyclic pipeline to production only if, on EPL 2022-2024 walk-forward: (i) lack-of-fit flags >= 1 season at p < 0.01; (ii) FTBS-augmented model beats the transitive baseline by >= 0.005 log-loss on flagged-season holdout; (iii) the cyclic-edge betting simulation shows positive expected gain net of vig; otherwise keep the test as a monitoring diagnostic (cheap) without acting on it.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}

{"arxiv_id": "2406.12084", "title": "1723 When reasoning meets information aggregation: a case study with sports narratives", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Adopt the DCA metric and divide-and-conquer batching (DnC-10-style) as GSE's standard for aggregating LLM-generated game narratives, then extend past the paper by measuring the team-to-player attribution accuracy gap and mapping accuracy-per-dollar across batch sizes to pick the Pareto-optimal production batching.", "gate": "ADAPT proceeds if the NFL replication shows the same qualitative pattern (batching helps, dense scoring hurts, symbolic substitution hurts); REJECT monolithic inference for any GSE aggregation task", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2406.12913v1", "title": "T-JEPA: A Joint-Embedding Predictive Architecture for Trajectory Similarity Computation", "normalized_lane": "selfsupervised_tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a T-JEPA-style trajectory encoder for NFL tracking with relative (ball/LOS-referenced) coordinates into AdjFuse and play-phase-conditioned mask tokens, replacing absolute-grid encodings and linear interpolation for masked-frame position imputation and same-play-concept retrieval.", "gate": "ADOPT if: (a) AdjFuse-augmented model achieves ≥15% lower masked-frame position RMSE than linear interpolation on held-out weeks, OR (b) T-JEPA embeddings reach same-play-concept top-1 accuracy ≥35% (vs ≤15% random, ≥10pp over raw-DTW). REJECT if neither holds.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2406.13749", "title": "The Impact of Expert Interaction Networks on Forecast Pooling", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Rebuild the GSE ensemble so component models draw on diversified information channels (not just diversified model classes), and add a variance audit that caps the single most-shared input (NGS features, injury reports, market lines) since shared channels inflate pooled-forecast variance with zero bias reduction, worst in star topologies.", "gate": "Ledger states no explicit numeric gate; operational check implied by the paper's result: pooled-forecast variance falls when the most-shared input is capped versus uncapped, with no change in pooled bias.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2406.14877", "title": "Sports Intelligence: Assessing the Sports Understanding Capabilities of Language Models through Question Answering from Text to Video", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build an NFL-live multi-hop question benchmark auto-generated from fresh game logs (win-probability swings plus down/distance/clock/score context) as a contamination-proof regression test for GSE's content pipeline, using the paper's error taxonomy (nuance confusion, reasoning errors) to route chained sports reasoning to human review where the human gap is quantified.", "gate": "ADAPT — not a method to adopt but the evaluation discipline GSE's NLP lane was missing: a concrete error taxonomy, a prompting standard with measured gains, and a quantified human-gap that justifies human review on chained sports reasoning.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2406.15760", "title": "ICM Ensemble with Novel Betting Functions for Concept Drift", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Deploy a weekly ICM concept-drift monitor that uses a market-relative nonconformity score α = |p̂_engine − q_market| on posted picks, so it tests exchangeability of the edge distribution and fires when GSE's edge regime decays (e.g., the market catching up to an angle) instead of tracking raw accuracy.", "gate": "ADAPT if the offline replay fires an alarm within 3 weeks of the 2024 kickoff-rule change on the TOTALS stream with ≤1 false alarm per season on 2024–2026 data — then deploy the monitor as a weekly cron job feeding the recalibration queue. Reject if alarms are dominated by noise (≥3 false alarms/season) or if detection latency exceeds 6 weeks.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
