{"arxiv_id": "2408.06292v3", "title": "The AI Scientist: Towards Fully Automated Open-Ended Scientific Discovery", "normalized_lane": "llm_agents_ai_scientist", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Run a nightly AI-Scientist-style agent loop that proposes, implements, and backtests new NFL signals, with an evolutionary archive and cross-run memory so the idea generator composes/mutates past successful signals (weather × matchup interactions) instead of proposing from scratch, promoting only signals that clear the sports gate with byte-identical reproducibility.", "gate": "**ADOPT the agent into production if:** (a) ≥3 agent-generated signals pass the **promotion gate of ΔBrier ≥ 0.002 vs baseline on the 2025 held-out season** (the task's mandated sports gate), with zero non-reproducible results (every promoted signal's log re-runs byte-identical), and (b) the reviewer agent's accept/reject decisions agree with a human analyst on ≥80% of a 20-idea calibration set. **REJECT (return to lab) if** fewer than 3 signals clear the gate in 30 nights, or any promoted signal fails reproducibility, or the agent bypasses a sandbox constraint (runaway process / constraint editing — the paper's Section 8 safety failure modes — triggers immediate shutdown of that run).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INVENT", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
