{"arxiv_id": "2409.13098v1", "title": "Predicting soccer matches with complex networks and machine learning", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Run an ablation experiment fusing the paper's network-centrality metric set (per-quarter networks, flow motifs, dynamic node sets for in-game personnel changes) into NGS target networks with 3-class cover/push/no-cover modeling, using strictly time-ordered splits to fix the paper's leakage risk.", "gate": "Reproduction criterion: reimplement on the Pappalardo dataset with time-ordered replication; verdict rationale — a modest, honest paper with no direct NFL method, so the transfer bar is an ablation showing incremental gain on NGS target networks.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2409.13888v2", "title": "Causal Feature Selection Method for Contextual Multi-Armed Bandits in Recommender System", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Select pick/staking-model features with causal HIE/HDD instead of correlation, extended to continuous graded rewards (ROI per pick via per-bin reward densities) and time-varying HIE in rolling 4-week windows, feeding the changepoint-resetting bandit from ledger 0810 to close the loop between feature selection and non-stationary model selection.", "gate": "ADAPT if on the GSE 2025 holdout replay (a) HIE/HDD rank a known-spurious correlate (e.g., raw team win%) below true HTE features like line-movement buckets, AND (b) the LinUCB selector using HIE/HDD top features beats the correlation-selected selector by ≥ 1.5 ROI points per 100 picks.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2409.13934v1", "title": "On the Extrapolation of Generative Adversarial Networks for Downscaling Precipitation Extremes in Warmer Climates", "normalized_lane": "weather", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Justify generative extreme-weather simulation for GSE game-impact scenarios using the paper's 77%-vs-65% historical-training result as the evidence that GAN tails extrapolate without future data, then condition the generator on large-scale circulation indices (ENSO/NAO) and ensemble GAN seeds to measure tail-spread calibration, testing diffusion downscalers against the GAN on the same capture-fraction metric.", "gate": "ADAPT: the 77%-vs-65% historical-training result is exactly the evidence GSE needs to justify generative extreme-weather simulation — tails that extrapolate without future data (ledger states no further numeric gate).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2409.17077v1", "title": "Efficient Feature Interactions with Transformers: Improving User Spending Propensity Predictions in Gaming", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Replace the paper's fixed t±5 positional contextual windows with time-decayed contextual features (exponential decay on game-clock distance, explicit inter-play time gaps as token features) for drive-outcome prediction, and add isotonic/temperature-scaled calibration with ECE reporting that the paper ignored.", "gate": "ADAPT in two stages. Stage 1 (features): adopt the t±5 contextual-window features if challenger A beats baseline XGBoost on 2023–2024 test MAE by ≥ 1% with non-overlapping 10-seed intervals. Stage 2 (architecture): adopt the transformer only if challenger B beats *both* baseline and challenger A by ≥ 1% MAE *and* the inference cost passes the ledger's latency check.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2409.17129v1", "title": "Bayesian Bivariate Conway-Maxwell-Poisson Regression Model for Correlated Count Data in Sports", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add the bivariate Conway-Maxwell-Poisson as a totals-modeling option with time-varying (random-walk) dispersion so variance itself is predictable (e.g., weather-driven variance inflation in wind games), extended to a multivariate CMP over (home points, away points, home turnovers, away turnovers) for a joint spread/total/turnover model.", "gate": "Adopt CMP as a totals-modeling option if, on the reproducible test, its out-of-sample joint log-loss beats bivariate Poisson and NB (or ties with demonstrably better tail calibration) and a full-season fit runs in <24 h on GSE hardware.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2409.18645v1", "title": "The Craft of Selective Prediction: Towards Reliable Case Outcome Classification", "normalized_lane": "mixed", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add MC-dropout plus certainty-based rejection (CER) selective prediction to the engine with γ learned per market type, so GSE abstains on low-confidence picks at fixed coverage; if the abstention moves metrics but not ROI, keep it as a risk–coverage monitoring layer rather than a selection change.", "gate": "ADAPT bar: MC-dropout + CER must beat the current single-pass baseline on AURCC and realized ROI at fixed coverage on a hold-out season; if only the metrics move but ROI doesn't, adopt the abstention machinery as a monitoring layer (risk–coverage reporting) rather than a selection change.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2410.00943v1", "title": "RisingBALLER: A Player is a Token, a Match is a Sentence — A Path Towards a Foundational Model for Football Players Data Analytics", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Pre-train a player-as-token foundation model on NFL event data with two-tower pre-training (masked player-token prediction plus masked game-context prediction, masking the opponent's defensive stats to force offense-vs-defense interaction embeddings), earning a place in the projection stack.", "gate": "ADAPT if Test 1 passes (embeddings capture real player structure) AND Test 2 shows ≥5% MAE improvement. REJECT if MPP accuracy is near chance or downstream gains are <2%.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2410.01304v1", "title": "Deep Learning for Action Spotting in Association Football Videos", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a two-stream (video + NGS tracking coordinates as auxiliary neck input) action spotter for NFL core classes (snap, handoff, pass release, off-ball actions) as GSE's charting pipeline, which neither pure-video nor pure-tracking methods can match on unshown/off-ball actions.", "gate": "Adopt (proceed to scale-up) if the fine-tuned spotter reaches mAP@1 ≥ 0.60 on the 3 held-out NFL games for the core classes (snap, handoff, pass release). Reject/shelve otherwise.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2410.01307v1", "title": "FanCric: Multi-Agentic Framework for Crafting Fantasy 11 Cricket Teams", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Add a multi-agent context layer to the weekly DFS pipeline where each agent's qualitative signal enters as a prior with explicit uncertainty calibrated from 2024 backtest hit rates, with reliability-weighted shrinkage damping the hallucinated signals while keeping the useful fraction of context adjustments.", "gate": "ADOPT the context-agent layer into the weekly DFS pipeline only if it beats the projection-only MILP baseline by ≥ 3 percentile points over a full 17-week backtest AND the per-player multiplier JSON is auditable (every multiplier traceable to a cited data source — no LLM-invented narratives).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2410.02519", "title": "A Report on Semantic-Guided RL for Interpretable Feature Engineering (SMART)", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Deploy semantic-guided RL feature engineering with SWRL semantic veto and temporal leakage rules, and test the untested transfer claim by freezing the KG-grounded state encoder trained on the NFL panel and transferring the policy to a CFB panel to get a multi-sport FE policy for one sport's exploration budget.", "gate": "ADAPT if: ≥0.003 held-out NFL log-loss improvement on 2025 games versus the raw-features baseline, zero semantically invalid features in the final set (SWRL veto pass), no post-kickoff leakage, and mean human interpretability rating ≥4.0/5.0 on the top-20 features.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2410.05431v2", "title": "Continuous Ensemble Weather Forecasting with Diffusion Models", "normalized_lane": "mixed", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Adopt a continuous-trajectory diffusion weather forecaster for in-game conditions, conditioned on the pregame spread/total as a market-consistency constraint so the same ensemble stays calibrated to the closing line and serves both live-betting win probability and pregame pricing.", "gate": "ADOPT the continuous-trajectory forecaster if, on 2024, its CRPS at 30- and 60-minute leads beats the per-horizon baselines by ≥5% AND sampled trajectories are monotone-coherent (no lead-time crossing artifacts in ≥95% of sampled members).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2410.08474v4", "title": "SPORTU: A Comprehensive Sports Understanding Benchmark for Multimodal Large Language Models", "normalized_lane": "mixed", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Fine-tune an open video model on GSE's NFL clip annotations with direct-answer training (no CoT) to test whether domain tuning closes the gap to proprietary models at ~1/50th inference cost, and gate any video model entering the content pipeline on ≥65% NFL-split MCQs and open-ended G-Eval ≥ 2.5.", "gate": "Route any video model into the content pipeline only if it scores ≥65% on the NFL split MCQs AND its open-ended G-Eval ≥ 2.5 — otherwise keep the human-in-the-loop workflow.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2410.09068", "title": "Modeling and Prediction of the UEFA EURO 2024 via Combined Statistical Learning Approaches", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Upgrade the pregame spread/total pipeline to a bivariate-Poisson combined score model (correlation ρ estimated per matchup-total band) and extend it in-game by re-estimating (λ₁,λ₂) from the pregame ensemble plus live score/clock state each minute with a short 10k-sim Monte Carlo, capturing the garbage-time correlation that independence assumptions miss.", "gate": "Adopt the enhanced-variable + ensemble pipeline if the combined score model beats the engine's current spread/total probability layer on Brier score for game winner AND margin MAE over 2023–2024 by ≥0.003 / ≥0.15 points respectively, with the logability (market-consensus) variable showing positive permutation importance.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2410.09180v2", "title": "Convergence and stationary distribution of Elo rating systems", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Schedule GSE's Elo K-factors from the paper's √K scaling frontier (making K choices from an explicit error budget) and apply an empirically estimated bias curve E[X]−ρ (final Elo vs next-season win total, 2015–2025) as a shrinkage correction to preseason Elo — a debiased Elo the authors themselves list as desirable future work.", "gate": "Adopt the √K frontier for K-factor scheduling if the 2015–2025 fit yields R² ≥ 0.6 on the √K regression of team-level rating dispersion. Reject if the relationship fails (R² < 0.3).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2410.09190v2", "title": "Time to Retrain? Detecting Concept Drifts in Machine Learning Systems", "normalized_lane": "continual_online_learning", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Deploy a two-stage concept-drift detector in the weekly cron: stage 1 pre-game inspector-disagreement PHT on the upcoming slate as a cheap early filter, stage 2 post-game PUDD chi-square on the resolved PU-index, trading weak precision for combination specificity on retrain decisions.", "gate": "ADOPT the inspector monitor if on 2020–2025 nflverse: (i) PHT disagreement alarms precede ≥50% of labeled regime-change episodes by ≥1 week, (ii) ≤2 false alarms per season, (iii) refit-on-alarm does not degrade Brier by more than 0.002 vs frozen baseline on non-alarm weeks, and (iv) the pipeline runs end-to-end in the weekly cron in <5 minutes.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2410.11078v2", "title": "Predicting Chess Puzzle Difficulty with Transformers", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace fixed Gaussian label-noise clipping in GSE's spread-margin models with a two-component label-noise mixture (Gaussian plus heavy-tailed component for known noisy regimes like backup-QB games and extreme weather), with the mixture weight a function of game metadata (roster flags, wind), so the outliers are modeled explicitly instead of clipped away.", "gate": "Adopt if any of: (a) sampled-target model reduces held-out MAE on 2023–2024 by ≥ 0.15 points vs the identical point-target baseline (averaged over 5 seeds), or (b) the MAZ analogue improves ≥ 3% relative while MAE does not worsen; improvement experiment adds per-slice (weather/roster-flag) MAZ improvement ≥ 5%.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2410.11185", "title": "Neural Symbolic Regression of Complex Network Dynamics", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Discover symbolic laws of NFL team dynamics with PIND-style coordinated search (F and G skeletons recovered separately) on time-varying matchup graphs with edge features (rest differential, travel distance, weather), training across 2015–2024 and freezing the equations to transfer-test on 2024–2025 without refitting constants.", "gate": "ADAPT if: on synthetic league data, coordinated search recovers both F and G skeletons in ≥ 8/10 seeds (vs ≤ 5/10 for joint search) AND on real 2025 data the F+G model matches the engine's spread MAE within 0.3 points. Transfer success = equations transfer with < 5% MAE degradation.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2410.16333", "title": "Conformal Predictive Portfolio Selection", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build DFS portfolio selection on conformal predictive intervals with a cost-aware high-risk/low-risk rule: select the maximum upper bound among low-risk candidates after subtracting expected rake and fading high-ownership lineups, correcting the paper's frictionless 3-asset orientation (verified against the sign error in an A/B) before it ever touches real slates.", "gate": "ADOPT the corrected rule if it beats projection-maximizing selection on 2024–2025 ROI with statistical significance (paired test over slates); REJECT the paper's as-written orientation if the A/B shows the literal lowest-r version underperforms (confirming the sign error).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2410.17238v1", "title": "SELA: Tree-Search Enhanced LLM Agents for Automated Machine Learning", "normalized_lane": "llm_agents_ai_scientist", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Upgrade the nightly signal-discovery agent with SELA-style MCTS structured as a hierarchy over signal families (matchup / weather / rest / market / special-teams as level-1 branches, hypotheses as level-2) with progressive widening, so thin-lane winners like special teams and referees get explicitly budgeted early exploration instead of being starved.", "gate": "ADOPT if: MCTS arm finds ≥1.5× the gate-passing signals of round-robin at equal budget, wasted rollouts drop by ≥30%, and the tree's value estimates correlate (Spearman ≥ 0.5) with final holdout scores. REJECT if MCTS ≈ round-robin within 20%.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INVENT", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
