{"arxiv_id": "2503.19355v2", "title": "ST-VLM: Kinematic Instruction Tuning for Spatio-Temporal Reasoning in Vision-Language Models", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Ship a KinQA-tuned vision-language assistant for GSE content work that answers kinematic questions from video, trained on multi-step kinematic reasoning chains grounded in exact NGS labels (e.g., was separation at catch point above league-average NGS separation for this route type?) to exploit the label luxury the paper's pseudo-labeling lacked.", "gate": "ADOPT the KinQA-tuned assistant for GSE content work only if it reaches ≥55% accuracy on the 5,000-pair held-out set with paraphrased questions AND ≥95% on comparison questions; otherwise REJECT.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2503.19809v1", "title": "Simulating Tracking Data to Advance Sports Analytics Research", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the entity-schema plus event/stint extraction layer for GSE's NGS pipeline, and close the paper's admitted gap quantitatively by computing MMD on player-velocity and spacing distributions between simulated and real NGS frames, measuring the sim-to-real degradation of models trained in simulation as the transferability score gating which model classes are safe to prototype there.", "gate": "Adopt the entity-schema + event/stint extraction layer for GSE's NGS pipeline if the reproducible test passes (it is pure engineering with no downside); adopt the simulation-first prototyping lane only after identifying a football simulator with adequate behavioral realism.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2503.20082", "title": "Optimizing Forecast Combination Weights Using Exponentially Weighted Hit and Win Rate Losses", "normalized_lane": "ensembles", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Set ensemble combination weights with exponentially weighted hit/win-rate losses, upgrading the paper's symmetric win loss to a magnitude-weighted Cauchy surrogate w_t·F_Cauchy(|R_t|−1) with w_t = |actual − consensus| — so the combiner concentrates weight where the CLV dollars are largest, directly optimizing expected CLV instead of win frequency.", "gate": "ADOPT if on the 2025 holdout the combiner achieves win rate vs. consensus ≥ 55% and beat-the-close rate ≥ 52.5% (the standard -110 breakeven is 52.38%) and Brier score no worse than +1% vs. simple average. REJECT if win rate ≤ 52% or beat-the-close < 52.38%.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2503.21067", "title": "1716 AskSport: Web application for sports question-answering", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Ship a sports QA interface on the AskSport contract — answer plus temperature-scaled calibrated confidence, source title and URL, and explicit abstention — with the retrieval-confidence gate (joint calibration of retrieval score × reader confidence as the displayed number) and an abstention experiment on 50 injected unanswerable questions to convert the demo into a deployable product decision.", "gate": "ADAPT the interface contract only — answer + calibrated confidence + source title + source URL + explicit abstention. ADAPT proceeds if the reproducible test above passes on GSE's corpus; REJECT the raw-softmax confidence display unconditionally.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2503.23782v1", "title": "Distributional regression with reject option", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace the static ε=0.15–0.2 plug-in rejection budget with a regime-conditional one: allocate larger sit-out fractions to high-entropy regimes (division games, heavy weather, short rest) and smaller ones to clean games, testing whether it improves published ROI over the global ε.", "gate": "ADAPT if the ε=0.15–0.2 plug-in rule achieves |r̂−ε| ≤ 2pp and beats the no-gate baseline on published-game ROI by ≥1pp with lower CRPS error; adopt the entropy criterion if it also beats the 0700 conformal gate.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.00767v1", "title": "Automated Explanation of Machine Learning Models of Footballing Actions in Words", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Auto-generate wordalised explanations of the engine's daily output for content drafts (human/voice-gate approval before posting), with deterministic fidelity checking (parse claimed factor directions from text and compare against true contribution signs, no LLM judge) and SHAP-based wordalisation of the actual non-additive model instead of requiring a linear one.", "gate": "Adopt as a draft-generation step if: (a) sentence-level fidelity ≥ 90% on the 50-pick test, and (b) Garrett's blinded engagement rating favors wordalised by ≥ 0.5 points, and (c) contribution extraction runs automatically on the daily engine output. Reject (keep as reference) if fidelity < 85%.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.01781", "title": "Proper Scoring Rules for Estimation and Forecast Evaluation", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the proper-scoring framework as GSE's forecast-evaluation doctrine — Brier for cover probabilities, CRPS primary for margin/total distributions, threshold-weighted CRPS for blowout tails — implemented as crps.ts scoring every model version against market-implied distributions weekly, giving a proper-score skill-gap decomposition (where GSE beats the market vs. where it loses) as the weekly model-vs-market scoreboard.", "gate": "ADOPT CRPS as primary if: model rankings by CRPS are stable across 2023/2024/2025 (Spearman ≥ 0.8 year-to-year) and CRPS-selected models also win on realized betting utility (CLV). REJECT minimum-CRPS training if it degrades NLL-based tail diagnostics (log score) by >10% — keep NLL training, CRPS evaluation.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.04186v1", "title": "AutoComp: Automated Data Compaction for Log-Structured Tables in Data Lakes", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Add a weekly OPTIMIZE hook for GSE's log-structured tables and replace the weighted-sum compaction objective with an enumerated multi-objective Pareto frontier over (ΔF, GBHr) for all compactable tables weekly, picking the Pareto knee — producing the first empirical Pareto study of compaction trade-offs the authors left as future work.", "gate": "ADOPT the hook iff: (a) uncompacted 8-week fragmentation degrades the training-path join by ≥ 20% vs post-OPTIMIZE; (b) weekly OPTIMIZE cost < 5% of the weekly build's compute cost; (c) zero write-write conflicts over 4 consecutive weeks of hook operation.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.04798v1", "title": "TabRep: Roots-of-Unity Categorical Encoding for Unified Tabular Diffusion", "normalized_lane": "synthetic_data", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Adopt TabRep (Flow variant, roots-of-unity categorical encoding) as the fast-sampling tabular diffusion backbone, with a learned per-category residual rotation δ_k (small, regularized) on top of Elo-ordered base angles so the geometric prior keeps order semantics while the model fine-tunes angular positions to actual team-similarity structure (dome teams cluster, rival schemes cluster).", "gate": "ADOPT TabRep (Flow variant) as the fast-sampling backbone if: (a) log-loss gain ≥0.003 on held-out 2024, AND (b) Elo-ordered beats lexicographic on pair-correlation fidelity by ≥10% relative, AND (c) OOI-cast index-0 bias ≤ 25% relative overrepresentation vs uniform.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.06163v1", "title": "Action Valuation in Sports: A Survey", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Build an expected route value (ERV) model from NGS tracking for off-ball receiver valuation: predict the completion-probability surface over the field given play state, value the actual route as ∫(ERV at actual position − ERV at league-average route) over the play, and sum to a per-player off-ball contribution — the football instantiation of the survey's multi-agent credit-assignment problem that no surveyed paper does for American football.", "gate": "ADOPT the survey's recommendations into GSE's methods docs only if test (a) shows any alternative horizon beats the drive-level baseline by ≥0.005 AUC on the 2024–2025 out-of-sample window; otherwise record the taxonomy as a reference and REJECT immediate pipeline changes.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.08066v1", "title": "The AI Scientist-v2: Workshop-Level Automated Scientific Discovery via Agentic Tree Search", "normalized_lane": "llm_agents_ai_scientist", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Upgrade the nightly signal-discovery loop to a manager-plus-agentic-tree-search with replication discipline and budget-adaptive branch allocation — the manager allocates more branches to hypotheses whose early nodes show high variance across replications (uncertain but promising) and prunes low-variance losers early, finding the same winners at ~50% of the backtest compute.", "gate": "ADOPT the manager + replication discipline if: (a) ≥80% of signals that pass under the tree+replication protocol still pass on an independent re-run with fresh bootstrap seeds (reproducibility), vs ≤60% for the linear protocol; and (b) the manager's best-node selection agrees with the deterministic evaluator's ranking on ≥90% of stages.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INVENT", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.08110v1", "title": "Towards Unconstrained 2D Pose Estimation of the Human Spine", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add SpinePose-style spine-keypoint estimation to the video lane with pad-occlusion augmentation during fine-tuning (randomly mask the torso with jersey-colored rectangles and supervise spine keypoints with higher uncertainty) and a temporal consistency term penalizing frame-to-frame spine-curvature jumps, so curvature can be inferred from shoulder/hip cues when pads hide vertebral cues.", "gate": "ADOPT the SpinePose fine-tune recipe for a GSE video lane only if replication lands within the §12 tolerances AND the model yields ≥85 AP on a held-out set of football-pad torso images annotated with the nine spine keypoints; otherwise REJECT — pads likely invalidate the paper's claimed generalization.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.08175v3", "title": "Multi-person Physics-based Pose Estimation for Combat Sports", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add the iLQR physics-based collision-refinement stage to GSE's pose pipeline, replacing the paper's empirical loss-weight schedule with automated Bayesian weight-tuning over w_1…w_6 and testing capsule-based collision geometry to see whether the Hi4D penetration regression is a geometry-resolution artifact.", "gate": "ADOPT the iLQR collision-refinement stage only if, on the paper's released supplementary dataset, it beats the kinematics-only baseline by the paper's own margins (≥10% reduction in e_MPJPE and ≥50% reduction in e_foot,vxy); otherwise REJECT.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.08222v2", "title": "F³Set: Towards Analyzing Fast, Frequent, and Fine-grained Events from Videos", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build NFL fine-grained event spotting with multi-label factorization and replace the BiGRU context refiner with constrained decoding: a learned NFL play-grammar (down/distance → legal next events) as hard constraints on the event sequence, turning invalid-sequence errors into a guarantee (a touchdown event can only follow a catch/run event).", "gate": "PURSUE if the pilot reproduces the paper's two structural findings on NFL data: (a) multi-label factorization beats multi-class by ≥ 5 pp F1_evt, and (b) CTX eliminates the invalid-sequence errors the baseline produces; REJECT the architecture if F³ED fails to beat a plain E2E-Spot-style baseline on NFL clips.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.08747v1", "title": "GridMind: A Multi-Agent NLP Framework for Unified, Cross-Modal NFL Data Insights", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build GSE's conversational data layer on the GridMind architecture (agent decomposition + RAG + NL-to-SQL + synthesis) as the reference design, closing its two admitted gaps with parallel agent execution plus query-result caching and a deterministic executed-query eval, and add the wordalisation synthesis head on top for the full ask-and-explain loop.", "gate": "Adopt the architecture (agent decomposition + RAG + NL-to-SQL + synthesis) as GSE's conversational-layer reference design. Do not adopt GridMind itself — no code/data, vendor-locked metrics, 58% accuracy. Kill the fan-facing variant if the eval in §12 doesn't clear 85% accuracy.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.08764", "title": "1725 Evaluation of the phi-3-mini SLM for identification of texts related to medicine, health, and sports injuries", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Use the SLM strictly as a recall-oriented triage filter in the news cascade — never as a standalone labeler — with Platt/isotonic-calibrated 1–10 scores, thresholds re-tuned on calibrated probabilities, a reporter-specialty prior multiplied into the score, and a fine-tuned BERT-class classifier baseline to test whether the smaller model beats the SLM at 1/10th the inference cost.", "gate": "ADAPT strictly as a recall-oriented triage filter in a cascade — never as a standalone labeler. ADAPT proceeds if the reproducible test shows recall ≥ 0.95 at an affordable operating point.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.09759v1", "title": "Enhancing Classifier Evaluation: A Fairer Benchmarking Strategy Based on Ability and Robustness", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add an IRT-for-games evaluation layer with a graded ordinal response model (beat close by >3 pts / beat close / miss close / miss badly) that credits how much a model beat the market, turning the Glicko tournament into a money-weighted ranking tied to CLV magnitude instead of plain hit rate.", "gate": "Adopt IRT-for-games as a GSE model-evaluation layer if (a) per-game difficulty is temporally stable (r ≥ 0.5 across disjoint season blocks) AND (b) the IRT ability ranking of engine versions matches the Glicko-2 ranking and both disagree with plain accuracy by at least one rank flip among the top 3.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.09953v1", "title": "Efficient 2D to Full 3D Human Pose Uplifting including Joint Rotations", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build full 3D pose uplifting (including joint rotations) for the video lane, removing the biggest deployment blocker by estimating per-player body shape from a few frames via the A2B anthropometric approach and fine-tuning the uplifter jointly with shape estimation instead of requiring GT body shapes.", "gate": "PURSUE full replication if the plausibility test passes with zero twist failures and end-to-end runtime ≤ 50 ms/frame; REJECT for broadcast use if twist failures persist despite the VPoser prior or the detector pushes the pipeline past 100 ms/frame.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.10106v1", "title": "SoccerNet-v3D: Leveraging Sports Broadcast Replays for 3D Scene Understanding", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Mint 3D ball and pose ground truth from existing NFL broadcast footage with the paper's annotation-mining recipe — calibration quality gates, reprojection-filtered triangulation, closed-loop box optimizer (engineering directive: optimize size, not center) — the cheapest credible path to 3D ball ground truth for NGS-replacement, with no wearables and no camera rigs.", "gate": "Ledger states no numeric gate; the transferable asset is the annotation-mining recipe (calibration gates, triangulation, box optimizer), and the football-shape caveat is an adaptation task: the sphere prior (Eq. 7) must be re-derived for a prolate-spheroid football with unknown orientation.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.10415v2", "title": "LLM-SRBench: A New Benchmark for Scientific Equation Discovery with Large Language Models", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the bench as GSE's symbolic-regression evaluation standard (keeping the OOD-NMSE protocol regardless) and run an obfuscation audit on GSE-SR: algebraically transform 10 previously discovered nflverse equations, hide variable names, and re-run discovery — re-discovery of the transformed forms proves it's discovering, textbook-forms-only proves it's reciting.", "gate": "ADOPT the bench as GSE's SR evaluation standard if a pilot (10 sports tasks) shows it discriminates between SR variants (≥10pp symbolic-accuracy spread between best and worst variant); REJECT as overkill if all variants score within noise.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.10936v1", "title": "Can LLMs Leverage Observational Data? Towards Data-Driven Causal Discovery with LLMs", "normalized_lane": "causal_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build closed-loop LLM causal discovery: the LLM proposes edges from data, PC conditional-independence tests and a probe battery accept/reject them, and rejections are fed back into the prompt as constraints (\"V3 does NOT cause V7; propose alternatives\"), so the model stops re-proposing statistically-dead edges — with anonymized-label controls separating reasoning gains from memorization.", "gate": "ADOPT the LLM proposal layer if: (a) anonymized-label LLM F1 ≥ PC F1 on synthetic; (b) LLM priors reduce NOTEARS SHD on synthetic by ≥10% or raise probe hit rate by ≥0.05; (c) per-edge cost stays under $0.50 at 35 vars. Reject if (a) fails.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.12100v1", "title": "Generalized Visual Relation Detection with Diffusion Models", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt generative open-vocabulary relation decoding with a large rounding vocabulary as GSE's paradigm for semantically ambiguous sports action/event vocabularies (quarterback-releases-ball type relations instead of fixed-class discrimination), evaluated with the T2I-retrieval/SPICE proxy metrics that solve the models-richer-than-annotations evaluation problem.", "gate": "Ledger states no numeric gate: this is a stills-only research prototype (50 DDIM steps, no sports data, no latency numbers) — the adaptation is conceptual and evaluative, not a pipeline to deploy.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.17355v1", "title": "Collaborative Multi-Agent RL for Automated Feature Transformation with Graph-Driven Path Optimization (TCTO)", "normalized_lane": "auto_feature_eng", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Make the TCTO graph-driven feature-transformation roadmap temporal: weight roadmap edges by recency (recent seasons' mutual-information scores count more in node-wise pruning) and re-run the multi-agent search each offseason, converting TCTO from a one-shot search into a self-updating feature factory that tests whether discovered interactions are stable across NFL seasons or regime-specific.", "gate": "Accept the adaptation iff on the 2024 holdout TCTO's discovered feature set improves LightGBM log-loss by ≥ 0.003 over the raw-metric baseline AND matches-or-beats exhaustive pairwise crosses with ≤ half the feature count.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.17365", "title": "TimeSoccer: An End-to-End Multimodal Large Language Model for Soccer Commentary Generation", "normalized_lane": "nlp", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build end-to-end NFL commentary generation with an MLLM trained on GSE's recipe, adopting the paper's training-free MoFA-Select compression module, adding a jersey-number detection head for player-identity grounding (fixing the anonymity limitation), and testing MoFA-Select standalone as a motion-budget-driven highlight-clip selector.", "gate": "ACCEPTED (ADAPT): first end-to-end SDVC MLLM + training-free reusable compression module + systematic ablations. ADAPT (not ADOPT): no code release, soccer-only, modest absolute precision — adopt the MoFA-Select module and training recipe, retrain the MLLM on NFL data.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.19612v1", "title": "Relative Advantage: Quantifying Performance in Noisy Competitive Settings", "normalized_lane": "experimental", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace absolute team-stat features with relative-difference features and model differential environmental sensitivity: estimate team-specific environmental loadings η_i = λ_i·η and use the adjusted relative metric R_adj = (X_A − λ̂_A η̂) − (X_B − λ̂_B η̂), so a dome team's stats in wind are discounted differently than its opponent's — the heterogeneous-environment extension the authors list as future work.", "gate": "Adopt the principle if relative-difference features beat the two-feature absolute baseline on held-out 2024–2025 NFL games by ≥ 0.01 AUC on log-loss-neutral comparison.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.20052v1", "title": "Can Geometry Save Central Views for Sports Field Registration?", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Re-derive the pole-polar correspondence trick for the NFL's parallel yard-line primitive (two parallel lines fix a vanishing point; hash-mark ticks at known 1-yard spacing along a known world line construct the pole-polar analog), generating virtual correspondences for field registration without any circle primitive.", "gate": "ADOPT the pole-polar correspondence trick only if, on the 50-still NFL set, the derived correspondences reduce MRE by ≥20% vs the line-only baseline, or enable calibration on ≥10 stills where the line-only baseline has <4 correspondences.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.20768v2", "title": "LakeVilla: Multi-Table Transactions for Lakehouses", "normalized_lane": "data_infra", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "INFRA", "improvement": "Adopt the LakeVilla manifest pattern for multi-table atomicity in GSE's lakehouse builds, then log one full season's commit latencies and orphan-sweep results to publish the first public \"multi-table atomicity at small-team scale\" operational record — the data point the paper's enterprise numbers lack.", "gate": "ADOPT the manifest pattern iff: (a) the kill-mid-write test passes 10/10 runs; (b) orphan sweep runs clean weekly with zero false positives for 4 weeks; (c) manifest-flip + read-path change adds < 1% to build wall-clock. REJECT full LakeVilla beyond the pattern.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2504.20877v2", "title": "Preference-centric Bandits: Optimality of Mixtures and Regret-efficient Algorithms", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Allocate weekly stakes with the CVaR preference-mixture selector over GSE's own pick history (Neon picks table, model v5.2.7, SPREAD/MONEYLINE/TOTAL): walk-forward comparison of (a) PM mixture allocation vs (b) quarter-Kelly on the single highest-edge pick — the mixture should achieve strictly better preference-mixture value (lower drawdown at similar growth) than any solitary pick when outcomes are heterogeneous.", "gate": "At T=60k under GD on the paper's 2-arm Bernoulli setup, PM-UCB-M's average regret must be ≤ 50% of uniform sampling's average regret, with regret decreasing monotonically across T∈{20k,40k,60k}.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2505.00724", "title": "Optimal Blackjack Betting Strategies Through Dynamic Programming and Expected Utility Theory", "normalized_lane": "sizing", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Solve a per-pick stake MDP per season (CRRA utility) and distill linear-in-edge staking rules for GSE's per-pick stakes, then re-solve the DP on expected utility under the engine's posterior over edge — testing whether internalizing edge uncertainty flattens the policy the way the paper's α-dial does, yielding a single calibration-driven staking rule instead of a hand-picked α.", "gate": "ADOPT the DP-distilled linear staking rule if it beats half-Kelly on terminal log growth with max drawdown ≤ half-Kelly's across the 2023–2025 second-half windows, and the distilled slope m is within 25% of the Kelly slope; REJECT otherwise.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2505.02170v3", "title": "Data-Driven Team Selection in Fantasy Premier League Using Integer Programming and Predictive Modeling Approach", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the IP optimizer for the weekly DFS packet with correlation-aware stacking built into the objective — bonus term λ·Σ_{(qb,wr)} corr_{qb,wr}·x_qb·x_wr linearized with auxiliary binaries, tuned on 2022–2023 and tested on 2024–2025 — the tournament edge the paper's plain formulation omits.", "gate": "ADOPT the IP optimizer into the weekly DFS packet iff it beats the greedy baseline's realized score in ≥ 60% of 2022–2025 slates AND the weighted-average-vs-current-projection bake-off winner is documented with a ≥ 3% mean-score edge. Otherwise REJECT.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2505.03585v1", "title": "Decision Making under Model Misspecification: DRO with Robust Bayesian Ambiguity Sets", "normalized_lane": "uncertainty_decision_theory", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace standard Kelly with robust Kelly under MMD-ball ambiguity sets, using an adaptive ε per game from the misspecification detector (high MMD distance → larger ambiguity ball) and a learned deep kernel on game features so the ball respects football-relevant similarity (divisional games near each other in kernel space) instead of a fixed Gaussian on outcomes.", "gate": "ACCEPT if walk-forward: final bankroll ≥ 1.1 × best baseline AND max drawdown ≤ 0.85 × best baseline's AND the predicted-vs-realized edge gap is ≤ 0.7 × the standard-Kelly baseline's. REJECT if robust Kelly posts <50% of the baseline's bet volume (degenerate conservatism).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2505.03991v3", "title": "Action Spotting and Precise Event Detection in Sports: Datasets, Methods, and Challenges", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the survey's formal action-spotting task taxonomy with tolerance windows (TAL/AS/PES tiers) and the 17-method leaderboard for video event-detection prototype selection (E2E-Spot/T-DEED/UGL), using the active-learning data-efficiency result (1/3 labels suffice) to de-risk the labeling budget before spending on annotation or training.", "gate": "Ledger states no numeric gate — a survey; the immediately actionable assets are the taxonomy, the tolerance-window evaluation equations, the 17-method leaderboard, and the 16-dataset catalog (Table II numbers are cross-paper and directional, not gospel).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2505.08342", "title": "Optimal Prize Design in Parallel Rank-order Contests", "normalized_lane": "props_dfs", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add a contest-routing layer to GSE's DFS play that selects GPPs by estimated field skill-share from the x(φ) sorting simulation, then extend the model with the missing multi-entry margin (each contestant chooses contest plus #entries with convex costs) to test whether pros buying 150 entries reverses the soft-field ranking — opening a quantitative case for selective GPP shots with duplicated-core/leveraged lineups rather than blanket avoidance.", "gate": "ADAPT if the offline replay shows routed contest selection beating uniform GPP entry by ≥5 pp ROI over 4 weeks AND the x(φ) sorting simulation reproduces the known qualitative pattern (top-heavy large-field GPPs concentrate the highest estimated skill share).", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2505.11841v2", "title": "Framing Causal Questions in Sports Analytics: A Tutorial on Estimand Choice Illustrated Through Crossing in Soccer", "normalized_lane": "causal_injury", "verdict": "ADOPT", "doctrine_tag": "SITUATIONAL", "improvement": "Adopt the estimand-first causal protocol as GSE's causal SOP — estimand before estimator — with interference-aware estimands (exposure mappings at the game level to sidestep within-game interference, e.g., the causal effect of a run-heavy game script on fourth-quarter EPA) and Rosenbaum-bounds/E-value sensitivity reporting as standard output so every causal claim ships with \"how strong would unmeasured confounding need to be to kill this result.\"", "gate": "ADOPT the estimand-first protocol as GSE's causal SOP if the QB-injury replication (§12) passes its balance gate (all SMDs < 10%) and produces an ATT with bootstrap SE that is stable across two independent season-blocks (2016–2020 vs 2021–2024, same sign, overlapping CIs).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2505.16630v1", "title": "SoccerChat: Integrating Multimodal Data for Enhanced Soccer Game Understanding", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build GSE's broadcast-video understanding QA pipeline on the SoccerChat recipe: turn NFL broadcast video into a ~49k-pair QA instruction dataset (the \"labeling factory\" pattern with the QA-generation layer added), training jointly on multiple datasets rather than sequentially (joint > sequential is the empirical rule) on top of the strongest general pretraining base available.", "gate": "Ledger states no numeric gate; the durable contributions are the reproducible instruction-dataset pipeline (49,120 QA pairs, 90,834 clips) and the empirical rule that joint multi-dataset training beats sequential fine-tuning.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2505.20922v1", "title": "Revisiting Multi-Agent World Modeling from a Diffusion-Inspired Perspective (DIMA)", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a diffusion-style multi-agent world model for play simulation that conditions each denoising step on a role+matchup embedding (\"WR3 vs CB2 in Cover-3\") and reveals agents in football-meaningful orders (ball carrier first, then blockers, then defenders) as a curriculum vs random permutations — testing whether role-aware reveal ordering improves +1s error by 10%+ over uniform permutation sampling.", "gate": "ADOPT if on held-out 2024 plays: (a) +0.5s mean player position error ≤ 0.8 yards (beats independent baseline by ≥20%), AND (b) reward head predicts play EPA within ±0.75 on ≥70% of plays, AND (c) permutation-invariance holds (order-shuffled rollouts diverge <5% at +1s).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2505.22422v2", "title": "STaR-Bets: Sequential Target-Recalculating Bets for Tighter Confidence Intervals", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace normal-approximation win-rate confidence intervals with STaR-Bets sequential target-recalculating intervals in the calibration lane: compute STaR-Bets vs normal-approx CIs on win-rate per probability decile of GSE's pick history (Neon picks, model v5.2.7), and count miscalibrated deciles each method flags — quantifying how much sample the tighter valid intervals save before a miscalibration is detected.", "gate": "At n = 256, Bernoulli(0.3), δ = 0.05, over 1,000 reps: STaR-Bets mean CI width must be ≤ 1.1× the randomized Clopper-Pearson mean width (near-optimality, Fig. 2R) with empirical coverage in [0.93, 0.97] (validity, Fig. 3).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}

{"arxiv_id": "2505.22954v3", "title": "Darwin Gödel Machine: Open-Ended Evolution of Self-Improving Agents", "normalized_lane": "llm_agents_ai_scientist", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the open-ended self-improving signal-factory: an archive of candidate signals with staging screening (Stage-0/1 discards ideas before the expensive Stage-2 holdout), and make parent selection multi-objective — gate margin, novelty vs archive embedding, lineage productivity, plus a MAP-Elites diversity bonus over signal families (matchup, weather, rest, market-microstructure) to fill the thin lanes the curriculum wants to target.", "gate": "ADOPT the archive + staging if: arm (b) produces ≥2× the Stage-3-passing signals of arm (a) over 30 nights, ≥1 winner has a failed node in its lineage (stepping stones are real), and Stage-0/1 screening discards ≥70% of ideas before the expensive Stage-2 holdout.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INVENT", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2505.23437v2", "title": "Bounded-Abstention Pairwise Learning to Rank", "normalized_lane": "abstention", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add a bounded-abstention pick-selection rule to the posting pipeline: select only picks whose confidence clears a conformalized conditional-risk threshold (Mondrian CP on edge-sign class) so risk estimates carry finite-sample coverage guarantees — replacing the paper's plug-in quantile threshold — and extend from pairwise to listwise (abstain on full slates, not pairs).", "gate": "ADOPT the rule into the posting pipeline only if, on the 2024–2025 test window, BALToR-selected picks beat the random-selection baseline by ≥1.5 pp hit rate at c=0.70 with empirical coverage within 0.02 of target, and beat the existing confidence-top-N rule (if any) by ≥0.5 pp. Otherwise REJECT.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "DECIDE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2505.24783", "title": "Paired comparison models with strength-dependent ties and order effects", "normalized_lane": "team_ratings", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt strength-dependent tie probabilities for GSE's soccer/NHL/boxing/push lanes — a Davidson-style tie parameter ν that rises with the average strength of the pair (β₁ > 0) rather than a constant ν — and test strength-dependent order (home-field) effects α₁ on NFL, including the HFA × quality interaction only if it improves ATS log-loss by ≥0.003 on 2018–2023 holdout, otherwise keeping flat HFA.", "gate": "Strength-dependent tie model must beat constant-ν Davidson by ≥ 0.005 out-of-sample 3-way log-loss on EPL 2022–2024 AND the β₁ coefficient must be positive with 95% CI excluding 0.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.00348", "title": "Beyond Winning: Margin of Victory Relative to Expectation Unlocks Accurate Skill Ratings", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace the ad-hoc tanh expected-margin curve with a market-informed one: E_MOV = spread-implied expected margin from the closing line, so the update's margin-surprise term becomes \"how much the result surprised the market\" rather than \"how much it surprised our own ratings\" — removing the circularity of ratings predicting margins that update ratings and connecting directly to the CLV lane.", "gate": "ADOPT the margin-surprise update into the team-strength layer if it clears the §12 gate on 2022–2025 NFL hold-out with no tuning after the gate is set. REJECT (do not merge) if it fails either metric, if the tanh fit is unstable across refits (parameter CV > 25%), or if it underperforms linear-MOV Elo.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.00613v1", "title": "WorldGym: World Model as An Environment for Policy Evaluation", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build the WorldGym-style harness for deployment decisions — a world-model environment for offline policy evaluation — replacing the single outcome head with a doubly robust estimator that combines the world-model rollout value with a model-free OPE estimator (weighted importance sampling on historical data) to correct the OOD-overestimation bias the authors flagged.", "gate": "ADOPT the harness for deployment decisions if: (a) Spearman ρ ≥ 0.7 between in-sim and real-backtest policy rankings on held-out 2024 (the paper's r=0.78 bar, rank version), AND (b) the harness identifies the best challenger variant using ≤50% of the real-game sample a pure backtest needs, AND (c) absolute value estimates track real backtest within the paper's reported band.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.01373v1", "title": "No Train Yet Gain: Towards Generic Multi-Object Tracking in Sports and Beyond", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt the McByte gating pattern for the video-tracking lane and fuse jersey-number OCR confidence as a third association cue alongside the mask: in ambiguity cases prefer the tracklet–detection pair whose OCR number matches the tracklet's majority-vote number — testing whether a football-specific identity cue beats the generic mask cue in same-uniform piles where masks are least reliable.", "gate": "ADOPT the McByte gating pattern if the McByte variant reduces ID switches by ≥ 30% vs ByteTrack on the 3-segment window with HOTA ≥ baseline; REJECT (keep ByteTrack/OC-SORT) if the gain is < 10% or throughput falls below 10 FPS offline-batch equivalent.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.02351v1", "title": "DIAMOND: An LLM-Driven Agent for Context-Aware Baseball Highlight Summarization", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Port DIAMOND to NFL as the automated first pass for weekly recap content and clip selection: replace the paper's hand-set scoring heuristics (1–60 bands, +1..+20 LLM adjustments, LI rank bonus) with a learned ranker trained on (play features, LLM narrative embedding) → human preference labels from GSE's own recap-selection history, optimizing pairwise ranking loss against broadcast ground truth.", "gate": "ADOPT as a GSE content tool if the NFL port beats WPA-only selection on F1 (≥5pp) and blinded narrative preference (≥60%) on the 20-game test; REJECT the LLM stages if no gain — ship the WPA+LI selector alone.", "owner": "Hermes", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.03057v1", "title": "Partially Regularized Ordinal Regression to Adjust Teams' Scoring for Strength of Schedule and Complementary Unit Performance in American Football", "normalized_lane": "win_spread_total", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add punter/kicker-specific field-position value (expected post-punt/kickoff starting position given returner and coverage units) to the partially-regularized ordinal-regression scoring model's complementary feature set — testing whether return-game quality is a stable, predictive team trait that survives the elastic-net selection across seasons.", "gate": "Adopt complementary features permanently if 10-fold CV on 2015–2024 shows MAE improvement with SE bars non-overlapping vs GS+SoS in ≥4 of 10 seasons; otherwise keep SoS-only.", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.03335v1", "title": "SportMamba Multi-Object Tracking", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adopt SportMamba's association design with jersey-number-conditioned association: replace the generic Re-ID embedding with a two-stream identity (a) a jersey-number OCR head producing a number posterior per detection and (b) team-side classification via jersey color clustering per game — association cost becomes a weighted sum of HA-EIoU, number-posterior agreement, and team agreement, attacking the paper's stated failure mode of near-identical uniforms.", "gate": "ADOPT the association design for GSE's video-tracking lane only if: on the football annotation set, the SportMamba-style pipeline beats ByteTrack by ≥ 3.0 HOTA points with the same detector, and the gain concentrates on occlusion-heavy plays.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.04282v1", "title": "DrSR: LLM based Scientific Equation Discovery with Dual Reasoning from Data and Experience", "normalized_lane": "symreg_equation_discovery", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Add the DrSR dual-reasoning loop (insight extraction π_data + idea generation from experience) to GSE-SR and run an analyst-in-the-loop insight audit: present π_data's structured insights to a human analyst weekly as \"what the machine thinks it's learning about football,\" turning the module into a discovery communication channel whose insights (e.g., \"pressure rate residuals spike in dome games\") may surface real football hypotheses even when the equations disappoint.", "gate": "ADOPT dual reasoning if full DrSR-style beats plain GSE-SR by ≥15% OOD NMSE on 2024–2025 AND valid-program rate ≥90% (vs whatever plain achieves); REJECT if the insight/idea modules add cost without ≥15% gain.", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.05763v1", "title": "Where Is The Ball: 3D Ball Trajectory Estimation From 2D Monocular Tracking", "normalized_lane": "world_models_simulators", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace the ballistic-only simulation with a 6-DoF football flight model including angular velocity state (spiral rate, wobble) and Magnus coefficients fit from NFL Next Gen Stats kick data, adding spin as a latent variable the end-of-trajectory network must implicitly detect from 2D wobble signatures — testing whether explicit orientation dynamics beat the sphere-assumption sim-to-real transfer on tumbling punts while matching on stable kickoffs.", "gate": "ADOPT the architecture if, on held-out real NFL kick/punt sequences with 2D tracks from broadcast video: (a) landing-spot error ≤ 1.5 yards mean absolute error, AND (b) beats the fitted-physics baseline by ≥25% on landing error, AND (c) sim-trained weights transfer (no more than 2× error inflation from synthetic validation to real).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "large", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.07860v1", "title": "Egocentric Event-Based Vision for Ping Pong Ball Trajectory Prediction", "normalized_lane": "tracking", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Adapt the event-based ball trajectory predictor to football flight with a drag+EKF model plus a Magnus/lift term whose spin-axis parameter is estimated from the ball ellipse's rotation across frames — testing whether spin-aware prediction beats drag-only on punts (highest spin) vs kickoffs.", "gate": "PURSUE the football flight-model adaptation if the drag+EKF model beats the constant-velocity baseline by ≥ 2 m on landing-point RMSE over the 20-clip window; otherwise REJECT and treat ball-flight estimation as buy-not-build (NGS air-distance family).", "owner": "Motif-lab", "bucket": "INGEST", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.09287", "title": "A Bayesian analysis of home advantage in professional squash", "normalized_lane": "bayesian", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Build a hierarchical Bayesian home model with team-specific home deviations (instead of a constant home field) plus an attendance/capacity-utilization interaction — testing whether real home-effect heterogeneity exists across NFL teams and how much of it crowds explain.", "gate": "Gate (ADAPT→keep): hierarchical home model beats constant-home baseline by ≥ 0.004 log-loss on 2022–2024 holdout AND ≥3 teams show |home deviation| > 2× posterior SD (i.e., real heterogeneity exists). Otherwise REJECT (keep constant home field).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "MODEL", "effort": "small", "depends_on": []}
{"arxiv_id": "2506.11399v1", "title": "Time-Varying Home Field Advantage in Football: Learning from a Non-Stationary Causal Process", "normalized_lane": "calibration", "verdict": "ADAPT", "doctrine_tag": "PROPRIETARY_EDGE", "improvement": "Replace the engine's static home-field number with a DYNAMO-style non-stationary causal learner that tracks how home advantage drifts over time, feeding DYNAMO-predicted per-drive expected points into the calibration layer so home edge is a time-varying causal quantity rather than a constant.", "gate": "Adopt the method for GSE only if, on the NFL reproducibility test, DYNAMO-predicted per-drive xP achieves MSE at least 10% lower than the raw-xP baseline on held-out weeks (the paper's Arsenal 2021-22 improvement, ≈29%, sets the bar; below 10% the complexity is not worth the NFL pipeline cost).", "owner": "Mimo", "bucket": "CALIBRATE", "effort": "medium", "depends_on": []}

