{"question": "What Are Games Played?", "answer": "Games played track the total number of games a player has appeared in. This stat reflects durability, career length, and availability."}
{"question": "What Are Games Started?", "answer": "Games started count the number of games a player begins in the starting lineup. This stat shows a player’s role and trust from coaches."}
{"question": "What Are Quarterback Wins?", "answer": "Quarterback wins record the number of games a quarterback won as a team's primary passer — the quarterback who took the most dropbacks in that game, which is the starter unless a reliever played most of it. Exactly one quarterback per team carries each game's result, so a reliever who threw a handful of passes is not credited with the win. This stat reflects overall success, team performance, and leadership."}
{"question": "What Are Quarterback Losses?", "answer": "QB losses record the number of games a quarterback lost as a team's primary passer — the quarterback who took the most dropbacks in that game. Exactly one quarterback per team carries each game's result, so a reliever who came in late is not charged with the loss. This stat provides context for career performance and team results."}
{"question": "What Are Quarterback Games Tied?", "answer": "QB games tied track the number of games a quarterback ended in a tie as a team's primary passer — the quarterback who took the most dropbacks in that game. This stat reflects rare outcomes in NFL competition."}
{"question": "What Is QB Winning Percentage?", "answer": "QB winning percentage measures wins as a share of the games a quarterback carried as a team's primary passer — wins plus losses plus ties, not every game the quarterback appeared in. This stat shows overall effectiveness and success as a starting quarterback."}
{"question": "What Are Total Touchdowns?", "answer": "Total touchdowns record the combined number of touchdowns a player scores in all situations. This stat reflects total scoring contribution."}
{"question": "What Are Games With A Touchdown?", "answer": "Games with a touchdown track how many games a player scores at least one touchdown. This stat reflects consistency in finding the end zone."}
{"question": "What Is Games With A Touchdown Percentage?", "answer": "Games with a touchdown percent measures the rate of games with at least one touchdown. This stat reflects scoring reliability."}
{"question": "What Is TD Rate?", "answer": "TD Rate measures how often a running back, wide receiver, or tight end scores a touchdown per touch -- where a touch is defined as a rushing attempt or a reception, not a target or other opportunity. This stat isolates finishing ability once the ball is in a player's hands, highlighting goal-line role and red-zone efficiency independent of raw touch volume."}
{"question": "What Are Two Point Conversions?", "answer": "Two-point conversions record the number of successful two-point plays scored. This stat reflects performance in critical scoring moments."}
{"question": "What Are Field Goals?", "answer": "Field goals record the total successful field goals made by a kicker. This stat reflects accuracy and scoring ability."}
{"question": "What Are Extra Points Kicked?", "answer": "Extra points kicked record the total number of successful extra points. This stat reflects consistency after touchdowns."}
{"question": "What Are Total Points Scored?", "answer": "Total points scored measures the combined points a player contributes through all scoring plays. This stat reflects total offensive or special teams output."}
{"question": "What Are Pass Completions?", "answer": "Pass completions count the total passes successfully caught from an NFL quarterback. This stat reflects accuracy, efficiency, and consistency in connecting with receivers, helping measure a passer’s reliability in sustaining drives."}
{"question": "What Are Pass Attempts?", "answer": "Pass attempts track the total times an NFL quarterback throws the ball, whether complete or not. This stat reflects workload, offensive style, and a quarterback’s involvement in the passing game, offering insight into a team’s play-calling balance."}
{"question": "What Are Passing Yards?", "answer": "Total passing yards highlight how quarterbacks contribute to their team’s offense across a season. This stat captures both volume and scheme — whether through heavy passing attacks, quick short-yardage gains, or explosive deep shots. Passing yard leaders often showcase high usage and adaptability within their offensive system."}
{"question": "What Are Passing Touchdowns?", "answer": "Passing touchdowns total the number of touchdowns thrown by an NFL quarterback. This stat measures their ability to finish drives, score through the air, and convert passing plays into points, reflecting both execution and red-zone efficiency."}
{"question": "What Is Touchdown Percentage?", "answer": "Passing touchdown percentage measures how often an NFL quarterback throws a touchdown per pass attempt. This stat reveals efficiency in turning throws into scores, indicating a passer’s effectiveness in capitalizing on scoring opportunities."}
{"question": "What Are Interceptions?", "answer": "Interceptions record the number of passes caught by the opposing defense from an NFL quarterback. This stat measures decision-making, accuracy, and risk-taking, showing how often mistakes result in turnovers that shift momentum."}
{"question": "What Is Interception Percentage?", "answer": "Interception percentage measures how often an NFL quarterback throws an interception per pass attempt. This stat highlights efficiency, accuracy, and ability to avoid costly mistakes that can swing a game’s outcome."}
{"question": "What Are Games With An Interception?", "answer": "Games with an interception track how many games an NFL quarterback throws at least one interception. This stat reflects consistency, decision-making under pressure, and the quarterback’s ability to protect the football."}
{"question": "What Is Percentage of Games With An Interception?", "answer": "Percent of game with an interception measures how often an NFL quarterback throws at least one interception in the games they play. This stat reflects decision-making, consistency, and ability to protect the football over the course of a season or career."}
{"question": "What Is Completion Percentage?", "answer": "Completion percentage measures the rate of passes completed out of total attempts for an NFL quarterback. This stat shows accuracy, efficiency, and ability to connect with receivers to sustain drives."}
{"question": "What Is Yards Per Pass Thrown?", "answer": "Yards per pass calculate the average yards gained per pass attempt. This stat reflects a quarterback’s ability to stretch the field and balance risk with production in the passing game."}
{"question": "What Is aDOT (Average Depth of Target)?", "answer": "aDOT, short for Average Depth of Target, measures how many yards downfield an NFL quarterback throws the ball on average, from the line of scrimmage to the spot of every pass attempt -- complete or not. This stat reflects a quarterback's aggressiveness and offensive scheme: a high aDOT signals a downfield, vertical passing attack, while a low aDOT points to a quick, short-passing game built around timing and yards after the catch."}
{"question": "What Is the Longest Pass?", "answer": "Longest pass records the single longest passing play completed by an NFL quarterback in a season or career. This stat showcases big-play potential and the ability to generate explosive offensive gains."}
{"question": "What Are QB Times Sacked?", "answer": "QB times sacked tracks the number of times a quarterback is tackled behind the line of scrimmage before releasing the ball. This stat reflects pass protection, awareness, and pocket mobility."}
{"question": "What Are Sack Yards Lost?", "answer": "Sack yards lost record the total yards lost when a quarterback is sacked. This stat shows the impact of sacks on offensive field position and overall efficiency."}
{"question": "What Is Yards Per Play?", "answer": "Yards per play calculate the average yards gained by the offense per play involving a quarterback. This stat reflects offensive efficiency and ability to sustain drives."}
{"question": "What Is Quarterback Rating?", "answer": "Quarterback rating combines passing stats into a single score that reflects a quarterback’s overall performance. This stat measures efficiency, accuracy, and scoring effectiveness."}
