{"question": "What Are Offensive QB Dropbacks?", "answer": "Offensive QB dropbacks counts the plays on which a team's quarterback dropped back to pass -- the play population behind our pressure metrics. It is the volume base for offensive QB pressures allowed and pressure rate, so heavy-volume passing teams naturally accumulate more raw pressures while their rates stay comparable."}
{"question": "What Are Offensive QB Pressures Allowed?", "answer": "Offensive QB pressures allowed counts the pass plays on which a team's offensive line let its quarterback come under pressure. Raw pressure counts track protection volume: comparing them against offensive QB dropbacks (via pressure rate) shows whether a line's total is a product of poor blocking or simply of passing volume."}
{"question": "What Are Pressures Allowed Per Game?", "answer": "Pressures allowed per game measures the average number of times a team's offensive line allows pressure on the quarterback each game. This stat reflects pass protection volume across the season."}
